13:59:24  DEBUG    [04e9585f5eeb4387]  sse_starlette.sse  chunk: b'event: result\r\ndata: {"query": "What are the default size limits for file uploads and total request size for the new multipart upload support on the OpenAI-compatible API endpoints?", "sections": [{"chunk_id": "a1b4fb27-784b-5167-88a7-eee7fadfbb39", "search_unit_id": "a1b4fb27-784b-5167-88a7-eee7fadfbb39", "block_from_id": "7b973113-64c9-54c6-82f0-a78cca2db581", "block_to_id": "7b973113-64c9-54c6-82f0-a78cca2db581", "section_path": "Pr 18421 Multipart File Validation Limits", "document_id": "196f5cda-0577-5c5b-88d5-a20d812333b4", "document_version_id": "b1a582e7-fa73-58af-bcea-6e975087fd50", "document_name": "github__dsid_ae068ee4aa9640159427cd941bef0238.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "p-2", "heading": "Pr 18421 Multipart File Validation Limits", "content": "Motivation: users integrating tool/function calling and file uploads via the OpenAI-compatibility endpoints were sending a wide variety of content-types and very large multipart requests which caused inconsistent runtime behavior, high memory pressure, and unexpected acceptance of unsupported payloads. This PR introduces a focused, backwards-compatible implementation for multipart/form-data parsing on the OpenAI-compatibility path, strict Content-Type validation for tool/file inputs, and deterministic payload limits both per-file and per-request. Summary of changes: 1) Add a streaming-safe multipart parser that yields parts rather than buffering entire requests; 2) Validate Content-Type of each part (whitelist: text/*, image/*, application/json, application/octet-stream with explicit size checks); 3) Enforce configurable limits: max_file_size (default 10MiB), max_total_request_size (default 50MiB), max_parts_count (default 20). These defaults are conservative and documented; they can be overridden at tenant or route level via API config. 4) Hook validation into the OpenAI-compat layer so existing client integrations get predictable errors (400/413) with structured error bodies when inputs are rejected. 5) Add detailed unit and integration tests and end-to-end tests for streaming uploads and for the dedicated Dedicated/Private ingress paths. Backwards compatibility notes: this does not change the non-multipart JSON body semantics. Existing users who relied on accepting arbitrary large file uploads should update their tenant config or use Redwood Dedicated with higher quotas. Rollout plan: feature-flagged behind feature.enable_multipart_input (off by default); staged rollout to internal dogfood tenants, then gradual roll to 10%, 50%, 100% via config rollout. Checklist: - [x] Streaming-safe multipart parser implemented - [x] Content-Type whitelist + validation errors - [x] Per-file and per-request size enforcement + configurable defaults - [x] OpenAI-compat error mapping and structured error shapes - [x] Tests: unit, integration, e2e - [x] Docs: compatibility notes and config guide - [x] Telemetry: counters for rejected parts and throttled requests - [x] Migration & rollout plan included Testing notes: the multipart parser uses a small constant memory footprint for each active part and yields part metadata to the handler; large parts trigger a streaming drain with early termination (413 response) to avoid OOM. Integration tests exercise combination of binary and text parts, wrong content-types, and boundary cases around the configured limits. Telemetry: added metrics api.multipart.rejected_content_type, api.multipart.rejected_size, api.multipart.accepted_parts and a hist for part sizes. Implementation details: - parser: runtime/multipart/stream_parser.py - validator: api/validation/multipart_validator.py - compat layer: api/openai_compat/input_adapter.py - config: config/defaults/multipart.yaml - docs: docs/openai-compat/multipart.md - tests: tests/unit/test_multipart_parser.py, tests/integration/test_openai_compat_multipart.py Error shape examples (structured output): when a part is rejected we return 413 with a JSON body {\\"error\\":{\\"type\\":\\"request_too_large\\",\\"message\\":\\"part exceeds max_file_size\\",\\"meta\\":{\\"part_name\\":\\"file\\",\\"limit_bytes\\":10485760}}} and 400 for unsupported content-types with type unsupported_media_type. Observability: trace spans added around parse->validate->route dispatch to help pinpoint latency regressions. Related items: Linear ENG-2728 (multipart uploader stability), PM-146 (OpenAI compat feature parity).\\nLiam Chen: key question \xe2\x80\x94 do we need to special-case application/pdf? many partners send PDFs as application/pdf; current whitelist would block it. Suggest adding application/pdf or making whitelist configurable per-tenant.\\nAisha Patel: replied \xe2\x80\x94 agreed, added application/pdf to tenant_whitelist in config and made default conservative. Added test case + note in docs explaining why binary blobs should be limited.", "score": 0.83337, "rank": 0, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "3a4f508e-d505-5831-8317-29e5fbf8fbde", "search_unit_id": "3a4f508e-d505-5831-8317-29e5fbf8fbde", "block_from_id": "7b973113-64c9-54c6-82f0-a78cca2db581", "block_to_id": "7b973113-64c9-54c6-82f0-a78cca2db581", "section_path": "Pr 18421 Multipart File Validation Limits", "document_id": "196f5cda-0577-5c5b-88d5-a20d812333b4", "document_version_id": "b1a582e7-fa73-58af-bcea-6e975087fd50", "document_name": "github__dsid_ae068ee4aa9640159427cd941bef0238.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "p-2", "heading": "Pr 18421 Multipart File Validation Limits", "content": "Ravi Singh: please ensure the validator surfaces clear errors for multipart boundary parsing failures; I saw a flaky crash in an initial run.\\nAisha Patel: replied \xe2\x80\x94 parser now catches malformed boundary exceptions and returns a 400 with error.type=malformed_multipart and includes low-signal debug id for tracing; updated tests.\\nSofia Alvarez: approved \xe2\x80\x94 addressed my comments about metrics naming and added a suggestion to include counter tags for tenant_id and route_id.\\nCI Bot: integration-tests failed on first run due to test harness timeout; rerun completed successfully.\\nQA: noted an edge case where client SDK retries might double-submit large files; added a recommendation in docs and an optional idempotency header support in adapter.\\nAdded multipart/form-data support on OpenAI-compat API paths with strict content-type validation and configurable per-file and per-request size limits. Default limits: 10MiB per file, 50MiB per request. Feature is behind a feature flag and can be enabled per-tenant. See docs/openai-compat/multipart.md for migration steps.", "score": 0.730857, "rank": 1, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "ff70e9ec-d728-5976-9455-7f05e9430350", "search_unit_id": "ff70e9ec-d728-5976-9455-7f05e9430350", "block_from_id": "a25777a0-b31c-5f44-b73b-2962e9689f84", "block_to_id": "2d852f06-59de-5930-a2c8-bd757767ba3c", "section_path": "Pr 18421 Multipart File Validation Limits", "document_id": "196f5cda-0577-5c5b-88d5-a20d812333b4", "document_version_id": "b1a582e7-fa73-58af-bcea-6e975087fd50", "document_name": "github__dsid_ae068ee4aa9640159427cd941bef0238.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h1-0", "heading": "Pr 18421 Multipart File Validation Limits", "content": "Pr 18421 Multipart File Validation Limits\\n\\nSource type: github\\nDocument ID: dsid_ae068ee4aa9640159427cd941bef0238\\nRelease: v1.0.0\\nBenchmark: EnterpriseRAG-Bench synthetic upstream data\\nadd multipart/form-data handling, strict content-type validation, and payload limit enforcement for API tool/file inputs", "score": 0.44718, "rank": 2, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}], "events": [], "entities": [], "relatio