14:01:32  DEBUG    [b5117b8eeff649f2]  sse_starlette.sse  chunk: b'event: summary.delta\r\ndata: {"delta": "MedThink specified the following failover sequence and recovery targets for handling an EU region outage:\\n\\n- **Preferred failover hierarchy:** EU primary -> EU warm standby -> US emergency failover.\\n- **Cross-region failover to US:** Permitted only for declared emergency windows, with a maximum of 4 hours, and requires pre-approval in the runbook.\\n- **RPO (Recovery Point Objective):** 15 minutes for active datasets.\\n- **RTO (Recovery Time Objective):** 30 minutes for critical APIs.\\n\\nAdditionally, the following constraints apply:\\n\\n- **Logs & telemetry:** Logs may contain limited PII (hashed patient IDs and occasional email addresses). Redaction is expected at ingest, and hashed IDs are acceptable if the hash keys are kept on-region. Default operational logs are retained for 90 days, and audit logs for 3 years. Long-term archival to a secure archive is possible after 90 days, but must be on-region for PHI.\\n- **Backups:** Backups of PHI can be stored in the US if encrypted with customer-managed keys and access is restricted to named personnel only. Otherwise, they must stay in the EU. Cross-region incremental copies are allowed for analytics (non-PHI) or encrypted/full-access restricted backups with CMK.\\n- **Key management:** Prefer CMK (KMS) for PHI datasets. Monthly HSM audit extracts are required if HSM is used.\\n- **Audit evidence:** SOC 2 Type II report, access log exports (filtered to the MedThink account), key rotation logs, and one sample sanitized query/log bundle showing redaction are required.\\n\\nThe evidence is derived from [1] and [31]."}\r\n\r\n'
14:01:32  DEBUG    [b5117b8eeff649f2]  sse_starlette.sse  chunk: b'event: completed\r\ndata: {"query": "What failover sequence and recovery targets did MedThink specify for handling an EU region outage, including any limits on how long traffic can shift to the US?", "sections": [{"chunk_id": "f7a34025-fd17-527c-9568-3a2625b0f6a0", "search_unit_id": "f7a34025-fd17-527c-9568-3a2625b0f6a0", "block_from_id": "814bed88-9888-557d-819c-e901145c8363", "block_to_id": "0aeb5b03-c680-5a65-b64d-f9b033358da9", "section_path": "20280503 Region Fallback Priority Ops Inventory", "document_id": "4da40c19-70f8-5526-806a-febdeb4668cd", "document_version_id": "521fe3cb-72a4-5a06-9a90-f3cf0d2048aa", "document_name": "gmail__dsid_8e838ab6a98f4cbcb672d41f210ff89c.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "list-12", "heading": "20280503 Region Fallback Priority Ops Inventory", "content": "- Patient clinical records (PHI) must remain in-region (EU) for EU patients.\\n- Operational metadata (service-level telemetry that does not include patient-identifiers) can be replicated to US for analytics if pseudonymized and access controlled.\\n- Backups of PHI: acceptable to store in US if encrypted with customer-managed keys and access is restricted to named personnel only \xe2\x80\x94 otherwise must stay in EU.\\n\\n2) Failover order and cross-region replication:\\n\\n- Preferred failover hierarchy: EU primary -> EU warm standby -> US emergency failover.\\n- Cross-region failover to US is permitted only for declared emergency windows (max 4 hours), must be pre-approved in runbook.\\n- Target RPO 15 minutes for active datasets; RTO target 30 minutes for critical APIs.\\n\\n3) Logs & telemetry:\\n\\n- Logs do contain limited PII (hashed patient IDs and occasional email addresses).\\n- We expect redaction at ingest for any free-text fields that might include PHI; hashed IDs are acceptable if the hash keys are kept on-region.\\n- Retention: default operational logs 90 days; audit logs 3 years. Long-term archival to our secure archive is possible after 90 days (encrypted, on-region if PHI).\\n\\n4) Backups & snapshots:\\n\\n- Daily incremental snapshots; weekly full snapshots.\\n- Immutable weekly snapshots for 90 days for critical datasets. Cross-region incremental copies only for analytics (non-PHI) or encrypted/full-access restricted backups with CMK.\\n\\n5) Key management and attestations:\\n\\n- Prefer CMK (KMS) for PHI datasets. We will require proof of key rotation logs and monthly HSM audit extracts if HSM used.\\n\\n6) Audit evidence:\\n\\n- SOC 2 Type II report, access log exports (filtered to our account), key rotation logs, and one sample sanitized query/log bundle showing redaction.\\n\\nAttachments: PHI_handling_requirements.pdf (internal control summary).\\n\\nAvailability: Tom and I are available Tue/Wed next week 10:00\xe2\x80\x9312:00 ET for the technical deep-dive. If you can send an invite with a short agenda, we\xe2\x80\x99ll confirm.\\n\\nThanks,\\nElena\\nDirector of Security & Compliance\\nMedThink Health\\nelena.ruiz@medthink.health\\nFrom: Rafael Mendes <rafael.mendes@redwoodinference.com>\\nTo: Elena Ruiz <elena.ruiz@medthink.health>\\nCc: Monica Patel <monica.patel@redwoodinference.com>, Stephanie Nguyen <stephanie.nguyen@redwoodinference.com>\\nDate: Mon, 5 May 2028 09:10:00 -0700\\nSubject: Re: Regional fallback priorities & logs \xe2\x80\x94 post-call inventory\\n\\nGreat \xe2\x80\x94 that is very clear, thanks Elena. Quick confirmation of next steps from us and ownership:\\n\\n- Rafael: schedule the 60m tech deep-dive for Tue 10:30 ET (I\xe2\x80\x99ll send the invite now) \xe2\x80\x94 agenda: pinning topology, failover runbook, log redaction patterns, and CMK flow.\\n- Monica (Solutions): prepare two sanitized log samples (one operational, one audit) and a small runbook snippet showing redaction at ingest. Deliverable: shared Drive folder by Tue EOD.\\n- Stephanie (Infra): draft a cost delta for region-locked snapshots vs cross-region incremental backups and include estimated storage + egress costs (deliver Thu COB).\\n\\nElena \xe2\x80\x94 we\xe2\x80\x99ll include a short section in the MAM covering the emergency failover approvals you mentioned (max 4 hours cross-region window). Also we\xe2\x80\x99ll prepare a short template for the key rotation proof to match your monthly request.\\n\\nAttachments to be circulated after the meeting: example redaction config, sample sanitized logs, runbook snippet. We\xe2\x80\x99ll also attach SOC 2 Type II in the Drive folder (redacted where necessary).", "score": 0.654095, "rank": 0, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "2492981b-b2d9-5b18-ae30-ecc8af9d3a18", "search_unit_id": "2492981b-b2d9-5b18-ae30-ecc8af9d3a18", "block_from_id": "2017ef93-6d74-5202-9e6a-751770578531", "block_to_id": "0a422d4e-f17d-5077-9a27-980e547a2c74", "section_path": "Dedicated Throughput Slo Escalation > Triage checklist (Support/CS) > 7) Mitigation options you can offer immediately (tier-dependent)", "document_id": "2aced3e3-1ed9-50b2-9ef8-a037c40fcfaf", "document_version_id": "5b0b49bf-5c10-5f9e-b6f9-1ae199865977", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_409618a3958944f9b78362ed7e01bb33.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-65", "heading": "Dedicated Throughput Slo Escalation > Triage checklist (Support/CS) > 7) Mitigation options you can offer immediately (tier-dependent)", "content": "7) Mitigation options you can offer immediately (tier-dependent)\\n\\nThese are customer-facing actions CS/Support may propose, with SRE confirmation where possible:\\n\\n- Temporarily reduce max context / max output tokens (if within acceptable product behavior).\\n- Temporarily shift traffic to the contracted primary route only (avoid experimental routes).\\n- Enable/disable streaming based on their client constraints (note: streaming affects perceived latency but should not invalidate throughput).\\n- If the customer has multi-deployment setup: fail over to a secondary deployment (Premium: may be Redwood-assisted).\\n\\nDo not promise failover across regions unless the tier/contract explicitly includes it.", "score": 0.652819, "rank": 1, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "eed9fa3f-4200-5bfb-8ae2-7eeb70b03277", "search_unit_id": "eed9fa3f-4200-5bfb-8ae2-7eeb70b03277", "block_from_id": "70290ae3-2269-565d-9ba7-051707666a4e", "block_to_id": "7d3b1e7b-4c85-53b7-b8c8-60dde669744a", "section_path": "Dedicated Throughput Slo Escalation > Common failure modes and quick routing hints", "document_id": "2aced3e3-1ed9-50b2-9ef8-a037c40fcfaf", "document_version_id": "5b0b49bf-5c10-5f9e-b6f9-1ae199865977", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_409618a3958944f9b78362ed7e01bb33.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-136", "heading": "Dedicated Throughput Slo Escalation > Common failure modes and quick routing hints", "content": "Common failure modes and quick routing hints\\n\\n- **Customer sees lower throughput than Redwood reports:** often a measurement mismatch (streaming token accounting, end-to-end latency vs throughput, counting input tokens). Engage Observability if persistent.\\n- **Throughput drops with GPU pegged:** suspect contention, node health, thermal throttling, network bottleneck; page Infra.\\n- **Throughput drops with low utilization:** suspect admission control limiting, customer throttling, or workload shift to longer contexts; page SRE; ask customer for concurrency/workload details.\\n- **Regional capacity constraint / failover behavior:** check tier failover posture; page Infra and SRE; do not promise cross-region without tier/contract confirmation.\\n\\n---", "score": 0.591636, "rank": 2, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "fcb786fb-2588-51a8-b994-9ca513b13b48", "search_unit_id": "fcb786fb-2588-51a8-b994-9ca513b13b48", "block_from_id": "b3e888d7-6cf3-58ed-93cc-e94a90932718", "block_to_id": "7cf69024-898f-5843-bf46-a37aa785485b", "section_path": "Dedicated Throughput Slo Escalation", "document_id": "2aced3e3-1ed9-50b2-9ef8-a037c40fcfaf", "document_version_id": "5b0b49bf-5c10-5f9e-b6f9-1ae199865977", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_409618a3958944f9b78362ed7e01bb33.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h1-0", "heading": "Dedicated Throughput Slo Escalation", "content": "Dedicated Throughput Slo Escalation\\n\\nSource type: confluence\\nDocument ID: dsid_409618a3958944f9b78362ed7e01bb33\\nRelease: v1.0.0\\nBenchmark: EnterpriseRAG-Bench synthetic upstream data\\nDedicated Throughput SLO Escalation Playbook", "score": 0.574481, "rank": 3, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "e2a1ef86-f272-548f-81c5-265d56a7e1d3", "search_unit_id": "e2a1ef86-f272-548f-81c5-265d56a7e1d3", "block_from_id": "6f134484-bb33-5444-bbd6-664babff7561", "block_to_id": "6a9abe59-2cc6-5852-b804-0b4ec3bbdd6c", "section_path": "Dedicated Throughput Slo Escalation > What is the Dedicated Throughput SLO (customer-facing summary)", "document_id": "2aced3e3-1ed9-50b2-9ef8-a037c40fcfaf", "document_version_id": "5b0b49bf-5c10-5f9e-b6f9-1ae199865977", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_409618a3958944f9b78362ed7e01bb33.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-7", "heading": "Dedicated Throughput Slo Escalation > What is the Dedicated Throughput SLO (customer-facing summary)", "content": "What is the Dedicated Throughput SLO (customer-facing summary)\\n\\nDedicated Throughput SLO guarantees a **minimum sustained throughput floor** for an eligible Dedicated deployment under defined conditions.\\n\\n**High-level definition (internal summary):**\\n\\n- Metric: throughput measured as **billable output tokens per second**, computed per deployment, aggregated over a rolling window.\\n- Scope: Dedicated deployments only (not Hosted API, not eval/sandbox deployments).\\n- Eligibility: model/version and configuration must be within the customer\xe2\x80\x99s contracted Dedicated configuration (e.g., pinned model family/version, supported max context, supported shape).\\n\\n**Common non-eligibility / exclusions (not exhaustive):**\\n\\n- Customer-side throttling or client concurrency limits causing underutilization.\\n- Customer workload violating sizing assumptions (e.g., contexts above configured limit, unsupported parameter combinations).\\n- Warm-up periods after scale-from-zero or cold start (tier-dependent; see \xe2\x80\x9cWarm pool / startup\xe2\x80\x9d below).\\n- Incidents due to customer networking/VPC misconfig in Private connectivity paths (if applicable).\\n\\nWhen in doubt, treat as potentially eligible, start the triage, and engage SRE.\\n\\n---", "score": 0.535312, "rank": 4, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "f46c4ba8-acff-59bb-8c27-9220cdeddcb0", "search_unit_id": "f46c4ba8-acff-59bb-8c27-9220cdeddcb0", "block_from_id": "3369b0e3-ccd4-536d-ad1f-a8f23c9764ac", "block_to_id": "3c097507-1408-5e77-886c-dbbc236d4a30", "section_path": "Dedicated Throughput Slo Escalation > Templates (copy/paste) > Template A \xe2\x80\x94 Initial acknowledgement (suspected throughput miss)", "document_id": "2aced3e3-1ed9-50b2-9ef8-a037c40fcfaf", "document_version_id": "5b0b49bf-5c10-5f9e-b6f9-1ae199865977", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_409618a3958944f9b78362ed7e01bb33.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-83", "heading": "Dedicated Throughput Slo Escalation > Templates (copy/paste) > Template A \xe2\x80\x94 Initial acknowledgement (suspected throughput miss)", "content": "Templates (copy/paste)\\n\\nTemplate A \xe2\x80\x94 Initial acknowledgement (suspected throughput miss)\\n\\nSubject: Dedicated deployment throughput investigation (Deployment {{deployment_id}})\\n\\nHi {{customer_name}},\\n\\nThanks for flagging this. We\xe2\x80\x99re investigating reduced throughput on your Dedicated deployment ({{deployment_id}}) in {{region}}.\\n\\nTo help us confirm impact and correlate logs/metrics, could you share:\\n\\n- The approximate start time and whether the issue is ongoing\\n- The model + version you\xe2\x80\x99re using\\n- A representative request ID (or a small set) from the impacted window\\n- Any recent traffic/concurrency changes on your side\\n\\nWe\xe2\x80\x99ll provide the next update by {{time}}.\\nBest,\\n{{agent_name}}", "score": 0.518522, "rank": 5, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "7ad7fa3e-f65e-5590-97d1-e985de4793f2", "search_unit_id": "7ad7fa3e-f65e-5590-97d1-e985de4793f2", "block_from_id": "f4038f70-1166-598a-ac1b-857ef2bae219", "block_to_id": "a2318620-fd88-5b5d-a51e-a6efe75caa19", "section_path": "Dedicated Throughput Slo Escalation > Roles and ownership during an SLO event", "document_id": "2aced3e3-1ed9-50b2-9ef8-a037c40fcfaf", "document_version_id": "5b0b49bf-5c10-5f9e-b6f9-1ae199865977", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_409618a3958944f9b78362ed7e01bb33.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-15", "heading": "Dedicated Throughput Slo Escalation > Roles and ownership during an SLO event", "content": "Roles and ownership during an SLO event\\n\\n**Support/CS (Incident Driver for customer comms)**\\n\\n- Owns the customer thread, updates, and expectation management.\\n- Owns the case record: timeline, impact, and customer confirmations.\\n- Initiates escalation and ensures correct teams are engaged.\\n\\n**SRE On-Call (Technical Incident Lead)**\\n\\n- Confirms whether the SLO is breached per the canonical evaluator.\\n- Drives mitigation and coordinates cross-functional response.\\n- Provides internal/external technical summary for comms.\\n\\n**Infra/Fleet On-Call (Capacity / shape / provisioning owner)**\\n\\n- Addresses capacity constraints, noisy-neighbor isolation issues, node failures, and shape-level performance anomalies.\\n\\n**Observability (as-needed)**\\n\\n- Validates metric correctness (e.g., streaming accounting anomalies), dashboard discrepancies, missing tags.\\n\\n**Product Dedicated (as-needed)**\\n\\n- Confirms entitlement interpretation (tier rules, burst policy, failover posture).\\n- Aligns on customer-facing messaging for edge cases.\\n\\n**Finance/FP&A + Legal (as-needed for credits/comp)**\\n\\n- Approves service credits above policy thresholds and any non-standard compensation.\\n\\n---", "score": 0.515727, "rank": 6, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "2e615fe1-08e1-5708-8bc2-6ac939ff2358", "search_unit_id": "2e615fe1-08e1-5708-8bc2-6ac939ff2358", "block_from_id": "cdf4547a-f291-5150-8a52-5e428cf23ee2", "block_to_id": "4666e94d-af90-5fd1-ae22-f3a1eb902904", "section_path": "Dedicated Throughput Slo Escalation > Severity levels (Support/CS view)", "document_id": "2aced3e3-1ed9-50b2-9ef8-a037c40fcfaf", "document_version_id": "5b0b49bf-5c10-5f9e-b6f9-1ae199865977", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_409618a3958944f9b78362ed7e01bb33.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-29", "heading": "Dedicated Throughput Slo Escalation > Severity levels (Support/CS view)", "content": "Severity levels (Support/CS view)\\n\\nUse these severities to standardize response; SRE may map to their incident severities.\\n\\n**SEV-1 (Critical, likely customer-impacting breach)**\\n\\n- Premium tier customer reports sustained throughput below floor OR SRE burn-rate alert is firing.\\n- Clear production impact (e.g., queue buildup, timeouts, user-visible latency spikes).\\n- Immediate paging required.\\n\\n**SEV-2 (High, likely degradation / at-risk of breach)**\\n\\n- Throughput is below expected but not yet confirmed as an SLO breach.\\n- Customer impact is moderate OR limited to a subset of traffic/routes.\\n- Paging may be required depending on tier and duration.\\n\\n**SEV-3 (Moderate, investigation / metrics discrepancy)**\\n\\n- Conflicting metrics (customer vs Redwood dashboards), short-lived dips, or suspected measurement artifacts.\\n- No clear production impact.\\n\\n---", "score": 0.496142, "rank": 7, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "ab995a63-5481-543d-941b-b8217d91b0eb", "search_unit_id": "ab995a63-5481-543d-941b-b8217d91b0eb", "block_from_id": "5bcac27e-19f6-5e67-9884-2b63ba8c4de6", "block_to_id": "4034474c-3965-544e-a134-3d9a75721b60", "section_path": "Dedicated Throughput Slo Escalation > Service credits / compensation (internal guidance) > Which tiers are typically credit-eligible?", "document_id": "2aced3e3-1ed9-50b2-9ef8-a037c40fcfaf", "document_version_id": "5b0b49bf-5c10-5f9e-b6f9-1ae199865977", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_409618a3958944f9b78362ed7e01bb33.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-122", "heading": "Dedicated Throughput Slo Escalation > Service credits / compensation (internal guidance) > Which tiers are typically credit-eligible?", "content": "Which tiers are typically credit-eligible?\\n\\n- **Premium:** written throughput commitment; credit review is standard for confirmed breaches.\\n- **Plus:** may be eligible depending on contract addenda; treat as \xe2\x80\x9creview required.\xe2\x80\x9d\\n- **Standard:** generally best-effort; credit requests require Product + Finance approval.", "score": 0.496142, "rank": 8, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "0202afcb-6bdb-5d77-bd7f-c8dabc6c1475", "search_unit_id": "0202afcb-6bdb-5d77-bd7f-c8dabc6c1475", "block_from_id": "3bf8a4c3-05b0-5866-944e-52f37b3fbb2c", "block_to_id": "62fdd968-9c43-5d3f-a2e6-7b3db87d94e6", "section_path": "Dedicated Throughput Slo Escalation > Customer communications guide > Communication principles", "document_id": "2aced3e3-1ed9-50b2-9ef8-a037c40fcfaf", "document_version_id": "5b0b49bf-5c10-5f9e-b6f9-1ae199865977", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_409618a3958944f9b78362ed7e01bb33.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-77", "heading": "Dedicated Throughput Slo Escalation > Customer communications guide > Communication principles", "content": "Customer communications guide\\n\\nCommunication principles\\n\\n- Use a single owner for customer updates (CS/Support), even if multiple engineering teams are engaged.\\n- Acknowledge impact quickly; avoid speculating on root cause.\\n- Provide time-bound next update (\xe2\x80\x9cnext update in 30 minutes\xe2\x80\x9d).\\n- For Premium accounts, default to more frequent updates and written summaries.", "score": 0.496142, "rank": 9, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "5900c2b6-db81-566e-93d3-4df758f2b8c3", "search_unit_id": "5900c2b6-db81-566e-93d3-4df758f2b8c3", "block_from_id": "1b0ef4bf-1c4c-5bd9-995c-e8abcb70d76e", "block_to_id": "5feaba5e-2a0b-5679-89f3-6b3d99e35326", "section_path": "Dedicated Throughput Slo Escalation > Warm pool / startup considerations", "document_id": "2aced3e3-1ed9-50b2-9ef8-a037c40fcfaf", "document_version_id": "5b0b49bf-5c10-5f9e-b6f9-1ae199865977", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_409618a3958944f9b78362ed7e01bb33.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-72", "heading": "Dedicated Throughput Slo Escalation > Warm pool / startup considerations", "content": "Warm pool / startup considerations\\n\\nSome tiers include warm pool guarantees (or faster recovery expectations). During triage, identify if the customer is within a warm-up window:\\n\\n- Did the deployment recently scale from zero?\\n- Was there a recent model reload, config change, or node replacement?\\n- Did traffic resume after prolonged inactivity?\\n\\nIf warm-up is suspected, note it explicitly in the customer thread and ask SRE to confirm whether the event is excluded by policy.\\n\\n---", "score": 0.496142, "rank": 10, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "b3c9c225-4cab-5ab1-a9e8-3ff8f900b32d", "search_unit_id": "b3c9c225-4cab-5ab1-a9e8-3ff8f900b32d", "block_from_id": "1ec6e868-a441-563f-a028-b62b45b187b5", "block_to_id": "07630a41-8095-5673-a96a-a33655fc7fff", "section_path": "Dedicated Throughput Slo Escalation > Triage checklist (Support/CS) > 4) Check the Dedicated Throughput dashboard for that deployment", "document_id": "2aced3e3-1ed9-50b2-9ef8-a037c40fcfaf", "document_version_id": "5b0b49bf-5c10-5f9e-b6f9-1ae199865977", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_409618a3958944f9b78362ed7e01bb33.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-57", "heading": "Dedicated Throughput Slo Escalation > Triage checklist (Support/CS) > 4) Check the Dedicated Throughput dashboard for that deployment", "content": "4) Check the Dedicated Throughput dashboard for that deployment\\n\\nLook for:\\n\\n- Rolling-window throughput vs committed floor\\n- Error rate/timeout correlation\\n- GPU saturation, queue depth, admission control shedding\\n- Recent routing pool changes or failovers", "score": 0.496142, "rank": 11, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "713f004d-833a-5c85-9c73-13bd31e75550", "search_unit_id": "713f004d-833a-5c85-9c73-13bd31e75550", "block_from_id": "ee21b1a9-374f-5027-8401-8b49829d0fdd", "block_to_id": "5d7c3e61-8c9d-5be5-b7d1-cc8660103639", "section_path": "Dedicated Throughput Slo Escalation > Evidence and logging requirements", "document_id": "2aced3e3-1ed9-50b2-9ef8-a037c40fcfaf", "document_version_id": "5b0b49bf-5c10-5f9e-b6f9-1ae199865977", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_409618a3958944f9b78362ed7e01bb33.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-132", "heading": "Dedicated Throughput Slo Escalation > Evidence and logging requirements", "content": "Evidence and logging requirements\\n\\nFor any SEV-1/SEV-2 and any credit review, capture:\\n\\n- Customer ticket link\\n- Incident link (if created)\\n- Dashboard links (throughput vs floor, saturation, errors)\\n- Request IDs / traces used for debugging\\n- Summary of customer-side traffic confirmation\\n- Timeline of mitigations and when throughput stabilized\\n\\n---", "score": 0.496142, "rank": 12, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "77aeddcb-cd7b-5e17-b86a-007450d674de", "search_unit_id": "77aeddcb-cd7b-5e17-b86a-007450d674de", "block_from_id": "f7839eb8-e349-5145-a947-acb587ffe9d9", "block_to_id": "0286a2cd-6a4e-5c5b-8db3-2aa376a12271", "section_path": "Dedicated Throughput Slo Escalation > Paging and escalation triggers (when to page SRE / Infra) > Page SRE On-Call immediately when any of the following is true", "document_id": "2aced3e3-1ed9-50b2-9ef8-a037c40fcfaf", "document_version_id": "5b0b49bf-5c10-5f9e-b6f9-1ae199865977", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_409618a3958944f9b78362ed7e01bb33.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-38", "heading": "Dedicated Throughput Slo Escalation > Paging and escalation triggers (when to page SRE / Infra) > Page SRE On-Call immediately when any of the following is true", "content": "Paging and escalation triggers (when to page SRE / Infra)\\n\\nPage SRE On-Call immediately when any of the following is true\\n\\n- Premium tier customer: reported throughput below committed floor for **>10 minutes**, AND they confirm they are not client-throttled.\\n- Any tier: a Dedicated Throughput SLO **burn-rate alert** is firing for the deployment.\\n- Any tier: repeated or escalating customer timeouts/5xx correlated with throughput drop.\\n- Any tier: throughput drop correlates with recent Redwood changes (rollout, routing, driver/runtime update).", "score": 0.496142, "rank": 13, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "20b4990d-22f4-5fcd-94df-733275f1c3bf", "search_unit_id": "20b4990d-22f4-5fcd-94df-733275f1c3bf", "block_from_id": "285f9994-d52a-563f-9580-d1d37f8bef4b", "block_to_id": "891701ab-082c-53f6-bd72-d69ea571477b", "section_path": "Dedicated Throughput Slo Escalation > Purpose", "document_id": "2aced3e3-1ed9-50b2-9ef8-a037c40fcfaf", "document_version_id": "5b0b49bf-5c10-5f9e-b6f9-1ae199865977", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_409618a3958944f9b78362ed7e01bb33.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-2", "heading": "Dedicated Throughput Slo Escalation > Purpose", "content": "Purpose\\n\\nThis playbook defines the end-to-end process for handling Dedicated **Throughput SLO** misses or suspected misses. It is designed for Customer Success (CS) and Support to:\\n\\n- Triage quickly and consistently.\\n- Engage the correct on-call teams (SRE / Infra / Observability) at the right time.\\n- Communicate clearly with customers, including status updates and written summaries.\\n- Route service-credit / compensation requests through the correct approval path.\\n\\nThis page is **restricted** because it includes internal paging triggers and credit approval guidance.\\n\\n---", "score": 0.49237, "rank": 14, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "229f3d9b-dc1a-5f98-9791-77f5fd170c0f", "search_unit_id": "229f3d9b-dc1a-5f98-9791-77f5fd170c0f", "block_from_id": "42771e82-7f8e-5b80-a2fa-ec3e46d2a0a7", "block_to_id": "dcf2be91-cf0c-59e4-82d0-178247a17745", "section_path": "Dedicated Throughput Slo Escalation > Triage checklist (Support/CS) > 5) Check if this is a metrics discrepancy", "document_id": "2aced3e3-1ed9-50b2-9ef8-a037c40fcfaf", "document_version_id": "5b0b49bf-5c10-5f9e-b6f9-1ae199865977", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_409618a3958944f9b78362ed7e01bb33.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-60", "heading": "Dedicated Throughput Slo Escalation > Triage checklist (Support/CS) > 5) Check if this is a metrics discrepancy", "content": "5) Check if this is a metrics discrepancy\\n\\nIf customer numbers differ from Redwood:\\n\\n- Ask what they are measuring (wall-clock end-to-end, tokens counted, streaming vs non-streaming).\\n- Request a single representative request ID and a 10\xe2\x80\x9320 minute sample window.", "score": 0.496142, "rank": 15, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "e4fb0db7-0d72-513c-864b-54ea9c98779a", "search_unit_id": "e4fb0db7-0d72-513c-864b-54ea9c98779a", "block_from_id": "aa4fd05e-834d-5c0d-94cf-fbfffbf445a6", "block_to_id": "d6208276-c1f2-59e6-8701-5418155a267e", "section_path": "Dedicated Throughput Slo Escalation > Triage checklist (Support/CS) > 2) Confirm the customer is driving enough load", "document_id": "2aced3e3-1ed9-50b2-9ef8-a037c40fcfaf", "document_version_id": "5b0b49bf-5c10-5f9e-b6f9-1ae199865977", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_409618a3958944f9b78362ed7e01bb33.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-51", "heading": "Dedicated Throughput Slo Escalation > Triage checklist (Support/CS) > 2) Confirm the customer is driving enough load", "content": "2) Confirm the customer is driving enough load\\n\\nAsk:\\n\\n- Current request concurrency\\n- Any client-side rate limiting (explicit QPS cap, worker pool limit)\\n- Any recent application deploy or traffic change\\n\\nIf the customer is under-driving load, throughput may be low without being an SLO failure.", "score": 0.496142, "rank": 16, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "e4972e4e-0a7d-52cf-a4cd-97ce1d1ea9d1", "search_unit_id": "e4972e4e-0a7d-52cf-a4cd-97ce1d1ea9d1", "block_from_id": "21f0be6b-f2a6-502e-abc0-d896c249d61d", "block_to_id": "df76eb78-b9e4-5188-a4cb-14b6cd89a405", "section_path": "Dedicated Throughput Slo Escalation > Paging and escalation triggers (when to page SRE / Infra) > Engage Observability (not a page; async unless SEV-1)", "document_id": "2aced3e3-1ed9-50b2-9ef8-a037c40fcfaf", "document_version_id": "5b0b49bf-5c10-5f9e-b6f9-1ae199865977", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_409618a3958944f9b78362ed7e01bb33.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-43", "heading": "Dedicated Throughput Slo Escalation > Paging and escalation triggers (when to page SRE / Infra) > Engage Observability (not a page; async unless SEV-1)", "content": "Engage Observability (not a page; async unless SEV-1)\\n\\n- Throughput dashboards disagree with billing/export numbers.\\n- Recent metric changes (e.g., streaming token accounting) suspected.\\n- Missing labels (deployment_id, model, region) prevents accurate attribution.\\n\\n---", "score": 0.496142, "rank": 17, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "0a1c5ddf-431d-5c70-94c5-e126dbae4f9c", "search_unit_id": "0a1c5ddf-431d-5c70-94c5-e126dbae4f9c", "block_from_id": "c5cf7e25-1588-51e2-996d-215d2679aa0c", "block_to_id": "b54ea0b4-06a5-58bb-8b14-8fcdcdef5576", "section_path": "Dedicated Throughput Slo Escalation > Triage checklist (Support/CS) > 1) Confirm customer context (capture in ticket)", "document_id": "2aced3e3-1ed9-50b2-9ef8-a037c40fcfaf", "document_version_id": "5b0b49bf-5c10-5f9e-b6f9-1ae199865977", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_409618a3958944f9b78362ed7e01bb33.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-48", "heading": "Dedicated Throughput Slo Escalation > Triage checklist (Support/CS) > 1) Confirm customer context (capture in ticket)", "content": "1) Confirm customer context (capture in ticket)\\n\\nCollect:\\n\\n- Deployment ID(s)\\n- Customer name + environment (prod/stage)\\n- Region\\n- Tier (Standard / Plus / Premium)\\n- Model + version (exact identifier)\\n- Shape (if known)\\n- Time window of impact (with timezone)\\n- Symptoms (queueing, latency, timeouts, functional failure)", "score": 0.496142, "rank": 18, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "a67f2750-1c21-5cac-85f6-d5afda9c7c84", "search_unit_id": "a67f2750-1c21-5cac-85f6-d5afda9c7c84", "block_from_id": "ee9e8133-b22c-5163-b735-ea75cbe2872d", "block_to_id": "92ca28d9-af56-5b6a-a13b-1b8ed6df3836", "section_path": "Dedicated Throughput Slo Escalation > Templates (copy/paste) > Template D \xe2\x80\x94 Resolution note + next steps", "document_id": "2aced3e3-1ed9-50b2-9ef8-a037c40fcfaf", "document_version_id": "5b0b49bf-5c10-5f9e-b6f9-1ae199865977", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_409618a3958944f9b78362ed7e01bb33.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-105", "heading": "Dedicated Throughput Slo Escalation > Templates (copy/paste) > Template D \xe2\x80\x94 Resolution note + next steps", "content": "Template D \xe2\x80\x94 Resolution note + next steps\\n\\nSubject: Resolved: Dedicated throughput issue (Deployment {{deployment_id}})\\n\\nHi {{customer_name}},\\n\\nThe throughput issue affecting your Dedicated deployment ({{deployment_id}}) is now resolved as of {{resolved_time_utc}}.\\n\\nSummary:\\n\\n- Root cause (preliminary): {{rca_summary}}\\n- What we changed: {{mitigation_actions}}\\n- Verification: throughput has been stable above the committed floor over the last {{window}}.\\n\\nWe\xe2\x80\x99ll follow up with a written incident summary and, if applicable under your Dedicated tier terms, guidance on service credits.\\n\\nBest,\\n{{agent_name}}", "score": 0.496142, "rank": 19, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "17efd8df-585c-5be4-b754-74e57e59e1d9", "search_unit_id": "17efd8df-585c-5be4-b754-74e57e59e1d9", "block_from_id": "9a75f4cf-e2f0-558c-b8ee-cae9834ee25e", "block_to_id": "7d722517-1aef-5ca5-a2dd-492059575a69", "section_path": "Dedicated Throughput Slo Escalation > Customer communications guide > Target update cadence (recommended)", "document_id": "2aced3e3-1ed9-50b2-9ef8-a037c40fcfaf", "document_version_id": "5b0b49bf-5c10-5f9e-b6f9-1ae199865977", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_409618a3958944f9b78362ed7e01bb33.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-80", "heading": "Dedicated Throughput Slo Escalation > Customer communications guide > Target update cadence (recommended)", "content": "Target update cadence (recommended)\\n\\n- SEV-1: initial response within 15 minutes; updates every 30 minutes until stable.\\n- SEV-2: initial response within 1 hour; updates every 2\xe2\x80\x934 hours until stable.\\n- SEV-3: initial response within 1 business day; updates daily or as material changes occur.\\n\\n---", "score": 0.496142, "rank": 20, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "fdafff65-101b-5de4-a9c1-c8784303b5c6", "search_unit_id": "fdafff65-101b-5de4-a9c1-c8784303b5c6", "block_from_id": "748d8c4f-d14f-5182-abbe-6834088b1456", "block_to_id": "2e5b51ba-3dd3-5472-89b8-1d4241bbca70", "section_path": "Dedicated Throughput Slo Escalation > Triage checklist (Support/CS) > 8) Open an incident record (internal) if SEV-1/SEV-2", "document_id": "2aced3e3-1ed9-50b2-9ef8-a037c40fcfaf", "document_version_id": "5b0b49bf-5c10-5f9e-b6f9-1ae199865977", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_409618a3958944f9b78362ed7e01bb33.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-69", "heading": "Dedicated Throughput Slo Escalation > Triage checklist (Support/CS) > 8) Open an incident record (internal) if SEV-1/SEV-2", "content": "8) Open an incident record (internal) if SEV-1/SEV-2\\n\\n- Create/associate the internal incident ticket.\\n- Add the customer support ticket link.\\n- Add a running timeline (timestamps for all key events).\\n\\n---", "score": 0.496142, "rank": 21, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "063fe319-15ac-5f21-bd67-1c6806816af4", "search_unit_id": "063fe319-15ac-5f21-bd67-1c6806816af4", "block_from_id": "bbaff1a0-9b78-5ea8-ad31-62854cca212c", "block_to_id": "5fc4951d-47cc-5122-ba0d-90d63e0573e5", "section_path": "Dedicated Throughput Slo Escalation > Triage checklist (Support/CS) > 3) Validate \xe2\x80\x9celigibility\xe2\x80\x9d red flags quickly", "document_id": "2aced3e3-1ed9-50b2-9ef8-a037c40fcfaf", "document_version_id": "5b0b49bf-5c10-5f9e-b6f9-1ae199865977", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_409618a3958944f9b78362ed7e01bb33.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-55", "heading": "Dedicated Throughput Slo Escalation > Triage checklist (Support/CS) > 3) Validate \xe2\x80\x9celigibility\xe2\x80\x9d red flags quickly", "content": "3) Validate \xe2\x80\x9celigibility\xe2\x80\x9d red flags quickly\\n\\n- Context lengths: are they within contracted max context / recommended ranges?\\n- Parameters: extreme max_tokens or non-streaming vs streaming changes?\\n- Model/version pin: did they change models recently?", "score": 0.496142, "rank": 22, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "c157cc82-b0b4-53da-97f6-de4b015a55fe", "search_unit_id": "c157cc82-b0b4-53da-97f6-de4b015a55fe", "block_from_id": "2732ea13-3e38-5f3c-8a49-89d54e521385", "block_to_id": "696339b6-da9b-5381-ad38-dad28e1eed1f", "section_path": "Dedicated Throughput Slo Escalation > Service credits / compensation (internal guidance) > What to include in the internal credit request", "document_id": "2aced3e3-1ed9-50b2-9ef8-a037c40fcfaf", "document_version_id": "5b0b49bf-5c10-5f9e-b6f9-1ae199865977", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_409618a3958944f9b78362ed7e01bb33.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-129", "heading": "Dedicated Throughput Slo Escalation > Service credits / compensation (internal guidance) > What to include in the internal credit request", "content": "What to include in the internal credit request\\n\\n- Customer + contract/tier\\n- Deployment ID(s)\\n- Breach window (start/end in UTC)\\n- Evidence links: dashboard screenshots/links, evaluator output\\n- Customer impact summary (what broke, business impact if shared)\\n- Exclusion checks performed (throttling, workload constraints, warm-up)\\n- Proposed remedy type (service credit vs other)\\n\\n---", "score": 0.496142, "rank": 23, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "b0be62d9-e6d8-5c78-8a99-278d236cb266", "search_unit_id": "b0be62d9-e6d8-5c78-8a99-278d236cb266", "block_from_id": "daf03560-bf88-56b6-a3bc-9b3c43bbd3df", "block_to_id": "8f1c4c1c-92d1-52f5-8d51-46665171b85d", "section_path": "Dedicated Throughput Slo Escalation > Templates (copy/paste) > Template C \xe2\x80\x94 Request customer confirmation on throttling / load", "document_id": "2aced3e3-1ed9-50b2-9ef8-a037c40fcfaf", "document_version_id": "5b0b49bf-5c10-5f9e-b6f9-1ae199865977", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_409618a3958944f9b78362ed7e01bb33.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-98", "heading": "Dedicated Throughput Slo Escalation > Templates (copy/paste) > Template C \xe2\x80\x94 Request customer confirmation on throttling / load", "content": "Template C \xe2\x80\x94 Request customer confirmation on throttling / load\\n\\nSubject: Quick check: request load/concurrency for Dedicated deployment {{deployment_id}}\\n\\nHi {{customer_name}},\\n\\nTo confirm whether the deployment is being fully utilized during the impacted window, can you confirm:\\n\\n- Current concurrency / worker count hitting the deployment\\n- Whether you have any client-side QPS limits or retries/backoff changes\\n- Whether the workload mix changed (context length, max output tokens, streaming on/off)\\n\\nThis helps us differentiate capacity/perf issues from under-driven traffic.\\n\\nThanks,\\n{{agent_name}}", "score": 0.496142, "rank": 24, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "28b86ac8-5dfb-5fc0-9cd5-ebdbfd1f1371", "search_unit_id": "28b86ac8-5dfb-5fc0-9cd5-ebdbfd1f1371", "block_from_id": "d27d4dda-2ee7-5a4d-b690-309c54c3dfea", "block_to_id": "1fea54c4-ad92-5ad3-b7c2-757f6412bb24", "section_path": "Dedicated Throughput Slo Escalation > Service credits / compensation (internal guidance) > Approval path (default)", "document_id": "2aced3e3-1ed9-50b2-9ef8-a037c40fcfaf", "document_version_id": "5b0b49bf-5c10-5f9e-b6f9-1ae199865977", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_409618a3958944f9b78362ed7e01bb33.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-127", "heading": "Dedicated Throughput Slo Escalation > Service credits / compensation (internal guidance) > Approval path (default)", "content": "Approval path (default)\\n\\n1) CS/Support compiles incident details and SRE confirmation.\\n2) SRE provides breach window + summary.\\n3) Product Dedicated confirms entitlement interpretation (tier/exclusions).\\n4) Finance (Laura Bennett / delegate) validates policy compliance and amount.\\n5) Legal (Sofia Mendes / delegate) reviews if there is contract ambiguity or if a non-standard remedy is proposed.\\n6) CS communicates outcome to customer.", "score": 0.496142, "rank": 25, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "1129a799-0cee-50df-998c-86588e9efe9c", "search_unit_id": "1129a799-0cee-50df-998c-86588e9efe9c", "block_from_id": "9ef7aa4e-0f30-5823-92d5-46e3f4640fdb", "block_to_id": "d84fc0ff-65fe-5ca5-8288-b2a66e07aa23", "section_path": "Dedicated Throughput Slo Escalation > Paging and escalation triggers (when to page SRE / Infra) > Page Infra/Fleet On-Call when any of the following is true (often in parallel)", "document_id": "2aced3e3-1ed9-50b2-9ef8-a037c40fcfaf", "document_version_id": "5b0b49bf-5c10-5f9e-b6f9-1ae199865977", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_409618a3958944f9b78362ed7e01bb33.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-41", "heading": "Dedicated Throughput Slo Escalation > Paging and escalation triggers (when to page SRE / Infra) > Page Infra/Fleet On-Call when any of the following is true (often in parallel)", "content": "Page Infra/Fleet On-Call when any of the following is true (often in parallel)\\n\\n- GPU/node health signals indicate failures, evictions, ECC errors, or repeated container restarts.\\n- Saturation: GPU utilization pinned while throughput drops (suspected contention, thermal throttling, network bottleneck).\\n- Capacity: the deployment appears mapped to the wrong pool/shape or lacks the expected headroom.\\n- Region-wide capacity constraint impacting Dedicated pools.", "score": 0.496142, "rank": 26, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "77be56ef-69e4-5002-b3f9-6a0bce3a933f", "search_unit_id": "77be56ef-69e4-5002-b3f9-6a0bce3a933f", "block_from_id": "faeb6b96-3b54-5e15-bdec-a761b0a33a45", "block_to_id": "3a662ad0-f25a-5ae4-a71a-9f12b08a0dbc", "section_path": "Dedicated Throughput Slo Escalation > Templates (copy/paste) > Template E \xe2\x80\x94 Service credit intake (do not pre-approve)", "document_id": "2aced3e3-1ed9-50b2-9ef8-a037c40fcfaf", "document_version_id": "5b0b49bf-5c10-5f9e-b6f9-1ae199865977", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_409618a3958944f9b78362ed7e01bb33.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-113", "heading": "Dedicated Throughput Slo Escalation > Templates (copy/paste) > Template E \xe2\x80\x94 Service credit intake (do not pre-approve)", "content": "Template E \xe2\x80\x94 Service credit intake (do not pre-approve)\\n\\nSubject: Dedicated throughput incident \xe2\x80\x94 service credit review\\n\\nHi {{customer_name}},\\n\\nWe can review this incident for service credits under your Dedicated terms. To proceed, we will document:\\n\\n- Deployment ID(s)\\n- Impact window (UTC)\\n- Confirmed SLO measurement from Redwood\xe2\x80\x99s evaluator\\n\\nWe\xe2\x80\x99ll share the outcome of the credit review by {{date}}.\\n\\nBest,\\n{{agent_name}}\\n---", "score": 0.496142, "rank": 27, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "a7ab9be8-f11a-57a2-a2b0-23d7e9ce8e62", "search_unit_id": "a7ab9be8-f11a-57a2-a2b0-23d7e9ce8e62", "block_from_id": "5bbceef9-cfff-56d1-8f35-35695e980b56", "block_to_id": "b9b9fc6c-d3c6-5f92-a8e8-9a100d3ba9fa", "section_path": "Dedicated Throughput Slo Escalation > Triage checklist (Support/CS) > 6) Determine if the issue is isolated or systemic", "document_id": "2aced3e3-1ed9-50b2-9ef8-a037c40fcfaf", "document_version_id": "5b0b49bf-5c10-5f9e-b6f9-1ae199865977", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_409618a3958944f9b78362ed7e01bb33.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-63", "heading": "Dedicated Throughput Slo Escalation > Triage checklist (Support/CS) > 6) Determine if the issue is isolated or systemic", "content": "6) Determine if the issue is isolated or systemic\\n\\n- One deployment vs multiple\\n- One region vs multiple\\n- One model family vs multiple", "score": 0.496142, "rank": 28, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "f27ed60f-5d0f-52d8-a7ed-8c1959f31d01", "search_unit_id": "f27ed60f-5d0f-52d8-a7ed-8c1959f31d01", "block_from_id": "891295cc-8ad8-53a2-abc3-080fef071b55", "block_to_id": "db2dd1f4-a878-57ba-aa85-4940b5765625", "section_path": "Dedicated Throughput Slo Escalation > Service credits / compensation (internal guidance) > When to initiate a credit review", "document_id": "2aced3e3-1ed9-50b2-9ef8-a037c40fcfaf", "document_version_id": "5b0b49bf-5c10-5f9e-b6f9-1ae199865977", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_409618a3958944f9b78362ed7e01bb33.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-124", "heading": "Dedicated Throughput Slo Escalation > Service credits / compensation (internal guidance) > When to initiate a credit review", "content": "When to initiate a credit review\\n\\nInitiate when:\\n\\n- SRE confirms an SLO breach per canonical evaluator, AND\\n- The breach is not excluded (e.g., customer throttling), AND\\n- The customer requests credits OR the account team recommends proactive review.", "score": 0.496142, "rank": 29, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "7d9c597e-d7a3-583c-8789-c62d6e710ac2", "search_unit_id": "7d9c597e-d7a3-583c-8789-c62d6e710ac2", "block_from_id": "28e9e867-e360-5a0a-800c-84ed79a67e0f", "block_to_id": "299c6adc-0d7e-5285-bc7b-beda7a5ca627", "section_path": "20280503 Region Fallback Priority Ops Inventory", "document_id": "4da40c19-70f8-5526-806a-febdeb4668cd", "document_version_id": "521fe3cb-72a4-5a06-9a90-f3cf0d2048aa", "document_name": "gmail__dsid_8e838ab6a98f4cbcb672d41f210ff89c.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "p-30", "heading": "20280503 Region Fallback Priority Ops Inventory", "content": "If that all sounds good I\xe2\x80\x99ll mark the deal record in HubSpot with the scheduled deep-dive and next-step tasks.\\n\\nBest,\\nRafael\\nSenior AE, Redwood Inference\\n\\nOn Fri, May 3, 2028 at 3:22 PM Rafael Mendes <rafael.mendes@redwoodinference.com> wrote:\\n> Thanks for the call earlier, Elena \xe2\x80\x94 good alignment on the high-level constraints. Per our discussion, I wanted to capture a short inventory of the items we need to confirm so we can scope a targeted technical deep-dive next week. I attached a simple diagram and an ops inventory CSV template to speed things up.\\n> \\n> Action items / clarifying questions for MedThink (please reply inline if easier):\\n> 1) Residency / pinning: which datasets must remain in-region (EU-only / US-only)? You mentioned patient records must stay in the EU for EU patients; confirm whether backups/snapshots are allowed outside the EU if they are encrypted and access-controlled.\\n> 2) Failover order and allowed cross-region replication: if a primary EU region is degraded, do you require warm-standby in the same region only, or is cross-region failover to US/APAC acceptable for short windows? Any maximum allowed RPO/RTO?\\n> 3) Logs & telemetry: do MedThink logs contain PII/PHI (patient identifiers, SSNs, full names)? If yes, do you expect redaction at ingest, tokenization, or that logs be retained on-region only? What is your default retention window (you mentioned 90 days as a baseline during the call) and do you need longer-term archival (e.g., 1\xe2\x80\x937 years) for audit?\\n> 4) Backups & snapshots: frequency expectations for DB/model snapshotting, and whether incremental backups may be stored cross-region. Are immutable snapshots required?\\n> 5) Key management and attestations: will you require customer-managed keys (KMS/HSM) for on-rest encryption? Any need for HSM-backed key rotation logs delivered monthly?\\n> 6) Audit evidence: please indicate the list of artifacts you need from Redwood to satisfy procurement/security (SOC 2, access logs, key rotation logs, model inference logs, redaction proofs).\\n> \\n> Proposed next steps (from our side):\\n> - We can run a focused tech session (45\xe2\x80\x9360m) with our infra engineer and a solution architect to walk through pinning flows, failover scenarios, and sample log redaction patterns.\\n> - If you can populate the attached ops inventory CSV and return it, we\xe2\x80\x99ll produce a draft MAM (mutual action map) with dates/cutovers.\\n> - We\xe2\x80\x99ll also prepare a short export of how logs look today (sanitized sample) and a preliminary cost delta for region-locked storage vs cross-region backups.\\n> \\n> Attachments: REDWOOD_PINNING_DIAGRAM.pdf (diagram), medthink-ops-inventory-template.csv (CSV).\\n> \\n> Thanks again \xe2\x80\x94 I\xe2\x80\x99ll coordinate scheduling once we see preferred attendees and availability.\\n> \\n> Best,\\n> Rafael Mendes\\n> Senior AE, Redwood Inference\\n> r.mendes@redwoodinference.com\\n> +1 415-555-0184", "score": 0.477892, "rank": 30, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "3d36a28d-6fc9-590f-9268-c8b257f3f647", "search_unit_id": "3d36a28d-6fc9-590f-9268-c8b257f3f647", "block_from_id": "0fc99e99-51f6-5095-9e68-9ebd09907f59", "block_to_id": "e06d56e3-dcb7-5729-a189-045ce618a381", "section_path": "Dedicated Throughput Slo Escalation > Service credits / compensation (internal guidance)", "document_id": "2aced3e3-1ed9-50b2-9ef8-a037c40fcfaf", "document_version_id": "5b0b49bf-5c10-5f9e-b6f9-1ae199865977", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_409618a3958944f9b78362ed7e01bb33.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-120", "heading": "Dedicated Throughput Slo Escalation > Service credits / compensation (internal guidance)", "content": "Service credits / compensation (internal guidance)\\n\\n**Important:** Do not commit to a credit amount in writing until approvals are complete.", "score": 0.496142, "rank": 31, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "818be0d7-2a89-52e2-9f97-254ad53e0ca3", "search_unit_id": "818be0d7-2a89-52e2-9f97-254ad53e0ca3", "block_from_id": "8ce6084e-1ee0-57bc-bc6a-2944826a5978", "block_to_id": "93436a27-fd3b-5c0e-8c17-be8a29a3fefa", "section_path": "Dedicated Throughput Slo Escalation > Triage checklist (Support/CS)", "document_id": "2aced3e3-1ed9-50b2-9ef8-a037c40fcfaf", "document_version_id": "5b0b49bf-5c10-5f9e-b6f9-1ae199865977", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_409618a3958944f9b78362ed7e01bb33.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-46", "heading": "Dedicated Throughput Slo Escalation > Triage checklist (Support/CS)", "content": "Triage checklist (Support/CS)\\n\\nPerform steps 1\xe2\x80\x938 before (or while) paging; do not block paging for SEV-1.", "score": 0.496142, "rank": 32, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "d02b4796-32e0-50c1-9673-14ea96c45f13", "search_unit_id": "d02b4796-32e0-50c1-9673-14ea96c45f13", "block_from_id": "a043b226-12b5-5251-a376-0cce2a7c3e37", "block_to_id": "f95739c6-2bbe-5e5f-b66a-bcbbd0adefa2", "section_path": "Dedicated Throughput Slo Escalation > Post-incident expectations", "document_id": "2aced3e3-1ed9-50b2-9ef8-a037c40fcfaf", "document_version_id": "5b0b49bf-5c10-5f9e-b6f9-1ae199865977", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_409618a3958944f9b78362ed7e01bb33.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-139", "heading": "Dedicated Throughput Slo Escalation > Post-incident expectations", "content": "Post-incident expectations\\n\\nFor confirmed Premium-tier breaches (and significant Plus-tier events), request:\\n\\n- SRE-written incident summary within 5 business days.\\n- Follow-up action items tagged to owning teams (SRE/Infra/Observability/Routing).\\n- If credits were issued: ensure the billing/metering record reflects committed vs burst usage correctly.\\n\\n---", "score": 0.341834, "rank": 33, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "2cc9377f-67a0-5bcf-8183-ece562049b82", "search_unit_id": "2cc9377f-67a0-5bcf-8183-ece562049b82", "block_from_id": "9146d58d-26d8-5d0c-9c47-fc24004dd6ab", "block_to_id": "be7cf20c-a3a1-5637-b882-4edf8254663f", "section_path": "Dedicated Throughput Slo Escalation > Templates (copy/paste) > Template B \xe2\x80\x94 Confirmed incident + engaged on-call", "document_id": "2aced3e3-1ed9-50b2-9ef8-a037c40fcfaf", "document_version_id": "5b0b49bf-5c10-5f9e-b6f9-1ae199865977", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_409618a3958944f9b78362ed7e01bb33.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-91", "heading": "Dedicated Throughput Slo Escalation > Templates (copy/paste) > Template B \xe2\x80\x94 Confirmed incident + engaged on-call", "content": "Template B \xe2\x80\x94 Confirmed incident + engaged on-call\\n\\nSubject: Update: Dedicated throughput degradation (Deployment {{deployment_id}})\\n\\nHi {{customer_name}},\\n\\nWe\xe2\x80\x99ve confirmed a throughput degradation affecting your Dedicated deployment ({{deployment_id}}). We\xe2\x80\x99ve engaged our Site Reliability Engineering and Infrastructure on-call teams and are actively mitigating.\\n\\nCurrent status:\\n\\n- Impact: {{impact_summary}}\\n- Start time (UTC): {{start_time_utc}}\\n- Mitigation in progress: {{mitigation_summary}}\\n\\nNext update by {{time}}.\\nBest,\\n{{agent_name}}", "score": 0.353617, "rank": 34, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "f03ecf70-fdfe-5656-b612-1cecce05c842", "search_unit_id": "f03ecf70-fdfe-5656-b612-1cecce05c842", "block_from_id": "208b5cc2-cb59-5058-bc6a-ba6b8286026b", "block_to_id": "ecbe7849-a8e0-56d7-90a5-849aeeaa743e", "section_path": "Dedicated Throughput Slo Escalation > Appendix: Minimal internal handoff note (for paging)", "document_id": "2aced3e3-1ed9-50b2-9ef8-a037c40fcfaf", "document_version_id": "5b0b49bf-5c10-5f9e-b6f9-1ae199865977", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_409618a3958944f9b78362ed7e01bb33.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-143", "heading": "Dedicated Throughput Slo Escalation > Appendix: Minimal internal handoff note (for paging)", "content": "Appendix: Minimal internal handoff note (for paging)\\n\\nWhen paging SRE/Infra, include:\\n\\n- \xe2\x80\x9cDedicated Throughput SLO: suspected/confirmed\xe2\x80\x9d\\n- Deployment ID\\n- Tier + region\\n- Time window and whether ongoing\\n- Customer-confirmed load/concurrency (if available)\\n- Dashboard link\\n- Any correlated symptoms (timeouts, 5xx, queue depth)\\n\\nThis reduces back-and-forth and speeds mitigation.", "score": 0.29686, "rank": 35, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "24e1e99e-8df1-5692-98b4-c450fb8eab04", "search_unit_id": "24e1e99e-8df1-5692-98b4-c450fb8eab04", "block_from_id": "0a019782-2548-558d-aaf8-d89fc9e5ec7b", "block_to_id": "4888eef5-9f0b-5bc1-9ac4-f3a213e13054", "section_path": "20280503 Region Fallback Priority Ops Inventory", "document_id": "4da40c19-70f8-5526-806a-febdeb4668cd", "document_version_id": "521fe3cb-72a4-5a06-9a90-f3cf0d2048aa", "document_name": "gmail__dsid_8e838ab6a98f4cbcb672d41f210ff89c.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h1-0", "heading": "20280503 Region Fallback Priority Ops Inventory", "content": "20280503 Region Fallback Priority Ops Inventory\\n\\nSource type: gmail\\nDocument ID: dsid_8e838ab6a98f4cbcb672d41f210ff89c\\nRelease: v1.0.0\\nBenchmark: EnterpriseRAG-Bench synthetic upstream data\\nRegional fallback priorities & logs \xe2\x80\x94 post-call inventory\\n\\nFrom: Rafael Mendes <rafael.mendes@redwoodinference.com>\\nTo: Elena Ruiz <elena.ruiz@medthink.health>\\nCc: Monica Patel <monica.patel@redwoodinference.com>, Stephanie Nguyen <stephanie.nguyen@redwoodinference.com>\\nDate: Fri, 3 May 2028 15:22:00 -0700\\nSubject: Regional fallback priorities & logs \xe2\x80\x94 post-call inventory\\n\\nThanks for the call earlier, Elena \xe2\x80\x94 good alignment on the high-level constraints. Per our discussion, I wanted to capture a short inventory of the items we need to confirm so we can scope a targeted technical deep-dive next week. I attached a simple diagram and an ops inventory CSV template to speed things up.\\n\\nAction items / clarifying questions for MedThink (please reply inline if easier):\\n1) Residency / pinning: which datasets must remain in-region (EU-only / US-only)? You mentioned patient records must stay in the EU for EU patients; confirm whether backups/snapshots are allowed outside the EU if they are encrypted and access-controlled.\\n2) Failover order and allowed cross-region replication: if a primary EU region is degraded, do you require warm-standby in the same region only, or is cross-region failover to US/APAC acceptable for short windows? Any maximum allowed RPO/RTO?\\n3) Logs & telemetry: do MedThink logs contain PII/PHI (patient identifiers, SSNs, full names)? If yes, do you expect redaction at ingest, tokenization, or that logs be retained on-region only? What is your default retention window (you mentioned 90 days as a baseline during the call) and do you need longer-term archival (e.g., 1\xe2\x80\x937 years) for audit?\\n4) Backups & snapshots: frequency expectations for DB/model snapshotting, and whether incremental backups may be stored cross-region. Are immutable snapshots required?\\n5) Key management and attestations: will you require customer-managed keys (KMS/HSM) for on-rest encryption? Any need for HSM-backed key rotation logs delivered monthly?\\n6) Audit evidence: please indicate the list of artifacts you need from Redwood to satisfy procurement/security (SOC 2, access logs, key rotation logs, model inference logs, redaction proofs).\\n\\nProposed next steps (from our side):\\n\\n- We can run a focused tech session (45\xe2\x80\x9360m) with our infra engineer and a solution architect to walk through pinning flows, failover scenarios, and sample log redaction patterns.\\n- If you can populate the attached ops inventory CSV and return it, we\xe2\x80\x99ll produce a draft MAM (mutual action map) with dates/cutovers.\\n- We\xe2\x80\x99ll also prepare a short export of how logs look today (sanitized sample) and a preliminary cost delta for region-locked storage vs cross-region backups.\\n\\nAttachments: REDWOOD_PINNING_DIAGRAM.pdf (diagram), medthink-ops-inventory-template.csv (CSV).\\n\\nThanks again \xe2\x80\x94 I\xe2\x80\x99ll coordinate scheduling once we see preferred attendees and availability.\\n\\nBest,\\nRafael Mendes\\nSenior AE, Redwood Inference\\nr.mendes@redwoodinference.com\\n+1 415-555-0184\\nFrom: Elena Ruiz <elena.ruiz@medthink.health>\\nTo: Rafael Mendes <rafael.mendes@redwoodinference.com>\\nCc: Tom Baxter <tbaxter@medthink.health>\\nDate: Sat, 4 May 2028 09:05:00 -0400\\nSubject: Re: Regional fallback priorities & logs \xe2\x80\x94 post-call inventory\\n\\nHi Rafael \xe2\x80\x94 thanks for the clear list. Below are our answers to help you scope the deep-dive; I pasted the items you asked for and added quick notes.\\n\\n1) Residency / pinning:", "score": 0.462443, "rank": 36, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "ac71ef7c-7162-548f-ae1c-cef9b82ec04e", "search_unit_id": "ac71ef7c-7162-548f-ae1c-cef9b82ec04e", "block_from_id": "d9331753-256a-5d3f-8366-5f2b891886af", "block_to_id": "6ea5aca9-f46d-5988-aab8-1689931ea184", "section_path": "Overload Errors And Retry Guidance > Known issues (Support-facing)", "document_id": "d1667e56-b0c3-5fb4-a769-9f13a8679e2f", "document_version_id": "a9986e4a-2cf0-5373-a739-d5611a7a824c", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_ca42a8f18d784c879c5a6fcfe3a484c0.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-65", "heading": "Overload Errors And Retry Guidance > Known issues (Support-facing)", "content": "Known issues (Support-facing)\\n\\n1) **Retry-After header missing on some overload responses**\\n\\n- Symptom: Customer receives 429/503 overload payload but no Retry-After.\\n- Workaround: Recommend exponential backoff with jitter as above.\\n- Action: Escalate if reproducible; include route + correlation IDs.\\n\\n2) **Fallback model not triggering as expected**\\n\\n- Symptom: Customer has configured fallback but still sees repeated 503 without failover.\\n- Workaround: Customer can temporarily specify an alternate model/region explicitly (if acceptable) while we investigate.\\n- Action: Escalate; include tenant ID, configured fallback policy (what they intended), and correlation IDs.\\n\\n3) **Customer interprets 503 as \xe2\x80\x9cplatform outage\xe2\x80\x9d**\\n\\n- Guidance: Use the approved response language; direct them to Retry-After and backoff guidance.", "score": 0.619189, "rank": 37, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "102d6b2f-e126-58de-b2fd-d2e60b9c7cdf", "search_unit_id": "102d6b2f-e126-58de-b2fd-d2e60b9c7cdf", "block_from_id": "7b34c526-4228-5c3a-a4c0-302a2713c937", "block_to_id": "c173e9e5-7af2-51bc-9a5d-08d6dc30f43b", "section_path": "Policy Engine Failover Extensions Draft", "document_id": "d6d26fd7-a1c4-5594-b8e3-2aa73c8f448d", "document_version_id": "5db22b04-2f5e-53d8-8bae-5ef192a1c767", "document_name": "google_drive__dsid_184be937d34a412ab5e61366d54d8ed6.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "list-44", "heading": "Policy Engine Failover Extensions Draft", "content": "- decision_id (stable hash of route_id + tenant_id + evaluation_time + policy_version)\\n- policy_version\\n- evaluation_time\\n- decision_type\\n- chosen_reason\\n- target_state (string encoding; owned by controller)\\n- requested_actions (string encoding; empty in recommend mode)\\n- evidence (string encoding; ordered)\\n- annotations (string encoding; includes thresholds, staleness, hold-down state)\\n\\nNote: In our implementation we\xe2\x80\x99ll likely use structured objects, but for logging/audit we must generate a stable, versioned string representation.\\n\\nSafety constraints (ADR-043 alignment)\\n\\n- Anti-flap:\\n  - Enforce hold-down between flips for non-reachability triggers.\\n  - Any rollback decision must respect a separate rollback hold-down (avoid ping-pong between primary and fallback).\\n- Rate limiting:\\n  - flip_budget_ok must be true, else HOLD.\\n- Approval hooks:\\n  - If require_approval is true, decision_type can still be FAILOVER but requested_actions must be empty and \xe2\x80\x9capproval_required=true\xe2\x80\x9d annotation set.\\n- Tenant/tier gates:\\n  - Enterprise/Dedicated can be configured with stricter \xe2\x80\x9cdo not cross data residency boundary\xe2\x80\x9d constraint (policy engine should surface \xe2\x80\x9cconstraint_violation:data_residency\xe2\x80\x9d rather than attempt partial shifts).\\n\\nEdge cases and expected behavior\\n1) Partial outage in primary region\\n\\n- Reachability degraded (not down), 5xx burn elevated, capacity OK in fallback.\\n- Expected: PARTIAL_SHIFT (e.g., shift 25\xe2\x80\x9350% depending on max_traffic_shift_percent) if corroborated. If sustained and escalates to reachability down or error burn becomes severe => FAILOVER.\\n\\n2) Signal missing / ingestion delayed\\n\\n- Any authoritative signal is stale beyond max_staleness_seconds.\\n- Expected: HOLD. Evidence must explicitly call out staleness and which signal blocked action.\\n\\n3) Fallback region constrained\\n\\n- Primary is failing (5xx burn), fallback capacity_hard_gate true.\\n- Expected: HOLD + annotate \xe2\x80\x9cfallback_unhealthy_due_to_capacity\xe2\x80\x9d. Controller should invoke load shedding and retry-after rather than shifting load.\\n\\n4) Control plane degraded\\n\\n- Control plane health degraded; data plane signals ambiguous.\\n- Expected: HOLD unless reachability down is authoritative. (Avoid flipping policies when control plane is suspect.)\\n\\n5) Multi-fallback selection\\n\\n- If multiple eligible fallback regions are healthy, selection tie-breakers:\\n  1) policy-specified order\\n  2) lowest latency probe (if available in inputs)\\n  3) highest capacity headroom\\n  4) stable sort by region name\\n\\nTesting plan (draft)\\nUnit tests\\n\\n- Determinism:\\n  - Same payload with randomized key order => same decision_id, decision_type, evidence ordering.\\n- Staleness gating:\\n  - Stale error burn + fresh reachability OK => HOLD.\\n- Priority:\\n  - Reachability DOWN overrides hold-down.\\n  - 5xx burn overrides latency burn when both exceed thresholds.\\n\\nIntegration tests\\n\\n- Replay recorded signal snapshots from staging incidents + controlled game day traces.\\n- Validate output is compatible with controller dry-run UX (must contain reasons + evidence).\\n\\nPerformance considerations\\n\\n- Evaluation must be cheap; do not add per-eval remote calls.\\n- Evidence strings must be bounded in size. Cap rejected_candidates and evidence list.\\n\\nOperational / observability hooks\\n\\n- Emit a single log line per decision with:\\n  - decision_id, route_id, tenant_id (hashed in shared Hosted contexts), decision_type, chosen_reason\\n  - key thresholds and freshness\\n- Export metrics:\\n  - policy_engine_decisions_total{decision_type, chosen_reason, tier}\\n  - policy_engine_hold_reasons_total{reason}\\n  - policy_engine_eval_latency_ms\\n\\nOpen questions", "score": 0.611068, "rank": 38, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "8c636936-30ed-5920-8bb7-d84f1ced6428", "search_unit_id": "8c636936-30ed-5920-8bb7-d84f1ced6428", "block_from_id": "acd99a23-582d-5e56-acc9-ba779fdceb07", "block_to_id": "5cba83c4-198d-506b-bb77-5de8e3840e81", "section_path": "1769014420 Eu Data Residency Objection Handling", "document_id": "7de58fe8-b874-5851-baa5-15763b7da158", "document_version_id": "1bc644e2-2e15-5a69-ac1f-de6bf0b68051", "document_name": "slack__dsid_b8f2f50607a0406f9733f2e9ba4281c8.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h1-0", "heading": "1769014420 Eu Data Residency Objection Handling", "content": "1769014420 Eu Data Residency Objection Handling\\n\\nSource type: slack\\nDocument ID: dsid_b8f2f50607a0406f9733f2e9ba4281c8\\nRelease: v1.0.0\\nBenchmark: EnterpriseRAG-Bench synthetic upstream data\\nsales\\n\\nHannah Schmitt: Need quick help on EU data residency objection. Prospect (EU bank) wants \xe2\x80\x9cEU-only processing + EU-only storage + no US access\xe2\x80\x9d for Hosted. What\xe2\x80\x99s the approved phrasing + what do we *not* promise? @Olga Petrov @Daniel Carter @Marcus Lin\\n\\nLukas Meyer: +1, similar objection came up in EMEA last week. They\xe2\x80\x99re asking if *anything* touches US systems (logs, support tooling, etc). Want to keep this clean.\\n\\nAvery Johnson: Same here on another deal. Can we get a pasteable paragraph + a \xe2\x80\x9cdon\xe2\x80\x99t say this\xe2\x80\x9d list?\\n\\nPriyom Das: They also asked if model routing could ever fail over to a non-EU region under load. Need to confirm.\\n\\nMarcus Lin: jumping in. First: do NOT promise \xe2\x80\x9cEU-only\xe2\x80\x9d unless we\xe2\x80\x99re talking Private deployment w/ customer-controlled infra, or we have a written contract amendment that explicitly defines what\xe2\x80\x99s in/out.\\n\\nMarcus Lin: For Hosted: we can support region selection (incl EU) for request processing, but we should be precise that some operational metadata may be processed/stored outside the selected region depending on the system (billing, abuse prevention, support). We need to use the approved language.\\n\\nNaomi Feldman: +1. Also: don\xe2\x80\x99t imply \xe2\x80\x9cno failover ever.\xe2\x80\x9d Our default is to keep traffic in-region if you\xe2\x80\x99ve selected EU, but we can\xe2\x80\x99t blanket guarantee \xe2\x80\x9cnever leaves EU under any condition\xe2\x80\x9d unless it\xe2\x80\x99s explicitly in the commercial terms / Private. Say \xe2\x80\x9cregion-pinned\xe2\x80\x9d and \xe2\x80\x9cno cross-region routing by default for customer content\xe2\x80\x9d (but avoid absolute words like \xe2\x80\x9cnever\xe2\x80\x9d).\\n\\nHannah Schmitt: got it. What\xe2\x80\x99s the exact approved snippet? They\xe2\x80\x99re literally asking for \xe2\x80\x9ccontractual commitment that all data incl logs stays in EU and only EU staff can access.\xe2\x80\x9d\\n\\nOlga Petrov: Here\xe2\x80\x99s what we can say (approved style). Use \xe2\x80\x9cCustomer Content\xe2\x80\x9d vs \xe2\x80\x9cdata\xe2\x80\x9d to avoid ambiguity. Also do not commit on \xe2\x80\x9cEU-only personnel\xe2\x80\x9d access.\\n\\nOlga Petrov: Pasteable response (Hosted + EU region):\\n\xe2\x80\x9cRedwood Inference supports regional processing for Hosted API workloads. When a customer selects an EU region, Customer Content (request prompts and model outputs) is processed in that region. Access to Customer Content is restricted to authorized personnel on a need-to-know basis and is logged. Certain limited operational metadata (e.g., account and billing information, service health telemetry) may be processed or stored outside the selected region as part of operating and securing the service. For stricter residency requirements (including customer-managed networking and data boundary controls), Redwood offers Dedicated capacity in-region and Private (VPC/on\xe2\x80\x91prem) deployments.\xe2\x80\x9d\\n\\nDaniel Carter: + a compliance note: we should add \xe2\x80\x9cDetails available under NDA / via the evidence request process.\xe2\x80\x9d Do not attach internal diagrams in email.\\n\\nDaniel Carter: Also, for \xe2\x80\x9ccontractual commitment\xe2\x80\x9d requests: route to Legal + GRC. We can say \xe2\x80\x9cWe can evaluate specific contractual residency requirements; please share the questionnaire language.\xe2\x80\x9d\\n\\nLukas Meyer: Can we explicitly address the \xe2\x80\x9cfailover\xe2\x80\x9d question? They\xe2\x80\x99re worried about cross-region fallback.", "score": 0.580422, "rank": 39, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "a6065907-1903-5b5e-bbdf-2d8f3e83c940", "search_unit_id": "a6065907-1903-5b5e-bbdf-2d8f3e83c940", "block_from_id": "0c2b8211-3c07-529a-838b-580603568a6b", "block_to_id": "9555bfc3-8e5e-5c74-857a-d7c54358bdbc", "section_path": "Hosted Api Slos Enterprise Route Tiers > SLOs (targets) > General notes", "document_id": "12efb103-6e2e-5955-be3e-431b65ac2bca", "document_version_id": "78cfdc0b-41fe-5614-b19f-c7d639aaa33b", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_49fa5cfd95624dbeb6eaa535f9959470.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-41", "heading": "Hosted Api Slos Enterprise Route Tiers > SLOs (targets) > General notes", "content": "SLOs (targets)\\n\\nGeneral notes\\n\\n- SLOs are evaluated over a **rolling 28-day window**.\\n- Unless specified, targets apply per region (e.g., us-east, eu-west).\\n- We define both **p95 and p99** latency objectives for enterprise; best-effort uses p95 as primary.", "score": 0.575089, "rank": 40, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "b9038493-5fb3-5ff1-adfd-a65a81e2fffc", "search_unit_id": "b9038493-5fb3-5ff1-adfd-a65a81e2fffc", "block_from_id": "46e6fcf0-e199-5b3d-af0c-ea67bc0ab9e1", "block_to_id": "ce50aab8-e958-5bb3-b105-184243cd579f", "section_path": "Overload Errors And Retry Guidance > Common customer questions + approved responses > \xe2\x80\x9cCan you increase my limits?\xe2\x80\x9d", "document_id": "d1667e56-b0c3-5fb4-a769-9f13a8679e2f", "document_version_id": "a9986e4a-2cf0-5373-a739-d5611a7a824c", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_ca42a8f18d784c879c5a6fcfe3a484c0.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-62", "heading": "Overload Errors And Retry Guidance > Common customer questions + approved responses > \xe2\x80\x9cCan you increase my limits?\xe2\x80\x9d", "content": "\xe2\x80\x9cCan you increase my limits?\xe2\x80\x9d\\n\\nGuidance:\\n\\n- Confirm whether they are hitting **429** (likely limit-related) vs **503** (regional/model saturation).\\n- If 429 is persistent at normal traffic levels, route to CS for capacity/tier discussion.\\n- If 503 is persistent, treat as reliability issue and escalate to Eng.", "score": 0.596673, "rank": 41, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "88855f6e-6c20-50aa-bfe7-f2291e19ee3a", "search_unit_id": "88855f6e-6c20-50aa-bfe7-f2291e19ee3a", "block_from_id": "aca002ea-b5f6-5eef-a351-afe10f404271", "block_to_id": "8c727e98-6019-5657-b4d6-19b73ac583e5", "section_path": "Policy Engine Failover Extensions Draft", "document_id": "d6d26fd7-a1c4-5594-b8e3-2aa73c8f448d", "document_version_id": "5db22b04-2f5e-53d8-8bae-5ef192a1c767", "document_name": "google_drive__dsid_184be937d34a412ab5e61366d54d8ed6.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "list-19", "heading": "Policy Engine Failover Extensions Draft", "content": "- Decision must include:\\n  - decision_type (NO_OP | FAILOVER | PARTIAL_SHIFT | ROLLBACK | HOLD)\\n  - chosen_reason (canonical enum)\\n  - evidence: ordered list of signals used, with values, freshness, and thresholds.\\n  - rejected_candidates: (optional) top 1\xe2\x80\x933 alternatives and why they were not selected.\\n\\nProposed changes to policy engine\\nA) New predicates / functions\\n1) region_health(region, signal_type) -> {status, value, confidence, freshness_seconds}\\n\\n- Wrapper that pulls normalized data from payload and enforces freshness calculations.\\n\\n2) is_authoritative_reachability_down(region) -> bool\\n\\n- True only if:\\n  - reachability.status == down\\n  - confidence >= configured_min_confidence (default 0.9)\\n  - freshness_seconds <= reachability_max_staleness (default 30s)\\n\\n3) burn_rate_exceeded(region, metric, window, threshold) -> bool\\n\\n- Works for errors_5xx_burn and tail_latency_burn.\\n- Window must be one of approved windows (e.g., 1m/5m/30m) to avoid configuration drift.\\n\\n4) capacity_hard_gate(region) -> bool\\n\\n- True if headroom below threshold AND capacity signal confidence is high.\\n- Intended to prevent shifting into an already overloaded region.\\n\\n5) corroborated(primary_signal, secondary_signal) -> bool\\n\\n- Enforces ADR-042 \xe2\x80\x9crequired corroboration signals\xe2\x80\x9d when configured.\\n- Example: if tail latency burn triggers, require either 5xx burn OR reachability degraded/down OR control plane degraded.\\n\\n6) hold_down_active(last_flip_at, min_hold_down_seconds) -> bool\\n\\n- If true, policy engine returns HOLD unless reachability down is authoritative.\\n\\n7) flip_budget_ok(tenant_id, route_id, max_flips_per_hour) -> bool\\n\\n- Input includes a precomputed counter from controller/state store (policy engine does not store state).\\n\\n8) blast_radius_ok(tenant_tier, requested_action) -> bool\\n\\n- Enforces \xe2\x80\x9ccan\xe2\x80\x99t shift more than X% traffic for tier Y without approval\xe2\x80\x9d.\\n- For Hosted, blast radius is route-scoped; for Dedicated, pool-scoped.\\n\\nB) Deterministic evaluation mode (required)\\n\\n- Add an \xe2\x80\x9cevaluation_mode\xe2\x80\x9d field:\\n  - recommend: compute decision + evidence; do not mark as executable\\n  - enforce: compute decision; include explicit requested_action(s)\\n- Engine must produce identical decision_type and evidence in both modes (action packaging differs).\\n\\nC) Signal hierarchy evaluation (ADR-042)\\nPriority order (proposed canonical order for v1):\\n1) Reachability DOWN (authoritative) => FAILOVER (unless no healthy fallback)\\n2) Errors (5xx) fast burn (high severity) => FAILOVER or PARTIAL_SHIFT depending on blast radius and capacity\\n3) Tail latency burn (p99/p95) => PARTIAL_SHIFT first; escalate to FAILOVER if corroborated and sustained\\n4) Capacity exhaustion / hard gate => HOLD + load shed (controller action), avoid shifting into constrained region\\n5) Control plane degradation => HOLD (do not flip rapidly; prevent oscillation)\\n\\nNotes:\\n\\n- \xe2\x80\x9cNo healthy fallback\xe2\x80\x9d means every eligible fallback region fails capacity_hard_gate OR reachability is down OR stale beyond threshold.\\n- If no healthy fallback, decision should be HOLD and include \xe2\x80\x9cdegrade_allowed=true\xe2\x80\x9d hint (controller can activate load shedding / retry-after).\\n\\nD) Policy language / config schema additions\\nAdd new fields (names tentative):\\n\\n- failover:\\n  - enabled: boolean\\n  - eligible_regions: [us-east, eu-west, ...]\\n  - signal_requirements:\\n    - primary_trigger: enum\\n    - corroboration: [enum]\\n    - min_confidence: float\\n    - max_staleness_seconds: int\\n  - dampening:\\n    - min_hold_down_seconds: int\\n    - require_sustain_seconds: int (for non-reachability triggers)\\n  - safety:\\n    - require_approval: boolean (default true for prod initially)\\n    - max_flips_per_hour: int\\n    - max_traffic_shift_percent: int\\n    - rollback:\\n      - auto_rollback_enabled: boolean\\n      - rollback_after_seconds: int\\n      - rollback_require_healthy_primary_seconds: int\\n\\nE) Output schema\\nDecision output (single object, JSON):", "score": 0.584826, "rank": 42, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "83ec62b5-f7e7-526f-8aac-42d5f516142e", "search_unit_id": "83ec62b5-f7e7-526f-8aac-42d5f516142e", "block_from_id": "50860677-0e07-5a22-b304-2a91252ff67f", "block_to_id": "dea4a6da-eac4-510f-a038-e3b04f86a397", "section_path": "Hosted Api Slos Enterprise Route Tiers > Revision history", "document_id": "12efb103-6e2e-5955-be3e-431b65ac2bca", "document_version_id": "78cfdc0b-41fe-5614-b19f-c7d639aaa33b", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_49fa5cfd95624dbeb6eaa535f9959470.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-94", "heading": "Hosted Api Slos Enterprise Route Tiers > Revision history", "content": "Revision history\\n\\n- 2025-12-10: Initial version drafted for hot-route protection MVP (enterprise vs best-effort split).\\n- 2026-01-12: Updated latency targets for embeddings after eu-west canary measurements.\\n- 2026-01-29: Finalized burn-rate thresholds and enterprise shed-rate paging criteria for GA.", "score": 0.553288, "rank": 43, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "61320e84-aae6-58b4-987b-b9f324e87b13", "search_unit_id": "61320e84-aae6-58b4-987b-b9f324e87b13", "block_from_id": "546aea4b-f8c5-5a61-b71f-69c8a66a99e5", "block_to_id": "83c797a1-75cb-54bf-8bc7-21b1c36afbb9", "section_path": "Policy Engine Failover Extensions Draft", "document_id": "d6d26fd7-a1c4-5594-b8e3-2aa73c8f448d", "document_version_id": "5db22b04-2f5e-53d8-8bae-5ef192a1c767", "document_name": "google_drive__dsid_184be937d34a412ab5e61366d54d8ed6.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h1-0", "heading": "Policy Engine Failover Extensions Draft", "content": "Policy Engine Failover Extensions Draft\\n\\nSource type: google_drive\\nDocument ID: dsid_184be937d34a412ab5e61366d54d8ed6\\nRelease: v1.0.0\\nBenchmark: EnterpriseRAG-Bench synthetic upstream data\\nDraft Spec: Policy Engine Extensions for Regional Failover Automation\\n\\nContext / why this exists\\n\\n- We\xe2\x80\x99re upgrading regional failover automation as part of Reliability Program (Q1\xe2\x80\x93Q2 2026). Today, routing policy evaluation has a few gaps:\\n  - Non-deterministic behavior in edge cases (e.g., multiple signals firing, partial signal availability, time-window ambiguity).\\n  - Hard to reason about priority across trigger signals (reachability, 5xx burn, tail latency burn, capacity exhaustion).\\n  - No first-class \xe2\x80\x9chold-down\xe2\x80\x9d / dampening in evaluation; logic is split between policy rules and external controller.\\n  - No consistent mechanism to enforce safety constraints per tenant/tier (max flips, blast radius caps, required approval).\\n\\nGoals\\n\\n- Add policy engine primitives so failover decisioning is:\\n  - Deterministic and auditable (same inputs => same decision; explainability built-in).\\n  - Compatible with ADR-042 (signal priority + corroboration) and ADR-043 (rollback + anti-flap).\\n  - Safe by default (rate limits, required corroboration, blast radius constraints).\\n- Support both:\\n  - \xe2\x80\x9cRecommend\xe2\x80\x9d (dry-run) mode: compute candidate flips + evidence.\\n  - \xe2\x80\x9cEnforce\xe2\x80\x9d mode: same evaluation but returns executable actions.\\n\\nNon-goals\\n\\n- Replace the automation controller. The controller still orchestrates execution, approvals, and cross-system workflow.\\n- Re-architect signal ingestion. We consume normalized, time-bucketed signals from Region Health + SLO toolkit.\\n- Build customer-facing UI here.\\n\\nTerminology\\n\\n- Policy: configuration describing routing behavior for a route/service/model/tier.\\n- Region set: primary and fallback regions eligible for this route.\\n- Trigger signal: normalized boolean or scalar indicating regional impairment or risk.\\n- Decision: computed outcome (no-op, failover, partial shift, rollback, hold).\\n- Action: executable change (policy flip, weight adjustment, circuit breaker mode) emitted by controller.\\n\\nInputs / data model assumptions\\n\\n- Policy engine receives inputs as a single evaluation payload, including:\\n  - route_id (e.g., hosted.chat.completions, dedicated.pool.<pool_id>)\\n  - tenant_id (optional for shared Hosted; required for Dedicated)\\n  - tenant_tier (free/pro/enterprise/dedicated)\\n  - current_routing_state (primary region, weights, last_flip_at)\\n  - signals (per region, per signal type):\\n    - reachability: ok|degraded|down + confidence + last_updated\\n    - errors_5xx_burn: burn_rate + window + confidence\\n    - tail_latency_burn: burn_rate + p95/p99 deltas + confidence\\n    - capacity_headroom: percent + \xe2\x80\x9chard gate\xe2\x80\x9d boolean\\n    - control_plane_health (optional): ok|degraded|down\\n  - evaluation_time (UTC epoch + monotonic sequence)\\n  - constraints (policy-level + tenant-level): max_flips_per_hour, min_hold_down_seconds, require_approval, blast_radius_limit\\n\\nDeterminism requirements (core)\\n1) Stable ordering\\n\\n- Evaluation must not depend on map iteration order.\\n- Rule matching must define explicit ordering: by priority, then by tie-breakers.\\n\\n2) Stable time semantics\\n\\n- All windowed signals must be anchored to evaluation_time and include:\\n  - effective_start, effective_end, and a \xe2\x80\x9cfreshness\xe2\x80\x9d timestamp.\\n- Engine must treat stale signals consistently:\\n  - If authoritative signals are stale beyond threshold, decision = HOLD (do not fail over) unless reachability is explicitly DOWN with high confidence.\\n\\n3) Single decision per evaluation\\n\\n- For a given (route_id, tenant_id, evaluation_time), engine emits exactly one decision object, even if multiple actions are possible.\\n- Multi-step actions (e.g., drain -> shift weights -> finalize) must be represented as a sequence recommendation but still within a single decision record.\\n\\n4) Explainability", "score": 0.542266, "rank": 44, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "78666fbe-0b98-571c-820d-c25aeb5777d8", "search_unit_id": "78666fbe-0b98-571c-820d-c25aeb5777d8", "block_from_id": "3799b33b-76e4-542c-ba64-13c225825417", "block_to_id": "a690b4fe-539c-5274-aaf5-5aa5a3eec022", "section_path": "Overload Errors And Retry Guidance > Purpose", "document_id": "d1667e56-b0c3-5fb4-a769-9f13a8679e2f", "document_version_id": "a9986e4a-2cf0-5373-a739-d5611a7a824c", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_ca42a8f18d784c879c5a6fcfe3a484c0.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-2", "heading": "Overload Errors And Retry Guidance > Purpose", "content": "Purpose\\n\\nThis page helps Support/CS respond to customer reports of new \xe2\x80\x9coverload protection\xe2\x80\x9d errors (circuit breakers + load shedding) on Redwood Hosted API.\\n\\nGoals:\\n\\n- Explain what the customer is seeing (stable semantics vs ambiguous timeouts/5xx).\\n- Provide canonical retry/backoff guidance to prevent retry storms.\\n- Show how to interpret correlation IDs so Engineering can quickly trace requests.\\n- Define escalation criteria and the minimum information to collect.", "score": 0.526311, "rank": 45, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "57b96fdd-0f5e-53b4-a310-daead3454531", "search_unit_id": "57b96fdd-0f5e-53b4-a310-daead3454531", "block_from_id": "0c3e2cf6-07f3-5d32-a0c7-a3ecaf18f79a", "block_to_id": "35a0efd4-14b1-5149-8872-366364ecc72c", "section_path": "Overload Errors And Retry Guidance > What changed (customer-facing)", "document_id": "d1667e56-b0c3-5fb4-a769-9f13a8679e2f", "document_version_id": "a9986e4a-2cf0-5373-a739-d5611a7a824c", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_ca42a8f18d784c879c5a6fcfe3a484c0.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-6", "heading": "Overload Errors And Retry Guidance > What changed (customer-facing)", "content": "What changed (customer-facing)\\n\\nWhen the platform is saturated (GPU capacity, scheduler backlog, downstream dependency brownout), Redwood may reject requests *early* and predictably rather than allowing them to time out or generate random 5xx.\\n\\nCustomers may now see:\\n\\n- **429** responses for admission / quota / per-tenant caps.\\n- **503** responses when a regional/model circuit breaker is open or the system is actively shedding load.\\n\\nThese responses:\\n\\n- Include stable **error codes** and a machine-readable JSON payload.\\n- Typically include a **Retry-After** header to indicate safe retry timing.\\n- Include Redwood request/correlation IDs for tracing.", "score": 0.507735, "rank": 46, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "f8d4590f-6d5f-56a1-8f95-17cb8cbf70d5", "search_unit_id": "f8d4590f-6d5f-56a1-8f95-17cb8cbf70d5", "block_from_id": "bf91ceec-bcda-59fd-b0ab-92bc9bb46071", "block_to_id": "e560db75-82d2-5766-a424-9cefdf581a82", "section_path": "Hosted Api Slos Enterprise Route Tiers > Purpose", "document_id": "12efb103-6e2e-5955-be3e-431b65ac2bca", "document_version_id": "78cfdc0b-41fe-5614-b19f-c7d639aaa33b", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_49fa5cfd95624dbeb6eaa535f9959470.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-2", "heading": "Hosted Api Slos Enterprise Route Tiers > Purpose", "content": "Purpose\\n\\nThis document defines **per-route SLOs and error budget policy** for Redwood Inference\xe2\x80\x99s **Hosted API** as it relates to **hot-route capacity protection** (tier-aware quotas, priority routing, and controlled shedding).\\n\\nThe intent is to:\\n\\n- Explicitly define **enterprise vs best-effort** expectations for the highest-traffic routes.\\n- Make overload behavior **measurable and supportable** (clear SLIs + dashboards + alerts).\\n- Align alerting to overload protection so we page on **enterprise degradation**, not expected best-effort shedding.", "score": 0.488826, "rank": 47, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "057534d2-d0d9-5b2c-ab50-d721b8ae029c", "search_unit_id": "057534d2-d0d9-5b2c-ab50-d721b8ae029c", "block_from_id": "c5e21672-449d-517e-ac07-12888219ff04", "block_to_id": "ca6b790f-d4f1-5fb5-ad45-20d884dd5cb4", "section_path": "1769014420 Eu Data Residency Objection Handling", "document_id": "7de58fe8-b874-5851-baa5-15763b7da158", "document_version_id": "1bc644e2-2e15-5a69-ac1f-de6bf0b68051", "document_name": "slack__dsid_b8f2f50607a0406f9733f2e9ba4281c8.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "p-15", "heading": "1769014420 Eu Data Residency Objection Handling", "content": "Marcus Lin: approved approach: \xe2\x80\x9cWe route based on the region selected; cross-region routing of customer content is not the standard behavior for region-pinned setups.\xe2\x80\x9d Don\xe2\x80\x99t use \xe2\x80\x9cnever.\xe2\x80\x9d If they require a hard guarantee, push to Dedicated/Private + contract language.\\n\\nNaomi Feldman: Also don\xe2\x80\x99t conflate \xe2\x80\x9cdata residency\xe2\x80\x9d with \xe2\x80\x9cdata retention.\xe2\x80\x9d They\xe2\x80\x99ll ask \xe2\x80\x9chow long do you store prompts/logs in EU.\xe2\x80\x9d That\xe2\x80\x99s a separate set of knobs depending on deployment.\\n\\nAvery Johnson: Can you list the top \xe2\x80\x9cDON\xe2\x80\x99T SAY\xe2\x80\x9d bullets? Helps AEs avoid stepping on landmines.\\n\\nOlga Petrov: DON\xe2\x80\x99T SAY / avoid:\\n\\n- \xe2\x80\x9cWe guarantee EU-only storage for all data, including logs/metadata\xe2\x80\x9d (too broad; depends on category + contract)\\n- \xe2\x80\x9cWe never route outside the EU under any circumstances\xe2\x80\x9d (absolute)\\n- \xe2\x80\x9cWe have ISO 27001 certification\xe2\x80\x9d (unless explicitly true; use \xe2\x80\x9calignment\xe2\x80\x9d language only if approved)\\n- \xe2\x80\x9cOnly EU employees can access your data\xe2\x80\x9d (personnel location commitments aren\xe2\x80\x99t part of standard controls)\\n- \xe2\x80\x9cWe can meet GDPR/Schrems II by default\xe2\x80\x9d (legal conclusion; we can describe controls + DPA)\\n\\nOlga Petrov: DO SAY:\\n\\n- \xe2\x80\x9cEU region selection / region-pinning for Customer Content processing\xe2\x80\x9d\\n- \xe2\x80\x9cAccess is least-privilege, audited, and requires authorization\xe2\x80\x9d\\n- \xe2\x80\x9cDedicated/Private options for stricter residency boundaries\xe2\x80\x9d\\n- \xe2\x80\x9cWe can review specific contractual requirements with Legal/GRC\xe2\x80\x9d\\n\\nPriyom Das: They asked if prompts are used to train models. Can we include that line or keep scoped?\\n\\nMarcus Lin: You can include the standard line if it comes up, but keep it separate from residency so it doesn\xe2\x80\x99t read like a new promise. Approved phrasing is \xe2\x80\x9cWe do not use Customer Content to train Redwood-provided models unless the customer explicitly opts in under a separate written agreement.\xe2\x80\x9d (Don\xe2\x80\x99t improvise.)\\n\\nStephanie Nguyen: For live deal: recommend we send the snippet + link the canonical residency/retention overview in Confluence, and offer a quick security call w/ GRC. @Hannah Schmitt I can help coordinate.\\n\\nHannah Schmitt: super helpful. Can someone drop the Confluence link name so I don\xe2\x80\x99t grab the wrong doc?\\n\\nDaniel Carter: Use the customer-facing page in the Security & Compliance space: \xe2\x80\x9cData retention and deletion overview\xe2\x80\x9d (has residency notes). If they want SOC 2 report / evidence, follow the \xe2\x80\x9cSOC 2 customer evidence request playbook\xe2\x80\x9d and ensure NDA is in place.\\n\\nLukas Meyer: :thumbsup: I\xe2\x80\x99ll reuse the snippet for my EMEA deal too.\\n\\nHannah Schmitt: Thanks all. I\xe2\x80\x99ll reply to the prospect with the approved paragraph + \xe2\x80\x9cwe can evaluate stricter residency / contractual needs via Dedicated/Private\xe2\x80\x9d and pull Legal/GRC if they push on absolute EU-only + EU-only personnel. :white_check_mark:\\n\\nJordan Blake: +1 on escalation. If this is a gating item, loop me in early so we don\xe2\x80\x99t burn cycles. Use the approved wording only\xe2\x80\x94no custom commitments in email.\\n\\nHannah Schmitt: ack. looping you + @Stephanie Nguyen on the thread w/ the account notes.", "score": 0.493359, "rank": 48, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "243aa4e1-ec00-57ad-bd06-c6f6b5c7ef5a", "search_unit_id": "243aa4e1-ec00-57ad-bd06-c6f6b5c7ef5a", "block_from_id": "780d9ed0-d169-5a86-9b48-f746b3595b01", "block_to_id": "cf0d9903-36e3-5187-bf17-795b8600e5b7", "section_path": "Hosted Api Slos Enterprise Route Tiers > SLOs (targets) > Latency SLOs by route and tier", "document_id": "12efb103-6e2e-5955-be3e-431b65ac2bca", "document_version_id": "78cfdc0b-41fe-5614-b19f-c7d639aaa33b", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_49fa5cfd95624dbeb6eaa535f9959470.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-46", "heading": "Hosted Api Slos Enterprise Route Tiers > SLOs (targets) > Latency SLOs by route and tier", "content": "Latency SLOs by route and tier\\n\\nLatency objectives are defined in terms of:\\n\\n- **Chat streaming:** TTFB p95/p99\\n- **Non-streaming:** E2E p95/p99\\n\\n| Route | Tier | Latency SLO (primary) | Latency SLO (secondary) | Measurement |\\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---|\\n| `/v1/chat/completions` (streaming) | Enterprise (Protected) | TTFB p95 \xe2\x89\xa4 450ms | TTFB p99 \xe2\x89\xa4 900ms | Gateway TTFB |\\n| `/v1/chat/completions` (streaming) | Best-effort | TTFB p95 \xe2\x89\xa4 900ms | (informational) p99 \xe2\x89\xa4 1800ms | Gateway TTFB |\\n| `/v1/chat/completions` (non-streaming) | Enterprise (Protected) | E2E p95 \xe2\x89\xa4 1.8s | E2E p99 \xe2\x89\xa4 3.5s | Gateway E2E |\\n| `/v1/embeddings` | Enterprise (Protected) | E2E p95 \xe2\x89\xa4 350ms | E2E p99 \xe2\x89\xa4 800ms | Gateway E2E |\\n| `/v1/embeddings` | Best-effort | E2E p95 \xe2\x89\xa4 700ms | (informational) p99 \xe2\x89\xa4 1.5s | Gateway E2E |\\n| `/v1/rerank` | Enterprise (Protected) | E2E p95 \xe2\x89\xa4 550ms | E2E p99 \xe2\x89\xa4 1.2s | Gateway E2E |\\n| `/v1/rerank` | Best-effort | E2E p95 \xe2\x89\xa4 1.2s | (informational) p99 \xe2\x89\xa4 2.5s | Gateway E2E |\\n\\n**Notes / caveats**\\n\\n- Latency SLOs assume nominal prompt and response sizes. Excessive prompt length or extreme max_tokens increases may be subject to policy limits; those requests are still included in latency metrics unless explicitly rejected by policy.\\n- Where fallback is permitted (route/model policy), latency SLI measures the actual served path; dashboards must annotate fallback activations.", "score": 0.482032, "rank": 49, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "d93d2bc8-b21e-5022-ab81-2171d5a9fc0a", "search_unit_id": "d93d2bc8-b21e-5022-ab81-2171d5a9fc0a", "block_from_id": "c63a6ebd-1b90-576f-a654-dab9c22a1640", "block_to_id": "2bf54639-15d2-5100-bd4f-2433409d5e0c", "section_path": "Overload Errors And Retry Guidance > Internal-only: where to look (for Support with access)", "document_id": "d1667e56-b0c3-5fb4-a769-9f13a8679e2f", "document_version_id": "a9986e4a-2cf0-5373-a739-d5611a7a824c", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_ca42a8f18d784c879c5a6fcfe3a484c0.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-78", "heading": "Overload Errors And Retry Guidance > Internal-only: where to look (for Support with access)", "content": "Internal-only: where to look (for Support with access)\\n\\n- Overload dashboards: shed rate, breaker-open rate, queue depth, saturation signals by region/model.\\n- Incident channels: #eng-oncall, #incidents (look for breaker announcements).\\n- Runbook: \xe2\x80\x9cHosted overload / circuit breaker runbook\xe2\x80\x9d (linked above).", "score": 0.470584, "rank": 50, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "6907986d-ae14-5167-af96-fb20158abed9", "search_unit_id": "6907986d-ae14-5167-af96-fb20158abed9", "block_from_id": "f8735775-a5c2-55df-9eee-44825a4ca655", "block_to_id": "3e381144-1521-5137-b4bb-9113bc2ac936", "section_path": "Overload Errors And Retry Guidance > Retry & backoff guidance (what we should recommend) > Streaming-specific guidance", "document_id": "d1667e56-b0c3-5fb4-a769-9f13a8679e2f", "document_version_id": "a9986e4a-2cf0-5373-a739-d5611a7a824c", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_ca42a8f18d784c879c5a6fcfe3a484c0.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-41", "heading": "Overload Errors And Retry Guidance > Retry & backoff guidance (what we should recommend) > Streaming-specific guidance", "content": "Streaming-specific guidance\\n\\nStreaming workloads can worsen overload if clients open many concurrent streams.\\n\\n- Recommend **lower streaming concurrency** during peak periods.\\n- If the customer can tolerate it, recommend **shorter outputs** (reduce `max_tokens`) and/or **shorter prompts**.\\n- If a stream fails mid-response with an overload error on reconnect attempts, advise them to back off and resume with a bounded number of attempts.", "score": 0.470584, "rank": 51, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "8fbf98ac-7f3c-5420-b5f9-f2b57fd5b758", "search_unit_id": "8fbf98ac-7f3c-5420-b5f9-f2b57fd5b758", "block_from_id": "56349e95-55f8-548a-9ce0-9740e41b3f1b", "block_to_id": "a8e2c43d-8b94-507e-b7c4-45bd307f72c0", "section_path": "Overload Errors And Retry Guidance > When to escalate to Engineering (Eng Oncall / SRE)", "document_id": "d1667e56-b0c3-5fb4-a769-9f13a8679e2f", "document_version_id": "a9986e4a-2cf0-5373-a739-d5611a7a824c", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_ca42a8f18d784c879c5a6fcfe3a484c0.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-72", "heading": "Overload Errors And Retry Guidance > When to escalate to Engineering (Eng Oncall / SRE)", "content": "When to escalate to Engineering (Eng Oncall / SRE)\\n\\nEscalate immediately if any of the following are true:\\n\\n- **Enterprise customer** reporting sustained overload errors impacting production.\\n- Overload errors persist for **>15 minutes** with correct backoff behavior.\\n- **No Retry-After** observed on multiple responses for the same route/region/model.\\n- Suspected **misclassification** (e.g., 500s that should be 429/503 overload, or overload codes returned with 200/stream interruptions).\\n- **Fallback routing configured** but not activating.\\n- Customer reports sharp regression (new errors) coincident with a canary/rollout and provides IDs.", "score": 0.470584, "rank": 52, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "139b27e1-b120-500b-8afb-187e49be95e0", "search_unit_id": "139b27e1-b120-500b-8afb-187e49be95e0", "block_from_id": "4d0b355d-cd97-5fc3-9b5a-3e0d47653a45", "block_to_id": "fc7e5142-2524-5128-96f5-869cfa6333e8", "section_path": "Overload Errors And Retry Guidance > Canonical mapping: status \xe2\x86\x92 meaning \xe2\x86\x92 what we tell customers", "document_id": "d1667e56-b0c3-5fb4-a769-9f13a8679e2f", "document_version_id": "a9986e4a-2cf0-5373-a739-d5611a7a824c", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_ca42a8f18d784c879c5a6fcfe3a484c0.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-26", "heading": "Overload Errors And Retry Guidance > Canonical mapping: status \xe2\x86\x92 meaning \xe2\x86\x92 what we tell customers", "content": "Canonical mapping: status \xe2\x86\x92 meaning \xe2\x86\x92 what we tell customers\\n\\nUse this table to drive consistent customer guidance.\\n\\n| HTTP | Typical meaning | What Support should say | Customer action |\\n|------|------------------|--------------------------|-----------------|\\n| 429 | Admission control / rate limiting / tier cap hit | \xe2\x80\x9cYour request was rejected to protect system stability. This is not a model failure; it indicates you are sending requests faster than the current allowed rate/concurrency.\xe2\x80\x9d | Respect Retry-After; implement exponential backoff + jitter; reduce concurrency; consider batching; if persistent, discuss tier/capacity options. |\\n| 503 | Regional/model breaker open or load shedding | \xe2\x80\x9cRedwood is temporarily overloaded in the requested region/model. We are rejecting early to avoid timeouts and protect overall reliability.\xe2\x80\x9d | Respect Retry-After; backoff + jitter; optionally route to another region/model if configured; reduce max_tokens/streaming concurrency; retry with bounded attempts. |\\n\\nNotes:\\n\\n- If the customer reports **timeouts** with no JSON error, treat as a separate issue (possible client/network or upstream timeouts) and escalate based on impact.\\n- If the customer gets **5xx** without the overload payload, collect details; it may be an unrelated incident.", "score": 0.470584, "rank": 53, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "bc401c57-33c3-50bd-a410-5c9ee1c0fc4a", "search_unit_id": "bc401c57-33c3-50bd-a410-5c9ee1c0fc4a", "block_from_id": "5ea22243-12c2-530f-9cb8-add8278b88ee", "block_to_id": "871e0af5-521e-5c9d-b5b2-18b6f26b0243", "section_path": "Overload Errors And Retry Guidance > How to recognize overload-protection responses > Expected headers (may vary by route)", "document_id": "d1667e56-b0c3-5fb4-a769-9f13a8679e2f", "document_version_id": "a9986e4a-2cf0-5373-a739-d5611a7a824c", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_ca42a8f18d784c879c5a6fcfe3a484c0.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-18", "heading": "Overload Errors And Retry Guidance > How to recognize overload-protection responses > Expected headers (may vary by route)", "content": "Expected headers (may vary by route)\\n\\n- **Retry-After**: integer seconds is preferred (e.g., `Retry-After: 2`).\\n- **x-redwood-request-id**: unique ID for a single request attempt.\\n- **x-redwood-correlation-id**: groups related attempts across services (gateway \xe2\x86\x92 routing \xe2\x86\x92 runtime). Some clients/logs only show one of these; either is helpful.\\n\\nIf the response is 429/503 *and* includes a Redwood overload error code in the JSON body, treat it as overload protection.", "score": 0.470584, "rank": 54, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "6a555b8d-f11b-51e1-8bd3-9079a846097a", "search_unit_id": "6a555b8d-f11b-51e1-8bd3-9079a846097a", "block_from_id": "3800f0b7-5683-5bb7-bf2a-9fb1804d1876", "block_to_id": "23bb2a3a-ae5c-5f88-aeaa-1e1bc35ce7e4", "section_path": "Overload Errors And Retry Guidance > How to interpret and use correlation IDs > How Support should use them internally", "document_id": "d1667e56-b0c3-5fb4-a769-9f13a8679e2f", "document_version_id": "a9986e4a-2cf0-5373-a739-d5611a7a824c", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_ca42a8f18d784c879c5a6fcfe3a484c0.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-51", "heading": "Overload Errors And Retry Guidance > How to interpret and use correlation IDs > How Support should use them internally", "content": "How Support should use them internally\\n\\n- Paste the ID(s) into the internal log search / tracing tool.\\n- Capture:\\n  - the **error.code**\\n  - the **route** (e.g., `/v1/chat/completions`, `/v1/responses`, embeddings endpoint)\\n  - the **region** (requested + served)\\n  - whether **Retry-After** was present and its value\\n\\nIf Support cannot access dashboards/tracing, escalate with the IDs and all details in the escalation template below.", "score": 0.470584, "rank": 55, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "fcf908f4-3acc-5496-bdaa-657f90a3cad2", "search_unit_id": "fcf908f4-3acc-5496-bdaa-657f90a3cad2", "block_from_id": "d026b7e6-a9d0-52b2-b51b-ecdea495ce10", "block_to_id": "a0b81b9f-bd1c-5ec3-89dc-80aab513ae28", "section_path": "Overload Errors And Retry Guidance > Revision history", "document_id": "d1667e56-b0c3-5fb4-a769-9f13a8679e2f", "document_version_id": "a9986e4a-2cf0-5373-a739-d5611a7a824c", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_ca42a8f18d784c879c5a6fcfe3a484c0.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-80", "heading": "Overload Errors And Retry Guidance > Revision history", "content": "Revision history\\n\\n- 2025-11-10: Initial publication for overload error rollout (Support readiness).\\n- 2025-12-05: Updated retry guidance; clarified correlation IDs and escalation thresholds.", "score": 0.470584, "rank": 56, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "6ec7073f-b628-5f9d-9589-eaaedd0e1c04", "search_unit_id": "6ec7073f-b628-5f9d-9589-eaaedd0e1c04", "block_from_id": "0b7e415a-871b-5ee2-9715-3a8c6a09800b", "block_to_id": "48ae9f4c-5300-53b0-ad8c-54c4bda1a255", "section_path": "Overload Errors And Retry Guidance > Error payload: what customers see", "document_id": "d1667e56-b0c3-5fb4-a769-9f13a8679e2f", "document_version_id": "a9986e4a-2cf0-5373-a739-d5611a7a824c", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_ca42a8f18d784c879c5a6fcfe3a484c0.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-21", "heading": "Overload Errors And Retry Guidance > Error payload: what customers see", "content": "Error payload: what customers see\\n\\nOverload errors are additive and JSON-compatible with existing response parsing.\\n\\nTypical shape (example):\\n\\n- `error.type`: `overload_error` (or `rate_limit_error` in some cases)\\n- `error.code`: stable machine code\\n- `error.message`: human-readable\\n- `error.request_id`: mirrors `x-redwood-request-id` where available\\n- `error.correlation_id`: mirrors `x-redwood-correlation-id` where available\\n\\nExample snippet (illustrative only):\\n{\\n  \\"error\\": {\\n    \\"type\\": \\"overload_error\\",\\n    \\"code\\": \\"BREAKER_OPEN\\",\\n    \\"message\\": \\"The service is temporarily overloaded. Please retry after the specified delay.\\",\\n    \\"request_id\\": \\"req_01J9...\\",\\n    \\"correlation_id\\": \\"corr_01J9...\\"\\n  }\\n}", "score": 0.470584, "rank": 57, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "0e9be2a7-c39f-5762-b7c6-a08b499e3bfc", "search_unit_id": "0e9be2a7-c39f-5762-b7c6-a08b499e3bfc", "block_from_id": "e2679d07-03c8-5704-a619-95bfdee31b55", "block_to_id": "40ac20d9-b556-5a2e-9dbc-7b20581770ee", "section_path": "Hosted Api Slos Enterprise Route Tiers > Scope", "document_id": "12efb103-6e2e-5955-be3e-431b65ac2bca", "document_version_id": "78cfdc0b-41fe-5614-b19f-c7d639aaa33b", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_49fa5cfd95624dbeb6eaa535f9959470.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-6", "heading": "Hosted Api Slos Enterprise Route Tiers > Scope", "content": "Scope\\n\\n**In scope**\\n\\n- Hosted API routes: `/v1/chat/completions`, `/v1/embeddings`, `/v1/rerank`, `/v1/completions`.\\n- Tiered behavior: **Enterprise (Protected)** vs **Best-effort (Standard/Self-serve)**.\\n- SLOs for **availability**, **latency**, and **overload responses (429)**.\\n- Alert thresholds and error budget burn policy.\\n\\n**Out of scope**\\n\\n- Dedicated and Private SLOs (tracked separately).\\n- Model-quality or semantic correctness SLIs.", "score": 0.471573, "rank": 58, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "5b491687-2e16-584c-a3e6-cab774cb2c89", "search_unit_id": "5b491687-2e16-584c-a3e6-cab774cb2c89", "block_from_id": "d1abd9f9-8d65-588d-b637-ea5cc6743aaf", "block_to_id": "58f5162d-c731-51a7-890d-1d874d9614c1", "section_path": "Overload Errors And Retry Guidance > Retry & backoff guidance (what we should recommend) > Recommended algorithm (support-approved)", "document_id": "d1667e56-b0c3-5fb4-a769-9f13a8679e2f", "document_version_id": "a9986e4a-2cf0-5373-a739-d5611a7a824c", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_ca42a8f18d784c879c5a6fcfe3a484c0.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-34", "heading": "Overload Errors And Retry Guidance > Retry & backoff guidance (what we should recommend) > Recommended algorithm (support-approved)", "content": "Recommended algorithm (support-approved)\\n\\nIf `Retry-After` is present:\\n\\n- Sleep `Retry-After` seconds, then retry.\\n\\nIf `Retry-After` is missing:\\n\\n- Backoff schedule suggestion: 0.5s, 1s, 2s, 4s, then stop (max 4 retries), each with \xc2\xb120\xe2\x80\x9340% jitter.\\n\\nBounds:\\n\\n- Maximum total retry time budget: **~10\xe2\x80\x9320 seconds** for interactive apps, **~60 seconds** for batch jobs.\\n- Maximum concurrent retries: keep to a small fraction of steady-state concurrency (e.g., 10\xe2\x80\x9320%).", "score": 0.470584, "rank": 59, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "4a7e3cce-c9c8-55b9-905f-703e61a38352", "search_unit_id": "4a7e3cce-c9c8-55b9-905f-703e61a38352", "block_from_id": "162248f9-343a-50bc-b5e0-c92001696295", "block_to_id": "ce6d9c24-4360-50c7-818e-46b0a9526337", "section_path": "Overload Errors And Retry Guidance > How to recognize overload-protection responses > Common HTTP statuses", "document_id": "d1667e56-b0c3-5fb4-a769-9f13a8679e2f", "document_version_id": "a9986e4a-2cf0-5373-a739-d5611a7a824c", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_ca42a8f18d784c879c5a6fcfe3a484c0.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-14", "heading": "Overload Errors And Retry Guidance > How to recognize overload-protection responses > Common HTTP statuses", "content": "How to recognize overload-protection responses\\n\\nCommon HTTP statuses\\n\\n- **429 Too Many Requests**\\n  - Used for admission controls such as per-tenant concurrency caps, token buckets, or tier limits.\\n  - Usually safe to retry with backoff if Retry-After is provided.\\n\\n- **503 Service Unavailable**\\n  - Used when the platform is overloaded at the regional/model level (breaker open) or actively shedding load to protect SLOs.\\n  - Usually safe to retry with backoff and/or reduce load. May persist until capacity recovers.", "score": 0.470584, "rank": 60, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "bdee7da0-de24-59e3-ab10-ea1d75bbaf31", "search_unit_id": "bdee7da0-de24-59e3-ab10-ea1d75bbaf31", "block_from_id": "ef3688e8-5268-5b0e-8ca9-1ca569e5f244", "block_to_id": "19329754-f309-5978-a5e3-d866fc0872fa", "section_path": "Overload Errors And Retry Guidance > How to interpret and use correlation IDs > Where customers can find them", "document_id": "d1667e56-b0c3-5fb4-a769-9f13a8679e2f", "document_version_id": "a9986e4a-2cf0-5373-a739-d5611a7a824c", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_ca42a8f18d784c879c5a6fcfe3a484c0.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-49", "heading": "Overload Errors And Retry Guidance > How to interpret and use correlation IDs > Where customers can find them", "content": "Where customers can find them\\n\\n- Response headers in their HTTP client.\\n- SDK exception fields (Python/TypeScript SDKs surface request IDs; newer versions surface correlation IDs when present).\\n- Their application logs if they log response headers.", "score": 0.470584, "rank": 61, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "c6a94887-e648-5d8d-9abe-f68b4bcca04e", "search_unit_id": "c6a94887-e648-5d8d-9abe-f68b4bcca04e", "block_from_id": "75c93691-1e39-59d3-8027-f907aa615e53", "block_to_id": "a92e60f5-8ecd-51cc-9b33-5a747158fb2b", "section_path": "Overload Errors And Retry Guidance > Common customer questions + approved responses > \xe2\x80\x9cWhy am I seeing 503 if this is overload?\xe2\x80\x9d", "document_id": "d1667e56-b0c3-5fb4-a769-9f13a8679e2f", "document_version_id": "a9986e4a-2cf0-5373-a739-d5611a7a824c", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_ca42a8f18d784c879c5a6fcfe3a484c0.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-57", "heading": "Overload Errors And Retry Guidance > Common customer questions + approved responses > \xe2\x80\x9cWhy am I seeing 503 if this is overload?\xe2\x80\x9d", "content": "\xe2\x80\x9cWhy am I seeing 503 if this is overload?\xe2\x80\x9d\\n\\nApproved response:\\n\xe2\x80\x9c503 is used when the platform is temporarily unable to serve the request due to load shedding or an open circuit breaker. It\xe2\x80\x99s a deliberate, controlled response (with stable error codes) to prevent cascading failures and long tail latency.\xe2\x80\x9d", "score": 0.470584, "rank": 62, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "d0ba3a34-6d9c-5187-8982-318b01a053c0", "search_unit_id": "d0ba3a34-6d9c-5187-8982-318b01a053c0", "block_from_id": "54b2b35e-ddfa-55af-9885-fab6dcddb921", "block_to_id": "ce4aa47e-1831-5ec1-a44f-6b21166e2f56", "section_path": "Overload Errors And Retry Guidance > Common customer questions + approved responses > \xe2\x80\x9cIs Redwood down?\xe2\x80\x9d", "document_id": "d1667e56-b0c3-5fb4-a769-9f13a8679e2f", "document_version_id": "a9986e4a-2cf0-5373-a739-d5611a7a824c", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_ca42a8f18d784c879c5a6fcfe3a484c0.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-54", "heading": "Overload Errors And Retry Guidance > Common customer questions + approved responses > \xe2\x80\x9cIs Redwood down?\xe2\x80\x9d", "content": "Common customer questions + approved responses\\n\\n\xe2\x80\x9cIs Redwood down?\xe2\x80\x9d\\n\\nApproved response:\\n\xe2\x80\x9cNot necessarily. These errors indicate Redwood is protecting service reliability during temporary saturation in a specific region/model. We reject early with clear retry guidance to avoid timeouts and degraded performance. Please follow the Retry-After header and exponential backoff. If the issue persists beyond a short window, share correlation IDs and we\xe2\x80\x99ll investigate.\xe2\x80\x9d", "score": 0.470584, "rank": 63, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "ab43dfc2-4541-55ca-83c4-b538991c0e67", "search_unit_id": "ab43dfc2-4541-55ca-83c4-b538991c0e67", "block_from_id": "f4567963-1d41-5eca-8075-72fdc54367a7", "block_to_id": "e78b061b-f023-578f-8842-03c5ebd267e4", "section_path": "Overload Errors And Retry Guidance > Retry & backoff guidance (what we should recommend) > Golden rules", "document_id": "d1667e56-b0c3-5fb4-a769-9f13a8679e2f", "document_version_id": "a9986e4a-2cf0-5373-a739-d5611a7a824c", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_ca42a8f18d784c879c5a6fcfe3a484c0.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-31", "heading": "Overload Errors And Retry Guidance > Retry & backoff guidance (what we should recommend) > Golden rules", "content": "Retry & backoff guidance (what we should recommend)\\n\\nGolden rules\\n\\n- **Always respect Retry-After** when provided.\\n- **Use exponential backoff with jitter**; do not retry immediately.\\n- **Cap retries** to avoid amplifying overload.\\n- **Reduce concurrency** rather than increasing it during overload.\\n- Prefer **idempotency keys** for safe retries on non-streaming requests.", "score": 0.470584, "rank": 64, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "2ecd7cd1-11cd-5948-9e75-9bcae5ba8648", "search_unit_id": "2ecd7cd1-11cd-5948-9e75-9bcae5ba8648", "block_from_id": "272e810a-0a1e-50fe-b260-3b60e2f93d3c", "block_to_id": "35af38c2-5431-554a-9cba-c854c0dd62f0", "section_path": "Overload Errors And Retry Guidance", "document_id": "d1667e56-b0c3-5fb4-a769-9f13a8679e2f", "document_version_id": "a9986e4a-2cf0-5373-a739-d5611a7a824c", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_ca42a8f18d784c879c5a6fcfe3a484c0.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h1-0", "heading": "Overload Errors And Retry Guidance", "content": "Overload Errors And Retry Guidance\\n\\nSource type: confluence\\nDocument ID: dsid_ca42a8f18d784c879c5a6fcfe3a484c0\\nRelease: v1.0.0\\nBenchmark: EnterpriseRAG-Bench synthetic upstream data\\nHosted API overload errors: support guidance, retry/backoff, and escalation", "score": 0.544886, "rank": 65, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "cd49e8e6-bdc5-5c01-a8f0-37450d10a51b", "search_unit_id": "cd49e8e6-bdc5-5c01-a8f0-37450d10a51b", "block_from_id": "1f31c549-698e-5181-95cb-c16fcb8db805", "block_to_id": "01945f51-74a3-5691-9964-001d14b8dc4a", "section_path": "Hosted Api Slos Enterprise Route Tiers > Definitions > Route tiers", "document_id": "12efb103-6e2e-5955-be3e-431b65ac2bca", "document_version_id": "78cfdc0b-41fe-5614-b19f-c7d639aaa33b", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_49fa5cfd95624dbeb6eaa535f9959470.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-11", "heading": "Hosted Api Slos Enterprise Route Tiers > Definitions > Route tiers", "content": "Definitions\\n\\nRoute tiers\\n\\nWe classify requests into one of the following tiers at the gateway/policy engine:\\n\\n- **Enterprise (Protected):** SLA-bearing tenants and allowlisted enterprise accounts for protected routes. These requests receive priority admission and are protected during fleet pressure.\\n- **Best-effort:** all other traffic. Best-effort may be throttled earlier and more aggressively to preserve fleet health and enterprise budgets.", "score": 0.45432, "rank": 66, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "d5c35f69-884a-5602-a3e7-e3b293289508", "search_unit_id": "d5c35f69-884a-5602-a3e7-e3b293289508", "block_from_id": "40f58b84-843e-58a9-80b8-ecdba4e8d23b", "block_to_id": "28699223-e704-5fd3-9de2-e027bfc184f2", "section_path": "Overload Errors And Retry Guidance > How to interpret and use correlation IDs > Which IDs to ask for", "document_id": "d1667e56-b0c3-5fb4-a769-9f13a8679e2f", "document_version_id": "a9986e4a-2cf0-5373-a739-d5611a7a824c", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_ca42a8f18d784c879c5a6fcfe3a484c0.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-46", "heading": "Overload Errors And Retry Guidance > How to interpret and use correlation IDs > Which IDs to ask for", "content": "How to interpret and use correlation IDs\\n\\nWhich IDs to ask for\\n\\nAsk the customer for (in order of preference):\\n1) `x-redwood-correlation-id` (best for cross-service tracing)\\n2) `x-redwood-request-id` (single request attempt)\\n3) Timestamp + region + model + route if IDs are not available", "score": 0.470584, "rank": 67, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "e534946f-6b15-55fa-94d0-63dd0bfb990e", "search_unit_id": "e534946f-6b15-55fa-94d0-63dd0bfb990e", "block_from_id": "0b5ad9a5-e47d-5b04-a4f8-5f31762fdd88", "block_to_id": "4474e74d-d55e-50e0-a7ee-0d9ef36ee6b9", "section_path": "Hosted Api Slos Enterprise Route Tiers > SLIs (what we measure) > 3) Overload activation SLI (operational)", "document_id": "12efb103-6e2e-5955-be3e-431b65ac2bca", "document_version_id": "78cfdc0b-41fe-5614-b19f-c7d639aaa33b", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_49fa5cfd95624dbeb6eaa535f9959470.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-36", "heading": "Hosted Api Slos Enterprise Route Tiers > SLIs (what we measure) > 3) Overload activation SLI (operational)", "content": "3) Overload activation SLI (operational)\\n\\nNot a customer-facing SLO, but required for on-call safety.\\n\\nWe track:\\n\\n- **shed_rate** (fraction of requests rejected due to overload by tier)\\n- **admission_control_active** (boolean/ratio time in state)\\n- **queue_depth / scheduler_lag** for the backing pools\\n\\nThese drive alerts and annotations on the enterprise SLO dashboards.", "score": 0.437068, "rank": 68, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "c00b44bb-1e2d-5032-98ac-eabb643e37ce", "search_unit_id": "c00b44bb-1e2d-5032-98ac-eabb643e37ce", "block_from_id": "43a0161c-c137-5e12-bf34-deb5614df57c", "block_to_id": "b07b5e8d-2bba-59b5-9b42-aa9ccbbe528b", "section_path": "Hosted Api Slos Enterprise Route Tiers > SLIs (what we measure) > 1) Availability SLI (server success)", "document_id": "12efb103-6e2e-5955-be3e-431b65ac2bca", "document_version_id": "78cfdc0b-41fe-5614-b19f-c7d639aaa33b", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_49fa5cfd95624dbeb6eaa535f9959470.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-26", "heading": "Hosted Api Slos Enterprise Route Tiers > SLIs (what we measure) > 1) Availability SLI (server success)", "content": "1) Availability SLI (server success)\\n\\n**Definition:** percentage of requests that return an eligible success response.\\n\\n- Success codes: `2xx` (and `3xx` if any internal redirects apply; typically none)\\n- Failures: `5xx`, `408`, `499` (client disconnect) are counted as failures unless explicitly excluded by route-specific rules below.\\n\\n**Tier handling of 429:**\\n\\n- **Enterprise:** `429` due to *overload shedding/admission control* counts as **unavailable** (because enterprise is protected; overload shed should be rare and indicates under-provisioning or misconfiguration).\\n- **Best-effort:** `429` due to overload shedding/admission control does **not** count as unavailable (it is expected behavior under pressure). Quota/rate-limit 429s are not counted as availability failures for either tier.\\n\\n**Note:** 429 classification must be based on the reason code emitted by gateway/policy engine, not inferred from rate.", "score": 0.437068, "rank": 69, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "f678312e-2816-51f5-8a37-a4d28bc0d31e", "search_unit_id": "f678312e-2816-51f5-8a37-a4d28bc0d31e", "block_from_id": "bcb5e610-4b5c-5a54-91be-23fcb89c4f92", "block_to_id": "0127f5ba-b07b-5d07-8c63-e3fc5f61a574", "section_path": "Hosted Api Slos Enterprise Route Tiers > Operational guidance > How to interpret 429s for SLOs", "document_id": "12efb103-6e2e-5955-be3e-431b65ac2bca", "document_version_id": "78cfdc0b-41fe-5614-b19f-c7d639aaa33b", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_49fa5cfd95624dbeb6eaa535f9959470.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-86", "heading": "Hosted Api Slos Enterprise Route Tiers > Operational guidance > How to interpret 429s for SLOs", "content": "Operational guidance\\n\\nHow to interpret 429s for SLOs\\n\\n- **Enterprise 429 overload-shed:** treat as incident-worthy and investigate capacity signals, admission thresholds, route budgets, and pool weights.\\n- **Best-effort 429 overload-shed:** expected under pressure; use this to validate the protection is working (enterprise should remain stable).\\n- **Quota 429 (any tier):** not an SLO failure; route to Support/Solutions for policy adjustment if needed.", "score": 0.437068, "rank": 70, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "5f87a7ec-6a84-5077-9637-43a2d538e29d", "search_unit_id": "5f87a7ec-6a84-5077-9637-43a2d538e29d", "block_from_id": "37cd6cb3-8c0a-50f7-ab06-abc75d1a1f54", "block_to_id": "bcde8b1d-1858-5d86-8ade-9c985f7b4164", "section_path": "Hosted Api Slos Enterprise Route Tiers > SLIs (what we measure) > 2) Latency SLI", "document_id": "12efb103-6e2e-5955-be3e-431b65ac2bca", "document_version_id": "78cfdc0b-41fe-5614-b19f-c7d639aaa33b", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_49fa5cfd95624dbeb6eaa535f9959470.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-32", "heading": "Hosted Api Slos Enterprise Route Tiers > SLIs (what we measure) > 2) Latency SLI", "content": "2) Latency SLI\\n\\nLatency is measured at the gateway edge (request receive to first byte / completion) and reported as:\\n\\n- **TTFB (time-to-first-byte)** for streaming endpoints.\\n- **E2E response time** for non-streaming.\\n\\nWe maintain distinct latency SLO targets per tier and route (see tables below).", "score": 0.437068, "rank": 71, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "0e220222-b88b-5e64-9355-bb13bd6432ab", "search_unit_id": "0e220222-b88b-5e64-9355-bb13bd6432ab", "block_from_id": "1097e02f-bddd-5b59-800e-4e309a05ea34", "block_to_id": "00662f96-ca52-524b-95ed-582364c94065", "section_path": "Hosted Api Slos Enterprise Route Tiers > Definitions > Overload / throttling semantics", "document_id": "12efb103-6e2e-5955-be3e-431b65ac2bca", "document_version_id": "78cfdc0b-41fe-5614-b19f-c7d639aaa33b", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_49fa5cfd95624dbeb6eaa535f9959470.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-20", "heading": "Hosted Api Slos Enterprise Route Tiers > Definitions > Overload / throttling semantics", "content": "Overload / throttling semantics\\n\\nRequests may be rejected with HTTP **429** for:\\n\\n- **Quota/rate limit enforcement** (tenant policy)\\n- **Overload shedding/admission control** (fleet protection)\\n\\nWe distinguish causes via standardized reason code headers/payloads (see Support doc for exact fields). For SLO accounting, we treat quota-throttled and overload-shed requests differently by tier (see SLI rules below).", "score": 0.437068, "rank": 72, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "32edec19-5981-5717-8440-1c0ecfedf3bd", "search_unit_id": "32edec19-5981-5717-8440-1c0ecfedf3bd", "block_from_id": "fb923860-bcb3-5033-81df-9e48baa2e320", "block_to_id": "001e456b-ee95-577b-ba26-27a8b5ab4208", "section_path": "Hosted Api Slos Enterprise Route Tiers > Alerting (paging + ticketing) > Paging routing", "document_id": "12efb103-6e2e-5955-be3e-431b65ac2bca", "document_version_id": "78cfdc0b-41fe-5614-b19f-c7d639aaa33b", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_49fa5cfd95624dbeb6eaa535f9959470.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-80", "heading": "Hosted Api Slos Enterprise Route Tiers > Alerting (paging + ticketing) > Paging routing", "content": "Paging routing\\n\\n- Primary: **#eng-oncall** and SRE pager rotation\\n- Secondary: **#eng-platform** for policy/gateway issues, **#eng-runtime** for scheduler lag/queue depth anomalies", "score": 0.437068, "rank": 73, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "4a3acd45-1a9a-517b-a605-39ba12ab2180", "search_unit_id": "4a3acd45-1a9a-517b-a605-39ba12ab2180", "block_from_id": "17ce7afa-bed8-5956-941f-ef0f72e58b09", "block_to_id": "ffab9b77-5166-5149-8d05-5f6621fe0c55", "section_path": "Hosted Api Slos Enterprise Route Tiers > Error budgets > Error budget policy (what we do when we burn)", "document_id": "12efb103-6e2e-5955-be3e-431b65ac2bca", "document_version_id": "78cfdc0b-41fe-5614-b19f-c7d639aaa33b", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_49fa5cfd95624dbeb6eaa535f9959470.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-60", "heading": "Hosted Api Slos Enterprise Route Tiers > Error budgets > Error budget policy (what we do when we burn)", "content": "Error budget policy (what we do when we burn)\\n\\n**Enterprise (Protected) routes**\\n\\n- If burn is elevated, the default stance is **protect SLOs over throughput**.\\n- Allowed mitigations (in priority order):\\n  1) Tighten best-effort admission control thresholds (shed earlier)\\n  2) Temporarily reduce best-effort burst allowances\\n  3) Increase enterprise reserved capacity / pool weights (if available)\\n  4) Enable guarded fallback policies where contractually allowed\\n  5) As last resort: temporary enterprise throttling with exec/on-call approval and proactive comms\\n\\n**Best-effort routes**\\n\\n- Best-effort can be shed under pressure; we do not page purely on best-effort 429 shedding.\\n- If best-effort availability drops due to 5xx (not 429 overload-shed), we investigate as a normal reliability regression.", "score": 0.437068, "rank": 74, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "3ac0f03e-be13-5959-bc3b-21b5800a2fb3", "search_unit_id": "3ac0f03e-be13-5959-bc3b-21b5800a2fb3", "block_from_id": "467c8227-b91c-541b-8dd6-a586c95c651f", "block_to_id": "6cba830f-b454-5c55-88a5-9939d11008a7", "section_path": "Hosted Api Slos Enterprise Route Tiers > Operational guidance > Change management", "document_id": "12efb103-6e2e-5955-be3e-431b65ac2bca", "document_version_id": "78cfdc0b-41fe-5614-b19f-c7d639aaa33b", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_49fa5cfd95624dbeb6eaa535f9959470.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-89", "heading": "Hosted Api Slos Enterprise Route Tiers > Operational guidance > Change management", "content": "Change management\\n\\nChanges that affect enterprise SLOs require:\\n\\n- Feature flag + region canary\\n- Dashboard annotation\\n- Rollback plan\\n- Confirmed alert routing and runbook link in incident-bot message", "score": 0.437068, "rank": 75, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "a3e54e4f-7341-58c6-b673-790f8dc189c5", "search_unit_id": "a3e54e4f-7341-58c6-b673-790f8dc189c5", "block_from_id": "3c3dbe92-f436-5016-b51c-d7546d9b8f00", "block_to_id": "85593ccd-fe4e-592c-acbf-78f8a7d921ad", "section_path": "Hosted Api Slos Enterprise Route Tiers > Alerting (paging + ticketing) > Alert principles", "document_id": "12efb103-6e2e-5955-be3e-431b65ac2bca", "document_version_id": "78cfdc0b-41fe-5614-b19f-c7d639aaa33b", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_49fa5cfd95624dbeb6eaa535f9959470.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-68", "heading": "Hosted Api Slos Enterprise Route Tiers > Alerting (paging + ticketing) > Alert principles", "content": "Alerting (paging + ticketing)\\n\\nAlert principles\\n\\n- Page on **enterprise** impact (availability/latency) and on conditions that predict imminent enterprise impact.\\n- Do not page on expected best-effort shedding unless it indicates misconfiguration or runaway protection (e.g., shedding at low utilization).\\n- Use multi-window burn rate to avoid flapping.", "score": 0.437068, "rank": 76, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "62fcc83f-b414-51cb-bcb2-209bbd1a09df", "search_unit_id": "62fcc83f-b414-51cb-bcb2-209bbd1a09df", "block_from_id": "7bb3447a-50dd-5a6f-be82-70df9ce725ae", "block_to_id": "e9103e26-8b73-51b7-911b-0f8f9f58012a", "section_path": "Overload Errors And Retry Guidance > Retry & backoff guidance (what we should recommend) > What NOT to recommend", "document_id": "d1667e56-b0c3-5fb4-a769-9f13a8679e2f", "document_version_id": "a9986e4a-2cf0-5373-a739-d5611a7a824c", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_ca42a8f18d784c879c5a6fcfe3a484c0.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-44", "heading": "Overload Errors And Retry Guidance > Retry & backoff guidance (what we should recommend) > What NOT to recommend", "content": "What NOT to recommend\\n\\n- \xe2\x80\x9cJust retry in a tight loop.\xe2\x80\x9d\\n- \xe2\x80\x9cRetry immediately with the same concurrency.\xe2\x80\x9d\\n- \xe2\x80\x9cSpin up many parallel retries to get through.\xe2\x80\x9d", "score": 0.470584, "rank": 77, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "65608456-3a44-5f00-9233-749e94d694a7", "search_unit_id": "65608456-3a44-5f00-9233-749e94d694a7", "block_from_id": "ff85e2bc-47fa-56eb-9cb8-f7704dcc70fd", "block_to_id": "95bc4171-61c8-584a-b5a0-d1ed1b5fb0a8", "section_path": "Hosted Api Slos Enterprise Route Tiers > Definitions > Protected routes", "document_id": "12efb103-6e2e-5955-be3e-431b65ac2bca", "document_version_id": "78cfdc0b-41fe-5614-b19f-c7d639aaa33b", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_49fa5cfd95624dbeb6eaa535f9959470.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-15", "heading": "Hosted Api Slos Enterprise Route Tiers > Definitions > Protected routes", "content": "Protected routes\\n\\nProtected routes are selected based on:\\n\\n- Fleet-wide traffic concentration (hot routes)\\n- High enterprise SLO/SLA coupling\\n- Known overload blast radius\\n\\nCurrent protected route set:\\n\\n- `/v1/chat/completions` (includes streaming)\\n- `/v1/embeddings`\\n- `/v1/rerank`\\n- `/v1/completions` (legacy; still used by some enterprise SDKs)", "score": 0.437068, "rank": 78, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "42378ef4-57c2-5454-b9a7-8e90730f3c5e", "search_unit_id": "42378ef4-57c2-5454-b9a7-8e90730f3c5e", "block_from_id": "dfb0dcb7-7641-50f8-890e-1cca9cb70242", "block_to_id": "a73aed1b-1158-50c2-9629-fd346db666ff", "section_path": "Hosted Api Slos Enterprise Route Tiers > SLIs (what we measure)", "document_id": "12efb103-6e2e-5955-be3e-431b65ac2bca", "document_version_id": "78cfdc0b-41fe-5614-b19f-c7d639aaa33b", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_49fa5cfd95624dbeb6eaa535f9959470.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-24", "heading": "Hosted Api Slos Enterprise Route Tiers > SLIs (what we measure)", "content": "SLIs (what we measure)\\n\\nAll SLIs are computed per **route x region x tier** using the standard metrics set.", "score": 0.437068, "rank": 79, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "ea913aa2-74a9-5230-91bf-983d0d58c6d9", "search_unit_id": "ea913aa2-74a9-5230-91bf-983d0d58c6d9", "block_from_id": "ed7c7ef6-7291-59dd-8bb5-06c6afb34224", "block_to_id": "810265e3-ce3f-5313-9cf4-0a7e2f41513a", "section_path": "Hosted Api Slos Enterprise Route Tiers > SLOs (targets) > Availability SLOs by route and tier", "document_id": "12efb103-6e2e-5955-be3e-431b65ac2bca", "document_version_id": "78cfdc0b-41fe-5614-b19f-c7d639aaa33b", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_49fa5cfd95624dbeb6eaa535f9959470.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-44", "heading": "Hosted Api Slos Enterprise Route Tiers > SLOs (targets) > Availability SLOs by route and tier", "content": "Availability SLOs by route and tier\\n\\n| Route | Tier | Availability SLO | Notes |\\n|---|---:|---:|---|\\n| `/v1/chat/completions` | Enterprise (Protected) | 99.95% | 429 overload-shed counts as failure. Quota 429 excluded. |\\n| `/v1/chat/completions` | Best-effort | 99.5% | 429 overload-shed excluded from availability; still tracked separately. |\\n| `/v1/embeddings` | Enterprise (Protected) | 99.95% | Batch requests included. |\\n| `/v1/embeddings` | Best-effort | 99.5% | 429 overload-shed excluded. |\\n| `/v1/rerank` | Enterprise (Protected) | 99.9% | Lower traffic; still protected. |\\n| `/v1/rerank` | Best-effort | 99.5% | 429 overload-shed excluded. |\\n| `/v1/completions` | Enterprise (Protected) | 99.9% | Legacy route; fewer dependencies but included for enterprise compatibility. |\\n| `/v1/completions` | Best-effort | 99.0% | Best-effort only; deprecation path in progress. |", "score": 0.437068, "rank": 80, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "a494e024-71d0-5d97-9144-bc164ae7f865", "search_unit_id": "a494e024-71d0-5d97-9144-bc164ae7f865", "block_from_id": "003b87dc-2fa7-50de-bdd3-a58e90891f06", "block_to_id": "4275183e-19cc-5054-b98a-4c75a73a265f", "section_path": "Hosted Api Slos Enterprise Route Tiers > Dashboard requirements (minimum)", "document_id": "12efb103-6e2e-5955-be3e-431b65ac2bca", "document_version_id": "78cfdc0b-41fe-5614-b19f-c7d639aaa33b", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_49fa5cfd95624dbeb6eaa535f9959470.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-82", "heading": "Hosted Api Slos Enterprise Route Tiers > Dashboard requirements (minimum)", "content": "Dashboard requirements (minimum)\\n\\nEvery protected route must have:\\n\\n- Availability by tier (enterprise vs best-effort)\\n- Latency p95/p99 by tier (and TTFB for streaming)\\n- 429 rate split by reason code (quota vs overload)\\n- shed_rate and admission_control_active\\n- queue depth and scheduler lag for backing pools\\n- Annotations for config changes, feature flag toggles, fallback activation\\n\\nSee the dashboard spec for panel/query naming conventions.", "score": 0.437068, "rank": 81, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "9d89662d-3914-5df3-b0c7-68c3e008f6fe", "search_unit_id": "9d89662d-3914-5df3-b0c7-68c3e008f6fe", "block_from_id": "d317fcfc-8ec5-5ce4-a3b4-ddaf4f730dce", "block_to_id": "4b794544-a5e2-5379-bfa8-fafab3c36f60", "section_path": "Hosted Api Slos Enterprise Route Tiers", "document_id": "12efb103-6e2e-5955-be3e-431b65ac2bca", "document_version_id": "78cfdc0b-41fe-5614-b19f-c7d639aaa33b", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_49fa5cfd95624dbeb6eaa535f9959470.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h1-0", "heading": "Hosted Api Slos Enterprise Route Tiers", "content": "Hosted Api Slos Enterprise Route Tiers\\n\\nSource type: confluence\\nDocument ID: dsid_49fa5cfd95624dbeb6eaa535f9959470\\nRelease: v1.0.0\\nBenchmark: EnterpriseRAG-Bench synthetic upstream data\\nHosted API SLOs: Enterprise Route Tiers (Hot-route capacity protection)", "score": 0.506078, "rank": 82, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "4ca0acae-f5f5-56d8-99ec-9ea26a528585", "search_unit_id": "4ca0acae-f5f5-56d8-99ec-9ea26a528585", "block_from_id": "d4f780a7-3c72-5e6e-81f7-5c439b0f3d47", "block_to_id": "121de8c0-61c4-5ff8-90ad-ad8a51ce21e8", "section_path": "Overload Errors And Retry Guidance > Common customer questions + approved responses > \xe2\x80\x9cShould I fail over to another model/region?\xe2\x80\x9d", "document_id": "d1667e56-b0c3-5fb4-a769-9f13a8679e2f", "document_version_id": "a9986e4a-2cf0-5373-a739-d5611a7a824c", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_ca42a8f18d784c879c5a6fcfe3a484c0.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-59", "heading": "Overload Errors And Retry Guidance > Common customer questions + approved responses > \xe2\x80\x9cShould I fail over to another model/region?\xe2\x80\x9d", "content": "\xe2\x80\x9cShould I fail over to another model/region?\xe2\x80\x9d\\n\\nGuidance:\\n\\n- If they have **fallback routing configured** (Dedicated/enterprise Hosted tiers or configured routing policies), yes\xe2\x80\x94recommend they enable/verify it.\\n- Otherwise, advise them to implement client-side fallback only if they can validate output compatibility and safety.", "score": 0.408558, "rank": 83, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "cdbb6d08-8ba1-5356-89c6-5f1be0d7a0d6", "search_unit_id": "cdbb6d08-8ba1-5356-89c6-5f1be0d7a0d6", "block_from_id": "465c7502-6eb1-50f3-862d-75e9129549d1", "block_to_id": "05603d51-0610-5c82-a53a-43ee96ba9c3e", "section_path": "Overload Errors And Retry Guidance > Escalation template (copy/paste)", "document_id": "d1667e56-b0c3-5fb4-a769-9f13a8679e2f", "document_version_id": "a9986e4a-2cf0-5373-a739-d5611a7a824c", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_ca42a8f18d784c879c5a6fcfe3a484c0.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-75", "heading": "Overload Errors And Retry Guidance > Escalation template (copy/paste)", "content": "Escalation template (copy/paste)\\n\\nSubject: Hosted API overload errors \xe2\x80\x93 customer impact\\n\\n- Customer / tenant: \\n- Tier: (Self-serve Hosted / Enterprise Hosted / Dedicated)\\n- Primary route(s): (e.g., /v1/chat/completions)\\n- Model(s): \\n- Region(s): requested / observed\\n- Time window (with timezone): \\n- Error HTTP status: 429 / 503\\n- Error code(s) from body: \\n- Retry-After present? value(s): \\n- x-redwood-correlation-id(s): \\n- x-redwood-request-id(s): \\n- Customer retry behavior (describe): \\n- Business impact: (prod down / degraded / batch delay)\\n- Attachments: sample responses (headers + body), client logs", "score": 0.364806, "rank": 84, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "027545ed-544d-59a4-ac84-be54d2a402a7", "search_unit_id": "027545ed-544d-59a4-ac84-be54d2a402a7", "block_from_id": "ec70ec29-2014-565d-af3f-a4647a389fab", "block_to_id": "199d7ca2-70e2-5a0c-bc52-0dbf99c4216f", "section_path": "Hosted Api Slos Enterprise Route Tiers > Error budgets > Budget stop-the-line triggers", "document_id": "12efb103-6e2e-5955-be3e-431b65ac2bca", "document_version_id": "78cfdc0b-41fe-5614-b19f-c7d639aaa33b", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_49fa5cfd95624dbeb6eaa535f9959470.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-65", "heading": "Hosted Api Slos Enterprise Route Tiers > Error budgets > Budget stop-the-line triggers", "content": "Budget stop-the-line triggers\\n\\nFor enterprise protected routes, any of the following triggers a \xe2\x80\x9cstop the line\xe2\x80\x9d review in the weekly reliability sync (or async in #eng-sre if urgent):\\n\\n- Availability error budget burn \xe2\x89\xa5 **50%** in 7 days\\n- p99 latency SLO violated for \xe2\x89\xa5 **2 hours** in a day (sustained)\\n- Overload shedding observed for enterprise traffic (non-zero sustained) outside planned game day / load test windows", "score": 0.340901, "rank": 85, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "94f8473e-6fa7-5ca7-b28d-fd0d06dc1ff1", "search_unit_id": "94f8473e-6fa7-5ca7-b28d-fd0d06dc1ff1", "block_from_id": "5924c214-0cba-5898-8186-88e78be523d2", "block_to_id": "f7410cc1-70a0-522d-ae36-40ed819db9ab", "section_path": "Hosted Api Slos Enterprise Route Tiers > Alerting (paging + ticketing) > Overload protection operational alerts", "document_id": "12efb103-6e2e-5955-be3e-431b65ac2bca", "document_version_id": "78cfdc0b-41fe-5614-b19f-c7d639aaa33b", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_49fa5cfd95624dbeb6eaa535f9959470.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-77", "heading": "Hosted Api Slos Enterprise Route Tiers > Alerting (paging + ticketing) > Overload protection operational alerts", "content": "Overload protection operational alerts\\n\\nThese are predictive/guardrail alerts. Configure as:\\n\\n- **Page (Sev2):** enterprise overload shedding sustained\\n  - enterprise `shed_rate` > **0.1%** for **10 minutes** (any protected route)\\n- **Ticket:** best-effort shedding unexpectedly high at low utilization\\n  - best-effort `shed_rate` > **20%** for **15 minutes** AND GPU utilization < **65%** (indicates policy mis-tuning or signal errors)\\n- **Ticket:** queue depth / scheduler lag sustained without corresponding shedding\\n  - queue depth > threshold for **10 minutes** with `admission_control_active=false` (indicates missing trigger wiring)", "score": 0.347411, "rank": 86, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "708e5a9c-86f5-506e-8da1-295220bce219", "search_unit_id": "708e5a9c-86f5-506e-8da1-295220bce219", "block_from_id": "4161f767-6da3-52a1-88f6-d87da4574795", "block_to_id": "b9fa1aed-e707-55e1-8810-924abf1845c1", "section_path": "Overload Errors And Retry Guidance > Quick triage checklist (Support)", "document_id": "d1667e56-b0c3-5fb4-a769-9f13a8679e2f", "document_version_id": "a9986e4a-2cf0-5373-a739-d5611a7a824c", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_ca42a8f18d784c879c5a6fcfe3a484c0.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-12", "heading": "Overload Errors And Retry Guidance > Quick triage checklist (Support)", "content": "Quick triage checklist (Support)\\n\\n1) Confirm this is an overload-protection response (see \xe2\x80\x9cHow to recognize\xe2\x80\x9d below).\\n2) Verify the customer is following recommended retry/backoff (or advise them to change).\\n3) Collect required debug info (IDs, time window, region/model, response headers).\\n4) Determine if this is expected transient overload vs a bug/misconfig (missing Retry-After, incorrect status mapping, fallback not triggering).\\n5) Escalate to Eng Oncall when criteria are met (see \xe2\x80\x9cWhen to escalate\xe2\x80\x9d).", "score": 0.328833, "rank": 87, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "aa0f59b2-aca1-5600-bb3d-4cf5046b5503", "search_unit_id": "aa0f59b2-aca1-5600-bb3d-4cf5046b5503", "block_from_id": "cf85636a-e739-574b-8011-19c00953672a", "block_to_id": "08f43229-8e9e-508c-aade-f7961cd4576d", "section_path": "Hosted Api Slos Enterprise Route Tiers > Alerting (paging + ticketing) > Enterprise availability burn alerts (recommended)", "document_id": "12efb103-6e2e-5955-be3e-431b65ac2bca", "document_version_id": "78cfdc0b-41fe-5614-b19f-c7d639aaa33b", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_49fa5cfd95624dbeb6eaa535f9959470.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-71", "heading": "Hosted Api Slos Enterprise Route Tiers > Alerting (paging + ticketing) > Enterprise availability burn alerts (recommended)", "content": "Enterprise availability burn alerts (recommended)\\n\\nFor each protected route x region:\\n\\n- **Page (Sev2):** 28d SLO burn rate with multi-window thresholds\\n  - Fast burn: 5m and 1h windows > **14x** budget burn\\n  - Slow burn: 30m and 6h windows > **6x** budget burn\\n- **Ticket:** 2h and 1d windows > **2x** burn", "score": 0.312899, "rank": 88, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "ced36279-cc11-5c4d-8eac-bc2d66b3503c", "search_unit_id": "ced36279-cc11-5c4d-8eac-bc2d66b3503c", "block_from_id": "bcc637d9-40d0-5e94-b04b-555981b6ceeb", "block_to_id": "650f9b93-6af2-505d-9998-28cbbeb5d4ea", "section_path": "Policy Engine Failover Extensions Draft", "document_id": "d6d26fd7-a1c4-5594-b8e3-2aa73c8f448d", "document_version_id": "5db22b04-2f5e-53d8-8bae-5ef192a1c767", "document_name": "google_drive__dsid_184be937d34a412ab5e61366d54d8ed6.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "list-67", "heading": "Policy Engine Failover Extensions Draft", "content": "- Exact shape of \xe2\x80\x9ctarget_state\xe2\x80\x9d string: should it be a controller-owned serialization of desired weights, or should the policy engine output high-level intent only?\\n- Do we want PARTIAL_SHIFT as a first-class decision type (recommended), or represent it as FAILOVER with weight < 100%?\\n- How strict should corroboration be for tail latency burn? (ADR-042 indicates corroboration required; we need the exact default set.)\\n- Where should data residency constraints live?\\n  - Option A: policy engine validates \xe2\x80\x9cregion set allowed\xe2\x80\x9d and blocks action.\\n  - Option B: upstream policy compilation prevents invalid eligible_regions.\\n\\nNear-term next steps\\n\\n- Align with Miles/Ravi on canonical signal enum + reason enum.\\n- Draft schema PR for policy config additions (behind feature flag).\\n- Implement deterministic ordering + evidence output in policy engine.\\n- Wire to dry-run mode (ENG-2415) so the controller can display \xe2\x80\x9crecommended action + confidence + evidence\xe2\x80\x9d on game day.\\n\\nAppendix: candidate enums (WIP)\\nchosen_reason\\n\\n- REACHABILITY_DOWN\\n- ERROR_BURN_FAST\\n- LATENCY_BURN_SUSTAINED\\n- CAPACITY_HARD_GATE\\n- SIGNALS_STALE\\n- HOLD_DOWN_ACTIVE\\n- FLIP_BUDGET_EXCEEDED\\n- CONSTRAINT_VIOLATION_DATA_RESIDENCY\\n- NO_HEALTHY_FALLBACK\\n\\nsignal_type\\n\\n- REACHABILITY\\n- ERRORS_5XX_BURN\\n- TAIL_LATENCY_BURN\\n- CAPACITY_HEADROOM\\n- CONTROL_PLANE_HEALTH", "score": 0.290984, "rank": 89, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "ff3757e1-0f21-5dd7-aba5-64ae45c41dc1", "search_unit_id": "ff3757e1-0f21-5dd7-aba5-64ae45c41dc1", "block_from_id": "a3ec1d56-3a0f-5ebe-8586-0bd60428ded1", "block_to_id": "fce94957-09da-5f78-a49c-7776db4c356e", "section_path": "Hosted Api Slos Enterprise Route Tiers > Error budgets > Error budget calculation", "document_id": "12efb103-6e2e-5955-be3e-431b65ac2bca", "document_version_id": "78cfdc0b-41fe-5614-b19f-c7d639aaa33b", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_49fa5cfd95624dbeb6eaa535f9959470.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-52", "heading": "Hosted Api Slos Enterprise Route Tiers > Error budgets > Error budget calculation", "content": "Error budgets\\n\\nError budget calculation\\n\\nFor an SLO target **T** over a 28-day window:\\n\\n- Error budget = **1 \xe2\x88\x92 T**\\n\\nExamples:\\n\\n- 99.95% availability \xe2\x87\x92 0.05% error budget (\xe2\x89\x88 21.6 minutes of downtime equivalent over 28 days)\\n- 99.5% availability \xe2\x87\x92 0.5% error budget\\n\\nWe track budgets separately per:\\n\\n- route\\n- region\\n- tier", "score": 0.288152, "rank": 90, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "1bed7f84-10e9-5901-9e71-655b5a96d238", "search_unit_id": "1bed7f84-10e9-5901-9e71-655b5a96d238", "block_from_id": "de04aadd-8eb6-52aa-babb-9e97778ad93a", "block_to_id": "5fb120e4-395a-5358-8250-00d3116fd776", "section_path": "Hosted Api Slos Enterprise Route Tiers > Alerting (paging + ticketing) > Enterprise latency alerts", "document_id": "12efb103-6e2e-5955-be3e-431b65ac2bca", "document_version_id": "78cfdc0b-41fe-5614-b19f-c7d639aaa33b", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_49fa5cfd95624dbeb6eaa535f9959470.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-74", "heading": "Hosted Api Slos Enterprise Route Tiers > Alerting (paging + ticketing) > Enterprise latency alerts", "content": "Enterprise latency alerts\\n\\nFor each protected route x region:\\n\\n- **Page (Sev2):** p99 latency SLO violated for **15 minutes** AND admission control active (or queue depth high)\\n- **Ticket:** p95 latency SLO violated for **60 minutes**", "score": 0.304482, "rank": 91, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}], "events": [], "entities": [], "relations": [], "source_hits": [], "summary": "MedThink specified the following failover sequence and recovery targets for handling an EU region outage:\\n\\n- **Preferred failover hierarchy:** EU primary -> EU warm standby -> US emergency failover.\\n- **Cross-region failover to US:** Permitted only for declared emergency windows, with a maximum of 4 hours, and requires pre-approval in the runbook.\\n- **RPO (Recovery Point Objective):** 15 minutes for active datasets.\\n- **RTO (Recovery Time Objective):** 30 minutes for critical APIs.\\n\\nAdditionally, the following constraints apply:\\n\\n- **Logs & telemetry:** Logs may contain limited PII (hashed patient IDs and occasional email addresses). Redaction is expected at ingest, and hashed IDs are acceptable if the hash keys are kept on-region. Default operational logs are retained for 90 days, and audit logs for 3 years. Long-term archival to a secure archive is possible after 90 days, but must be on-region for PHI.\\n- **Backups:** Backups of PHI can be stored in the US if encrypted with customer-managed keys and access is restricted to named personnel only. Otherwise, they must stay in the EU. Cross-region incremental copies are allowed for analytics (non-PHI) or encrypted/full-access restricted backups with CMK.\\n- **Key management:** Prefer CMK (KMS) for PHI datasets. Monthly HSM audit extracts are required if HSM is used.\\n- **Audit evidence:** SOC 2 Type II report, access log exports (filtered to the MedThink account), key rotation logs, and one sample sanitized query/log bundle showing redaction are required.\\n\\nThe evidence is derived from [1] and [31].", "citations": [{"kind": "internal", "n": 1, "document_id": "4da40c19-70f8-5526-806a-febdeb4668cd", "document_version_id": "521fe3cb-72a4-5a06-9a90-f3cf0d2048aa", "document_name": "gmail__dsid_8e838ab6a98f4cbcb672d41f210ff89c.md", "version_no": 1, "chunk_id": "f7a34025-fd17-527c-9568-3a2625b0f6a0", "search_unit_id": "f7a34025-fd17-527c-9568-3a2625b0f6a0", "block_from_id": "814bed88-9888-557d-819c-e901145c8363", "block_to_id": "0aeb5b03-c680-5a65-b64d-f9b033358da9", "section_path": "20280503 Region Fallback Priority Ops Inventory", "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "list-12", "heading": "20280503 Region Fallback Priority Ops Inventory", "snippet": "- Patient clinical records (PHI) must remain in-region (EU) for EU patients. - Operational metadata (service-level telemetry that does not include patient-identifiers) can be replicated to US for analytics if pseudonymized and access controlled. - Backups of PHI: acceptable to store in US if encrypted with customer-managed keys and access is restricted to named personnel only \xe2\x80\x94 otherwise must stay in EU. 2) Failover order and cross-region replication: - Preferred failover hierarchy: EU primary -> EU warm standby -> US emergency failover. - Cross-region failover to US is permitted only for declared emergency windows (max 4 hours), must be pre-approved in runbook. - Target RPO 15 minutes for active datasets; RTO\xe2\x80\xa6", "score": 0.6541, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"kind": "internal", "n": 31, "document_id": "4da40c19-70f8-5526-806a-febdeb4668cd", "document_version_id": "521fe3cb-72a4-5a06-9a90-f3cf0d2048aa", "document_name": "gmail__dsid_8e838ab6a98f4cbcb672d41f210ff89c.md", "version_no": 1, "chunk_id": "7d9c597e-d7a3-583c-8789-c62d6e710ac2", "search_unit_id": "7d9c597e-d7a3-583c-8789-c62d6e710ac2", "block_from_id": "28e9e867-e360-5a0a-800c-84ed79a67e0f", "block_to_id": "299c6adc-0d7e-5285-bc7b-beda7a5ca627", "section_path": "20280503 Region Fallback Priority Ops Inventory", "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "p-30", "heading": "20280503 Region Fallback Priority Ops Inventory", "snippet": "If that all sounds good I\xe2\x80\x99ll mark the deal record in HubSpot with the scheduled deep-dive and next-step tasks. Best, Rafael Senior AE, Redwood Inference On Fri, May 3, 2028 at 3:22 PM Rafael Mendes <rafael.mendes@redwoodinference.com> wrote: > Thanks for the call earlier, Elena \xe2\x80\x94 good alignment on the high-level constraints. Per our discussion, I wanted to capture a short inventory of the items we need to confirm so we can scope a targeted technical deep-dive next week. I attached a simple diagram and an ops inventory CSV template to speed things up. > > Action items / clarifying questions for MedThink (please reply inline if easier): > 1) Residency / pinning: which datasets must remain in-region (EU-only / US-\xe2\x80\xa6", "score": 0.4779, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}], "answer_status": "answered", "no_answer_reason": null, "exploration_id": null, "stats": {"canonical_index": true, "ready_versions": 81, "requested_top_k": null, "candidate_top_k": 64, "candidate_unit_pool_limit": 1024, "candidate_pool_saturated": true, "candidate_units_before_cap": 152, "candidate_units_after_cap": 152, "candidate_units_truncated": 0, "semantic_candidates": 87, "lexical_candidates": 82, "candidates": 152, "relevant": 152, "filtered_irrelevant": 0, "fusion_method": "rrf", "selection_method": "authorized_content_dedup_mmr", "cross_scope_merge": "rank_interleave", "coverage": {"candidate_count": 128, "deduplicated_count": 0, "diversity_weight": 0.5, "near_duplicate_similarity": 0.98, "required_anchor_count": 0, "covered_anchor_count": 0, "anchor_coverage": "not_required", "status": "unknown", "canonical_locator_verified": true, "semantic_answerability": "unknown"}, "routing": {"planner": {"planner_version": "qsp-v1", "requested_strategy": "AUTO", "effective_strategy": "LOCAL_FACTUAL", "modifiers": [], "reason_codes": ["DEFAULT_LOCAL_FACTUAL"], "multi_hop_eligible": false}, "request_snapshot_id": "2d3ed491-5e18-4fc3-b35e-8aff3b3ecc11", "groups": [{"project_id": "b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c", "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "partition_id": "b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c", "snapshot_id": "8eba35e6-37cc-4e36-8360-085dff7dbd5f", "request_snapshot_id": "2d3ed491-5e18-4fc3-b35e-8aff3b3ecc11", "acl_scope_fingerprint": "328ac326f64690733d385248a99659bc5ed25e83991108887c7a3367d2d5c51e", "tree_version": "tree-50bdd85ee0f1111bfecc7840", "routing_slot": "SLOT_A", "search_epoch": 2, "selected_nodes": ["56053360af7bd0c00b3c23b570340db9", "d48df15e10c1588c77a8ea414162a6c5", "dc5e9d2b3217fb92f90abc62415f1131"], "membership_count": 168, "entropy": 0.9997313777093949, "margin": 0.014212597443833963, "broad_route": true, "reason_code": "ROUTE_UNCERTAIN_BROADENED", "fallback_reason": null, "branch_local_candidates": 113, "global_candidates": 118, "escape_recovered_candidates": 39, "escape_attempted": true, "escape_trigger": "reserved_parallel_global_escape", "local_failure": null, "escape_failure": null, "blackhole_detected": false}], "coverage": {"candidate_count": 128, "deduplicated_count": 0, "diversity_weight": 0.5, "near_duplicate_similarity": 0.98, "required_anchor_count": 0, "covered_anchor_count": 0, "anchor_coverage": "not_required", "status": "unknown", "canonical_locator_verified": true, "semantic_answerability": "unknown"}, "selection_fallback_reason": null, "multi_hop": {"eligible": false, "effective": "LOCAL_FACTUAL", "graph_expansion_attempted": false, "graph_expanded_candidates": 0, "graph_expansion_skip_reason": null}, "fallback_used": true}, "selection_fallback_reason": null, "stage_latencies_ms": {"auth_scope": 43.29, "tree_route": 1073.35, "candidate_retrieval": 2870.83, "evidence_hydration": 38.44, "rank_fusion": 120.77000000000001, "graph_expansion": 0.0, "diversity_selection": 7378.639999999999, "total_retrieval": 11545.33}, "latency_total_ms": 11545.33, "automatic_top