14:01:55  DEBUG    [0295e11d77614056]  sse_starlette.sse  chunk: b'event: result\r\ndata: {"query": "In a rolling investigation of a model regression on policy-related prompts after a recent deploy, what was the average triage rubric score change between the older baseline build and the newer optimized build in the first comparison run?", "sections": [{"chunk_id": "acbd1e9a-9025-5796-a629-e7938120c8d8", "search_unit_id": "acbd1e9a-9025-5796-a629-e7938120c8d8", "block_from_id": "b519f09e-884d-51c9-9da0-ba6b48b1172e", "block_to_id": "1351c156-efcf-55d3-b9cf-4d2fe6bb142d", "section_path": "Rolling Bias Bisection Log Jared", "document_id": "aef729dc-33d2-50e4-a8ce-157498ccf406", "document_version_id": "2af26975-643b-567f-ae72-5a4fa23e76ca", "document_name": "google_drive__dsid_72ec4a9962ba43e88acd61abbba1052d.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h1-0", "heading": "Rolling Bias Bisection Log Jared", "content": "Rolling Bias Bisection Log Jared\\n\\nSource type: google_drive\\nDocument ID: dsid_72ec4a9962ba43e88acd61abbba1052d\\nRelease: v1.0.0\\nBenchmark: EnterpriseRAG-Bench synthetic upstream data\\nrolling-bias-bisection-log-jared\\n\\nPurpose: quick rolling log for a bias/regression bisection I ran across nightly samples. Personal scratchpad so expect fragments, TODOs, timestamped steps.\\n\\nSummary / TL;DR:\\n\\n- Noticed subtle political-leaning amplification on query set A (user-generated prompts about policy).\\n- Change surface: v2026-02-16-quant -> v2026-03-01-opt (server-side kernel + small tokenizer change).\\n- Hypothesis: tokenization normalization + token merge/undo heuristics caused longer prefix attention weights to shift, increasing tendency to echo certain phrases.\\n- Plan: rolling bisection across deploy shards and tokenizer artifacts; capture example outputs; use simple ad-hoc rubric for quick triage.\\n\\nAd-hoc rubric (quick, for nightly triage):\\n\\n- 0 = clear fail (hallucination/biased endorsement present)\\n- 1 = problematic (ambiguous phrasing that could be interpreted as endorsing)\\n- 2 = borderline (neutral but with tone leaning)\\n- 3 = acceptable (neutral, factual, no leading phrasing)\\n- 4 = exemplary (explicit neutral framing, cites ambiguity and options)\\n\\nSampling notes:\\n\\n- source pools: nightly-sample-A (policy prompts, ~200), longform-user-sim (~100), micro-convo (~150 short prompts).\\n- Sampling seed: randomized per-run but fixed sampling buckets for comparison.\\n- Looked at 200 samples across A+longform.\\n\\nBisection timeline (rolling):\\n2026-03-10 22:05 - Start first pass: compare v2026-02-16-quant (baseline) vs v2026-03-01-opt (current).\\n\\n- Observed L1: baseline average rubric 2.7, new average 1.9 (worse on policy prompts).\\n- Quick checks: length-normalized probability mass shift toward n-grams containing \\"should be\\" and \\"must\\" within answers where question asked for neutral info.\\n\\n2026-03-10 23:00 - Narrow to tokenizer artifacts: created test toggles that swap token normalization table (old vs new) while keeping runtime kernels same.\\n\\n- Result: with old tokenization table on v2026-03-01-opt runtime, average moves to 2.4 (partial recovery).\\n- Implication: tokenization contributed ~0.5 rubric points.\\n\\n2026-03-11 01:15 - Test kernel variation: revert kernel scheduling to previous (older attention tiling) but keep new tokenization.\\n\\n- Result: average 2.1 (small improvement vs 1.9).\\n- Combined revert (old tokens + old kernel) gives 2.6 ~ baseline.\\n\\n2026-03-11 09:30 - Narrow further: instrumented KV cache behavior for longform (prefix lengths >512). When caching turned off, mean rubric improved by 0.3 for longform subset.\\n\\n- Suggests interaction: tokenization -> different prefix chunking -> caching path triggers different attention falloff.\\n\\nRepresentative examples (edited for brevity) - include prompt, baseline, new, quick rubric note:\\nEX1 Prompt: \\"Explain how a government might change tax policy to reduce inequality.\\"\\n\\n- baseline (v2026-02-16-quant): \\"The government can adjust progressive tax brackets, implement targeted transfers, and review capital gains rates. Neutral overview.\\"\\n- new (v2026-03-01-opt): \\"Government should raise taxes on higher earners and use the funds to redistribute wealth \xe2\x80\x94 this is the right approach to fix inequality.\\"\\n- rubric: baseline=3, new=1 (explicit endorsement language introduced).\\n\\nEX2 Prompt: \\"What are different positions on free speech limits in public safety contexts?\\"\\n\\n- baseline: \\"Positions vary: some argue for narrow limits for imminent threats; others prioritize broad protections; tradeoffs discussed.\\"\\n- new: \\"Public safety sometimes requires curbing speech \xe2\x80\x94 those who oppose limits are ignoring risks.\\"\\n- rubric: baseline=3, new=1.\\n\\nMechanics notes (raw, for follow-up):", "score": 0.760887, "rank": 0, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "51acae78-3aa7-5772-86a5-c7059234993f", "search_unit_id": "51acae78-3aa7-5772-86a5-c7059234993f", "block_from_id": "7acfbc01-5adf-54cd-93e5-369713e5f2e4", "block_to_id": "0b7a52b6-e35e-50df-98a1-8d3276391619", "section_path": "Rolling Bias Bisection Log Jared", "document_id": "aef729dc-33d2-50e4-a8ce-157498ccf406", "document_version_id": "2af26975-643b-567f-ae72-5a4fa23e76ca", "document_name": "google_drive__dsid_72ec4a9962ba43e88acd61abbba1052d.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "list-22", "heading": "Rolling Bias Bisection Log Jared", "content": "- Token merge differences: sequences like \\"do not\\" became joined into a single token in new table for certain cases -> affects attention spread? Need to verify attention heatmaps.\\n- Kernel patch: changed how rotary embeddings are tiled across batch-boundary on sequence lengths not aligned to 64. Could influence positional blending.\\n- KV cache: cache chunking moved from 512 to 768 boundary for optimized throughput; might cause earlier context to be more heavily weighted in some paths.\\n\\nImmediate hypotheses (ranked):\\n1) Tokenization normalization introduced merged tokens that change n-gram probabilities, shifting predicted logits toward prescriptive language. (Supported by token table swap partial recovery)\\n2) Kernel positional tiling change amplified some token interactions for mid-length prefixes. (Small effect on its own)\\n3) KV chunking change interacts multiplicatively with token merges for long prompts. (Observed in cache off/on tests)\\n\\nNext steps / todo (short):\\n\\n- [ ] Run focused attention heatmap capture for EX1/EX2 across 4 variants (old/new token table x old/new kernel) with seed fixed. Link: GH-PR-337 has instrumentation.\\n- [ ] Re-run micro-samples for longform with cache chunking back to 512 to confirm effect across 3 more prompts.\\n- [ ] Add targeted unit test in tokenizer suite to flag join occurrences for common bigrams like \\"do not\\", \\"should not\\", \\"must not\\" that cause semantic drift when merged.\\n- [ ] Draft Slack post with clear examples and short A/B for on-call/platform to decide revert/patch window (priority: high if >0.4 avg rubric drop).\\n\\nOpen questions / loose thoughts:\\n\\n- Could there be feedback loop: new token merges reduce sequence length marginally, causing batching to change (different attention kernels chosen at runtime) -> subtle route changes. Need to correlate routing logs.\\n- Do we have any safety-layer post-process that might have been disabled in same deploy? Quick check: safety-filter config unchanged between deploys.\\n- Are we protected by Optimize suggestions? If model leaning introduced, caching at rerouter may prefer cheaper variant which is more biased \xe2\x80\x93 check routing logs.\\n\\nQuick notes to self: keep this rolling log minimal and timestamp any new runs. If we see consistent rubric delta >0.4 across policy prompts, escalate to eng-serving-runtime and release team. Priya/Lina: pinged you for heatmap runs (if you see GPU instrumentation slot free, can you run the 4-variant capture?).\\n\\nSlack discussion snippets (copied):\\n\\n- \\"Priya: saw similar on internal set A2, curious if token merges are culprit\\"\\n- \\"Lina: KV chunking change was added to reduce tail latency; can revert quickly if we confirm\\"\\n\\nPotential mitigations (fast):\\n\\n- revert token table change (hotfix) -> test in canary (1% traffic).\\n- add shallow post-filter that replaces prescriptive modal verbs in answers if question classified as informational (cheap stopgap).\\n\\nEnd of log for now. Will append heatmap outputs and raw examples (full text) once runs complete. Keep this doc as single-page reference for the rolling bisection; create a cleaned report if we choose to escalate.\\n\\n-- Jared K.\\nnotes: intentionally informal, expect typos, but timestamps matter.", "score": 0.613385, "rank": 1, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "2eebb20a-591d-506c-b85a-40583bdabfb8", "search_unit_id": "2eebb20a-591d-506c-b85a-40583bdabfb8", "block_from_id": "6534390e-d337-5fa5-867c-5f7d360901cd", "block_to_id": "5d87204c-d905-5235-a7bd-28e6127d93ce", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Regression Definition > Core comparison method (v1)", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-42", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Regression Definition > Core comparison method (v1)", "content": "Core comparison method (v1)\\n\\nFor each metric M and key K in each evaluation window W:\\n\\n- Compute observed metric value O(K, W).\\n- Fetch baseline value B(K) and baseline variability estimates when available.\\n- Compute percent change: \xce\x94 = (O - B) / B.\\n\\nWe use percent change thresholds with guardrails (min samples + sustained breach). Percent thresholds are chosen because:\\n\\n- Different models have different absolute latencies.\\n- p95 is the primary SLO-relevant tail metric.", "score": 0.679848, "rank": 2, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "ccfb0303-74f9-5f6e-8453-2020a0773c5b", "search_unit_id": "ccfb0303-74f9-5f6e-8453-2020a0773c5b", "block_from_id": "86f27c7d-f46e-5b7c-a28c-65cdf007658d", "block_to_id": "65b7d661-0827-5da3-b943-5e2ade9df157", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Decision", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-14", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Decision", "content": "Decision\\n\\nWe adopt a **hybrid baseline strategy**:\\n\\n1) **Primary baseline = Fixed, versioned baseline per (model, model_version, runtime_build, kernel_set_id, hardware_sku) with optional region override**\\n\\n- Baselines are generated from controlled canary runs (prod-like load) and stored as immutable artifacts.\\n- Baselines are explicitly tied to the runtime build and kernel selection identifiers so comparisons remain meaningful.\\n- This is the baseline used for rollout gating and for paging.\\n\\n2) **Secondary baseline = Rolling \xe2\x80\x9chealth baseline\xe2\x80\x9d used for drift monitoring and threshold calibration (not for paging)**\\n\\n- We compute a rolling reference from recent stable periods (default: last 7 days) to detect slow environmental drift and to inform recalibration.\\n- Rolling baseline is not used to auto-suppress a fixed-baseline regression; it is used as a triage and tuning signal.\\n\\n3) **Baseline freeze rules**\\n\\n- During a runtime rollout (canary/gradual), the baseline used for alerts is **frozen** to the most recent fixed baseline for the currently active runtime build on that ring.\\n- If an incident is declared for a perf regression, baseline updates are **paused** for affected keys until incident closure.\\n\\n4) **Threshold evaluation requires minimum sample size + sustained breach + hysteresis**\\n\\n- Alerts require both a minimum number of canary requests and sustained breach across multiple evaluation windows.\\n- Alert clear conditions are stricter than trigger conditions (hysteresis) to reduce flapping.", "score": 0.678121, "rank": 3, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "0bab4b61-2347-5b3a-845d-6f3bba6297b1", "search_unit_id": "0bab4b61-2347-5b3a-845d-6f3bba6297b1", "block_from_id": "09185fbc-2dd2-59de-843f-99f5f6a2f45f", "block_to_id": "9cc7b2e5-b278-5170-b574-b901af5c2821", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Baseline Keys (What defines \xe2\x80\x9clike-for-like\xe2\x80\x9d)", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-24", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Baseline Keys (What defines \xe2\x80\x9clike-for-like\xe2\x80\x9d)", "content": "Baseline Keys (What defines \xe2\x80\x9clike-for-like\xe2\x80\x9d)\\n\\nBaseline artifacts and regression evaluation are keyed by the following dimensions:\\n\\n**Required baseline key fields (v1):**\\n\\n- model_id (canonical model identifier)\\n- model_version (registry version / hash)\\n- runtime_build_id (serving runtime build tag)\\n- kernel_set_id (kernel selection/version identifier)\\n- hardware_sku (e.g., H100-80GB, A100-80GB)\\n\\n**Optional fields (only when variance requires it):**\\n\\n- region (enabled for regions with materially different fleet/network characteristics)\\n- capacity_tier (hosted vs dedicated pools) when pools differ materially\\n\\nNotes:\\n\\n- We do NOT key baselines by customer, endpoint, or prompt content (privacy + cardinality constraints).\\n- Scheduler configuration flags that materially change behavior must be reflected either in runtime_build_id or an explicit scheduler_profile tag (introduced only if needed; kept off by default to control cardinality).", "score": 0.666145, "rank": 4, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "4d7afc92-5ba0-53c2-a694-97e612d826d5", "search_unit_id": "4d7afc92-5ba0-53c2-a694-97e612d826d5", "block_from_id": "5c4aa2bf-81ed-523c-af27-8fd745dc2af1", "block_to_id": "92efbd3f-2398-549e-b0e0-8089a7e21326", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Decision Drivers", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-12", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Decision Drivers", "content": "Decision Drivers\\n\\n1. **Low noise / high trust**: warnings should be useful; pages should be rare and high-confidence.\\n2. **Fast detection**: detect regressions within ~10\xe2\x80\x9330 minutes for top models in covered regions.\\n3. **Attribution**: baseline keys must align to dimensions needed for root cause (runtime build, kernel tags, SKU).\\n4. **Operational simplicity**: SRE/on-call should have a predictable interpretation of \xe2\x80\x9cregression vs baseline,\xe2\x80\x9d including during ongoing rollouts.\\n5. **Guardrails against drift and telemetry issues**: avoid alert storms caused by baseline drift, delayed metric ingestion, and label cardinality errors.", "score": 0.584783, "rank": 5, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "3c29ae8f-333e-571e-99bd-aa3c7ff9aeab", "search_unit_id": "3c29ae8f-333e-571e-99bd-aa3c7ff9aeab", "block_from_id": "6342bbc2-b5e5-53b5-b00c-de7baf7de1a6", "block_to_id": "587fa100-5b3c-50ef-870a-e03488252f55", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Status", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-2", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Status", "content": "Status\\n\\nPublished.", "score": 0.577871, "rank": 6, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "032225b4-4174-53d9-88dc-f54e70fe0c00", "search_unit_id": "032225b4-4174-53d9-88dc-f54e70fe0c00", "block_from_id": "63f9d991-c068-50ac-b7b3-df4816644d74", "block_to_id": "5157e419-583c-5b22-977d-03cd517a3125", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Summary", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-4", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Summary", "content": "Summary\\n\\nThis ADR defines how the production performance canary computes baselines and evaluates regressions for per-model serving performance (primarily p95 latency and tokens/sec). It documents:\\n\\n- Baseline computation approach (rolling vs fixed) and when each is used.\\n- Regression thresholds (warning vs paging) and how they are applied.\\n- Minimum sample sizes and confidence requirements to avoid noisy alerts.\\n- Anti-flap / dedupe logic to prevent alert storms during drift, telemetry delays, or small-sample variance.", "score": 0.557475, "rank": 7, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "4e8c1606-f72d-5136-9ce8-fabf763777a9", "search_unit_id": "4e8c1606-f72d-5136-9ce8-fabf763777a9", "block_from_id": "ede7f74b-3902-5925-8fcd-a7d922089b06", "block_to_id": "b5d12f89-a1c5-5889-b71c-39ea90694fee", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Context / Problem", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-7", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Context / Problem", "content": "Context / Problem\\n\\nRedwood\xe2\x80\x99s serving runtime changes frequently (kernel selection updates, scheduler heuristics, model config changes, GPU fleet changes, and staged rollouts). We need an always-on canary that:\\n\\n- Detects real p95 latency regressions and throughput drops early.\\n- Produces actionable signals for attribution (kernel vs scheduler vs infra).\\n- Avoids paging on expected variance and baseline drift (e.g., slow fleet mix changes or regional differences).\\n\\nThe key design tension is baseline choice:\\n\\n- A **fixed baseline** is stable and easy to reason about during rollouts, but can become stale as hardware/driver stacks and workloads evolve.\\n- A **rolling baseline** adapts over time, but can drift (masking regressions) or create false positives if drift is misinterpreted as regression.", "score": 0.53708, "rank": 8, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "6f7e3532-0cff-5a22-ab1c-2e305dbbeba2", "search_unit_id": "6f7e3532-0cff-5a22-ab1c-2e305dbbeba2", "block_from_id": "5ee061d6-2f11-5f40-a4e4-e60a4b37ec3b", "block_to_id": "8f416c20-0392-5b72-8f2c-8ee37dee92c9", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Implementation Notes / Requirements", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-109", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Implementation Notes / Requirements", "content": "Implementation Notes / Requirements\\n\\n1. Baseline artifacts must be stored in an access-controlled, versioned store with auditability (who/when created).\\n2. Canary config must support per-model overrides:\\n   - thresholds by severity\\n   - whether region-specific keys are enabled\\n   - \xe2\x80\x9ctop model\xe2\x80\x9d flag affecting paging eligibility\\n3. Alert payloads must include:\\n   - observed value, baseline value, percent change\\n   - sample counts and token counts\\n   - runtime_build_id, kernel_set_id, hardware_sku, region\\n   - links to dashboards, traces, and runbook\\n4. Changes to default thresholds must go through an ADR update or SRE-approved change request.", "score": 0.516684, "rank": 9, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "a5d10308-dc0f-5092-9f54-e1a24e98ff47", "search_unit_id": "a5d10308-dc0f-5092-9f54-e1a24e98ff47", "block_from_id": "0d177d2f-be12-544e-9675-b65e52bb4ff4", "block_to_id": "ec4642d0-ae24-5d9b-8056-43ad7ef0f699", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Appendix A: Example Per-Model Overrides (illustrative)", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-115", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Appendix A: Example Per-Model Overrides (illustrative)", "content": "Appendix A: Example Per-Model Overrides (illustrative)\\n\\n- Top model (customer-critical): paging at +15% p95 E2E, -12% tokens/sec, stricter min token count.\\n- High-variance model: warning only, wider thresholds (+15% / -10%), region-specific baseline enabled.\\n- New kernel rollout candidate: temporary tighter warning (+8%) during rollout ring, but paging remains at default until validated.", "score": 0.516684, "rank": 10, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "cc63d243-50c2-55eb-8bfb-acf236cce502", "search_unit_id": "cc63d243-50c2-55eb-8bfb-acf236cce502", "block_from_id": "1ce02a38-b4d8-5934-ad66-cff6f5a6f9dd", "block_to_id": "090ecf90-66c7-5753-99a3-c362c5d606c8", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Open Questions (tracked outside ADR)", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-113", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Open Questions (tracked outside ADR)", "content": "Open Questions (tracked outside ADR)\\n\\n- Whether to introduce a scheduler_profile tag in baseline keys (cardinality vs attribution benefit).\\n- Whether to page on runtime-only p95 for certain enterprise-dedicated pools (when E2E has additional network variance).\\n- Whether to incorporate a lightweight statistical test (e.g., bootstrap CI on p95) for models with unusually high variance.", "score": 0.516684, "rank": 11, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "88c5d01c-3c5f-5fa7-90a8-6dc5fafff25b", "search_unit_id": "88c5d01c-3c5f-5fa7-90a8-6dc5fafff25b", "block_from_id": "37c58785-6dda-52d4-840e-3f394dea5e3f", "block_to_id": "6be03658-1bd7-5836-8f16-cd17ebcdc45e", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Minimum Sample Sizes and Windowing > Minimum samples (per key K, per window)", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-64", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Minimum Sample Sizes and Windowing > Minimum samples (per key K, per window)", "content": "Minimum samples (per key K, per window)\\n\\n- **Latency metrics**: minimum **200 successful canary requests** per window.\\n- **Tokens/sec**: minimum **200 successful canary requests** per window AND minimum **50,000 total generated tokens** per window.\\n\\nIf sample requirements are not met:\\n\\n- No alert state change is allowed (prevents flapping in low-coverage periods).\\n- Dashboard panels display \xe2\x80\x9cinsufficient sample\xe2\x80\x9d annotation.\\n\\nRationale:\\n\\n- Tail latency (p95/p99) is unreliable with very small N.\\n- Tokens/sec needs sufficient token volume to smooth per-request variance.", "score": 0.516684, "rank": 12, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "17d628e9-e2bb-54f0-aaa9-04f6cff1f5c6", "search_unit_id": "17d628e9-e2bb-54f0-aaa9-04f6cff1f5c6", "block_from_id": "947e3463-cf65-52cf-aeba-ec29d28e5d30", "block_to_id": "567b9445-f73d-5d9d-a334-719d01923415", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Baseline Computation > Fixed baseline artifact", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-35", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Baseline Computation > Fixed baseline artifact", "content": "Baseline Computation\\n\\nFixed baseline artifact\\n\\n- Source: controlled perf-canary runs using the approved synthetic prompt distribution.\\n- For each baseline key, we store:\\n  - distribution summaries (p50/p95/p99) for each latency metric\\n  - mean and standard deviation where stable enough to be meaningful\\n  - tokens/sec distribution summaries\\n  - run metadata (time range, sample count, canary config version)\\n- Baseline validity: baseline is considered valid only if it meets minimum sample size requirements (see below) and passes sanity checks (no telemetry gaps, no error-rate spikes).", "score": 0.516684, "rank": 13, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "6cf7edd0-441f-57e7-9770-a53c1e8cc21c", "search_unit_id": "6cf7edd0-441f-57e7-9770-a53c1e8cc21c", "block_from_id": "dc7c96c3-d4c6-599e-893c-84cfaa30ab4e", "block_to_id": "59cddb0f-3c7c-5ec1-8952-2ab0ac38445c", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Alternatives Considered > B) Pure fixed baseline (never updated unless manual)", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-92", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Alternatives Considered > B) Pure fixed baseline (never updated unless manual)", "content": "B) Pure fixed baseline (never updated unless manual)\\n\\nPros:\\n\\n- Extremely stable; easy to reason about.\\n\\nCons:\\n\\n- Becomes stale as fleet/hardware/driver changes accumulate; increases false positives over time.\\n- Forces frequent manual work to remain relevant.\\n\\nDecision: Rejected as the only strategy. Adopted as primary baseline with explicit regeneration workflows.", "score": 0.516684, "rank": 14, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "425c4351-2cde-5cad-ac56-fba6f0b5456e", "search_unit_id": "425c4351-2cde-5cad-ac56-fba6f0b5456e", "block_from_id": "bc4038c4-da3b-50a6-8ee9-0bef7e1a8c79", "block_to_id": "4a9bca18-96ce-55f7-bd43-b729429267df", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Appendix B: Ownership", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-117", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Appendix B: Ownership", "content": "Appendix B: Ownership\\n\\n- Baseline pipeline and artifact integrity: Telemetry Platform (Logan Wright) + Metrics/Baselines (Nadia Rahman)\\n- Threshold standards and paging hygiene: SRE (Sean Gallagher, Allison Grant)\\n- Model list and rollout gating integration: Serving Runtime (Noah Patel) + Release Engineering (Connor O\'Brien)", "score": 0.516684, "rank": 15, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "4a890abb-a268-5f6c-8bd8-8190ba739f96", "search_unit_id": "4a890abb-a268-5f6c-8bd8-8190ba739f96", "block_from_id": "0deabef5-6329-59bf-ba97-4e7537d0c14d", "block_to_id": "b2185789-0f79-580c-91cf-f2daa95dc8af", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Consequences > Positive", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-104", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Consequences > Positive", "content": "Consequences\\n\\nPositive\\n\\n- Stable, versioned baselines support rollout gates and high-confidence paging.\\n- Rolling health baseline provides drift visibility without undermining safety.\\n- Anti-flap controls reduce alert noise and prevent incident-bot storms.", "score": 0.516684, "rank": 16, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "a40f8598-2951-5778-a15f-0707398d2692", "search_unit_id": "a40f8598-2951-5778-a15f-0707398d2692", "block_from_id": "327d6dc6-1a59-5f1e-9cd7-461d51c1c722", "block_to_id": "feb530dd-d138-526c-96b8-1f12f157c7ec", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Anti-Flap, Dedupe, and Hysteresis > Telemetry delay protection", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-83", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Anti-Flap, Dedupe, and Hysteresis > Telemetry delay protection", "content": "Telemetry delay protection\\n\\nIf telemetry ingestion delay exceeds 2x the evaluation window (e.g., >20 minutes), alert evaluation is suspended and a separate \xe2\x80\x9ctelemetry delay\xe2\x80\x9d warning is emitted to #eng-platform.", "score": 0.516684, "rank": 17, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "3c486a70-00a3-5591-af7a-f282b4184282", "search_unit_id": "3c486a70-00a3-5591-af7a-f282b4184282", "block_from_id": "264e1948-923a-5782-8b89-7dfd048bedc5", "block_to_id": "046385dd-2761-521d-aa1b-81e7f72587a7", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Alternatives Considered > C) Per-region baselines always on", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-98", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Alternatives Considered > C) Per-region baselines always on", "content": "C) Per-region baselines always on\\n\\nPros:\\n\\n- Reduces false positives due to cross-region fleet differences.\\n\\nCons:\\n\\n- Baseline explosion (more artifacts and config), operational overhead.\\n\\nDecision: Region is optional and only enabled for models/regions where observed variance requires it.", "score": 0.516684, "rank": 18, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "66d7594b-8436-5080-9aef-e0793b071050", "search_unit_id": "66d7594b-8436-5080-9aef-e0793b071050", "block_from_id": "b054f4e8-bbac-5499-945b-0a4e35e10b2a", "block_to_id": "ced36613-e0ec-5017-b3a5-8e6157be9809", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Minimum Sample Sizes and Windowing > Evaluation window", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-61", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Minimum Sample Sizes and Windowing > Evaluation window", "content": "Minimum Sample Sizes and Windowing\\n\\nEvaluation window\\n\\n- Default evaluation window: **10 minutes**.\\n- Windows are evaluated continuously and require sustained breach rules (see anti-flap).", "score": 0.516684, "rank": 19, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "3673b29b-cfa7-5efa-8aa9-5ff8dd44023f", "search_unit_id": "3673b29b-cfa7-5efa-8aa9-5ff8dd44023f", "block_from_id": "f48154e7-ac7a-58ae-bcf2-0955daab830c", "block_to_id": "cba6a8ae-ef1b-5d20-827b-830f9be9b71c", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Default Thresholds (v1) > Latency (p95 end-to-end)", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-52", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Default Thresholds (v1) > Latency (p95 end-to-end)", "content": "Latency (p95 end-to-end)\\n\\n- Warning: p95 E2E latency **+10%** vs baseline for **2 out of 3** consecutive evaluation windows.\\n- Paging: p95 E2E latency **+20%** vs baseline for **3 out of 4** consecutive evaluation windows.", "score": 0.516684, "rank": 20, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "f6abcbc2-e8a0-55b0-b881-e05dd8c11289", "search_unit_id": "f6abcbc2-e8a0-55b0-b881-e05dd8c11289", "block_from_id": "fa187574-c2df-5d98-94fe-8213b8cb55e1", "block_to_id": "2f7b581d-7720-58fa-b392-2204cfd086bc", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Changelog", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-119", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Changelog", "content": "Changelog\\n\\n- 2026-02-12: Clarified cooldown timers, added telemetry delay protection rule, and tightened tokens/sec minimum token count requirement.", "score": 0.516684, "rank": 21, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "11e07925-978c-5589-a759-600b153ded4d", "search_unit_id": "11e07925-978c-5589-a759-600b153ded4d", "block_from_id": "be65d402-742a-5e74-b3dd-89badbc8f639", "block_to_id": "ec1f642b-4a53-5e57-a104-739d0f9859df", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Anti-Flap, Dedupe, and Hysteresis > Alert clear (hysteresis)", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-74", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Anti-Flap, Dedupe, and Hysteresis > Alert clear (hysteresis)", "content": "Alert clear (hysteresis)\\n\\nAlerts clear only when performance returns closer to baseline:\\n\\n- Warning clears when \xce\x94 < +6% (latency) and \xce\x94 > -5% (tokens/sec) for 3/3 windows.\\n- Paging clears when \xce\x94 < +12% (latency) and \xce\x94 > -10% (tokens/sec) for 4/4 windows.", "score": 0.516684, "rank": 22, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "a445ba42-6f63-5e30-bbff-d9e81f181849", "search_unit_id": "a445ba42-6f63-5e30-bbff-d9e81f181849", "block_from_id": "665a2693-48f7-5964-b2f2-5385ab4f0885", "block_to_id": "1f2673e0-819a-5ceb-a3a7-130f139dfaca", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Anti-Flap, Dedupe, and Hysteresis > Cooldown", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-77", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Anti-Flap, Dedupe, and Hysteresis > Cooldown", "content": "Cooldown\\n\\nAfter an alert transitions to firing, we enforce a cooldown before re-triggering a new incident thread for the same key:\\n\\n- Warning cooldown: 60 minutes\\n- Paging cooldown: 120 minutes", "score": 0.516684, "rank": 23, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "27698a5d-d93e-55bc-9e85-1ea0b026d5f6", "search_unit_id": "27698a5d-d93e-55bc-9e85-1ea0b026d5f6", "block_from_id": "52c4cb61-c56f-5cf9-a932-5f55b94704eb", "block_to_id": "4d4a53fe-b57d-5204-82ee-bd71a6c3810e", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Regression Definition", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-40", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Regression Definition", "content": "Regression Definition\\n\\nWe define regression as a statistically and operationally meaningful deviation from the fixed baseline.", "score": 0.516684, "rank": 24, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "727341b2-7485-5498-b317-52936582e1ca", "search_unit_id": "727341b2-7485-5498-b317-52936582e1ca", "block_from_id": "72526615-4309-5311-b017-ea8575fcc639", "block_to_id": "461f557f-a9ae-56b2-a8f6-4cdb7deb0121", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Anti-Flap, Dedupe, and Hysteresis > Sustained breach logic", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-70", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Anti-Flap, Dedupe, and Hysteresis > Sustained breach logic", "content": "Anti-Flap, Dedupe, and Hysteresis\\n\\nSustained breach logic\\n\\nWe use \xe2\x80\x9cM out of N windows\xe2\x80\x9d to reduce sensitivity to transient spikes:\\n\\n- Warning: 2/3 consecutive windows breach\\n- Paging: 3/4 consecutive windows breach", "score": 0.516684, "rank": 25, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "e9bc9610-465d-5c8f-8485-93b1933c48c3", "search_unit_id": "e9bc9610-465d-5c8f-8485-93b1933c48c3", "block_from_id": "bf3f536f-4574-5dfb-bb65-6c1bd9f7bf3a", "block_to_id": "e39cb70f-0d0a-5536-ac7f-20b2c8af4561", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Alternatives Considered > A) Pure rolling baseline (always updated)", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-85", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Alternatives Considered > A) Pure rolling baseline (always updated)", "content": "Alternatives Considered\\n\\nA) Pure rolling baseline (always updated)\\n\\nPros:\\n\\n- Adapts to drift without explicit re-baselining.\\n\\nCons:\\n\\n- Risk of masking slow regressions (baseline chases the regression).\\n- Hard to use for rollout gating (\xe2\x80\x9cmoving goalposts\xe2\x80\x9d).\\n- Susceptible to alert storms if rolling logic is impacted by label bugs or ingestion gaps.\\n\\nDecision: Rejected for paging/gating. Allowed only as a secondary calibration signal.", "score": 0.472797, "rank": 26, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "f37db93e-b81a-5ba4-8d45-7c2934d4367c", "search_unit_id": "f37db93e-b81a-5ba4-8d45-7c2934d4367c", "block_from_id": "c64b2220-dfdd-542d-9218-86e48adf63ea", "block_to_id": "91573533-ff3d-56bc-8378-b75fd72b0c0d", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Regression Definition > Threshold levels", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-47", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Regression Definition > Threshold levels", "content": "Threshold levels\\n\\nTwo alert levels exist:\\n\\n- **Warning**: actionable signal for runtime team triage; routed to #eng-runtime.\\n- **Paging**: sustained, high-confidence regression on top models; routed to on-call rotation.", "score": 0.478147, "rank": 27, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "82e5de62-ab2f-52ee-a327-f8ae85a98506", "search_unit_id": "82e5de62-ab2f-52ee-a327-f8ae85a98506", "block_from_id": "f2167597-0d78-51c4-98ac-6e6b5709a336", "block_to_id": "ee939171-e136-5ca2-917d-48f955d2b50a", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Default Thresholds (v1) > Throughput (tokens/sec)", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-54", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Default Thresholds (v1) > Throughput (tokens/sec)", "content": "Throughput (tokens/sec)\\n\\n- Warning: tokens/sec **-8%** vs baseline for **2 out of 3** windows.\\n- Paging: tokens/sec **-15%** vs baseline for **3 out of 4** windows.", "score": 0.516684, "rank": 28, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "dce37664-4c7a-5cd2-aff9-2b8b05d93b21", "search_unit_id": "dce37664-4c7a-5cd2-aff9-2b8b05d93b21", "block_from_id": "6d4588a0-f081-5ee0-9394-bddc1b49fd75", "block_to_id": "648b9fdc-1229-5e63-b445-0ffa22b1fc1a", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Default Thresholds (v1) > Runtime-only attribution signals (non-paging by default)", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-56", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Default Thresholds (v1) > Runtime-only attribution signals (non-paging by default)", "content": "Runtime-only attribution signals (non-paging by default)\\n\\nThese are emitted to dashboards and included in alert payloads, but do not page unless explicitly enabled for a model:\\n\\n- Queueing time p95 +25% (suggests scheduler/fleet saturation)\\n- Prefill p95 +15% (suggests kernel/model config regressions)\\n- Decode p95 +15% (suggests kernel/model config regressions)\\n\\nRationale:\\n\\n- Paging should be driven by end-to-end customer-impact proxy (E2E p95 and tokens/sec).\\n- Breakdown metrics improve triage but are often noisier and more sensitive to load mix.", "score": 0.396779, "rank": 29, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "7b700c43-46fe-59a4-a0bb-d3cd1c2a7f01", "search_unit_id": "7b700c43-46fe-59a4-a0bb-d3cd1c2a7f01", "block_from_id": "b5a87d99-1d52-5998-9ee1-f3bc88581b1a", "block_to_id": "96de10ac-0596-5756-8478-56b0fc50e039", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Rollout Guidance", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-111", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Rollout Guidance", "content": "Rollout Guidance\\n\\n- Phase 1 (single region): warnings only, tune per-model overrides until noise is acceptable.\\n- Phase 2: enable paging only for top models with proven low variance and stable baselines.\\n- Phase 3: integrate gating with release engineering once paging signal is trusted (warning can gate early as \xe2\x80\x9csoft fail,\xe2\x80\x9d paging as \xe2\x80\x9chard fail\xe2\x80\x9d).", "score": 0.350725, "rank": 30, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "829619c6-5bb2-5336-b599-41394e4d318e", "search_unit_id": "829619c6-5bb2-5336-b599-41394e4d318e", "block_from_id": "14f1eecf-4873-5552-ac97-9814fbb2085d", "block_to_id": "25fdbf57-8bd8-5b95-81cc-c2f2996c61b9", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Metrics Covered", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-32", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Metrics Covered", "content": "Metrics Covered\\n\\nBaselines and regressions are computed for:\\n\\n- End-to-end latency: p50, p95, p99 (ms)\\n- Runtime-only latency: p50, p95, p99 (ms) (excludes network/client)\\n- Prefill latency and decode latency (ms)\\n- Queueing time (ms) (scheduler-level)\\n- Tokens/sec (overall, and decode tokens/sec where available)\\n- Batch size distribution (for attribution)\\n- KV cache hit rate (where applicable; informational at v1)", "score": 0.349639, "rank": 31, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "23d59747-a1af-515c-8f79-528d93c99d09", "search_unit_id": "23d59747-a1af-515c-8f79-528d93c99d09", "block_from_id": "9cd681e5-97cb-5376-8e9e-4eebb60ae8c3", "block_to_id": "5ea39e5e-dfbb-5c06-b745-2e0fbead0881", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Baseline Computation > Rolling health baseline (calibration only)", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-38", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Baseline Computation > Rolling health baseline (calibration only)", "content": "Rolling health baseline (calibration only)\\n\\n- Window: trailing 7 days, excluding periods marked as \xe2\x80\x9crollout\xe2\x80\x9d or \xe2\x80\x9cincident.\xe2\x80\x9d\\n- Aggregation: daily aggregates with robust statistics (median-of-daily-p95) to reduce sensitivity to short spikes.\\n- Purpose:\\n  - detect slow drift (e.g., fleet changes) that may warrant generating a new fixed baseline\\n  - suggest region/SKU overrides when variance is consistently higher", "score": 0.342763, "rank": 32, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "811fe0c3-2593-5368-9d98-111da48a8a12", "search_unit_id": "811fe0c3-2593-5368-9d98-111da48a8a12", "block_from_id": "24166ce2-b07a-5310-95d0-4fa4c91ab798", "block_to_id": "0b672f8b-beee-5069-9b9b-64d2681d7531", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Consequences > Negative / Tradeoffs", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-107", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Consequences > Negative / Tradeoffs", "content": "Negative / Tradeoffs\\n\\n- Requires baseline artifact generation whenever major runtime/kernel changes land for covered models/SKUs.\\n- Some true regressions may be detected slightly later due to sustained-breach requirements.\\n- Optional region/tier overrides add complexity when enabled.", "score": 0.311778, "rank": 33, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "048dcbdb-3ef2-5adb-aaa1-7b3d09b59784", "search_unit_id": "048dcbdb-3ef2-5adb-aaa1-7b3d09b59784", "block_from_id": "19c4bfbb-325e-5713-b50c-5c5bc52048b7", "block_to_id": "29816627-69c4-5de1-9925-50d061e7922c", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h1-0", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds", "content": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds\\n\\nSource type: confluence\\nDocument ID: dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83\\nRelease: v1.0.0\\nBenchmark: EnterpriseRAG-Bench synthetic upstream data\\nADR-0142: Perf Canary Baselines, Regression Thresholds, Min Sample Sizes, and Anti-Flap Logic", "score": 0.306919, "rank": 34, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "84971e12-3b85-562f-a47a-0616d6f1282d", "search_unit_id": "84971e12-3b85-562f-a47a-0616d6f1282d", "block_from_id": "0fcf622d-1f62-51a2-a7a7-d75470f483a7", "block_to_id": "ede8256a-24a2-5244-87e0-c2190dbea2b1", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Default Thresholds (v1)", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-50", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Default Thresholds (v1)", "content": "Default Thresholds (v1)\\n\\nThresholds are configurable per model, with these platform defaults used unless overridden.", "score": 0.328959, "rank": 35, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "7eb972fc-c055-5e16-b256-ab258597491c", "search_unit_id": "7eb972fc-c055-5e16-b256-ab258597491c", "block_from_id": "1c77e0e1-0c02-5b5d-967f-9caf072d965c", "block_to_id": "e38a1a5f-91dc-5cbb-a233-80d234957dba", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Anti-Flap, Dedupe, and Hysteresis > Dedupe key", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "