14:02:06  DEBUG    [cab30e383db544af]  sse_starlette.sse  chunk: b'event: result\r\ndata: {"query": "In the internal shiproom runner notes, what is the target time-to-recover threshold for a verified rollback in staging?", "sections": [{"chunk_id": "30770cfd-abf7-5487-b3e4-5407cf0107a1", "search_unit_id": "30770cfd-abf7-5487-b3e4-5407cf0107a1", "block_from_id": "559cadbb-bcaf-591e-943c-3540439c59a5", "block_to_id": "ee195e6e-fdf0-52ae-a64a-c08de528f292", "section_path": "Shiproom Runner Personal Prep Log", "document_id": "2c3a4afd-6872-53a7-92b5-63332031d3d8", "document_version_id": "bcdc4a63-5718-5cd6-aa82-092158b55d4f", "document_name": "google_drive__dsid_5fc2dba9f6ac4af2b49b4f546a4298d0.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h1-0", "heading": "Shiproom Runner Personal Prep Log", "content": "Shiproom Runner Personal Prep Log\\n\\nSource type: google_drive\\nDocument ID: dsid_5fc2dba9f6ac4af2b49b4f546a4298d0\\nRelease: v1.0.0\\nBenchmark: EnterpriseRAG-Bench synthetic upstream data\\nShiproom runner: personal prep log and sticky notes\\n\\nPurpose: quick, scannable personal notes for running the shiproom and weekly readiness sync. Organized as prep items, live-run cues, and follow-up actions. Not a polished playbook \xe2\x80\x94 my sticky running list + prompts to escalate.\\n\\nDAY-BEFORE / 24-48H CHECKS (quick hits)\\n\\n- Validate Dedicated pool health dashboard (console > Dedicated > Pool-5). Look for 90th pct latency spike > 20% vs baseline. If spike: page SRE and tag \'pool-5\'.\\n- Confirm model pin assignments for weekend rollouts: model = rwx-v2-quant, pinned to image-2026-02-28. Cross-check with model-catalog ticket.\\n- Ensure canary capacity reserved: 3 instances w/ low-priority burst. If not reserved, open ticket to infra (email infra-runbooks).\\n- Verify last smoke-run results (smoke/last-run.json) \xe2\x80\x94 critical checks: health endpoints, prefix caching, stream stability. Mark any failing check with TODO.\\n\\nMEETING AGENDA (for my 10\xe2\x80\x9315 min run)\\n1) Quick status (30s each): Hosted API, Dedicated, Private \xe2\x80\x94 3 bullet lines max.\\n2) Go/No-Go candidate items (3) \xe2\x80\x94 call out owner for decision.\\n3) High-risk regressions & mitigations (A/B, rollbacks, fallback).\\n4) Open action items from last week (owners + ETA).\\n5) Escalations and customer-impacting items.\\nGO/NO-GO CHECKLIST (my shorthand)\\n\\n- Safety: latest canary passed golden prompt set? [yes/no] \xe2\x80\x94 if no -> NO-GO and block rollout. Owner: Priya.\\n- Latency: 95th <= SLO (hosted) and Dedicated 90th within committed window? [ok/warn/fail] Owner: Jordan.\\n- Throughput: capacity test at target qps for model variant (rwx-v2-quant) >= 90% predicted. Owner: Marco (perf eng).\\n- Telemetry: traces + logs flowing to observability (no gaps > 5 min). Owner: Observability on-call.\\n- Rollback plan: image rollback verified in staging (time-to-recover < 10m). Owner: me (Aisha) \xe2\x80\x94 pre-check: rehearse command set.\\n\\nLIVE-RUN CUES (during shiproom)\\n\\n- If latency alert fires: call out metric, ask SRE to confirm impact (hosted vs dedicated). If impact is hosted only -> consider global throttles, otherwise trigger capacity burst.\\n- If canary fails: pause rollout, gather failing prompts, escalate to Applied ML for quality triage. Capture failing prompt examples in the meeting notes.\\n- If control plane flaps: deploy cross-region fallback policy, set communication to CS + site-status.\\n\\nSMOKE-TEST QUICK-LOOK (ordered)\\n1) /health (all regions) \xe2\x80\x94 expect 200 and healthy=true.\\n2) golden prompt generation (3 variants) \xe2\x80\x94 check for coherent output and stable token length.\\n3) streaming socket smoke (5 simulated clients) \xe2\x80\x94 no connection resets.\\n4) KV cache hit-rate sanity check (> 30% for typical workloads).\\n5) auth flow: token validation for dev key and prod key.\\nRISKS I CARE ABOUT (notes to self)\\n\\n- Quantized model edge cases: hallucinations on long-context prompts unseen in evals. Watch for uptick in hallucination rate on live eval monitors.\\n- Autoscale cold starts: small percentage of cold starts can push P95 over threshold. Keep warmup policy on for first 2h post-deploy.\\n- Third-party infra patch windows (cloud provider) could impact Dedicated zones \xe2\x80\x94 pre-check weekly maintenance calendar.\\n\\nOPEN ACTIONS (make sure to call out in meeting)", "score": 0.840515, "rank": 0, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "ebaf51ab-b1cb-5a2d-8b45-628f1659ae8b", "search_unit_id": "ebaf51ab-b1cb-5a2d-8b45-628f1659ae8b", "block_from_id": "da634021-5dfd-5b41-9138-aab61fa821a0", "block_to_id": "bbdc773a-da4b-50b7-9525-4e8d21556259", "section_path": "Shiproom Runner Personal Prep Log", "document_id": "2c3a4afd-6872-53a7-92b5-63332031d3d8", "document_version_id": "bcdc4a63-5718-5cd6-aa82-092158b55d4f", "document_name": "google_drive__dsid_5fc2dba9f6ac4af2b49b4f546a4298d0.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "list-12", "heading": "Shiproom Runner Personal Prep Log", "content": "- A1: Priya \xe2\x80\x94 re-run golden prompt suite with latest model (due 2026-03-03). Status: running.\\n- A2: Jordan \xe2\x80\x94 validate Dedicated pool latency anomaly root cause, post short RCA (due 2026-03-05). Status: investigating.\\n- A3: Marco \xe2\x80\x94 confirm scaling headroom numbers for expected QPS spike; provide conservative headroom estimate (due 2026-03-04).\\n- A4: Aisha (me) \xe2\x80\x94 rehearse rollback commands in staging and record exact steps in private playbook (due 2026-03-02).\\n- A5: Eng-sre on-call \xe2\x80\x94 add trace tag for canary requests to make debugging faster (due 2026-03-03).\\n\\nNOTES-TO-SELF / RUN-TIME SNIPPETS\\n\\n- Keep the Launch Channel pinned and set ephemeral notifications: only @here for major go/no-go decisions.\\n- One-sentence status template for quick updates: \\"Area \xe2\x80\x94 short-state (ok/warn/fail) \xe2\x80\x94 top-1 mitigation if warn/fail\\". Use this when I call status.\\n- If we need to delay: propose a 1-hour cool-down + redo canary after fixes.\\n\\nESCALATION CONTACTS (quick)\\n\\n- SRE on-call (pager): pager.sre@redwood.internal \xe2\x80\x94 send with subject: \\"shiproom: [area] [short tag]\\"\\n- Applied ML: priya.nair@redwood.com (for model-quality escalations)\\n- Infra runbook slack: #infra-runbooks (use slash /runbook deploy-rollback)\\n\\nPOST-MEETING FOLLOW-UP FORMAT (what I send to channel)\\n\\n- TL;DR (1 line)\\n- Decisions (go/no-go + what changed)\\n- Owners + actions (one-line per action with ETA)\\n- Customer-facing items (any comms to CS + suggested text)\\n\\nEXAMPLE QUICK COMMS (copyable)\\n\\n- \\"TL;DR: Go for staged rollout (canary ok). Action: Priya to finish regression suite; Jordan to monitor Dedicated P95. Aisha to coordinate rollback rehearsal.\\"\\n- \\"Customer note (for CS): We observed intermittent latency in Dedicated pool during preflight; mitigation is increased warmup and a temporary capacity bump. ETA for final fix: 48h.\\"\\n\\nMY PERSONAL CHECKLIST BEFORE HAND-OFF\\n\\n- Confirm notes & action items added to central release tracker (JIRA-RELEASE-2026).\\n- Make sure ownership is explicit (no ambiguous \\"eng team\\" lines).\\n- Leave a 15-min buffer after the meeting for async follow-ups and handover to ops.\\n\\nFRAGMENTS / THINGS I WANT TO INVESTIGATE (later)\\n\\n- Can we automate the canary prompt selection so it\'s representative of top-100 queries? (pitch to applied-ml)\\n- Metric to add: per-model hallucination delta vs baseline (daily) \xe2\x80\x94 needs logging hook.\\n- Explore a one-click rollback UI in console for small teams (longer-term product ask).\\n\\nEND-OF-DAY LOG (fill after shiproom)\\n\\n- Outcome: [GO / NO-GO] \xe2\x80\x94 notes: _____\\n- Actions I triggered: list with timestamps\\n- Follow-ups I delegated: list with owner + ETA\\n\\n(Misc scratch lines)\\n\\n- remember: breathe. keep the meeting short. if debate > 3min, move to async deep-dive.\\n\\n-- Aisha", "score": 0.528716, "rank": 1, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}], "events": [], "entities": [], "relations": [], "source_hits": [], "summary": "", "citations": [], "answer_status": "pending", "no_answer_reason": null, "exploration_id": null, "stats": {"canonical_index": true, "ready_versions": 81, "requested_top_k": null, "candidate_top_k": 32, "candidate_unit_pool_limit": 1024, "candidate_pool_saturated": true, "candidate_units_before_cap": 67, "candidate_units_after_cap": 67, "candidate_units_truncated": 0, "semantic_candidates": 41, "lexical_candidates": 36, "candidates": 67, "relevant": 67, "filtered_irrelevant": 0, "fusion_method": "rrf", "selection_method": "authorized_content_dedup_mmr", "cross_scope_merge": "rank_interleave", "coverage": {"candidate_count": 64, "deduplicated_count": 0, "diversity_weight": 0.5, "near_duplicate_similarity": 0.98, "required_anchor_count": 0, "covered_anchor_count": 0, "anchor_coverage": "not_required", "status": "unknown", "canonical_locator_verified": true, "semantic_answerability": "unknown"}, "routing": {"planner": {"planner_version": "qsp-v1", "requested_strategy": "AUTO", "effective_strategy": "LOCAL_FACTUAL", "modifiers": [], "reason_codes": ["DEFAULT_LOCAL_FACTUAL"], "multi_hop_eligible": false}, "request_snapshot_id": "62109744-c263-4f67-834b-d4eed03a8324", "groups": [{"project_id": "b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c", "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "partition_id": "b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c", "snapshot_id": "cf24f842-b4b6-4ab3-82d3-37e16b67b992", "request_snapshot_id": "62109744-c263-4f67-834b-d4eed03a8324", "acl_scope_fingerprint": "328ac326f64690733d385248a99659bc5ed25e83991108887c7a3367d2d5c51e", "tree_version": "tree-50bdd85ee0f1111bfecc7840", "routing_slot": "SLOT_A", "search_epoch": 2, "selected_nodes": ["50f5b8fbcaab2e34ad30