14:02:45  DEBUG    [42fefad1875748b2]  sse_starlette.sse  chunk: b'event: summary.delta\r\ndata: {"delta": "Redwood proposed an alternative Year 1 pricing package with a 40% effective discount on committed prepay buckets and a $50,000 one-time onboarding credit tied to migration milestones, instead of matching the competitor\'s 50% first-year discount and $60k migration credit. This is cited in [3]."}\r\n\r\n'
14:02:45  DEBUG    [42fefad1875748b2]  sse_starlette.sse  chunk: b'event: completed\r\ndata: {"query": "In the EdgePath evaluation email thread, what alternative Year 1 pricing package did Redwood propose instead of matching the competitor\'s 50 percent first-year discount and migration credit?", "sections": [{"chunk_id": "7f24bf98-0f57-552b-a4ff-b8f9e6282813", "search_unit_id": "7f24bf98-0f57-552b-a4ff-b8f9e6282813", "block_from_id": "76edbbae-f05b-5989-a55d-51aa51344883", "block_to_id": "ad7a90e9-9ebe-5614-924e-02337267dc7c", "section_path": "20250803 License Offsets And Migration Incentive", "document_id": "84c4044d-8fe9-59e3-a2c5-93da9dfddc73", "document_version_id": "de571634-f822-5e30-b058-7696ced021b6", "document_name": "gmail__dsid_85deb10a652742baaf28af6149600001.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "p-17", "heading": "20250803 License Offsets And Migration Incentive", "content": "High\xe2\x80\x91level, two commercial paths:\\n1) Elastic (PAYG) \xe2\x80\x94 tiered per\xe2\x80\x91token rates with a 5/3/2% volume stepdown at $25k/$75k/$250k monthly spend. No onboarding credit.\\n2) Committed (12/24 mo) \xe2\x80\x94 prepay buckets that reduce effective unit cost by 25% for Year 1 at a 12\xe2\x80\x91month commit; onboarding credit up to $45k for migration milestones. Includes a seat license option that adds predictable monthlies and entitles to 1:1 ECC.\\n\\nNotes on migration costs: we estimate ~5\xe2\x80\x938 engineer days of effort for a light integration (if they use standard SDKs). For a heavy custom runtime integration (self\xe2\x80\x91hosted/private), estimate 20\xe2\x80\x9340 engineer days and potential hardware egress fees (we modeled both).\\n\\nI put conservative numbers in Redwood_Tiered_Offer.pdf; if procurement is pushing for a headline credit, we can backfill with a one\xe2\x80\x91time migration allowance instead of deeper recurring discounts.\\n\\n--- END MODEL SUMMARY ---\\n\\nI recommend offering the committed route with a midline onboarding credit \xe2\x80\x94 that reduces Year 1 sticker while preserving unit economics.\\n\\nKarthik\\nPrincipal Solutions Architect, Redwood\\n---\\nFrom: Sarah Lin <sarah.lin@edgepath.ai>\\nTo: Avery Johnson <avery.johnson@redwood.com>\\nCc: Dan Richards <dan+procurement@cloudorbit.io>\\nDate: Mon, 4 Aug 2025 16:41:00 -07:00\\nSubject: Re: Licensing/packaging questions ahead of our evaluation\\n\\nThanks \xe2\x80\x94 appreciate the quick turnaround and the attachments. A couple of clarifying points from procurement:\\n\\n- CloudOrbit (the incumbent) is offering a 50% discount off list for Year 1 + a $60k migration credit if we sign a 24\xe2\x80\x91month commitment. They\xe2\x80\x99ve also offered a bundled seat/license that caps our variable spend.\\n- Procurement wants to know whether Redwood will match that structure (50% + $60k credit) or whether you can provide a superior operational carveout (e.g., guaranteed latency SLO + extended onboarding).\\n\\nFrom a negotiation perspective, we prefer lower effective Year 1 cost even if Year 2 rates normalize (procurement wants to reduce first\xe2\x80\x91year spend to make the budget).\\n\\nHappy to review whatever counteroffer you can put on paper; Dan is copied and will feed to finance.\\n\\n\xe2\x80\x94Sarah\\n\\nOn Mon, Aug 4, 2025 at 10:03 AM Karthik Iyer <karthik.iyer@redwood.com> wrote:\\n> We ran EdgePath\'s Q2 export on Redwood\'s standard runtime assumptions:\\n> - Token mix: 70% prompts / 30% generations (avg 28 tokens generated)\\n> - Avg concurrency window: 6 concurrent requests during peak 10\xe2\x80\x9316 PST\\n>\\n> High\xe2\x80\x91level, two commercial paths:\\n> 1) Elastic (PAYG) \xe2\x80\x94 tiered per\xe2\x80\x91token rates with a 5/3/2% volume stepdown at $25k/$75k/$250k monthly spend. No onboarding credit.\\n> 2) Committed (12/24 mo) \xe2\x80\x94 prepay buckets that reduce effective unit cost by 25% for Year 1 at a 12\xe2\x80\x91month commit; onboarding credit up to $45k for migration milestones.\\n\\nFrom: Avery Johnson <avery.johnson@redwood.com>\\nTo: Sarah Lin <sarah.lin@edgepath.ai>, Dan Richards <dan+procurement@cloudorbit.io>\\nCc: Karthik Iyer <karthik.iyer@redwood.com>, Connor O\'Brien <connor.obrien@redwood.com>, Monica Patel <monica.patel@redwood.com>\\nDate: Tue, 5 Aug 2025 15:22:00 -07:00\\nSubject: Re: Licensing/packaging questions ahead of our evaluation\\n\\nSarah / Dan \xe2\x80\x94\\n\\nThanks for the context. We won\xe2\x80\x99t match a 50% blanket list cut for Year 1; that would put unit economics below where we can sustainably operate for the workload described. That said, we can meet your objective of lowering Year 1 cash outlay with an alternative package:", "score": 0.780613, "rank": 0, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "b5836bc5-cac2-5ba7-bdd6-43128e01794e", "search_unit_id": "b5836bc5-cac2-5ba7-bdd6-43128e01794e", "block_from_id": "b0375853-4311-5b0f-9f35-29161463e1a3", "block_to_id": "b7d41b36-2122-5e1e-81bf-67126fea20d1", "section_path": "20250803 License Offsets And Migration Incentive", "document_id": "84c4044d-8fe9-59e3-a2c5-93da9dfddc73", "document_version_id": "de571634-f822-5e30-b058-7696ced021b6", "document_name": "gmail__dsid_85deb10a652742baaf28af6149600001.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h1-0", "heading": "20250803 License Offsets And Migration Incentive", "content": "20250803 License Offsets And Migration Incentive\\n\\nSource type: gmail\\nDocument ID: dsid_85deb10a652742baaf28af6149600001\\nRelease: v1.0.0\\nBenchmark: EnterpriseRAG-Bench synthetic upstream data\\nLicensing offsets & packaging for potential migration\\n\\nFrom: Sarah Lin <sarah.lin@edgepath.ai>\\nTo: Avery Johnson <avery.johnson@redwood.com>\\nDate: Sun, 3 Aug 2025 09:12:00 -0700\\nSubject: Licensing/packaging questions ahead of our evaluation\\n\\nHi Avery,\\n\\nThanks again for the demo last week \xe2\x80\x94 the latency profile looked promising. We\xe2\x80\x99re running a parallel evaluation with another vendor (CloudOrbit) and procurement is pushing for a side\xe2\x80\x91by\xe2\x80\x91side commercial comparison before we move to execs. I attached our internal usage export (summary) so you can see the mix.\\n\\nWhat we need from Redwood to make the case internally:\\n\\n- A clear mapping of your runtime pricing to our usage (per\xe2\x80\x91token + GPU/hr assumptions you used).\\n- Options for licensing offsets or prepay buckets vs. per\xe2\x80\x91use billing.\\n- Any migration/onboarding credit you\xe2\x80\x99d consider if we commit to a 12\xe2\x80\x9324 month term.\\n\\nProcurement has asked for an apples\xe2\x80\x91to\xe2\x80\x91apples seat + runtime cost for Year 1 and Year 2, plus an example amendment that shows how credits would be applied to invoices. Can you turn something around early this week?\\n\\nAttachments: EdgePath_usage_Q2_2025.csv (summary)\\n\xe2\x80\x94Sarah\\nSarah Lin\\nHead of ML Platform, EdgePath\\n---\\nFrom: Avery Johnson <avery.johnson@redwood.com>\\nTo: Sarah Lin <sarah.lin@edgepath.ai>\\nCc: Karthik Iyer <karthik.iyer@redwood.com>, Connor O\'Brien <connor.obrien@redwood.com>, Monica Patel <monica.patel@redwood.com>\\nDate: Sun, 3 Aug 2025 14:20:00 -07:00\\nSubject: Re: Licensing/packaging questions ahead of our evaluation\\n\\nHi Sarah \xe2\x80\x94\\n\\nReally appreciate the usage file, that helps a lot. We can definitely produce the apples\xe2\x80\x91to\xe2\x80\x91apples comparison. Next steps from our side: \\n1) Karthik/Connor will run your usage through a short cost model (token mix, avg seq len, concurrency) \xe2\x80\x94 expect a first pass within 24 business hours.\\n2) We\xe2\x80\x99ll propose 2 packaging options: (A) pay\xe2\x80\x91as\xe2\x80\x91you\xe2\x80\x91go with volume tiers, (B) prepay bucket + seat licenses with an onboarding credit.\\n3) We\xe2\x80\x99ll include example invoice math and an amendment language stub for credits.\\n\\nQuick question for procurement: are they prioritizing lower headline discount or predictable unit economics (i.e., committed spend)? If you can flag that, it will change whether we push prepay vs. discount on list.\\n\\nI\xe2\x80\x99ve asked Karthik to include a technical appendix (egress/egress charges, GPU amortization assumptions) so finance can reconcile. Expect the model tomorrow morning.\\n\\nTalk soon,\\nAvery\\nAvery Johnson\\nSenior Account Executive | Redwood Inference\\n---\\nFrom: Karthik Iyer <karthik.iyer@redwood.com>\\nTo: Avery Johnson <avery.johnson@redwood.com>\\nCc: Connor O\'Brien <connor.obrien@redwood.com>, Monica Patel <monica.patel@redwood.com>\\nDate: Mon, 4 Aug 2025 10:03:00 -07:00\\nSubject: Fwd: Licensing/packaging questions \xe2\x80\x94 cost model and offers\\n\\nForwarding the first pass. Attachments: CO_Usage_Report.xlsx (normalized), Redwood_Tiered_Offer.pdf, migration_scope.docx\\n\\n--- START OF MODEL SUMMARY ---\\nWe ran EdgePath\'s Q2 export on Redwood\'s standard runtime assumptions:\\n\\n- Token mix: 70% prompts / 30% generations (avg 28 tokens generated)\\n- Avg concurrency window: 6 concurrent requests during peak 10\xe2\x80\x9316 PST\\n- Baseline per\xe2\x80\x91token runtime cost (hosted): $0.0008 prompt / $0.0024 gen (model mix adjusted)", "score": 0.714808, "rank": 1, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "00f7a748-c7cc-56e1-bbef-12bdb3ed65b1", "search_unit_id": "00f7a748-c7cc-56e1-bbef-12bdb3ed65b1", "block_from_id": "85ad9c2c-0b21-52b8-a4d7-f7f2aeec25dd", "block_to_id": "e83c9fdc-fc55-519d-9758-d8407923495a", "section_path": "20250803 License Offsets And Migration Incentive", "document_id": "84c4044d-8fe9-59e3-a2c5-93da9dfddc73", "document_version_id": "de571634-f822-5e30-b058-7696ced021b6", "document_name": "gmail__dsid_85deb10a652742baaf28af6149600001.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "p-32", "heading": "20250803 License Offsets And Migration Incentive", "content": "Proposal (summarized):\\n\\n- Term: 12 months commit (option to extend to 24 with prepay ladder)\\n- Effective Year 1 discount: ~40% off list on committed prepay buckets (applies to token spend covered by the bucket).\\n- Onboarding allowance: $50,000 one\xe2\x80\x91time credit tied to migration milestones (applies as invoice credit, sample amendment attached).\\n- Seat/license option: add predictable monthly seat fee to cap variable spend; seat fees reduce effective unit cost further for covered traffic.\\n- Operational concession: 99.9% latency SLO for hosted instances in our US region; we\xe2\x80\x99ll include a short remediation runbook in the SOW.\\n\\nWhy this helps EdgePath: it materially reduces Year 1 outlay (comparable to a 50% headline for the token spend that\xe2\x80\x99s covered by the prepay), preserves sustainable unit economics for Redwood, and gives you a meaningful migration credit plus an ops SLA that helps your reliability case.\\n\\nNext steps: \\n1) If that framework is acceptable, Karthik will formalize numbers in the attached Redwood_Tiered_Offer.pdf and we\xe2\x80\x99ll produce an amendment (DocuSign link) for the onboarding credit and prepay buckets.\\n2) If procurement insists on deeper headline discount in exchange for 24 months, we can discuss a revised committed ladder (we\xe2\x80\x99d need a firm usage baseline to go deeper).\\n\\nI\xe2\x80\x99ll hold a tentative slot Thursday for a quick alignment call \xe2\x80\x94 can you confirm procurement\xe2\x80\x99s preference (cash reduction now vs. multi\xe2\x80\x91year commitment)?\\n\\nBest,\\nAvery\\nSenior Account Executive | Redwood Inference\\nAttachments: Redwood_Tiered_Offer.pdf, migration_scope.docx\\n\\n---", "score": 0.448157, "rank": 2, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}], "events": [], "entities": [], "relations": [], "source_hits": [], "summary": "Redwood proposed an alternative Year 1 pricing package with a 40% effective discount on committed prepay buckets and a $50,000 one-time onboarding credit tied to migration milestones, instead of matching the competitor\'s 50% first-year discount and $60k migration credit. This is cited in [3].", "citations": [{"kind": "internal", "n": 3, "document_id": "84c4044d-8fe9-59e3-a2c5-93da9dfddc73", "document_version_id": "de571634-f822-5e30-b058-7696ced021b6", "document_name": "gmail__dsid_85deb10a652742baaf28af6149600001.md", "version_no": 1, "chunk_id": "00f7a748-c7cc-56e1-bbef-12bdb3ed65b1", "search_unit_id": "00f7a748-c7cc-56e1-bbef-12bdb3ed65b1", "block_from_id": "85ad9c2c-0b21-52b8-a4d7-f7f2aeec25dd", "block_to_id": "e83c9fdc-fc55-519d-9758-d8407923495a", "section_path": "20250803 License Offsets And Migration Incentive", "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "p-32", "heading": "20250803 License Offsets And Migration Incentive", "snippet": "Proposal (summarized): - Term: 12 months commit (option to extend to 24 with prepay ladder) - Effective Year 1 discount: ~40% off list on committed prepay buckets (applies to token spend covered by the bucket). - Onboarding allowance: $50,000 one\xe2\x80\x91time credit tied to migration milestones (applies as invoice credit, sample amendment attached). - Seat/license option: add predictable monthly seat fee to cap variable spend; seat fees reduce effective unit cost further for covered traffic. - Operational concession: 99.9% latency SLO for hosted instances in our US region; we\xe2\x80\x99ll include a short remediation runbook in the SOW. Why this helps EdgePath: it materially reduces Year 1 outlay (comparable to a 50% headline for\xe2\x80\xa6", "score": 0.4482, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}], "answer_status": "answered", "no_answer_reason": null, "exploration_id": null, "stats": {"canonical_index": true, "ready_versions": 81, "requested_top_k": null, "candidate_top_k": 32, "candidate_u