14:03:05  DEBUG    [b4b874d336694dc4]  sse_starlette.sse  chunk: b'event: summary.delta\r\ndata: {"delta": "The new alerting approach groups model-serving requests by stages they pass through using **token stage cohorting** and a **route x stage alert matrix**. This grouping is based on stage-level metrics such as token counts per stage, KV-cache hit patterns, and decode-batch size, allowing the system to compute a deterministic cohort key per invocation. The alert route-matrix generator then biases escalation to the top-k stages most likely responsible for SLO violations, thereby reducing noisy alerts and speeding up root cause analysis by focusing on the relevant stages. [2]"}\r\n\r\n'
14:03:05  DEBUG    [b4b874d336694dc4]  sse_starlette.sse  chunk: b'event: completed\r\ndata: {"query": "How does the new alerting approach group model-serving requests by the stages they pass through to reduce noisy alerts and speed up root cause analysis?", "sections": [{"chunk_id": "8aa43619-d554-556b-be98-c2b5a25c54f4", "search_unit_id": "8aa43619-d554-556b-be98-c2b5a25c54f4", "block_from_id": "5e9e4896-a00f-5fe9-8b50-ba59b5d92b87", "block_to_id": "a57d4a1a-dea4-5bb8-8a25-c72059e53439", "section_path": "Postmortem Perf Canary False Positive Alert Storm > Root cause > RC3: Alert policy mismatch with evaluator grouping (contributing)", "document_id": "020f768f-b114-5ca7-94ee-64447a4e421c", "document_version_id": "aac8c399-c8c4-5179-91b0-c93e8328a769", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_58bdb9f3bb4241e089f4f2b102765db4.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-31", "heading": "Postmortem Perf Canary False Positive Alert Storm > Root cause > RC3: Alert policy mismatch with evaluator grouping (contributing)", "content": "RC3: Alert policy mismatch with evaluator grouping (contributing)\\n\\nThe alert rules aggregated time series on a different dimension set than the evaluator used for baseline comparison.\\n\\n- The evaluator grouped by (model, model_version, region, hardware_sku, runtime_build).\\n- Warning alert queries grouped by (model, region) for readability.\\n- Paging rules grouped by (model) only for top-model simplicity.\\n\\nThis mismatch made it possible for a small, noisy slice (e.g., one SKU) to trigger evaluator regressions while alerts appeared \xe2\x80\x9cglobal\xe2\x80\x9d, causing confusion in triage.", "score": 0.724729, "rank": 0, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "9c804c59-28d4-5181-a82c-4d21a74164b9", "search_unit_id": "9c804c59-28d4-5181-a82c-4d21a74164b9", "block_from_id": "b50bd054-8862-56ed-877d-fa49bddb3786", "block_to_id": "bf6cdc59-7507-5d6d-84d0-f5eeda9d7618", "section_path": "Pr 867001 Introduce Token Stage Cohorting And Route Matrix Alerting", "document_id": "0303466c-7aac-5c67-aacb-e29c1951d5c0", "document_version_id": "730b4462-65f2-5ed8-a97f-f3fc91d91088", "document_name": "github__dsid_c1a6a71323c04c1ba5445aadea340362.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h1-0", "heading": "Pr 867001 Introduce Token Stage Cohorting And Route Matrix Alerting", "content": "Pr 867001 Introduce Token Stage Cohorting And Route Matrix Alerting\\n\\nSource type: github\\nDocument ID: dsid_c1a6a71323c04c1ba5445aadea340362\\nRelease: v1.0.0\\nBenchmark: EnterpriseRAG-Bench synthetic upstream data\\nintroduce-token-stage-cohorting-and-route-matrix-alerting\\n\\nContext: long-tail token cost and multi-stage latency spikes frequently surface only when a request traverses several model-serving stages (tokenization, encoder, decode, fallback). Existing alerts were per-route and per-quantile but lacked a compact way to group requests by \'stage footprint\' and automatically route alerting weight to the stage(s) most likely responsible. Motivation: reduce alert noise and accelerate RCA by grouping invocations into stage-aware cohorts and deriving a route x stage alert matrix that attributes SLO violations to the most likely pipeline stage. What this PR does: 1) Adds a lightweight token_stage_cohort service that computes a deterministic cohort key per invocation based on stage-level metrics (token counts per stage, kv-cache hit pattern, decode-batch size) and stores short-lived cohort aggregates. 2) Introduces an alert route-matrix generator that consumes cohort rollups and emits alert bindings which bias escalation to the top-k stages for that route. 3) Adds a new dashboard focused on cohort drift, stage heatmaps, and per-cohort cost/latency breakdown to help oncall quickly validate root cause hypotheses. 4) Wires the generator into the existing alerting pipeline with a safe canary rollout and automatic quiet-window attenuation to avoid regressing noise. Compatibility and rollout: service defaults to read-only mode until flagged by a feature flag; alert generation starts cross-account in a low-sensitivity mode (only P90/P99) and is then ramped after 72h of monitoring. Testing: unit and integration tests added; ran a 48h synthetic replay against production-like traces (see test run in CI). Checklist: - [x] Unit tests - [x] Integration tests - [x] Dashboard panels - [x] Docs for oncall and runbook - [x] Feature-flagged rollout Plan for operators: deploy to staging -> enable feature flag -> monitor cohort drift and false-positive rate -> bump sensitivity -> full rollout. Links: Linear ENG-1248 (cohorting design) and PM-432 (dashboard spec).\\nDiego: Can cohort keys be stable across model version rollouts? Added suggestion to include model-version hash in key derivation. Response: we now namespace cohort keys with model-major-version and include fallback mapping in cohort_store.proto.\\nPriya: Alert noise risk\xe2\x80\x94please limit initial sensitivity and provide quiet-window behavior. Response: implemented quiet-window attenuation and low-sensitivity defaults; documented in docs/observability/token-cohorting.md.\\nLiam: test coverage looks good but add an e2e replay with partial KV-cache misses. Response: added synthetic KV miss replay in tests/integration/test_cohorting_flow.py and CI run shows stable results.", "score": 0.70159, "rank": 1, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "bf59dd69-5ef0-54b7-b09f-2cdce964833d", "search_unit_id": "bf59dd69-5ef0-54b7-b09f-2cdce964833d", "block_from_id": "be570446-0721-51a6-865d-2922fd5a1516", "block_to_id": "9fa72a23-2854-52a5-8095-c8b6ad7c45a4", "section_path": "Postmortem Perf Canary False Positive Alert Storm > Root cause > RC4: Incident-bot dedupe gaps (contributing)", "document_id": "020f768f-b114-5ca7-94ee-64447a4e421c", "document_version_id": "aac8c399-c8c4-5179-91b0-c93e8328a769", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_58bdb9f3bb4241e089f4f2b102765db4.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-35", "heading": "Postmortem Perf Canary False Positive Alert Storm > Root cause > RC4: Incident-bot dedupe gaps (contributing)", "content": "RC4: Incident-bot dedupe gaps (contributing)\\n\\nincident-bot dedupe was based on (alert_name, model) only.\\n\\n- As a result, changes in alert labels and repeated firing produced new threads/pages.\\n- With many models firing simultaneously, this amplified perceived severity and burden.", "score": 0.672197, "rank": 2, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "044adb1f-0be3-5dec-9a27-03b53bb43ffa", "search_unit_id": "044adb1f-0be3-5dec-9a27-03b53bb43ffa", "block_from_id": "b755b153-6626-5230-b93f-5134889d8505", "block_to_id": "38d9a3da-dc14-553b-99ba-d2bd089e0884", "section_path": "Postmortem Perf Canary False Positive Alert Storm", "document_id": "020f768f-b114-5ca7-94ee-64447a4e421c", "document_version_id": "aac8c399-c8c4-5179-91b0-c93e8328a769", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_58bdb9f3bb4241e089f4f2b102765db4.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h1-0", "heading": "Postmortem Perf Canary False Positive Alert Storm", "content": "Postmortem Perf Canary False Positive Alert Storm\\n\\nSource type: confluence\\nDocument ID: dsid_58bdb9f3bb4241e089f4f2b102765db4\\nRelease: v1.0.0\\nBenchmark: EnterpriseRAG-Bench synthetic upstream data\\nPostmortem: Perf Canary False-Positive Alert Storm (baseline drift + cardinality)", "score": 0.637762, "rank": 3, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "278c554f-2f3c-5117-8fca-18819f8ba7f9", "search_unit_id": "278c554f-2f3c-5117-8fca-18819f8ba7f9", "block_from_id": "3326fd7c-938f-5b5e-a1e1-fb9f594e1119", "block_to_id": "5634704f-f1ed-5d72-aca3-7d8230fd7429", "section_path": "Postmortem Perf Canary False Positive Alert Storm > Impact > Customer impact", "document_id": "020f768f-b114-5ca7-94ee-64447a4e421c", "document_version_id": "aac8c399-c8c4-5179-91b0-c93e8328a769", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_58bdb9f3bb4241e089f4f2b102765db4.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-5", "heading": "Postmortem Perf Canary False Positive Alert Storm > Impact > Customer impact", "content": "Impact\\n\\nCustomer impact\\n\\n- **None confirmed.** Runtime and customer SLO dashboards did not show correlated sustained p95 latency increases for customer traffic.", "score": 0.594278, "rank": 4, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "20b7bcdd-9f4d-53b9-9150-7854120213d1", "search_unit_id": "20b7bcdd-9f4d-53b9-9150-7854120213d1", "block_from_id": "bfdadc6c-3f69-574b-acb3-1090d55059b8", "block_to_id": "ad40db24-9ed6-5a8b-b576-0cdd2d03db08", "section_path": "Postmortem Perf Canary False Positive Alert Storm > Summary", "document_id": "020f768f-b114-5ca7-94ee-64447a4e421c", "document_version_id": "aac8c399-c8c4-5179-91b0-c93e8328a769", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_58bdb9f3bb4241e089f4f2b102765db4.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-2", "heading": "Postmortem Perf Canary False Positive Alert Storm > Summary", "content": "Summary\\n\\nOn 2026-02-12, the production performance canary generated a burst of false-positive alerts across multiple models and regions shortly after enabling warning + paging rules in the first expansion beyond the initial 2-model rollout. Alerts were high volume (warning + paging) and repeatedly reopened due to dedupe failures, resulting in on-call interruption and a temporary release freeze request.\\n\\nThere was **no confirmed customer-facing latency regression** attributable to this incident. The event was an alerting/observability failure caused primarily by (1) **baseline drift + baseline key mismatch** and (2) **metric label cardinality inflation** that fragmented the canary\xe2\x80\x99s time series, defeating min-sample gating and dedupe.", "score": 0.585361, "rank": 5, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "9be67b26-26c5-5283-808e-cfe955c1ef76", "search_unit_id": "9be67b26-26c5-5283-808e-cfe955c1ef76", "block_from_id": "d61b3955-0b76-505e-aa8d-1b62c023f705", "block_to_id": "fe291e98-4874-5a60-ae7d-f1694b159e25", "section_path": "Postmortem Perf Canary False Positive Alert Storm > Impact > Internal impact", "document_id": "020f768f-b114-5ca7-94ee-64447a4e421c", "document_version_id": "aac8c399-c8c4-5179-91b0-c93e8328a769", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_58bdb9f3bb4241e089f4f2b102765db4.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-8", "heading": "Postmortem Perf Canary False Positive Alert Storm > Impact > Internal impact", "content": "Internal impact\\n\\n- **Paging noise:** 19 paging alerts over ~38 minutes (with multiple re-pages due to missing dedupe keys).\\n- **Warning noise:** 60+ warning alerts over ~75 minutes.\\n- **Operational disruption:** SRE on-call and runtime on-call diverted to triage; release engineering requested a short freeze while signals stabilized.\\n- **Confidence impact:** Reduced trust in the perf canary as a rollout gate until remediations were in place.", "score": 0.572536, "rank": 6, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "1776622b-8c1b-5172-8b73-71769f77be40", "search_unit_id": "1776622b-8c1b-5172-8b73-71769f77be40", "block_from_id": "227f114a-7408-57a6-bb5b-bc4c60cbeb9f", "block_to_id": "519b9666-26d2-5e4a-af49-888f7966fa2d", "section_path": "Postmortem Perf Canary False Positive Alert Storm > Resolution and immediate mitigations", "document_id": "020f768f-b114-5ca7-94ee-64447a4e421c", "document_version_id": "aac8c399-c8c4-5179-91b0-c93e8328a769", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_58bdb9f3bb4241e089f4f2b102765db4.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-40", "heading": "Postmortem Perf Canary False Positive Alert Storm > Resolution and immediate mitigations", "content": "Resolution and immediate mitigations\\n\\nActions taken during the incident:\\n\\n1. **Disabled paging rules** for perf-canary regressions (kept warning-level visibility). (Owner: SRE on-call)\\n2. **Rolled back canary model coverage** to the previously stable 3-model configuration. (Owner: Runtime on-call)\\n3. **Pinned evaluator to fixed baseline artifacts** (no rolling updates) until schema/keys were corrected. (Owner: Nadia Rahman)\\n4. **Hotfix to drop high-cardinality labels** from canary metrics (`workload_run_id`, `prompt_template_id`, full `route`). (Owner: Logan Wright)", "score": 0.550794, "rank": 7, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "d7aa5000-5b84-5b58-8f3a-0d6aaf52fd8e", "search_unit_id": "d7aa5000-5b84-5b58-8f3a-0d6aaf52fd8e", "block_from_id": "0efd0dfd-cd7f-563a-92a4-c30d60910979", "block_to_id": "9339743c-8e51-53b0-9fc0-64e3ae412cde", "section_path": "Postmortem Perf Canary False Positive Alert Storm > Appendix > Key decision: baseline missing is a health signal", "document_id": "020f768f-b114-5ca7-94ee-64447a4e421c", "document_version_id": "aac8c399-c8c4-5179-91b0-c93e8328a769", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_58bdb9f3bb4241e089f4f2b102765db4.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-60", "heading": "Postmortem Perf Canary False Positive Alert Storm > Appendix > Key decision: baseline missing is a health signal", "content": "Appendix\\n\\nKey decision: baseline missing is a health signal\\n\\nWe changed behavior from:\\n\\n- \xe2\x80\x9cbaseline missing \xe2\x86\x92 compare against default thresholds (often too strict)\xe2\x80\x9d\\n\\nto:\\n\\n- \xe2\x80\x9cbaseline missing \xe2\x86\x92 emit canary health warning + stop regression evaluation for that grouping until baseline exists\xe2\x80\x9d.\\n\\nRationale: baseline absence is an operational/config issue. Treating it as a performance regression creates noisy pages and reduces trust.", "score": 0.550794, "rank": 8, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "dd182f45-c0e2-58a9-9493-9ffbd872e14f", "search_unit_id": "dd182f45-c0e2-58a9-9493-9ffbd872e14f", "block_from_id": "223314fd-0c4f-5c21-9e10-a9786353c651", "block_to_id": "8e0e0bfe-4c5a-5ce6-b7ca-35d0dd05e9c5", "section_path": "Postmortem Perf Canary False Positive Alert Storm > Appendix > References", "document_id": "020f768f-b114-5ca7-94ee-64447a4e421c", "document_version_id": "aac8c399-c8c4-5179-91b0-c93e8328a769", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_58bdb9f3bb4241e089f4f2b102765db4.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-67", "heading": "Postmortem Perf Canary False Positive Alert Storm > Appendix > References", "content": "References\\n\\n- ADR: Baseline computation + thresholds: sources/confluence/architecture-and-standards/decision-records/adr-perf-canary-baseline-and-thresholds.json\\n- Runbook: Responding to perf canary regression alerts: sources/confluence/eng-sre/runbooks/runbook-perf-regression-canary-alert.json\\n- Dashboard spec: sources/confluence/eng-platform/dashboards-and-alerts/perf-canary-dashboards-spec.json", "score": 0.550794, "rank": 9, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "84887386-4147-58f8-85d9-ff55617092d0", "search_unit_id": "84887386-4147-58f8-85d9-ff55617092d0", "block_from_id": "83fbd98b-2dab-523c-b245-e82f3d451c48", "block_to_id": "b7d8a011-7456-518c-b9ff-d1fd77117f9b", "section_path": "Postmortem Perf Canary False Positive Alert Storm > Lessons learned > What didn\xe2\x80\x99t go well", "document_id": "020f768f-b114-5ca7-94ee-64447a4e421c", "document_version_id": "aac8c399-c8c4-5179-91b0-c93e8328a769", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_58bdb9f3bb4241e089f4f2b102765db4.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-53", "heading": "Postmortem Perf Canary False Positive Alert Storm > Lessons learned > What didn\xe2\x80\x99t go well", "content": "What didn\xe2\x80\x99t go well\\n\\n- Baseline missing \xe2\x86\x92 fallback thresholds created a failure mode where instrumentation/config drift looked like performance regressions.\\n- Cardinality review was incomplete; labels that seemed \xe2\x80\x9charmless\xe2\x80\x9d for logs caused large fragmentation for metrics.\\n- Alert grouping mismatch created confusion (alerts appeared \xe2\x80\x9cglobal\xe2\x80\x9d while underlying series were per-SKU/per-region slices).\\n- Dedupe failures amplified the incident by creating parallel incident-bot threads and repeated pages.", "score": 0.550794, "rank": 10, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "901445b3-4708-58c4-94be-189f040d739c", "search_unit_id": "901445b3-4708-58c4-94be-189f040d739c", "block_from_id": "1c8c49e8-0223-5019-963a-16ae568ef17c", "block_to_id": "b71c7e19-0c12-5048-851e-cf30d62a3b5e", "section_path": "Postmortem Perf Canary False Positive Alert Storm > Lessons learned > What went well", "document_id": "020f768f-b114-5ca7-94ee-64447a4e421c", "document_version_id": "aac8c399-c8c4-5179-91b0-c93e8328a769", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_58bdb9f3bb4241e089f4f2b102765db4.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-50", "heading": "Postmortem Perf Canary False Positive Alert Storm > Lessons learned > What went well", "content": "Lessons learned\\n\\nWhat went well\\n\\n- On-call validated against independent customer-traffic dashboards quickly and avoided an unnecessary rollback of the runtime.\\n- Teams (Runtime/SRE/Telemetry) coordinated rapidly; paging rules were disabled within ~20 minutes.\\n- The canary\xe2\x80\x99s strict \xe2\x80\x9cno customer prompts\xe2\x80\x9d policy kept investigation clean (no privacy concerns during deep dive).", "score": 0.550794, "rank": 11, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "6b97f72d-68f2-546e-ac23-d2b4a4681c3d", "search_unit_id": "6b97f72d-68f2-546e-ac23-d2b4a4681c3d", "block_from_id": "22af3c52-e932-5a90-8c7f-fd0bdb3d5656", "block_to_id": "28356beb-eb55-527d-9624-9d762075b09c", "section_path": "Postmortem Perf Canary False Positive Alert Storm > Lessons learned > Where we got lucky", "document_id": "020f768f-b114-5ca7-94ee-64447a4e421c", "document_version_id": "aac8c399-c8c4-5179-91b0-c93e8328a769", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_58bdb9f3bb4241e089f4f2b102765db4.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-55", "heading": "Postmortem Perf Canary False Positive Alert Storm > Lessons learned > Where we got lucky", "content": "Where we got lucky\\n\\n- The storm happened during an expansion window and not during a high-risk runtime rollout; impact was primarily internal.", "score": 0.550794, "rank": 12, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "0ea65a7a-739d-58fc-b1c2-df8aa12c3f5b", "search_unit_id": "0ea65a7a-739d-58fc-b1c2-df8aa12c3f5b", "block_from_id": "81f13012-a03d-557c-ba58-f64ab339264a", "block_to_id": "a67afa4d-c5d3-5922-9e4f-f0b6d051f6ab", "section_path": "Postmortem Perf Canary False Positive Alert Storm > Root cause > RC1: Baseline drift + key mismatch (primary)", "document_id": "020f768f-b114-5ca7-94ee-64447a4e421c", "document_version_id": "aac8c399-c8c4-5179-91b0-c93e8328a769", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_58bdb9f3bb4241e089f4f2b102765db4.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-19", "heading": "Postmortem Perf Canary False Positive Alert Storm > Root cause > RC1: Baseline drift + key mismatch (primary)", "content": "Root cause\\n\\nRC1: Baseline drift + key mismatch (primary)\\n\\nBaselines were stored per (model, runtime_version, hardware_sku, region) in the baseline store, but the canary emitted/evaluated metrics with an expanded set of labels including transient fields and \xe2\x80\x9cbucketed\xe2\x80\x9d dimensions that were not part of the baseline artifact key.\\n\\nSpecifically:\\n\\n- The canary evaluation path constructed a baseline key using **(model, model_version, runtime_build, region, hardware_sku, prompt_shape_bucket)**.\\n- Baseline artifacts were generated for **(model, model_version, runtime_build, region, hardware_sku)** only (no prompt bucket), and in some cases had **region omitted** (older artifacts) because early staging used a simplified schema.\\n- When the lookup did not match, the evaluator fell back to default thresholds, which are intentionally conservative and therefore easier to breach.\\n\\nAdditionally, baseline updates were set to a rolling policy during the first expansion.\\n\\n- A rolling baseline can be valid, but in this case it introduced \xe2\x80\x9cbaseline drift\xe2\x80\x9d during a period of changing model coverage and metric schema. Drift made alerts oscillate because the baseline distribution was not stable across the same label set.", "score": 0.537798, "rank": 13, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "ca7a60a0-4f48-5d62-b77d-f2dbc0e98665", "search_unit_id": "ca7a60a0-4f48-5d62-b77d-f2dbc0e98665", "block_from_id": "640ca302-cb90-5f7d-9927-971365fe2733", "block_to_id": "2965d38c-b1d4-54c0-991a-2bf3ff81b2ff", "section_path": "Postmortem Perf Canary False Positive Alert Storm > Root cause > RC2: Metric label cardinality inflation (primary)", "document_id": "020f768f-b114-5ca7-94ee-64447a4e421c", "document_version_id": "aac8c399-c8c4-5179-91b0-c93e8328a769", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_58bdb9f3bb4241e089f4f2b102765db4.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-26", "heading": "Postmortem Perf Canary False Positive Alert Storm > Root cause > RC2: Metric label cardinality inflation (primary)", "content": "RC2: Metric label cardinality inflation (primary)\\n\\nSeveral labels unintentionally increased cardinality:\\n\\n- `prompt_template_id` (seeded but still high cardinality across the prompt set)\\n- `workload_run_id` (unique per canary run)\\n- `route` (included full internal route string with version suffix)\\n\\nThis caused:\\n\\n- Fragmentation of histograms/counters into many short-lived series.\\n- \xe2\x80\x9cMin samples\xe2\x80\x9d checks passing on one series while the alert query aggregated differently.\\n- Increased ingestion lag and higher query variance due to sparse buckets.", "score": 0.518178, "rank": 14, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "5c7c90ee-0449-5d9c-a77c-42a2d4f2369c", "search_unit_id": "5c7c90ee-0449-5d9c-a77c-42a2d4f2369c", "block_from_id": "4ad70ac7-de9e-52e1-bc19-755225dc6d59", "block_to_id": "a1e3fd67-2144-5898-a757-2b28130e3db6", "section_path": "Postmortem Perf Canary False Positive Alert Storm > What happened (symptoms)", "document_id": "020f768f-b114-5ca7-94ee-64447a4e421c", "document_version_id": "aac8c399-c8c4-5179-91b0-c93e8328a769", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_58bdb9f3bb4241e089f4f2b102765db4.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-16", "heading": "Postmortem Perf Canary False Positive Alert Storm > What happened (symptoms)", "content": "What happened (symptoms)\\n\\nThe canary\xe2\x80\x99s regression evaluator compared observed p95 latency/tokens-sec against per-model baselines. After model expansion:\\n\\n- Many evaluations used **fallback baseline values** because the baseline lookup key did not match (baseline existed under a different dimension set).\\n- Metric series were fragmented by high-cardinality labels; the regression evaluator saw many \xe2\x80\x9csmall-N\xe2\x80\x9d series and oscillated between \xe2\x80\x9cenough samples\xe2\x80\x9d and \xe2\x80\x9cnot enough samples\xe2\x80\x9d depending on which series was queried.\\n- Alert rules did not consistently enforce **minimum sample size across the same grouping** used by the evaluator, which allowed small, noisy slices to trip thresholds.\\n- incident-bot dedupe keys lacked stable identifiers for (model, version, region, sku, runtime_build), so the same underlying symptom created repeated threads/pages.", "score": 0.394935, "rank": 15, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "d67cd807-8044-52ee-8cc7-9a7214000ddd", "search_unit_id": "d67cd807-8044-52ee-8cc7-9a7214000ddd", "block_from_id": "fda46b32-b398-5767-8ff4-24ee542c02f9", "block_to_id": "50bf4522-7c8d-56dd-95bc-64b90a152934", "section_path": "Postmortem Perf Canary False Positive Alert Storm > Corrective and preventative actions (CPAs) > Implemented (completed)", "document_id": "020f768f-b114-5ca7-94ee-64447a4e421c", "document_version_id": "aac8c399-c8c4-5179-91b0-c93e8328a769", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_58bdb9f3bb4241e089f4f2b102765db4.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-43", "heading": "Postmortem Perf Canary False Positive Alert Storm > Corrective and preventative actions (CPAs) > Implemented (completed)", "content": "Corrective and preventative actions (CPAs)\\n\\nImplemented (completed)\\n\\n- **Baseline key normalization:** Baseline lookup now uses a canonical key:\\n  - `model_id` (canonical registry ID)\\n  - `model_version` (registry version)\\n  - `runtime_build_id`\\n  - `hardware_sku`\\n  - `region`\\n  - (explicitly does *not* include prompt bucket or run IDs)\\n- **Metric label contract:** Reduced emitted labels to an approved set; added a CI check that fails if new labels are added without review.\\n- **Evaluator \xe2\x80\x9cbaseline missing\xe2\x80\x9d behavior:** Baseline missing is now treated as **\xe2\x80\x9ccanary unhealthy\xe2\x80\x9d** (warn once) rather than \xe2\x80\x9cassume default regression thresholds\xe2\x80\x9d.\\n- **Min-sample + dampening alignment:** Alert rules now match the evaluator grouping and require:\\n  - minimum N requests per grouping\\n  - sustained breach across multiple evaluation intervals\\n- **Incident-bot dedupe key update:** Dedupe keys now include (model_id, model_version, region, hardware_sku, runtime_build_id, alert_type).", "score": 0.390443, "rank": 16, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "d74399fb-275f-5fdf-8f6b-ee7950d57fd6", "search_unit_id": "d74399fb-275f-5fdf-8f6b-ee7950d57fd6", "block_from_id": "904875f5-0603-5f66-b912-4a16526b6a7f", "block_to_id": "808f8a13-a2a5-5c77-a49d-285a0f26dfa4", "section_path": "Postmortem Perf Canary False Positive Alert Storm > Timeline (UTC)", "document_id": "020f768f-b114-5ca7-94ee-64447a4e421c", "document_version_id": "aac8c399-c8c4-5179-91b0-c93e8328a769", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_58bdb9f3bb4241e089f4f2b102765db4.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-14", "heading": "Postmortem Perf Canary False Positive Alert Storm > Timeline (UTC)", "content": "Timeline (UTC)\\n\\n- **2026-02-12 16:05** \xe2\x80\x93 Expanded canary coverage from 3 \xe2\x86\x92 8 models in us-east; enabled paging rule for \xe2\x80\x9ctop models\xe2\x80\x9d.\\n- **16:12** \xe2\x80\x93 First warning alerts fire for 3 models (p95 latency regression > threshold). Incident-bot starts threads.\\n- **16:16** \xe2\x80\x93 Paging alerts begin for a top model; on-call acknowledges.\\n- **16:18** \xe2\x80\x93 Additional paging alerts fire for multiple models; dedupe fails and creates multiple parallel threads.\\n- **16:23** \xe2\x80\x93 Runtime on-call compares canary runtime-only latency vs customer e2e; no matching regression observed.\\n- **16:28** \xe2\x80\x93 Telemetry team notices time series fragmentation: unexpected label combinations, very low samples per series.\\n- **16:34** \xe2\x80\x93 SRE disables paging rules (keeps warnings) and increases dampening window.\\n- **16:41** \xe2\x80\x93 Baseline store reads show frequent \xe2\x80\x9cbaseline not found\xe2\x80\x9d with fallback to default thresholds.\\n- **16:46** \xe2\x80\x93 Canary config rolled back to previous 3-model set; alert volume drops.\\n- **17:02** \xe2\x80\x93 Incident declared resolved; follow-up investigation assigned.", "score": 0.349414, "rank": 17, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "2b993d8a-324d-5d8b-94cd-1c296bebe114", "search_unit_id": "2b993d8a-324d-5d8b-94cd-1c296bebe114", "block_from_id": "af19b812-b2ba-57e3-adfd-03063bbf82a5", "block_to_id": "58f0446c-9ca1-52bb-89f0-9fadd1165c6a", "section_path": "Postmortem Perf Canary False Positive Alert Storm > Follow-up validation plan", "document_id": "020f768f-b114-5ca7-94ee-64447a4e421c", "document_version_id": "aac8c399-c8c4-5179-91b0-c93e8328a769", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_58bdb9f3bb4241e089f4f2b102765db4.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-57", "heading": "Postmortem Perf Canary False Positive Alert Storm > Follow-up validation plan", "content": "Follow-up validation plan\\n\\nBefore re-enabling paging and using signals as rollout gates, we will:\\n\\n1. Run a **7-day warning-only bake** with expanded coverage and confirm:\\n   - baseline hit-rate > 99.5%\\n   - no unexpected label growth (cardinality budget)\\n   - alert volume within noise budget\\n2. Re-enable paging for **one top model** in one region with clear success criteria.\\n3. Only after stable paging, enable rollout gate consumption in \xe2\x80\x9cadvisory\xe2\x80\x9d mode for 2 weeks, then move to \xe2\x80\x9cblocking\xe2\x80\x9d mode.", "score": 0.341584, "rank": 18, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "48b911a7-9f2d-5db7-8558-9d4c1a99bb42", "search_unit_id": "48b911a7-9f2d-5db7-8558-9d4c1a99bb42", "block_from_id": "790b0500-fc58-59c0-9f06-5c47bc23c1a0", "block_to_id": "18763212-ff2c-5f07-9144-ea9d60ee2884", "section_path": "Postmortem Perf Canary False Positive Alert Storm > Corrective and preventative actions (CPAs) > Planned (in progress)", "document_id": "020f768f-b114-5ca7-94ee-64447a4e421c", "document_version_id": "aac8c399-c8c4-5179-91b0-c93e8328a769", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_58bdb9f3bb4241e089f4f2b102765db4.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-46", "heading": "Postmortem Perf Canary False Positive Alert Storm > Corrective and preventative actions (CPAs) > Planned (in progress)", "content": "Planned (in progress)\\n\\n- **Region/SKU-aware thresholds:** Allow thresholds that differ by SKU/region where variance is known to differ (documented + versioned).\\n- **Baseline drift guardrails:** Rolling baselines require an explicit \xe2\x80\x9cbaseline update window\xe2\x80\x9d and block updates during rollout expansion or telemetry schema changes.\\n- **Canary alert gating:** Rollout gates will consume only \xe2\x80\x9chigh-confidence\xe2\x80\x9d regression signals (enforced min samples + stable baseline + low ingestion lag).", "score": 0.316895, "rank": 19, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "918b8002-0348-5561-9510-1c4509968098", "search_unit_id": "918b8002-0348-5561-9510-1c4509968098", "block_from_id": "7c4d27a8-8885-563d-a66f-f1026b90f1a7", "block_to_id": "fb09b8d6-3283-5191-b8d8-a2089b059f1e", "section_path": "Postmortem Perf Canary False Positive Alert Storm > Detection", "document_id": "020f768f-b114-5ca7-94ee-64447a4e421c", "document_version_id": "aac8c399-c8c4-5179-91b0-c93e8328a769", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_58bdb9f3bb4241e089f4f2b102765db4.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-12", "heading": "Postmortem Perf Canary False Positive Alert Storm > Detection", "content": "Detection\\n\\n- Detected via automated paging to the on-call channel and incident-bot threads.\\n- Secondary signal: Grafana dashboard showed many \xe2\x80\x9cregression detected\xe2\x80\x9d annotations without corresponding customer latency change.", "score": 0.322825, "rank": 20, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "8729e5bf-c462-5331-beb7-0db524306cd4", "search_unit_id": "8729e5bf-c462-5331-beb7-0db524306cd4", "block_from_id": "58d88af2-a028-5509-a8ef-de1b6c829597", "block_to_id": "2ca91e38-16e1-5d9d-a976-46815a6cc45c", "section_path": "Postmortem Perf Canary False Positive Alert Storm > Impact > Services/systems involved", "document_id": "020f768f-b114-5ca7-94ee-64447a4e421c", "document_version_id": "aac8c399-c8c4-5179-91b0-c93e8328a769", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_58bdb9f3bb4241e089f4f2b102765db4.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-10", "heading": "Postmortem Perf Canary False Positive Alert Storm > Impact > Services/systems involved", "content": "Services/systems involved\\n\\n- perf-canary service (prod)\\n- observability-pack alert rules + Grafana dashboards\\n- baseline store + baseline fetch client\\n- telemetry pipeline (metrics ingestion + aggregation)\\n- incident-bot alert handler", "score": 0.308481, "rank": 21, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "0866595b-8743-5bfb-a3c9-ae41a73974aa", "search_unit_id": "0866595b-8743-5bfb-a3c9-ae41a73974aa", "block_from_id": "0aca799d-2e15-5dec-936e-df2e98c71b82", "block_to_id": "79efee97-dab9-50a3-b64c-678a7181ed34", "section_path": "Postmortem Perf Canary False Positive Alert Storm > Action items", "document_id": "020f768f-b114-5ca7-94ee-64447a4e421c", "document_version_id": "aac8c399-c8c4-5179-91b0-c93e8328a769", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_58bdb9f3bb4241e089f4f2b102765db4.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-48", "heading": "Postmortem Perf Canary False Positive Alert Storm > Action items", "content": "Action items\\n\\n| ID | Action | Owner | Due date | Status |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| ENG-4882 | Noise reduction: add smoothing (EWMA) + sustained-breach logic + ingestion-lag guard | Allison Grant | 2026-03-08 | In progress |\\n| ENG-4874 | Baseline store versioning: pin artifact schema + backfill missing region/SKU fields | Nadia Rahman | 2026-03-01 | In progress |\\n| ENG-4873 | Publish metric contract: required labels, forbidden labels, query examples | Logan Wright | 2026-02-28 | Complete |\\n| ENG-4878 | Update alert rules to align grouping with evaluator + enforce min samples | Aisha Bello | 2026-02-26 | Complete |\\n| ENG-4883 | Update runbook: add baseline-missing play + dedupe verification steps | Rafael Mendes | 2026-02-27 | In progress |\\n| ENG-4884 | CI perf smoke: verify metrics emission + no-cardinality regression + dashboards load | Caleb Johnson | 2026-03-15 | Not started |\\n| PM-642 | Rollout gates integration: define \xe2\x80\x9cauto-pause\xe2\x80\x9d policy + UX for confidence level | Paula Mendes | 2026-03-22 | Not started |", "score": 0.293994, "rank": 22, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "746030fa-d193-53ef-b3e9-e4a713fbafcf", "search_unit_id": "746030fa-d193-53ef-b3e9-e4a713fbafcf", "block_from_id": "2f89250f-cded-5eb7-b0b9-9c4d06af6b99", "block_to_id": "56ca52b9-93d6-57d4-b06d-9a73d44a1660", "section_path": "Postmortem Perf Canary False Positive Alert Storm > Contributing factors", "document_id": "020f768f-b114-5ca7-94ee-64447a4e421c", "document_version_id": "aac8c399-c8c4-5179-91b0-c93e8328a769", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_58bdb9f3bb4241e089f4f2b102765db4.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-38", "heading": "Postmortem Perf Canary False Positive Alert Storm > Contributing factors", "content": "Contributing factors\\n\\n- **Schema change during rollout:** Metric label set changed between the initial 3-model rollout and expansion.\\n- **Baseline artifact heterogeneity:** Some baseline artifacts were generated in a prod-like shadow environment with a different region/SKU mapping.\\n- **Telemetry ingestion delay:** During the event, ingestion lag fluctuated (minutes), causing \xe2\x80\x9csawtooth\xe2\x80\x9d alert evaluation.\\n- **Runbook ambiguity:** The runbook guided \xe2\x80\x9ccompare to baseline\xe2\x80\x9d but didn\xe2\x80\x99t explicitly call out \xe2\x80\x9cbaseline not found \xe2\x86\x92 fallback thresholds\xe2\x80\x9d as a first-class failure mode.", "score": 0.290942, "rank": 23, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "032225b4-4174-53d9-88dc-f54e70fe0c00", "search_unit_id": "032225b4-4174-53d9-88dc-f54e70fe0c00", "block_from_id": "63f9d991-c068-50ac-b7b3-df4816644d74", "block_to_id": "5157e419-583c-5b22-977d-03cd517a3125", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Summary", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-4", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Summary", "content": "Summary\\n\\nThis ADR defines how the production performance canary computes baselines and evaluates regressions for per-model serving performance (primarily p95 latency and tokens/sec). It documents:\\n\\n- Baseline computation approach (rolling vs fixed) and when each is used.\\n- Regression thresholds (warning vs paging) and how they are applied.\\n- Minimum sample sizes and confidence requirements to avoid noisy alerts.\\n- Anti-flap / dedupe logic to prevent alert storms during drift, telemetry delays, or small-sample variance.", "score": 0.666326, "rank": 24, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "4d7afc92-5ba0-53c2-a694-97e612d826d5", "search_unit_id": "4d7afc92-5ba0-53c2-a694-97e612d826d5", "block_from_id": "5c4aa2bf-81ed-523c-af27-8fd745dc2af1", "block_to_id": "92efbd3f-2398-549e-b0e0-8089a7e21326", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Decision Drivers", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-12", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Decision Drivers", "content": "Decision Drivers\\n\\n1. **Low noise / high trust**: warnings should be useful; pages should be rare and high-confidence.\\n2. **Fast detection**: detect regressions within ~10\xe2\x80\x9330 minutes for top models in covered regions.\\n3. **Attribution**: baseline keys must align to dimensions needed for root cause (runtime build, kernel tags, SKU).\\n4. **Operational simplicity**: SRE/on-call should have a predictable interpretation of \xe2\x80\x9cregression vs baseline,\xe2\x80\x9d including during ongoing rollouts.\\n5. **Guardrails against drift and telemetry issues**: avoid alert storms caused by baseline drift, delayed metric ingestion, and label cardinality errors.", "score": 0.601539, "rank": 25, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "3c29ae8f-333e-571e-99bd-aa3c7ff9aeab", "search_unit_id": "3c29ae8f-333e-571e-99bd-aa3c7ff9aeab", "block_from_id": "6342bbc2-b5e5-53b5-b00c-de7baf7de1a6", "block_to_id": "587fa100-5b3c-50ef-870a-e03488252f55", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Status", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-2", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Status", "content": "Status\\n\\nPublished.", "score": 0.566377, "rank": 26, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "4e8c1606-f72d-5136-9ce8-fabf763777a9", "search_unit_id": "4e8c1606-f72d-5136-9ce8-fabf763777a9", "block_from_id": "ede7f74b-3902-5925-8fcd-a7d922089b06", "block_to_id": "b5d12f89-a1c5-5889-b71c-39ea90694fee", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Context / Problem", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-7", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Context / Problem", "content": "Context / Problem\\n\\nRedwood\xe2\x80\x99s serving runtime changes frequently (kernel selection updates, scheduler heuristics, model config changes, GPU fleet changes, and staged rollouts). We need an always-on canary that:\\n\\n- Detects real p95 latency regressions and throughput drops early.\\n- Produces actionable signals for attribution (kernel vs scheduler vs infra).\\n- Avoids paging on expected variance and baseline drift (e.g., slow fleet mix changes or regional differences).\\n\\nThe key design tension is baseline choice:\\n\\n- A **fixed baseline** is stable and easy to reason about during rollouts, but can become stale as hardware/driver stacks and workloads evolve.\\n- A **rolling baseline** adapts over time, but can drift (masking regressions) or create false positives if drift is misinterpreted as regression.", "score": 0.526398, "rank": 27, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "11e07925-978c-5589-a759-600b153ded4d", "search_unit_id": "11e07925-978c-5589-a759-600b153ded4d", "block_from_id": "be65d402-742a-5e74-b3dd-89badbc8f639", "block_to_id": "ec1f642b-4a53-5e57-a104-739d0f9859df", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Anti-Flap, Dedupe, and Hysteresis > Alert clear (hysteresis)", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-74", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Anti-Flap, Dedupe, and Hysteresis > Alert clear (hysteresis)", "content": "Alert clear (hysteresis)\\n\\nAlerts clear only when performance returns closer to baseline:\\n\\n- Warning clears when \xce\x94 < +6% (latency) and \xce\x94 > -5% (tokens/sec) for 3/3 windows.\\n- Paging clears when \xce\x94 < +12% (latency) and \xce\x94 > -10% (tokens/sec) for 4/4 windows.", "score": 0.531446, "rank": 28, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "048dcbdb-3ef2-5adb-aaa1-7b3d09b59784", "search_unit_id": "048dcbdb-3ef2-5adb-aaa1-7b3d09b59784", "block_from_id": "19c4bfbb-325e-5713-b50c-5c5bc52048b7", "block_to_id": "29816627-69c4-5de1-9925-50d061e7922c", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h1-0", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds", "content": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds\\n\\nSource type: confluence\\nDocument ID: dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83\\nRelease: v1.0.0\\nBenchmark: EnterpriseRAG-Bench synthetic upstream data\\nADR-0142: Perf Canary Baselines, Regression Thresholds, Min Sample Sizes, and Anti-Flap Logic", "score": 0.586367, "rank": 29, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "23d59747-a1af-515c-8f79-528d93c99d09", "search_unit_id": "23d59747-a1af-515c-8f79-528d93c99d09", "block_from_id": "9cd681e5-97cb-5376-8e9e-4eebb60ae8c3", "block_to_id": "5ea39e5e-dfbb-5c06-b745-2e0fbead0881", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Baseline Computation > Rolling health baseline (calibration only)", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-38", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Baseline Computation > Rolling health baseline (calibration only)", "content": "Rolling health baseline (calibration only)\\n\\n- Window: trailing 7 days, excluding periods marked as \xe2\x80\x9crollout\xe2\x80\x9d or \xe2\x80\x9cincident.\xe2\x80\x9d\\n- Aggregation: daily aggregates with robust statistics (median-of-daily-p95) to reduce sensitivity to short spikes.\\n- Purpose:\\n  - detect slow drift (e.g., fleet changes) that may warrant generating a new fixed baseline\\n  - suggest region/SKU overrides when variance is consistently higher", "score": 0.506408, "rank": 30, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "e9bc9610-465d-5c8f-8485-93b1933c48c3", "search_unit_id": "e9bc9610-465d-5c8f-8485-93b1933c48c3", "block_from_id": "bf3f536f-4574-5dfb-bb65-6c1bd9f7bf3a", "block_to_id": "e39cb70f-0d0a-5536-ac7f-20b2c8af4561", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Alternatives Considered > A) Pure rolling baseline (always updated)", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-85", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Alternatives Considered > A) Pure rolling baseline (always updated)", "content": "Alternatives Considered\\n\\nA) Pure rolling baseline (always updated)\\n\\nPros:\\n\\n- Adapts to drift without explicit re-baselining.\\n\\nCons:\\n\\n- Risk of masking slow regressions (baseline chases the regression).\\n- Hard to use for rollout gating (\xe2\x80\x9cmoving goalposts\xe2\x80\x9d).\\n- Susceptible to alert storms if rolling logic is impacted by label bugs or ingestion gaps.\\n\\nDecision: Rejected for paging/gating. Allowed only as a secondary calibration signal.", "score": 0.506408, "rank": 31, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "cc63d243-50c2-55eb-8bfb-acf236cce502", "search_unit_id": "cc63d243-50c2-55eb-8bfb-acf236cce502", "block_from_id": "1ce02a38-b4d8-5934-ad66-cff6f5a6f9dd", "block_to_id": "090ecf90-66c7-5753-99a3-c362c5d606c8", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Open Questions (tracked outside ADR)", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-113", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Open Questions (tracked outside ADR)", "content": "Open Questions (tracked outside ADR)\\n\\n- Whether to introduce a scheduler_profile tag in baseline keys (cardinality vs attribution benefit).\\n- Whether to page on runtime-only p95 for certain enterprise-dedicated pools (when E2E has additional network variance).\\n- Whether to incorporate a lightweight statistical test (e.g., bootstrap CI on p95) for models with unusually high variance.", "score": 0.506408, "rank": 32, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "829619c6-5bb2-5336-b599-41394e4d318e", "search_unit_id": "829619c6-5bb2-5336-b599-41394e4d318e", "block_from_id": "14f1eecf-4873-5552-ac97-9814fbb2085d", "block_to_id": "25fdbf57-8bd8-5b95-81cc-c2f2996c61b9", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Metrics Covered", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-32", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Metrics Covered", "content": "Metrics Covered\\n\\nBaselines and regressions are computed for:\\n\\n- End-to-end latency: p50, p95, p99 (ms)\\n- Runtime-only latency: p50, p95, p99 (ms) (excludes network/client)\\n- Prefill latency and decode latency (ms)\\n- Queueing time (ms) (scheduler-level)\\n- Tokens/sec (overall, and decode tokens/sec where available)\\n- Batch size distribution (for attribution)\\n- KV cache hit rate (where applicable; informational at v1)", "score": 0.506408, "rank": 33, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "88c5d01c-3c5f-5fa7-90a8-6dc5fafff25b", "search_unit_id": "88c5d01c-3c5f-5fa7-90a8-6dc5fafff25b", "block_from_id": "37c58785-6dda-52d4-840e-3f394dea5e3f", "block_to_id": "6be03658-1bd7-5836-8f16-cd17ebcdc45e", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Minimum Sample Sizes and Windowing > Minimum samples (per key K, per window)", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-64", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Minimum Sample Sizes and Windowing > Minimum samples (per key K, per window)", "content": "Minimum samples (per key K, per window)\\n\\n- **Latency metrics**: minimum **200 successful canary requests** per window.\\n- **Tokens/sec**: minimum **200 successful canary requests** per window AND minimum **50,000 total generated tokens** per window.\\n\\nIf sample requirements are not met:\\n\\n- No alert state change is allowed (prevents flapping in low-coverage periods).\\n- Dashboard panels display \xe2\x80\x9cinsufficient sample\xe2\x80\x9d annotation.\\n\\nRationale:\\n\\n- Tail latency (p95/p99) is unreliable with very small N.\\n- Tokens/sec needs sufficient token volume to smooth per-request variance.", "score": 0.506408, "rank": 34, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "17d628e9-e2bb-54f0-aaa9-04f6cff1f5c6", "search_unit_id": "17d628e9-e2bb-54f0-aaa9-04f6cff1f5c6", "block_from_id": "947e3463-cf65-52cf-aeba-ec29d28e5d30", "block_to_id": "567b9445-f73d-5d9d-a334-719d01923415", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Baseline Computation > Fixed baseline artifact", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-35", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Baseline Computation > Fixed baseline artifact", "content": "Baseline Computation\\n\\nFixed baseline artifact\\n\\n- Source: controlled perf-canary runs using the approved synthetic prompt distribution.\\n- For each baseline key, we store:\\n  - distribution summaries (p50/p95/p99) for each latency metric\\n  - mean and standard deviation where stable enough to be meaningful\\n  - tokens/sec distribution summaries\\n  - run metadata (time range, sample count, canary config version)\\n- Baseline validity: baseline is considered valid only if it meets minimum sample size requirements (see below) and passes sanity checks (no telemetry gaps, no error-rate spikes).", "score": 0.506408, "rank": 35, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "425c4351-2cde-5cad-ac56-fba6f0b5456e", "search_unit_id": "425c4351-2cde-5cad-ac56-fba6f0b5456e", "block_from_id": "bc4038c4-da3b-50a6-8ee9-0bef7e1a8c79", "block_to_id": "4a9bca18-96ce-55f7-bd43-b729429267df", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Appendix B: Ownership", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-117", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Appendix B: Ownership", "content": "Appendix B: Ownership\\n\\n- Baseline pipeline and artifact integrity: Telemetry Platform (Logan Wright) + Metrics/Baselines (Nadia Rahman)\\n- Threshold standards and paging hygiene: SRE (Sean Gallagher, Allison Grant)\\n- Model list and rollout gating integration: Serving Runtime (Noah Patel) + Release Engineering (Connor O\'Brien)", "score": 0.506408, "rank": 36, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "811fe0c3-2593-5368-9d98-111da48a8a12", "search_unit_id": "811fe0c3-2593-5368-9d98-111da48a8a12", "block_from_id": "24166ce2-b07a-5310-95d0-4fa4c91ab798", "block_to_id": "0b672f8b-beee-5069-9b9b-64d2681d7531", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Consequences > Negative / Tradeoffs", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-107", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Consequences > Negative / Tradeoffs", "content": "Negative / Tradeoffs\\n\\n- Requires baseline artifact generation whenever major runtime/kernel changes land for covered models/SKUs.\\n- Some true regressions may be detected slightly later due to sustained-breach requirements.\\n- Optional region/tier overrides add complexity when enabled.", "score": 0.506408, "rank": 37, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "3c486a70-00a3-5591-af7a-f282b4184282", "search_unit_id": "3c486a70-00a3-5591-af7a-f282b4184282", "block_from_id": "264e1948-923a-5782-8b89-7dfd048bedc5", "block_to_id": "046385dd-2761-521d-aa1b-81e7f72587a7", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Alternatives Considered > C) Per-region baselines always on", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-98", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Alternatives Considered > C) Per-region baselines always on", "content": "C) Per-region baselines always on\\n\\nPros:\\n\\n- Reduces false positives due to cross-region fleet differences.\\n\\nCons:\\n\\n- Baseline explosion (more artifacts and config), operational overhead.\\n\\nDecision: Region is optional and only enabled for models/regions where observed variance requires it.", "score": 0.506408, "rank": 38, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "4a890abb-a268-5f6c-8bd8-8190ba739f96", "search_unit_id": "4a890abb-a268-5f6c-8bd8-8190ba739f96", "block_from_id": "0deabef5-6329-59bf-ba97-4e7537d0c14d", "block_to_id": "b2185789-0f79-580c-91cf-f2daa95dc8af", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Consequences > Positive", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-104", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Consequences > Positive", "content": "Consequences\\n\\nPositive\\n\\n- Stable, versioned baselines support rollout gates and high-confidence paging.\\n- Rolling health baseline provides drift visibility without undermining safety.\\n- Anti-flap controls reduce alert noise and prevent incident-bot storms.", "score": 0.506408, "rank": 39, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "6cf7edd0-441f-57e7-9770-a53c1e8cc21c", "search_unit_id": "6cf7edd0-441f-57e7-9770-a53c1e8cc21c", "block_from_id": "dc7c96c3-d4c6-599e-893c-84cfaa30ab4e", "block_to_id": "59cddb0f-3c7c-5ec1-8952-2ab0ac38445c", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Alternatives Considered > B) Pure fixed baseline (never updated unless manual)", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-92", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Alternatives Considered > B) Pure fixed baseline (never updated unless manual)", "content": "B) Pure fixed baseline (never updated unless manual)\\n\\nPros:\\n\\n- Extremely stable; easy to reason about.\\n\\nCons:\\n\\n- Becomes stale as fleet/hardware/driver changes accumulate; increases false positives over time.\\n- Forces frequent manual work to remain relevant.\\n\\nDecision: Rejected as the only strategy. Adopted as primary baseline with explicit regeneration workflows.", "score": 0.506408, "rank": 40, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "66d7594b-8436-5080-9aef-e0793b071050", "search_unit_id": "66d7594b-8436-5080-9aef-e0793b071050", "block_from_id": "b054f4e8-bbac-5499-945b-0a4e35e10b2a", "block_to_id": "ced36613-e0ec-5017-b3a5-8e6157be9809", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Minimum Sample Sizes and Windowing > Evaluation window", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-61", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Minimum Sample Sizes and Windowing > Evaluation window", "content": "Minimum Sample Sizes and Windowing\\n\\nEvaluation window\\n\\n- Default evaluation window: **10 minutes**.\\n- Windows are evaluated continuously and require sustained breach rules (see anti-flap).", "score": 0.506408, "rank": 41, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "3673b29b-cfa7-5efa-8aa9-5ff8dd44023f", "search_unit_id": "3673b29b-cfa7-5efa-8aa9-5ff8dd44023f", "block_from_id": "f48154e7-ac7a-58ae-bcf2-0955daab830c", "block_to_id": "cba6a8ae-ef1b-5d20-827b-830f9be9b71c", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Default Thresholds (v1) > Latency (p95 end-to-end)", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-52", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Default Thresholds (v1) > Latency (p95 end-to-end)", "content": "Latency (p95 end-to-end)\\n\\n- Warning: p95 E2E latency **+10%** vs baseline for **2 out of 3** consecutive evaluation windows.\\n- Paging: p95 E2E latency **+20%** vs baseline for **3 out of 4** consecutive evaluation windows.", "score": 0.506408, "rank": 42, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "f6abcbc2-e8a0-55b0-b881-e05dd8c11289", "search_unit_id": "f6abcbc2-e8a0-55b0-b881-e05dd8c11289", "block_from_id": "fa187574-c2df-5d98-94fe-8213b8cb55e1", "block_to_id": "2f7b581d-7720-58fa-b392-2204cfd086bc", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Changelog", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-119", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Changelog", "content": "Changelog\\n\\n- 2026-02-12: Clarified cooldown timers, added telemetry delay protection rule, and tightened tokens/sec minimum token count requirement.", "score": 0.506408, "rank": 43, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "a40f8598-2951-5778-a15f-0707398d2692", "search_unit_id": "a40f8598-2951-5778-a15f-0707398d2692", "block_from_id": "327d6dc6-1a59-5f1e-9cd7-461d51c1c722", "block_to_id": "feb530dd-d138-526c-96b8-1f12f157c7ec", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Anti-Flap, Dedupe, and Hysteresis > Telemetry delay protection", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-83", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Anti-Flap, Dedupe, and Hysteresis > Telemetry delay protection", "content": "Telemetry delay protection\\n\\nIf telemetry ingestion delay exceeds 2x the evaluation window (e.g., >20 minutes), alert evaluation is suspended and a separate \xe2\x80\x9ctelemetry delay\xe2\x80\x9d warning is emitted to #eng-platform.", "score": 0.506408, "rank": 44, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "7eb972fc-c055-5e16-b256-ab258597491c", "search_unit_id": "7eb972fc-c055-5e16-b256-ab258597491c", "block_from_id": "1c77e0e1-0c02-5b5d-967f-9caf072d965c", "block_to_id": "e38a1a5f-91dc-5cbb-a233-80d234957dba", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Anti-Flap, Dedupe, and Hysteresis > Dedupe key", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-80", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Anti-Flap, Dedupe, and Hysteresis > Dedupe key", "content": "Dedupe key\\n\\nIncident-bot dedupes based on:\\n\\n- model_id + model_version + runtime_build_id + kernel_set_id + hardware_sku (+ region if present) + metric_type + severity", "score": 0.506408, "rank": 45, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "27698a5d-d93e-55bc-9e85-1ea0b026d5f6", "search_unit_id": "27698a5d-d93e-55bc-9e85-1ea0b026d5f6", "block_from_id": "52c4cb61-c56f-5cf9-a932-5f55b94704eb", "block_to_id": "4d4a53fe-b57d-5204-82ee-bd71a6c3810e", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Regression Definition", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-40", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Regression Definition", "content": "Regression Definition\\n\\nWe define regression as a statistically and operationally meaningful deviation from the fixed baseline.", "score": 0.506408, "rank": 46, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "727341b2-7485-5498-b317-52936582e1ca", "search_unit_id": "727341b2-7485-5498-b317-52936582e1ca", "block_from_id": "72526615-4309-5311-b017-ea8575fcc639", "block_to_id": "461f557f-a9ae-56b2-a8f6-4cdb7deb0121", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Anti-Flap, Dedupe, and Hysteresis > Sustained breach logic", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-70", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Anti-Flap, Dedupe, and Hysteresis > Sustained breach logic", "content": "Anti-Flap, Dedupe, and Hysteresis\\n\\nSustained breach logic\\n\\nWe use \xe2\x80\x9cM out of N windows\xe2\x80\x9d to reduce sensitivity to transient spikes:\\n\\n- Warning: 2/3 consecutive windows breach\\n- Paging: 3/4 consecutive windows breach", "score": 0.506408, "rank": 47, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "84971e12-3b85-562f-a47a-0616d6f1282d", "search_unit_id": "84971e12-3b85-562f-a47a-0616d6f1282d", "block_from_id": "0fcf622d-1f62-51a2-a7a7-d75470f483a7", "block_to_id": "ede8256a-24a2-5244-87e0-c2190dbea2b1", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Default Thresholds (v1)", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-50", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Default Thresholds (v1)", "content": "Default Thresholds (v1)\\n\\nThresholds are configurable per model, with these platform defaults used unless overridden.", "score": 0.506408, "rank": 48, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "6f7e3532-0cff-5a22-ab1c-2e305dbbeba2", "search_unit_id": "6f7e3532-0cff-5a22-ab1c-2e305dbbeba2", "block_from_id": "5ee061d6-2f11-5f40-a4e4-e60a4b37ec3b", "block_to_id": "8f416c20-0392-5b72-8f2c-8ee37dee92c9", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Implementation Notes / Requirements", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-109", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Implementation Notes / Requirements", "content": "Implementation Notes / Requirements\\n\\n1. Baseline artifacts must be stored in an access-controlled, versioned store with auditability (who/when created).\\n2. Canary config must support per-model overrides:\\n   - thresholds by severity\\n   - whether region-specific keys are enabled\\n   - \xe2\x80\x9ctop model\xe2\x80\x9d flag affecting paging eligibility\\n3. Alert payloads must include:\\n   - observed value, baseline value, percent change\\n   - sample counts and token counts\\n   - runtime_build_id, kernel_set_id, hardware_sku, region\\n   - links to dashboards, traces, and runbook\\n4. Changes to default thresholds must go through an ADR update or SRE-approved change request.", "score": 0.472152, "rank": 49, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "ccfb0303-74f9-5f6e-8453-2020a0773c5b", "search_unit_id": "ccfb0303-74f9-5f6e-8453-2020a0773c5b", "block_from_id": "86f27c7d-f46e-5b7c-a28c-65cdf007658d", "block_to_id": "65b7d661-0827-5da3-b943-5e2ade9df157", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Decision", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-14", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Decision", "content": "Decision\\n\\nWe adopt a **hybrid baseline strategy**:\\n\\n1) **Primary baseline = Fixed, versioned baseline per (model, model_version, runtime_build, kernel_set_id, hardware_sku) with optional region override**\\n\\n- Baselines are generated from controlled canary runs (prod-like load) and stored as immutable artifacts.\\n- Baselines are explicitly tied to the runtime build and kernel selection identifiers so comparisons remain meaningful.\\n- This is the baseline used for rollout gating and for paging.\\n\\n2) **Secondary baseline = Rolling \xe2\x80\x9chealth baseline\xe2\x80\x9d used for drift monitoring and threshold calibration (not for paging)**\\n\\n- We compute a rolling reference from recent stable periods (default: last 7 days) to detect slow environmental drift and to inform recalibration.\\n- Rolling baseline is not used to auto-suppress a fixed-baseline regression; it is used as a triage and tuning signal.\\n\\n3) **Baseline freeze rules**\\n\\n- During a runtime rollout (canary/gradual), the baseline used for alerts is **frozen** to the most recent fixed baseline for the currently active runtime build on that ring.\\n- If an incident is declared for a perf regression, baseline updates are **paused** for affected keys until incident closure.\\n\\n4) **Threshold evaluation requires minimum sample size + sustained breach + hysteresis**\\n\\n- Alerts require both a minimum number of canary requests and sustained breach across multiple evaluation windows.\\n- Alert clear conditions are stricter than trigger conditions (hysteresis) to reduce flapping.", "score": 0.448872, "rank": 50, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "82e5de62-ab2f-52ee-a327-f8ae85a98506", "search_unit_id": "82e5de62-ab2f-52ee-a327-f8ae85a98506", "block_from_id": "f2167597-0d78-51c4-98ac-6e6b5709a336", "block_to_id": "ee939171-e136-5ca2-917d-48f955d2b50a", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Default Thresholds (v1) > Throughput (tokens/sec)", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-54", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Default Thresholds (v1) > Throughput (tokens/sec)", "content": "Throughput (tokens/sec)\\n\\n- Warning: tokens/sec **-8%** vs baseline for **2 out of 3** windows.\\n- Paging: tokens/sec **-15%** vs baseline for **3 out of 4** windows.", "score": 0.506408, "rank": 51, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "dce37664-4c7a-5cd2-aff9-2b8b05d93b21", "search_unit_id": "dce37664-4c7a-5cd2-aff9-2b8b05d93b21", "block_from_id": "6d4588a0-f081-5ee0-9394-bddc1b49fd75", "block_to_id": "648b9fdc-1229-5e63-b445-0ffa22b1fc1a", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Default Thresholds (v1) > Runtime-only attribution signals (non-paging by default)", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-56", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Default Thresholds (v1) > Runtime-only attribution signals (non-paging by default)", "content": "Runtime-only attribution signals (non-paging by default)\\n\\nThese are emitted to dashboards and included in alert payloads, but do not page unless explicitly enabled for a model:\\n\\n- Queueing time p95 +25% (suggests scheduler/fleet saturation)\\n- Prefill p95 +15% (suggests kernel/model config regressions)\\n- Decode p95 +15% (suggests kernel/model config regressions)\\n\\nRationale:\\n\\n- Paging should be driven by end-to-end customer-impact proxy (E2E p95 and tokens/sec).\\n- Breakdown metrics improve triage but are often noisier and more sensitive to load mix.", "score": 0.388608, "rank": 52, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "f37db93e-b81a-5ba4-8d45-7c2934d4367c", "search_unit_id": "f37db93e-b81a-5ba4-8d45-7c2934d4367c", "block_from_id": "c64b2220-dfdd-542d-9218-86e48adf63ea", "block_to_id": "91573533-ff3d-56bc-8378-b75fd72b0c0d", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Regression Definition > Threshold levels", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-47", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Regression Definition > Threshold levels", "content": "Threshold levels\\n\\nTwo alert levels exist:\\n\\n- **Warning**: actionable signal for runtime team triage; routed to #eng-runtime.\\n- **Paging**: sustained, high-confidence regression on top models; routed to on-call rotation.", "score": 0.381699, "rank": 53, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "a445ba42-6f63-5e30-bbff-d9e81f181849", "search_unit_id": "a445ba42-6f63-5e30-bbff-d9e81f181849", "block_from_id": "665a2693-48f7-5964-b2f2-5385ab4f0885", "block_to_id": "1f2673e0-819a-5ceb-a3a7-130f139dfaca", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Anti-Flap, Dedupe, and Hysteresis > Cooldown", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-77", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Anti-Flap, Dedupe, and Hysteresis > Cooldown", "content": "Cooldown\\n\\nAfter an alert transitions to firing, we enforce a cooldown before re-triggering a new incident thread for the same key:\\n\\n- Warning cooldown: 60 minutes\\n- Paging cooldown: 120 minutes", "score": 0.334357, "rank": 54, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "7b700c43-46fe-59a4-a0bb-d3cd1c2a7f01", "search_unit_id": "7b700c43-46fe-59a4-a0bb-d3cd1c2a7f01", "block_from_id": "b5a87d99-1d52-5998-9ee1-f3bc88581b1a", "block_to_id": "96de10ac-0596-5756-8478-56b0fc50e039", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Rollout Guidance", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-111", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Rollout Guidance", "content": "Rollout Guidance\\n\\n- Phase 1 (single region): warnings only, tune per-model overrides until noise is acceptable.\\n- Phase 2: enable paging only for top models with proven low variance and stable baselines.\\n- Phase 3: integrate gating with release engineering once paging signal is trusted (warning can gate early as \xe2\x80\x9csoft fail,\xe2\x80\x9d paging as \xe2\x80\x9chard fail\xe2\x80\x9d).", "score": 0.304117, "rank": 55, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "a5d10308-dc0f-5092-9f54-e1a24e98ff47", "search_unit_id": "a5d10308-dc0f-5092-9f54-e1a24e98ff47", "block_from_id": "0d177d2f-be12-544e-9675-b65e52bb4ff4", "block_to_id": "ec4642d0-ae24-5d9b-8056-43ad7ef0f699", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Appendix A: Example Per-Model Overrides (illustrative)", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-115", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Appendix A: Example Per-Model Overrides (illustrative)", "content": "Appendix A: Example Per-Model Overrides (illustrative)\\n\\n- Top model (customer-critical): paging at +15% p95 E2E, -12% tokens/sec, stricter min token count.\\n- High-variance model: warning only, wider thresholds (+15% / -10%), region-specific baseline enabled.\\n- New kernel rollout candidate: temporary tighter warning (+8%) during rollout ring, but paging remains at default until validated.", "score": 0.294072, "rank": 56, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "0bab4b61-2347-5b3a-845d-6f3bba6297b1", "search_unit_id": "0bab4b61-2347-5b3a-845d-6f3bba6297b1", "block_from_id": "09185fbc-2dd2-59de-843f-99f5f6a2f45f", "block_to_id": "9cc7b2e5-b278-5170-b574-b901af5c2821", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Baseline Keys (What defines \xe2\x80\x9clike-for-like\xe2\x80\x9d)", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-24", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Baseline Keys (What defines \xe2\x80\x9clike-for-like\xe2\x80\x9d)", "content": "Baseline Keys (What defines \xe2\x80\x9clike-for-like\xe2\x80\x9d)\\n\\nBaseline artifacts and regression evaluation are keyed by the following dimensions:\\n\\n**Required baseline key fields (v1):**\\n\\n- model_id (canonical model identifier)\\n- model_version (registry version / hash)\\n- runtime_build_id (serving runtime build tag)\\n- kernel_set_id (kernel selection/version identifier)\\n- hardware_sku (e.g., H100-80GB, A100-80GB)\\n\\n**Optional fields (only when variance requires it):**\\n\\n- region (enabled for regions with materially different fleet/network characteristics)\\n- capacity_tier (hosted vs dedicated pools) when pools differ materially\\n\\nNotes:\\n\\n- We do NOT key baselines by customer, endpoint, or prompt content (privacy + cardinality constraints).\\n- Scheduler configuration flags that materially change behavior must be reflected either in runtime_build_id or an explicit scheduler_profile tag (introduced only if needed; kept off by default to control cardinality).", "score": 0.277056, "rank": 57, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "2eebb20a-591d-506c-b85a-40583bdabfb8", "search_unit_id": "2eebb20a-591d-506c-b85a-40583bdabfb8", "block_from_id": "6534390e-d337-5fa5-867c-5f7d360901cd", "block_to_id": "5d87204c-d905-5235-a7bd-28e6127d93ce", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Regression Definition > Core comparison method (v1)", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-42", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Regression Definition > Core comparison method (v1)", "content": "Core comparison method (v1)\\n\\nFor each metric M and key K in each evaluation window W:\\n\\n- Compute observed metric value O(K, W).\\n- Fetch baseline value B(K) and baseline variability estimates when available.\\n- Compute percent change: \xce\x94 = (O - B) / B.\\n\\nWe use percent change thresholds with guardrails (min samples + sustained breach). Percent thresholds are chosen because:\\n\\n- Different models have different absolute latencies.\\n- p95 is the primary SLO-relevant tail metric.", "score": 0.276161, "rank": 58, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}], "events": [], "entities": [], "relations": [], "source_hits": [], "summary": "The new alerting approach groups model-serving requests by stages they pass through using **token stage cohorting** and a **route x stage alert matrix**. This grouping is based on stage-level metrics such as token counts per stage, KV-cache hit patterns, and decode-batch size, allowing the system to compute a deterministic cohort key per invocation. The alert route-matrix generator then biases escalation to the top-k stages most likely responsible for SLO violations, thereby reducing noisy alerts and speeding up root cause analysis by focusing on the relevant stages. [2]", "citations": [{"kind": "internal", "n": 2, "document_id": "0303466c-7aac-5c67-aacb-e29c1951d5c0", "document_version_id": "730b4462-65f2-5ed8-a97f-f3fc91d91088", "document_name": "github__dsid_c1a6a71323c04c1ba5445aadea340362.md", "version_no": 1, "chunk_id": "9c804c59-28d4-5181-a82c-4d21a74164b9", "search_unit_id": "9c804c59-28d4-5181-a82c-4d21a74164b9", "block_from_id": "b50bd054-8862-56ed-877d-fa49bddb3786", "block_to_id": "bf6cdc59-7507-5d6d-84d0-f5eeda9d7618", "section_path": "Pr 867001 Introduce Token Stage Cohorting And Route Matrix Alerting", "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h1-0", "heading": "Pr 867001 Introduce Token Stage Cohorting And Route Matrix Alerting", "snippet": "Pr 867001 Introduce Token Stage Cohorting And Route Matrix Alerting Source type: github Document ID: dsid_c1a6a71323c04c1ba5445aadea340362 Release: v1.0.0 Benchmark: EnterpriseRAG-Bench synthetic upstream data introduce-token-stage-cohorting-and-route-matrix-alerting Context: long-tail token cost and multi-stage latency spikes frequently surface only when a request traverses several model-serving stages (tokenization, encoder, decode, fallback). Existing alerts were per-route and per-quantile but lacked a compact way to group requests by \'stage footprint\' and automatically route alerting weight to the stage(s) most likely responsible. Motivation: reduce alert noise and accelerate RCA by grouping invocations int\xe2\x80\xa6", "score": 0.7016, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}], "answer_status": "answered", "no_answer_reason": null, "exploration_id": null, "stats": {"canonical_index": true, "ready_versions": 81, "requested_top_k": null, "candidate_top_k": 64, "candidate_unit_pool_limit": 1024, "candidate_pool_saturated": true, "candidate_units_before_cap": 157, "candidate_units_after_cap": 157, "candidate_units_truncated": 0, "semantic_candidates": 99, "lexical_candidates": 83, "candidates": 157, "relevant": 157, "filtered_irrelevant": 0, "fusion_method": "rrf", "selection_method": "authorized_content_dedup_mmr", "cross_scope_merge": "rank_interleave", "coverage": {"candidate_count": 128, "deduplicated_count": 0, "diversity_weight": 0.5, "near_duplicate_similarity": 0.98, "required_anchor_count": 0, "covered_anchor_count": 0, "anchor_coverage": "not_required", "status": "unknown", "canonical_locator_verified": true, "semantic_answerability": "unknown"}, "routing": {"planner": {"planner_version": "qsp-v1", "requested_strategy": "AUTO", "effective_strategy": "LOCAL_FACTUAL", "modifiers": [], "reason_codes": ["DEFAULT_LOCAL_FACTUAL"], "multi_hop_eligible": false}, "request_snapshot_id": "e97d156c-759b-444a-af41-eaac17b63323", "groups": [{"project_id": "b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c", "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "partition_id": "b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c", "snapshot_id": "903abeac-1bc1-4081-a0f2-a040e25c78d6", "request_snapshot_id": "e97d