14:03:11  DEBUG    [d99e21dce0c24bb4]  sse_starlette.sse  chunk: b'event: result\r\ndata: {"query": "How long is the validity period for the telemetry driven runbook author certification from the operator training bootcamp?", "sections": [{"chunk_id": "d1d375d2-778d-52fb-83f5-f90e8efe324e", "search_unit_id": "d1d375d2-778d-52fb-83f5-f90e8efe324e", "block_from_id": "bf2fcbda-3766-5633-b55a-a93a60d1c8bf", "block_to_id": "2d96f9f9-ea0e-5c60-9bf1-223d1772afba", "section_path": "Runbook Writing And Telemetry Bootcamp Curriculum 2026", "document_id": "44347108-84e3-5700-88c1-0908504bfbbc", "document_version_id": "272e8348-5212-5c0b-90e9-c0f139aa873a", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_46a4cb87db414e769f2df86f01626948.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h1-0", "heading": "Runbook Writing And Telemetry Bootcamp Curriculum 2026", "content": "Runbook Writing And Telemetry Bootcamp Curriculum 2026\\n\\nSource type: confluence\\nDocument ID: dsid_46a4cb87db414e769f2df86f01626948\\nRelease: v1.0.0\\nBenchmark: EnterpriseRAG-Bench synthetic upstream data\\nRunbook Writing and Telemetry Bootcamp Curriculum \xe2\x80\x94 Operator Training\\n\\nSummary\\n\\nThis page documents a repeatable, instructor-led bootcamp to train platform operators and engineers to write high-quality runbooks that are telemetry-driven, testable, and maintainable. The curriculum is designed for new operators, service owners, and incident responders who will author or own runbooks for platform services (prefix cache, allocator, tenant-slicing, model-variant router).\\n\\nAudience\\n\\n- Platform operators and SREs\\n- Service owners in eng-platform and eng-serving-runtime\\n- Oncall engineers who respond to latency/cost incidents\\n\\nLearning objectives (measurable)\\n\\n1. Produce a runbook that contains a clear escalation path, data-driven detection predicates, and an operator checklist.\\n2. Write two telemetry queries (one metric-based, one log-based) that reliably surface the condition the runbook describes.\\n3. Create a synthetic verification (unit) that validates the runbook\xe2\x80\x99s detection predicates against a small replay dataset.\\n4. Implement a post-incident update cycle and link to the action in the runbook so it can be closed by the owner.\\n\\nCurriculum overview (3-day instructor-led)\\nDay 0 \xe2\x80\x94 Prework (self-paced)\\n\\n- Read: \\"Runbook authoring and maintenance guidelines\\" (required).\\n- Complete a short quiz on SLO definitions and common platform failure modes.\\n- Setup: access to Grafana/Tempo, Kibana, and a sandbox tenant. Confirm permissions with infra-oncall.\\n\\nDay 1 \xe2\x80\x94 Foundations and detection\\n\\n- Morning: Lecture (1.5 hr) \xe2\x80\x94 Runbook structure and the telemetry-first principle.\\n  - Sections: Summary, Impact, Detection (metric + log predicates), Immediate actions, Escalation, Rollback, Postmortem link.\\n  - Example services: kv-prefix-cache, dynamic-allocator, model-variant-router.\\n- Lab (2.5 hr): Write detection predicates for a synthetic latency spike:\\n  1) Metric predicate: p95 latency > 300ms for 5m AND error rate > 1% for 2m.\\n  2) Log predicate: queries that include \\"kv-cache:miss\\" and \\"eviction-reason=reshuffle\\" for >50 events in 10m.\\n- Homework: Author a first draft runbook for a provided scenario.\\n\\nDay 2 \xe2\x80\x94 Triage, actions, and testability\\n\\n- Morning: Workshop (2 hr) \xe2\x80\x94 Mapping telemetry to operator actions.\\n  - Instrumentation checklist: SLI names, tag conventions (region, tenant_id, model_variant), and minimum retention expectations (30 days for alerts, 90 days for postmortem traces).\\n  - Ownership patterns: primary, secondary, oncall-runbook-maintainer.\\n- Lab (3 hr): Implement a synthetic verification for the runbook detection predicates using the synthetic-replay harness.\\n  - Deliverable: three test cases (baseline, transient spike, persistent degradation).\\n- Evening: Peer review session \xe2\x80\x94 teams exchange runbooks and provide 3 actionable comments.\\n\\nDay 3 \xe2\x80\x94 Escalation, de-escalation, and lifecycle\\n\\n- Morning: Tabletop simulation (2 hr) \xe2\x80\x94 live incident with operator rotation. Measured outcomes: time to detection, time to mitigate, number of escalations, checklist completeness.\\n- Afternoon: Retrospective (1.5 hr) \xe2\x80\x94 calibrate SLOs and adjust detection thresholds.\\n- Closing: Runbook merge checklist and post-incident update procedure.\\n\\nAssessment and certification\\n\\n- Pass criteria: runbook accepted in repo (PR merged), synthetic verification green, and at least one successful tabletop participation.\\n- Certificate: \\"Telemetry-Driven Runbook Author (Redwood)\\" valid for 18 months. Re-certification: 2-hour refresher + one tabletop.\\n\\nDelivery model and resourcing", "score": 0.842182, "rank": 0, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "ada5eeaa-7821-5cb2-8b91-2c6db85d02d3", "search_unit_id": "ada5eeaa-7821-5cb2-8b91-2c6db85d02d3", "block_from_id": "36c8f12f-02cb-55e1-b898-840eac831c9b", "block_to_id": "36c8f12f-02cb-55e1-b898-840eac831c9b", "section_path": "Runbook Writing And Telemetry Bootcamp Curriculum 2026", "document_id": "44347108-84e3-5700-88c1-0908504bfbbc", "document_version_id": "272e8348-5212-5c0b-90e9-c0f139aa873a", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_46a4cb87db414e769f2df86f01626948.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "list-40", "heading": "Runbook Writing And Telemetry Bootcamp Curriculum 2026", "content": "- 2025-09-10: Created by Priya Kapoor (initial curriculum draft).\\n- 2025-11-02: Added PromQL examples and tabletop scenarios (reviewers: Ethan, Marta).\\n- 2026-02-15: Adjusted assessment criteria and certification validity (finalized).", "score": 0.730374, "rank": 1, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "03cfd99c-43b8-5947-a128-6a5b47bf2a80", "search_unit_id": "03cfd99c-43b8-5947-a128-6a5b47bf2a80", "block_from_id": "20f03d69-75bb-5fcb-a936-b64581df9860", "block_to_id": "1e3c15de-7c70-587e-9b16-72aec0a4ed60", "section_path": "Runbook Writing And Telemetry Bootcamp Curriculum 2026", "document_id": "44347108-84e3-5700-88c1-0908504bfbbc", "document_version_id": "272e8348-5212-5c0b-90e9-c0f139aa873a", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_46a4cb87db414e769f2df86f01626948.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "list-19", "heading": "Runbook Writing And Telemetry Bootcamp Curriculum 2026", "content": "- Instructor: Platform training lead (approx. 1 dedicated trainer per cohort of 12).\\n- Duration: 3 days (24 total hours including pre/post work).\\n- Environment: sandbox cluster with one copy of kv-prefix-cache and dynamic-allocator seeded with synthetic load.\\n- Tools: Grafana (dashboards pre-built), Loki/Kibana, Tempo (trace slices), synthetic-replay harness (repo: infra/synthetic-replay).\\n\\nRunbook template (required fields)\\n1) Title (single line)\\n2) Summary (1\xe2\x80\x932 sentences) \xe2\x80\x94 short impact statement\\n3) Owner (primary, secondary) \xe2\x80\x94 team and pager alias\\n4) Impact and user-visible symptoms \xe2\x80\x94 list\\n5) Detection\\n\\n   - Metric predicate (exact expression)\\n   - Log predicate (example query)\\n   - Trace pattern (optional)\\n\\n6) Immediate mitigation steps (numbered)\\n7) Escalation path (names/roles and contact method)\\n8) Safe rollback / service-level de-escalation (how to revert changes)\\n9) Diagnostics checklist (commands, queries, dashboard links)\\n10) Post-incident required actions (TTR SLA for update: 7 days)\\n11) Verification tests (links to synthetic tests)\\n12) Related runbooks and runbook-ids\\nRequired telemetry examples (copyable)\\n\\n- Metric predicate (PromQL):\\n  sum(rate(request_duration_ms_bucket{job=\\"kv-prefix-cache\\",le=\\"0.3\\"}[5m])) by (region) / sum(rate(request_duration_ms_count{job=\\"kv-prefix-cache\\"}[5m])) by (region) > 0.95\\n- Log predicate (Loki):\\n  {app=\\"kv-prefix-cache\\",env=\\"prod\\"} |= \\"kv-cache:miss\\" | json | tenant_id!=\\"\\" | count_over_time(10m) > 50\\n- Trace predicate (Tempo/trace): search for spans with operation.name =~ \\"kv-prefix-cache.*evict\\" and duration > 100ms, aggregated by tenant_id.\\n\\nSynthetic verification example (bash)\\n\\n- Reproduce a persistent-degradation case with synthetic-replay:\\n  1) ./synthetic-replay --scenario=kv-cache-eviction-heavy --duration=15m --tenants=10\\n  2) Wait for PromQL predicate to evaluate true in the sandbox (check metrics-exporter).\\n  3) Run owner diagnostics script: tools/diagnostics/kv-cache-inspect.sh --tenant <id>\\n\\nTabletop scenarios (catalog)\\n\\n- KV cache shard reshuffle during black-box warmup\\n- Region-specific allocator starvation (spot preemption cascade)\\n- Model-variant fallback thrash causing token-cost spikes\\n- Multi-tenant cold-cache cold-start causing onboarding failures\\n\\nRetention and SLO guidance for runbooks\\n\\n- Telemetry retention required for runbook validation: metrics 30d, logs 90d, traces 90d.\\n- Alert SLO: detection-to-acknowledge median <= 3m for SEV2, median <= 1m for SEV1 during business hours.\\n- Escalation target: oncall primary owns initial mitigation within 15m of alert for SEV1.\\n\\nMerge checklist (PR to runbook repo)\\n\\n1) Runbook filled using template and linked to service metadata (service ID, repo).\\n2) At least one synthetic verification included and green in CI.\\n3) Two reviewers from different teams approved (one operator, one service owner).\\n4) Dashboard links present and dashboards annotated with threshold panels.\\n\\nOwnership and follow-up\\n\\n- Course owner: Priya Kapoor (eng-platform training). Contact: priya@redwood.ai (internal).\\n- Curriculum reviewers: see metadata above.\\n- Quarterly review: curriculum and scenario catalog reviewed each quarter; runbook templates updated at least annually.\\n\\nAppendix A \xe2\x80\x94 Example telemetry queries and dashboard panels\\n\\n- Grafana panel: \\"kv-prefix-cache p95 by region\\"\\n  - PromQL: histogram_quantile(0.95, sum(rate(request_duration_ms_bucket{job=\\\\\\"kv-prefix-cache\\\\\\"}[5m])) by (le, region))\\n- Alert rule: \\"kv-cache-p95-region-high\\"\\n  - Expression: histogram_quantile(0.95, sum(rate(request_duration_ms_bucket{job=\\\\\\"kv-prefix-cache\\\\\\"}[5m])) by (le, region)) > 0.3\\n  - For: 5m, Labels: severity=SEV2, owner=kv-cache-team\\n\\n- Example debug command (operator):\\n  - kubectl -n platform logs -l app=kv-prefix-cache --since=15m | jq -r \'.message\' | grep eviction\\n\\nRelated pages and templates\\n\\n- Runbook authoring guidelines (required pre-read) \xe2\x80\x94 /confluence/eng-platform/how-tos/runbook-authoring-and-maintenance-guidelines-2025\\n- Synthetic-replay repository \xe2\x80\x94 infra/synthetic-replay (internal git)\\n\\nRevision history", "score": 0.464048, "rank": 2, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}], "events": [], "entities": [], "relations": [], "source_hits": [], "summary": "", "citations": [], "answer_status": "pending", "no_answer_reason": null, "exploration_id": null, "stats": {"canonical_index": true, "ready_versions": 81, "requested_top_k": null, "candidate_top_k": 32, "candidate_unit_pool_limit": 1024, "candidate_pool_saturated": true, "candidate_units_before_cap": 84, "candidate_units_after_cap": 84, "candidate_units_truncated": 0, "semantic_candidates": 46, "lexical_candidates": 44, "candidates": 84, "relevant": 46, "filtered_irrelevant": 38, "fusion_method": "rrf", "selection_method": "authorized_content_dedup_mmr", "cross_scope_merge": "rank_interleave", "coverage": {"candidate_count": 64, "deduplicated_count": 0, "diversity_weight": 0.5, "near_duplicate_similarity": 0.98, "required_anchor_count": 0, "covered_anchor_count": 0, "anchor_coverage": "not_required", "status": "unknown", "canonical_locator_verified": true, "semantic_answerability": "unknown"}, "routing": {"planner": {"planner_version": "qsp-v1", "requested_strategy": "AUTO", "effective_strategy": "LOCAL_FACTUAL", "modifiers": [], "reason_codes": ["DEFAULT_LOCAL_FACTUAL"], "multi_hop_eligible": false}, "request_snapshot_id": "b8998cec-9fc0-4b24-a046-51726b8b49d3", "groups": [{"project_id": "b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c", "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "partition_id": "b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c", "snapshot_id": "c697c6c4-517d-4d6d-93c9-c9f6d1e73bb0", "request_snapshot_id": "b8998cec-9fc0-4b24-a046-51726b8b49d3", "acl_scope_fingerprint": "328ac326f64690733d385248a99659bc5ed25e83991108887c7a3367d2d5c51e", "tree_version": "tree-50bdd85ee0f1111bfecc7840", "routing_slot": "SLOT_A", "search_epoch": 2, "selected_nodes": ["5aacc2b21b3f97707f284f0fa55f0052", "9b5edf4d2d97aa2bd58ebaa1f0e11f73", "d48df15e10c1588c77a8ea414162a6c5"], "membership_count": 168, "entropy": 0.9996408089113832, "margin": 0.0014615474643761006, "broad_route": true, "reason_code": "ROUTE_UNCERTAIN_BROADENED", "fallback_reason": null, "branch_local_candidates": 61, "global_candidates": 59, "escape_recovered_candidates": 23, "escape_attempted": true, "escape_trigger": "reserved_parallel_global_escape", "local_failure": null, "escape_failure": null, "blackhole_detected": false}], "coverage": {"candidate_count": 64, "deduplicated_count": 0, "diversity_weight": 0.5, "near_duplicate_similarity": 0.98, "required_anchor_count": 0, "covered_anchor_count": 0, "anchor_coverage": "not_required", "status": "unknown", "canonical_locator_verified": true, "semantic_answerability": "unknown"}, "selection_fallback_reason": null, "multi_hop": {"eligible": false, "effective": "LOCAL_FACTUAL", "graph_expansion_attempted": false, "graph_expanded_candidates": 0, "graph_expansion_skip_reason": null}, "fallback_used": true}, "selection_fallback_reason": null, "stage_latencies_ms": {"auth_scope": 27.1, "tree_rou