14:03:24  DEBUG    [77ad975605d04ba2]  sse_starlette.sse  chunk: b'event: result\r\ndata: {"query": "What was identified as the root cause of the intermittent VPN connectivity blackholes and duplicate IP warnings for users on the corporate Wi-Fi in the SF2 building behind a specific edge switch?", "sections": [{"chunk_id": "5851ad70-5696-5b1f-b21e-5b0b7f32ea48", "search_unit_id": "5851ad70-5696-5b1f-b21e-5b0b7f32ea48", "block_from_id": "fd4cdd84-2ce4-56b4-9d8a-6f8f218c3787", "block_to_id": "fd4cdd84-2ce4-56b4-9d8a-6f8f218c3787", "section_path": "Int 460811 Edge Switch Arp Proxy Ip Duplication", "document_id": "5f928fa4-a80b-5b4b-8d56-f3a357498f86", "document_version_id": "e6c0e4cb-240e-54bc-9e85-42e72dfa44cd", "document_name": "jira__dsid_59cb294da8964683bb165a3bb615df71.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "p-2", "heading": "Int 460811 Edge Switch Arp Proxy Ip Duplication", "content": "Issue summary: Several users reporting intermittent loss of access to internal services while connected to corporate VPN. Symptoms include duplicate IP conflict alerts on endpoints, frequent VPN re-auth events, and traffic appearing to be routed to a different on-prem host (service 10.23.5.12). Impact: ~8% of VPN sessions in us-west over the last 48h experienced short blackholes (30-90s) impacting git pushes, internal CI jobs, and ssh sessions. Scope: affects users on Wi-Fi SSID \'Redwood-Corp\' behind specific edge switches in building SF2 rack 7.\\n1) Connect laptop to \'Redwood-Corp\' Wi-Fi in SF2 building (tested on macOS 13 and Ubuntu 22.04)\\n2) Establish VPN session to redwood-vpn-usw.redwood.net (WireGuard-based corporate VPN)\\n3) Trigger continuous ping to an internal host (ping -i 0.2 10.23.5.12)\\n4) Observe intermittent duplicate IP warnings on client and packets forwarded to an unexpected MAC on the L2 domain\\n5) Reproduce frequency increases when there is a short burst of multicast/mDNS traffic on the same AP\'s radio\\nClient syslog excerpt: \'kernel: arp: IP address 10.23.8.45 claimed by 00:11:22:33:44:55 (conflict)\'\\nSwitch (edge-sw-7) log: \'proxy-arp conflict detected for 10.23.8.45, source 00:66:77:88:99:AA bridging-port 5\'\\nPacket capture (pcap) snippet: ARP reply for 10.23.8.45 with two different source MACs within 120ms\\nVPN server metrics: client rekey count spike (client 10.23.8.45) correlated to timestamp 2026-03-12T14:12Z\\nInternal service (10.23.5.12) reported TCP reset spikes aligning with client blackholes\\nHypothesis 1: Edge switch proxy-arp configured for legacy NAT path is responding to ARP for VPN-assigned addresses from an overlapping DHCP pool, causing two active ARP entries on the LAN.\\nHypothesis 2: A misconfigured VXLAN/bridge on edge-sw-7 is advertising ARP for the VPN subnet into the campus L2 segment when multicast bursts occur.\\nWhat we tried: - Disabled proxy-arp on edge-sw-7 port-channel to AP group temporarily (no immediate reduction). - Isolated a suspect AP by moving a test client to a different AP (blackhole persisted only when client served by AP-7A). - Captured pcap on AP, switch uplink, and VPN server concurrently for correlated timestamps (pcaps saved to /mnt/logs/INT-460811/pcaps/).\\nPreliminary find: ARP \'gratuitous\' replies with VPN client IP are being injected by the switch\'s \'proxy-arp\' feature only when the AP\'s multicast queue exceeds threshold. The switch returns ARP for the same IP with a different MAC that matches a spare management interface in rack 7 (00:66:77:88:99:AA).\\nIntermittent connectivity loss for internal developer workflows (git/ssh/CI). Approximately 8% of VPN sessions in the SF2 us-west site affected in the window; potential for data-transfer retries and CI flakiness. No customer-facing outage but notable developer productivity hit.\\n1) Placed affected edge switch (edge-sw-7) in monitoring schedule and enabled debug logging for proxy-arp events.\\n2) Temporarily increased DHCP lease affinity for VPN pool for clients in SF2 to reduce the window for IP reuse.\\n3) Asked campus networking team to disable \'proxy-arp\' global feature on a staging switch and observe (ongoing).\\n4) Notified platform reliability and CI owners of potential re-run needs for impacted jobs (Slack #incidents and #platform-alerts).\\n2026-03-11 09:18 - Jonah Reed: Assigned to network; will coordinate switch config changes and gather pcaps. Next action: schedule maintenance window if we need to push config rollback.", "score": 0.849432, "rank": 0, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "333a37e2-157a-597d-b0cc-a2bc5a491b8e", "search_unit_id": "333a37e2-157a-597d-b0cc-a2bc5a491b8e", "block_from_id": "fd4cdd84-2ce4-56b4-9d8a-6f8f218c3787", "block_to_id": "fd4cdd84-2ce4-56b4-9d8a-6f8f218c3787", "section_path": "Int 460811 Edge Switch Arp Proxy Ip Duplication", "document_id": "5f928fa4-a80b-5b4b-8d56-f3a357498f86", "document_version_id": "e6c0e4cb-240e-54bc-9e85-42e72dfa44cd", "document_name": "jira__dsid_59cb294da8964683bb165a3bb615df71.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "p-2", "heading": "Int 460811 Edge Switch Arp Proxy Ip Duplication", "content": "2026-03-12 15:25 - Priya Shah (campus-net): Reproduced proxy-arp responses on edge-sw-7 when AP multicast queue > 70%. Suspect firmware 1.2.3 on these switches has a known misc bridging bug. Opened ticket with vendor (TAC-889233).\\n2026-03-13 08:52 - Jonah Reed: Vendor TAC confirmed the switch may respond to ARP for non-local subnets under multicast overload in 1.2.3. Recommended immediate mitigation: set \'proxy-arp disable\' on VRF for AP VLANs and upgrade firmware to 1.2.6.\\n2026-03-14 07:30 - Aisha Malik: Applied \'proxy-arp disable\' to edge-sw-7 in staged maintenance window (07:00-07:15). Monitoring: VPN rekey spikes reduced from 47/hr to 2/hr for affected clients in the first 24h.\\n2026-03-14 10:02 - Jonah Reed: Confirming RFC and rollout plan for global fix. Proposed follow-up: firmware upgrade across SF2 rack 4-9, audit for proxy-arp enabled on other edge switches, and update config baseline to explicitly disable proxy-arp for VPN/DHCP subnets.\\nSwitch firmware (1.2.3) bug caused proxy-arp behavior under high multicast load leading to ARP advertisements for VPN-assigned addresses. This created ephemeral duplicate IP assignments on the L2 domain and caused VPN clients to experience routing blackholes and rekeys.\\nMitigation applied: \'proxy-arp disable\' set on edge-sw-7 AP VLANs during maintenance window 2026-03-14 07:00-07:15.\\nTemporary workaround: increased DHCP lease affinity and moved high-multicast APs to separate RF profile to reduce multicast bursts.\\nPermanent fix: planned firmware upgrade to 1.2.6 across SF2 edge switches (racks 4-9) and config baseline change to disable proxy-arp for VPN/DHCP subnets. Vendor TAC provided patch notes and recommended upgrade path.\\nFollow-ups: - Create change request CR-2026-0415 for firmware rollout. - Run campus-wide audit script to detect \'proxy-arp\' enabled instances and remediate. - Add regression test to onboarding checklist for AP multicast stress.\\nStatus: Partial fix applied and validated; full remediation scheduled (see CR-2026-0415).", "score": 0.73578, "rank": 1, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "c4bdfef3-8d2c-59ab-95b5-ce7db7f8ec23", "search_unit_id": "c4bdfef3-8d2c-59ab-95b5-ce7db7f8ec23", "block_from_id": "e770368f-ef5f-5985-a96e-901a2c4ae259", "block_to_id": "5874d051-a5b9-521b-9783-c732b73da90c", "section_path": "Int 460811 Edge Switch Arp Proxy Ip Duplication", "document_id": "5f928fa4-a80b-5b4b-8d56-f3a357498f86", "document_version_id": "e6c0e4cb-240e-54bc-9e85-42e72dfa44cd", "document_name": "jira__dsid_59cb294da8964683bb165a3bb615df71.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h1-0", "heading": "Int 460811 Edge Switch Arp Proxy Ip Duplication", "content": "Int 460811 Edge Switch Arp Proxy Ip Duplication\\n\\nSource type: jira\\nDocument ID: dsid_59cb294da8964683bb165a3bb615df71\\nRelease: v1.0.0\\nBenchmark: EnterpriseRAG-Bench synthetic upstream data\\nEdge switch ARP proxying leads to VPN client IP duplication and intermittent routing to wrong host", "score": 0.657697, "rank": 2, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "0a58a634-684f-585b-8094-d0bebd88491f", "search_unit_id": "0a58a634-684f-585b-8094-d0bebd88491f", "block_from_id": "4c2c9e75-d6f6-5fb7-85be-5816243c7d07", "block_to_id": "508e7b61-3236-54fb-bea0-c9b052b85131", "section_path": "Int 738205 Wifi Bridge Nat Source Rewrite Breaks Vpn Policy", "document_id": "55914c4d-c24f-5a29-83b5-3903a3c442b4", "document_version_id": "42104d34-ecc8-5914-8bc1-e9268c9e181e", "document_name": "jira__dsid_e728a420a02a4ddcb125e6adb09d211e.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h1-0", "heading": "Int 738205 Wifi Bridge Nat Source Rewrite Breaks Vpn Policy", "content": "Int 738205 Wifi Bridge Nat Source Rewrite Breaks Vpn Policy\\n\\nSource type: jira\\nDocument ID: dsid_e728a420a02a4ddcb125e6adb09d211e\\nRelease: v1.0.0\\nBenchmark: EnterpriseRAG-Bench synthetic upstream data\\nOffice edge bridge in NAT mode rewriting source IPs and causing VPN policy routing failures and SSO timeouts\\n\\nIssue summary: After a recent office CAB change at the SoMa satellite office we started seeing a sustained increase in VPN session failures and SSO timeouts for users on the office Wi\xe2\x80\x91Fi. Impact: ~12-18% of users at SoMa experience intermittent 403/SSO timeouts or are unable to reach internal services that normally resolve via VPN private IPs. Service impact is localized to the office LAN and affects employees using company Wi\xe2\x80\x91Fi and a subset of developer services behind policy-based routing. Initial hypothesis: an intermediate bridge/AP that was re-provisioned to \'NAT\' mode is rewriting source addresses causing VPN policy lookup to fail, triggering mis-routed traffic and SSO token validation errors.\\n1) Connect a laptop to SoMa corporate Wi\xe2\x80\x91Fi (ssid: Redwood-Corp).\\n2) Establish Redwood VPN (WireGuard client) and authenticate via SSO (Okta).\\n3) Attempt to curl an internal service at 10.11.20.5: expect success; observed: connection resets or 403 responses.\\n4) Observe device local IP (e.g., 192.168.50.34) and the outbound NATed IP as seen by internal services (packets show 10.100.200.1 source after NAT rewrite).\\nClients on office Wi\xe2\x80\x91Fi see internal service requests fail intermittently. Packet captures from service frontends show source IPs mapped to 10.100.200.0/24 (bridge appliance SNAT pool) instead of clients\' VPN-assigned 10.8.0.0/16 addresses. Okta SSO validation rejects token assertions when source IP does not match expected corporate ranges, causing auth flows to fail.\\nTraffic from VPN clients should preserve VPN-assigned source addresses. Office bridge should be in passthrough mode for tunneled traffic so policy-based routing at the gateway can correctly match flows and SSO sees expected IP ranges.\\n2026-03-10T09:22:13Z firewall[gw-usw-1]: policy_lookup: src=10.8.12.45 dst=10.11.20.5 matched=internal-web-cluster action=allow\\n2026-03-10T09:22:13Z app-fw[web-01]: tcpdump: in.ether src=10.100.200.14:52344 > 10.11.20.5:443 SYN\\n2026-03-10T09:23:01Z okta-proxy[auth-01]: token_validation: ip_mismatch user=jared@example.com expected_range=10.8.0.0/16 seen_ip=10.100.200.14\\n\\n- Confirmed bridge device model: Ubiquiti UBB\xe2\x80\x91Edge v2 (serial: UB-1212). Reprovisioning on 2026-03-09 set its WAN mode to \'Gateway (NAT)\' instead of \'Bridge\'.\\n- tcpdump on web-01 shows multiple connections with SNATed sources 10.100.200.0/24. When testing from a home client via remote VPN this does not occur; home clients preserve 10.8.x source addresses.\\n- ip rule list on gw-usw-1 shows policy routing keyed on src network 10.8.0.0/16. Because SNAT rewrote source to 10.100.200.x the kernel falls back to default route and packets get dropped or mis-routed to edge ACLs.\\n- Quick check: ssh to bridge admin UI -> Network -> NAT Mode = Enabled. CLI \'iptables -t nat -L -n\' shows POSTROUTING MASQUERADE for bridge LAN range.\\n- Hypothesis validated by temporary change: disabled NAT on bridge -> source IPs preserved -> internal service connectivity restored and SSO token validations succeed.", "score": 0.749261, "rank": 3, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "d8d828de-3fd1-5a21-8cc8-cf1e3282e228", "search_unit_id": "d8d828de-3fd1-5a21-8cc8-cf1e3282e228", "block_from_id": "f11d70ac-f9f2-5493-9410-8ea6ca946367", "block_to_id": "f11d70ac-f9f2-5493-9410-8ea6ca946367", "section_path": "Int 738205 Wifi Bridge Nat Source Rewrite Breaks Vpn Policy", "document_id": "55914c4d-c24f-5a29-83b5-3903a3c442b4", "document_version_id": "42104d34-ecc8-5914-8bc1-e9268c9e181e", "document_name": "jira__dsid_e728a420a02a4ddcb125e6adb09d211e.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "p-4", "heading": "Int 738205 Wifi Bridge Nat Source Rewrite Breaks Vpn Policy", "content": "pcap snippet (web-01): 10.100.200.14.52344 > 10.11.20.5.443 Flags [S] seq 0 win 64240\\npcap snippet (after fix): 10.8.12.45.52344 > 10.11.20.5.443 Flags [S] seq 0 win 64240\\nOn affected office bridge, re-enable \'passthrough/bridge\' mode or add a NAT-exemption rule for VPN-assigned subnets (10.8.0.0/16). As an immediate mitigation, network ops applied a bridge-level configuration that disables MASQUERADE for src 10.8.0.0/16 which restored service for all connected clients.\\nTemporary mitigation applied on 2026-03-11: NAT exemption rule added to bridge and config pinned. Next steps: schedule coordinated firmware fix and update CAB provisioning template to ensure edge bridges are provisioned in \'bridge\' mode for corporate VLANs that host VPN clients. Postmortem to be created and template change rolled out to 5 remote offices.\\n2026-03-10 10:45 - Aisha Patel: Initial report from SoMa floor lead: multiple devs reporting 403s when accessing internal dashboards while on company Wi\xe2\x80\x91Fi. Filed ticket and added SRE on-call.\\n2026-03-10 11:05 - SRE Oncall (Riley Morgan): Did quick checks, observed SNATed sources on web frontends. Asking networking to verify bridge provisioning state and recent CAB changes.\\n2026-03-10 13:12 - Networking (Diego Alvarez): Confirmed bridge was reprovisioned yesterday as part of patch window; default image set WAN mode to Gateway/NAT. Preparing rollback of NAT change and plan for NAT-exempt rule for 10.8.0.0/16.\\n2026-03-11 08:30 - Liam Chen: Applied NAT-exemption rule on bridge (ubnt cli: iptables -t nat -D POSTROUTING -s 10.8.0.0/16 -j MASQUERADE). Verified tcpdump shows 10.8.x src to internal services and Okta validations succeed. Monitoring for 24h.\\n2026-03-12 09:05 - Product Ops (Nora Singh): Noted impact on engineers collaborating in SoMa. Requested postmortem and an automated check in provisioning pipeline to prevent future NAT mode flips.\\n2026-03-12 12:15 - Liam Chen: Created PR to office-configs to pin bridge mode and added validation unit test in provisioning flow (see linked PR). Scheduling CAB to apply template to 5 sites next week.", "score": 0.421142, "rank": 4, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}], "events": [], "entities": [], "relations": [], "source_hits": [], "summary": "", "citations": [], "answer_status": "pending", "no_answer_reason": null, "exploration_id": null, "stats": {"canonical_index": true, "ready_versions": 81, "requested_top_k": null, "candidate_top_k": 32, "candidate_unit_pool_limit": 1024, "candidate_pool_saturated": true, "candidate_units_before_cap": 80, "candidate_units_after_cap": 80, "candidate_units_truncated": 0, "semantic_candidates": 47, "lexical_candidates": 41, "candidates": 80, "relevant": 46, "filtered_irrelevant": 34, "fusion_method": "rrf", "selection_method": "authorized_content_dedup_mmr", "cross_scope_merge": "rank_interleave", "coverage": {"candidate_count": 64, "deduplicated_count": 0, "diversity_weight": 0.5, "near_duplicate_similarity": 0.98, "required_anchor_count": 1, "covered_anchor_count": 1, "anchor_coverage": "complete", "status": "structurally_sufficient", "canonical_locator_verified": true, "semantic_answerability": "unknown"}, "routing": {"planner": {"planner_version": "qsp-v1", "requested_strategy": "AUTO", "effective_strategy": "EXACT", "modifiers": [], "reason_codes": ["EXACT_IDENTIFIER_PRESENT"], "multi_hop_eligible": false}, "request_snapshot_id": "bafcc914-7b13-4b09-9473-09baf514321a", "groups": [{"project_id": "b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c", "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "partition_id": "b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c", "snapshot_id": "1d17c446-d387-45f6-8b8d-4c70462d698b", "request_snapshot_id": "bafcc914-7b13-4b09-9473-09baf514321a", "acl_scope_fingerprint": "328ac326f64690733d385248a99659bc5ed25e83991108887c7a3367d2d5c51e", "tree_version": "tree-50bdd85ee0f1111bfecc7840", "routing_slot": "SLOT_A", "search_epoch": 2, "selected_nodes": ["56053360af7bd0c00b3c23b570340db9", "7b2fc0831c2ad2df9911ec93ed403895", "d48df15e10c1588c77a8ea414162a6c5"], "membership_count": 168, "entropy": 0.9988127016321052, "margin": 0.025464700074790736, "broad_route": true, "reason_code": "ROUTE_UNCERTAIN_BROADENED", "fallback_reason": null, "branch_local_candidates": 57, "global_candidates": 60, "escape_recovered_candidates": 23, "escape_attempted": true, "escape_trigger": "reserved_parallel_global_escape", "local_failure": null, "escape_failure": null, "blackhole_detected": false}], "coverage": {"candidate_count": 64, "deduplicated_count": 0, "diversity_weight": 0.5, "near_duplicate_similarity": 0.98, "required_anchor_count": 1, "covered_anchor_count": 1, "anchor_coverage": "complete", "status": "structurally_sufficient", "canonical_locator_verified": true, "semantic_answerability": "unknown"}, "selection_fallback_reason": null, "multi_hop": {"eligible": false, "effective": "EXACT", "graph_expansion_attempted": false, "graph_expanded_candidates": 0, "graph_expansion_skip_reason": null}, "fallback_used": true}, "selection_fallback_reason": null, "stage_latencies_ms": {"auth_scope": 12.4, "tree_route": 628.52, "candidate_retrieval": 1992.14, "evidence_hydration": 17.01, "rank_fusion": 30.78, "graph_expansion": 0.0, "diversity_selection": 1836.78, "total_retrieval": 4527.38}, "latency_total_ms": 4527.38, "automatic_top_k": true, "effective_top_k": 5, "adaptive_waves": 1, "retrieval_stop_reason": "relevance_plateau", "budget_exhausted": false, "has_more": false, "acl_filtered_candidates": 0, "query_route": {"version": "query-flow-v1", "query_original": "What was identified as the root cause of the intermittent VPN connectivity blackholes and duplicate IP warnings for users on the corporate Wi-Fi in the SF2 building behind a specific edge switch?", "scope_source_ids": ["b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159"], "coarse_intent": "KNOWLEDGE", "confidence": 0.7138, "model": "Kev-4b", "suggested_strategy": "vector", "requested_strategy": "auto", "effective_strategy": "vector", "retrieval": "required", "fallback_used": false, "fallback_reason": null, "reason_codes": ["KNOWLEDGE_INTENT", "EXACT_IDENTIFIER"], "query_analysis": {"normalized_phrase": "whatwasidentifiedastherootcauseoftheintermittentvpnconnectivityblackholesandduplicateipwarningsforusersonthecorporatewifiinthesf2buildingbehindaspecificedgeswitch", "lookup_terms": ["identified", "root", "cause", "intermittent", "vpn", "connectivity", "blackholes", "duplicate", "ip", "warnings", "users", "corporate", "wi-fi", "sf2", "sf", "building"], "features": {"exact_terms": [], "identifier_terms": ["SF2"], "path_terms": [], "temporal_cues": [], "relation_cues": [], "global_cues": [], "multi_hop": false}}, "strategy_plan": {"planner_version": "qsp-v1", "requested_strategy": "AUTO", "effective_strategy": "EXACT", "modifiers": [], "reason_codes": ["EXACT_IDENTIFIER_PRESENT"], "multi_hop_eligible": false}, "retrieval_fallback_used": false}}}\r\n\r\n'
14:03:30  DEBUG    [77ad975605d04ba2]  sse_starlette.sse  chunk: b'event: summary.delta\r\ndata: {"delta": "The root cause of the intermittent VPN connectivity blackholes and duplicate IP warnings for users on the corporate Wi-Fi in the SF2 building behind a specific edge switch was identified as the switch\'s **proxy-arp** feature responding to ARP requests for VPN-assigned addresses when the AP\'s multicast queue exceeded a threshold. This caused **duplicate IP assignments** on the L2 domain, leading to **routing blackholes** and **VPN rekeys**. The switch firmware version 1.2.3 had a known bridging bug that triggered this behavior under high multicast load. [1]"}\r\n\r\n'
14:03:30  DEBUG    [77ad975605d04ba2]  sse_starlette.sse  chunk: b'event: completed\r\ndata: {"query": "What was identified as the root cause of the intermittent VPN connectivity blackholes and duplicate IP warnings for users on the corporate Wi-Fi in the SF2 building behind a specific edge switch?", "sections": [{"chunk_id": "5851ad70-5696-5b1f-b21e-5b0b7f32ea48", "search_unit_id": "5851ad70-5696-5b1f-b21e-5b0b7f32ea48", "block_from_id": "fd4cdd84-2ce4-56b4-9d8a-6f8f218c3787", "block_to_id": "fd4cdd84-2ce4-56b4-9d8a-6f8f218c3787", "section_path": "Int 460811 Edge Switch Arp Proxy Ip Duplication", "document_id": "5f928fa4-a80b-5b4b-8d56-f3a357498f86", "document_version_id": "e6c0e4cb-240e-54bc-9e85-42e72dfa44cd", "document_name": "jira__dsid_59cb294da8964683bb165a3bb615df71.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "p-2", "heading": "Int 460811 Edge Switch Arp Proxy Ip Duplication", "content": "Issue summary: Several users reporting intermittent loss of access to internal services while connected to corporate VPN. Symptoms include duplicate IP conflict alerts on endpoints, frequent VPN re-auth events, and traffic appearing to be routed to a different on-prem host (service 10.23.5.12). Impact: ~8% of VPN sessions in us-west over the last 48h experienced short blackholes (30-90s) impacting git pushes, internal CI jobs, and ssh sessions. Scope: affects users on Wi-Fi SSID \'Redwood-Corp\' behind specific edge switches in building SF2 rack 7.\\n1) Connect laptop to \'Redwood-Corp\' Wi-Fi in SF2 building (tested on macOS 13 and Ubuntu 22.04)\\n2) Establish VPN session to redwood-vpn-usw.redwood.net (WireGuard-based corporate VPN)\\n3) Trigger continuous ping to an internal host (ping -i 0.2 10.23.5.12)\\n4) Observe intermittent duplicate IP warnings on client and packets forwarded to an unexpected MAC on the L2 domain\\n5) Reproduce frequency increases when there is a short burst of multicast/mDNS traffic on the same AP\'s radio\\nClient syslog excerpt: \'kernel: arp: IP address 10.23.8.45 claimed by 00:11:22:33:44:55 (conflict)\'\\nSwitch (edge-sw-7) log: \'proxy-arp conflict detected for 10.23.8.45, source 00:66:77:88:99:AA bridging-port 5\'\\nPacket capture (pcap) snippet: ARP reply for 10.23.8.45 with two different source MACs within 120ms\\nVPN server metrics: client rekey count spike (client 10.23.8.45) correlated to timestamp 2026-03-12T14:12Z\\nInternal service (10.23.5.12) reported TCP reset spikes aligning with client blackholes\\nHypothesis 1: Edge switch proxy-arp configured for legacy NAT path is responding to ARP for VPN-assigned addresses from an overlapping DHCP pool, causing two active ARP entries on the LAN.\\nHypothesis 2: A misconfigured VXLAN/bridge on edge-sw-7 is advertising ARP for the VPN subnet into the campus L2 segment when multicast bursts occur.\\nWhat we tried: - Disabled proxy-arp on edge-sw-7 port-channel to AP group temporarily (no immediate reduction). - Isolated a suspect AP by moving a test client to a different AP (blackhole persisted only when client served by AP-7A). - Captured pcap on AP, switch uplink, and VPN server concurrently for correlated timestamps (pcaps saved to /mnt/logs/INT-460811/pcaps/).\\nPreliminary find: ARP \'gratuitous\' replies with VPN client IP are being injected by the switch\'s \'proxy-arp\' feature only when the AP\'s multicast queue exceeds threshold. The switch returns ARP for the same IP with a different MAC that matches a spare management interface in rack 7 (00:66:77:88:99:AA).\\nIntermittent connectivity loss for internal developer workflows (git/ssh/CI). Approximately 8% of VPN sessions in the SF2 us-west site affected in the window; potential for data-transfer retries and CI flakiness. No customer-facing outage but notable developer productivity hit.\\n1) Placed affected edge switch (edge-sw-7) in monitoring schedule and enabled debug logging for proxy-arp events.\\n2) Temporarily increased DHCP lease affinity for VPN pool for clients in SF2 to reduce the window for IP reuse.\\n3) Asked campus networking team to disable \'proxy-arp\' global feature on a staging switch and observe (ongoing).\\n4) Notified platform reliability and CI owners of potential re-run needs for impacted jobs (Slack #incidents and #platform-alerts).\\n2026-03-11 09:18 - Jonah Reed: Assigned to network; will coordinate switch config changes and gather pcaps. Next action: schedule maintenance window if we need to push config rollback.", "score": 0.849432, "rank": 0, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "333a37e2-157a-597d-b0cc-a2bc5a491b8e", "search_unit_id": "333a37e2-157a-597d-b0cc-a2bc5a491b8e", "block_from_id": "fd4cdd84-2ce4-56b4-9d8a-6f8f218c3787", "block_to_id": "fd4cdd84-2ce4-56b4-9d8a-6f8f218c3787", "section_path": "Int 460811 Edge Switch Arp Proxy Ip Duplication", "document_id": "5f928fa4-a80b-5b4b-8d56-f3a357498f86", "document_version_id": "e6c0e4cb-240e-54bc-9e85-42e72dfa44cd", "document_name": "jira__dsid_59cb294da8964683bb165a3bb615df71.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "p-2", "heading": "Int 460811 Edge Switch Arp Proxy Ip Duplication", "content": "2026-03-12 15:25 - Priya Shah (campus-net): Reproduced proxy-arp responses on edge-sw-7 when AP multicast queue > 70%. Suspect firmware 1.2.3 on these switches has a known misc bridging bug. Opened ticket with vendor (TAC-889233).\\n2026-03-13 08:52 - Jonah Reed: Vendor TAC confirmed the switch may respond to ARP for non-local subnets under multicast overload in 1.2.3. Recommended immediate mitigation: set \'proxy-arp disable\' on VRF for AP VLANs and upgrade firmware to 1.2.6.\\n2026-03-14 07:30 - Aisha Malik: Applied \'proxy-arp disable\' to edge-sw-7 in staged maintenance window (07:00-07:15). Monitoring: VPN rekey spikes reduced from 47/hr to 2/hr for affected clients in the first 24h.\\n2026-03-14 10:02 - Jonah Reed: Confirming RFC and rollout plan for global fix. Proposed follow-up: firmware upgrade across SF2 rack 4-9, audit for proxy-arp enabled on other edge switches, and update config baseline to explicitly disable proxy-arp for VPN/DHCP subnets.\\nSwitch firmware (1.2.3) bug caused proxy-arp behavior under high multicast load leading to ARP advertisements for VPN-assigned addresses. This created ephemeral duplicate IP assignments on the L2 domain and caused VPN clients to experience routing blackholes and rekeys.\\nMitigation applied: \'proxy-arp disable\' set on edge-sw-7 AP VLANs during maintenance window 2026-03-14 07:00-07:15.\\nTemporary workaround: increased DHCP lease affinity and moved high-multicast APs to separate RF profile to reduce multicast bursts.\\nPermanent fix: planned firmware upgrade to 1.2.6 across SF2 edge switches (racks 4-9) and config baseline change to disable proxy-arp for VPN/DHCP subnets. Vendor TAC provided patch notes and recommended upgrade path.\\nFollow-ups: - Create change request CR-2026-0415 for firmware rollout. - Run campus-wide audit script to detect \'proxy-arp\' enabled instances and remediate. - Add regression test to onboarding checklist for AP multicast stress.\\nStatus: Partial fix applied and validated; full remediation scheduled (see CR-2026-0415).", "score": 0.73578, "rank": 1, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "c4bdfef3-8d2c-59ab-95b5-ce7db7f8ec23", "search_unit_id": "c4bdfef3-8d2c-59ab-95b5-ce7db7f8ec23", "block_from_id": "e770368f-ef5f-5985-a96e-901a2c4ae259", "block_to_id": "5874d051-a5b9-521b-9783-c732b73da90c", "section_path": "Int 460811 Edge Switch Arp Proxy Ip Duplication", "document_id": "5f928fa4-a80b-5b4b-8d56-f3a357498f86", "document_version_id": "e6c0e4cb-240e-54bc-9e85-42e72dfa44cd", "document_name": "jira__dsid_59cb294da8964683bb165a3bb615df71.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h1-0", "heading": "Int 460811 Edge Switch Arp Proxy Ip Duplication", "content": "Int 460811 Edge Switch Arp Proxy Ip Duplication\\n\\nSource type: jira\\nDocument ID: dsid_59cb294da8964683bb165a3bb615df71\\nRelease: v1.0.0\\nBenchmark: EnterpriseRAG-Bench synthetic upstream data\\nEdge switch ARP proxying leads to VPN client IP duplication and intermittent routing to wrong host", "score": 0.657697, "rank": 2, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "0a58a634-684f-585b-8094-d0bebd88491f", "search_unit_id": "0a58a634-684f-585b-8094-d0bebd88491f", "block_from_id": "4c2c9e75-d6f6-5fb7-85be-5816243c7d07", "block_to_id": "508e7b61-3236-54fb-bea0-c9b052b85131", "section_path": "Int 738205 Wifi Bridge Nat Source Rewrite Breaks Vpn Policy", "document_id": "55914c4d-c24f-5a29-83b5-3903a3c442b4", "document_version_id": "42104d34-ecc8-5914-8bc1-e9268c9e181e", "document_name": "jira__dsid_e728a420a02a4ddcb125e6adb09d211e.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h1-0", "heading": "Int 738205 Wifi Bridge Nat Source Rewrite Breaks Vpn Policy", "content": "Int 738205 Wifi Bridge Nat Source Rewrite Breaks Vpn Policy\\n\\nSource type: jira\\nDocument ID: dsid_e728a420a02a4ddcb125e6adb09d211e\\nRelease: v1.0.0\\nBenchmark: EnterpriseRAG-Bench synthetic upstream data\\nOffice edge bridge in NAT mode rewriting source IPs and causing VPN policy routing failures and SSO timeouts\\n\\nIssue summary: After a recent office CAB change at the SoMa satellite office we started seeing a sustained increase in VPN session failures and SSO timeouts for users on the office Wi\xe2\x80\x91Fi. Impact: ~12-18% of users at SoMa experience intermittent 403/SSO timeouts or are unable to reach internal services that normally resolve via VPN private IPs. Service impact is localized to the office LAN and affects employees using company Wi\xe2\x80\x91Fi and a subset of developer services behind policy-based routing. Initial hypothesis: an intermediate bridge/AP that was re-provisioned to \'NAT\' mode is rewriting source addresses causing VPN policy lookup to fail, triggering mis-routed traffic and SSO token validation errors.\\n1) Connect a laptop to SoMa corporate Wi\xe2\x80\x91Fi (ssid: Redwood-Corp).\\n2) Establish Redwood VPN (WireGuard client) and authenticate via SSO (Okta).\\n3) Attempt to curl an internal service at 10.11.20.5: expect success; observed: connection resets or 403 responses.\\n4) Observe device local IP (e.g., 192.168.50.34) and the outbound NATed IP as seen by internal services (packets show 10.100.200.1 source after NAT rewrite).\\nClients on office Wi\xe2\x80\x91Fi see internal service requests fail intermittently. Packet captures from service frontends show source IPs mapped to 10.100.200.0/24 (bridge appliance SNAT pool) instead of clients\' VPN-assigned 10.8.0.0/16 addresses. Okta SSO validation rejects token assertions when source IP does not match expected corporate ranges, causing auth flows to fail.\\nTraffic from VPN clients should preserve VPN-assigned source addresses. Office bridge should be in passthrough mode for tunneled traffic so policy-based routing at the gateway can correctly match flows and SSO sees expected IP ranges.\\n2026-03-10T09:22:13Z firewall[gw-usw-1]: policy_lookup: src=10.8.12.45 dst=10.11.20.5 matched=internal-web-cluster action=allow\\n2026-03-10T09:22:13Z app-fw[web-01]: tcpdump: in.ether src=10.100.200.14:52344 > 10.11.20.5:443 SYN\\n2026-03-10T09:23:01Z okta-proxy[auth-01]: token_validation: ip_mismatch user=jared@example.com expected_range=10.8.0.0/16 seen_ip=10.100.200.14\\n\\n- Confirmed bridge device model: Ubiquiti UBB\xe2\x80\x91Edge v2 (serial: UB-1212). Reprovisioning on 2026-03-09 set its WAN mode to \'Gateway (NAT)\' instead of \'Bridge\'.\\n- tcpdump on web-01 shows multiple connections with SNATed sources 10.100.200.0/24. When testing from a home client via remote VPN this does not occur; home clients preserve 10.8.x source addresses.\\n- ip rule list on gw-usw-1 shows policy routing keyed on src network 10.8.0.0/16. Because SNAT rewrote source to 10.100.200.x the kernel falls back to default route and packets get dropped or mis-routed to edge ACLs.\\n- Quick check: ssh to bridge admin UI -> Network -> NAT Mode = Enabled. CLI \'iptables -t nat -L -n\' shows POSTROUTING MASQUERADE for bridge LAN range.\\n- Hypothesis validated by temporary change: disabled NAT on bridge -> source IPs preserved -> internal service connectivity restored and SSO token validations succeed.", "score": 0.749261, "rank": 3, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "d8d828de-3fd1-5a21-8cc8-cf1e3282e228", "search_unit_id": "d8d828de-3fd1-5a21-8cc8-cf1e3282e228", "block_from_id": "f11d70ac-f9f2-5493-9410-8ea6ca946367", "block_to_id": "f11d70ac-f9f2-5493-9410-8ea6ca946367", "section_path": "Int 738205 Wifi Bridge Nat Source Rewrite Breaks Vpn Policy", "document_id": "55914c4d-c24f-5a29-83b5-3903a3c442b4", "document_version_id": "42104d34-ecc8-5914-8bc1-e9268c9e181e", "document_name": "jira__dsid_e728a420a02a4ddcb125e6adb09d211e.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "p-4", "heading": "Int 738205 Wifi Bridge Nat Source Rewrite Breaks Vpn Policy", "content": "pcap snippet (web-01): 10.100.200.14.52344 > 10.11.20.5.443 Flags [S] seq 0 win 64240\\npcap snippet (after fix): 10.8.12.45.52344 > 10.11.20.5.443 Flags [S] seq 0 win 64240\\nOn affected office bridge, re-enable \'passthrough/bridge\' mode or add a NAT-exemption rule for VPN-assigned subnets (10.8.0.0/16). As an immediate mitigation, network ops applied a bridge-level configuration that disables MASQUERADE for src 10.8.0.0/16 which restored service for all connected clients.\\nTemporary mitigation applied on 2026-03-11: NAT exemption rule added to bridge and config pinned. Next steps: schedule coordinated firmware fix and update CAB provisioning template to ensure edge bridges are provisioned in \'bridge\' mode for corporate VLANs that host VPN clients. Postmortem to be created and template change rolled out to 5 remote offices.\\n2026-03-10 10:45 - Aisha Patel: Initial report from SoMa floor lead: multiple devs reporting 403s when accessing internal dashboards while on company Wi\xe2\x80\x91Fi. Filed ticket and added SRE on-call.\\n2026-03-10 11:05 - SRE Oncall (Riley Morgan): Did quick checks, observed SNATed sources on web frontends. Asking networking to verify bridge provisioning state and recent CAB changes.\\n2026-03-10 13:12 - Networking (Diego Alvarez): Confirmed bridge was reprovisioned yesterday as part of patch window; default image set WAN mode to Gateway/NAT. Preparing rollback of NAT change and plan for NAT-exempt rule for 10.8.0.0/16.\\n2026-03-11 08:30 - Liam Chen: Applied NAT-exemption rule on bridge (ubnt cli: iptables -t nat -D POSTROUTING -s 10.8.0.0/16 -j MASQUERADE). Verified tcpdump shows 10.8.x src to internal services and Okta validations succeed. Monitoring for 24h.\\n2026-03-12 09:05 - Product Ops (Nora Singh): Noted impact on engineers collaborating in SoMa. Requested postmortem and an automated check in provisioning pipeline to prevent future NAT mode flips.\\n2026-03-12 12:15 - Liam Chen: Created PR to office-configs to pin bridge mode and added validation unit test in provisioning flow (see linked PR). Scheduling CAB to apply template to 5 sites next week.", "score": 0.421142, "rank": 4, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}], "events": [], "entities": [], "relations": [], "source_hits": [], "summary": "The root cause of the intermittent VPN connectivity blackholes and duplicate IP warnings for users on the corporate Wi-Fi in the SF2 building behind a specific edge switch was identified as the switch\'s **proxy-arp** feature responding to ARP requests for VPN-assigned addresses when the AP\'s multicast queue exceeded a threshold. This caused **duplicate IP assignments** on the L2 domain, leading to **routing blackholes** and **VPN rekeys**. The switch firmware version 1.2.3 had a known bridging bug that triggered this behavior under high multicast load. [1]", "citations": [{"kind": "internal", "n": 1, "document_id": "5f928fa4-a80b-5b4b-8d56-f3a357498f86", "document_version_id": "e6c0e4cb-240e-54bc-9e85-42e72dfa44cd", "document_name": "jira__dsid_59cb294da8964683bb165a3bb615df71.md", "version_no": 1, "chunk_id": "5851ad70-5696-5b1f-b21e-5b0b7f32ea48", "search_unit_id": "5851ad70-5696-5b1f-b21e-5b0b7f32ea48", "block_from_id": "fd4cdd84-2ce4-56b4-9d8a-6f8f218c3787", "block_to_id": "fd4cdd84-2ce4-56b4-9d8a-6f8f218c3787", "section_path": "Int 460811 Edge Switch Arp Proxy Ip Duplication", "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "p-2", "heading": "Int 460811 Edge Switch Arp Proxy Ip Duplication", "snippet": "Issue summary: Several users reporting intermittent loss of access to internal services while connected to corporate VPN. Symptoms include duplicate IP conflict alerts on endpoints, frequent VPN re-auth events, and traffic appearing to be routed to a different on-prem host (service 10.23.5.12). Impact: ~8% of VPN sessions in us-west over the last 48h experienced short blackholes (30-90s) impacting git pushes, internal CI jobs, and ssh sessions. Scope: affects users on Wi-Fi SSID \'Redwood-Corp\' behind specific edge switches in building SF2 rack 7. 1) Connect laptop to \'Redwood-Corp\' Wi-Fi in SF2 building (tested on macOS 13 and Ubuntu 22.04) 2) Establish VPN session to redwood-vpn-usw.redwood.net (WireGuard-base\xe2\x80\xa6", "score": 0.8494, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}], "answer_status": "answered", "no_answer_reason": null, "exploration_id": null, "stats": {"canonical_index": true, "ready_versions": 81, "requested_top_k": null, "candidate_top_k": 32, "candidate_unit_pool_limit": 1024, "candidate_pool_saturated": true, "candidate_units_before_cap": 80, "candidate_units_after_cap": 80, "candidate_units_truncated": 0, "semantic_candidates": 47, "lexical_candidates": 41, "candidates": 80, "relevant": 46, "filtered_irrelevant": 34, "fusion_method": "rrf", "selection_method": "authorized_content_dedup_mmr", "cross_scope_merge": "rank_interleave", "coverage": {"candidate_count": 64, "deduplicated_count": 0, "diversity_weight": 0.5, "near_duplicate_similarity": 0.98, "required_anchor_count": 1, "covered_anchor_count": 1, "anchor_coverage": "complete", "status": "structurally_sufficient", "canonical_locator_verified": true, "semantic_answerability": "unknown"}, "routing": {"planner": {"planner_version": "qsp-v1", "requested_strategy": "AUTO", "effective_strategy": "EXACT", "modifiers": [], "reason_codes": ["EXACT_IDENTIFIER_PRESENT"], "multi_hop_eligible": false}, "request_snapshot_id": "bafcc914-7b13-4b09-9473-09baf514321a", "groups": [{"project_id": "b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c", "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "partition_id": "b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c", "snapshot_id": "1d17c446-d387-45f6-8b8d-4c70462d698b", "request_snapshot_id": "bafcc914-7b13-4b09-9473-09baf514321a", "acl_scope_fingerprint": "328ac326f64690733d385248a99659bc5ed25e83991108887c7a3367d2d5c51e", "tree_version": "tree-50bdd85ee0f1111bfecc7840", "routing_slot": "SLOT_A", "search_epoch": 2, "selected_nodes": ["56053360af7bd0c00b3c23b570340db9", "7b2fc0831c2ad2df9911ec93ed403895", "d48df15e10c1588c77a8ea414162a6c5"], "membership_count": 168, "entropy": 0.9988127016321052, "margin": 0.025464700074790736, "broad_route": true, "reason_code": "ROUTE_UNCERTAIN_BROADENED", "fallback_reason": null, "branch_local_candidates": 57, "global_candidates": 60, "escape_recovered_candidates": 23, "escape_attempted": true, "escape_trigger": "reserved_parallel_global_escape", "local_failure": null, "escape_failure": null, "blackhole_detected": false}], "coverage": {"candidate_count": 64, "deduplicated_count": 0, "diversity_weight": 0.5, "near_duplicate_similarity": 0.98, "required_anch