14:05:05  DEBUG    [0a696691441349e6]  sse_starlette.sse  chunk: b'event: result\r\ndata: {"query": "What is the company policy for how long contractor access should last by default before it expires, according to the access and permissions playbook?", "sections": [{"chunk_id": "cd97969a-d664-5c44-b40d-29de8e3aed7c", "search_unit_id": "cd97969a-d664-5c44-b40d-29de8e3aed7c", "block_from_id": "8e6320c4-e6f8-5d54-93df-d1029f47c012", "block_to_id": "57ca5e74-583f-5358-b18f-940f2bd5d127", "section_path": "Entitlements And Purchase Pathways Playbook 2030", "document_id": "98b6d795-d34b-588e-9f1d-b236110b9bba", "document_version_id": "9f88e88a-7404-5ed3-aeef-43374be1410f", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_ba7d1565b0694e359983bccaa4bf5977.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h1-0", "heading": "Entitlements And Purchase Pathways Playbook 2030", "content": "Entitlements And Purchase Pathways Playbook 2030\\n\\nSource type: confluence\\nDocument ID: dsid_ba7d1565b0694e359983bccaa4bf5977\\nRelease: v1.0.0\\nBenchmark: EnterpriseRAG-Bench synthetic upstream data\\nentitlements-and-purchase-pathways-playbook-2030\\nOverview\\n=======\\n\\nPurpose: This playbook consolidates company-wide procedures for entitlements (access and permissions), change governance, data handling expectations, procurement and expense approvals, vendor lifecycle management, and travel approvals. It is intended for all Redwood employees and contractors who request or approve resources, commit changes to production, or manage third-party relationships.\\n\\nScope: Applies to hosted, dedicated, and private deployment teams, platform and infra teams, procurement interactions, people-ops travel arrangements, and any third party that will access Redwood systems or customer data.\\n\\nQuick links: Access Portal (Okta + Access Request), VendorHub (procurement back-end), ExpenseFlow (employee expenses), Legal intake form, Security questionnaire (security.redwood.local).\\n\\nRoles and responsibilities\\n--------------------------\\n\\n- Requestor: person initiating an access, change, purchase, vendor relationship, or travel booking. Responsible for completeness and business justification.\\n- Manager/Approver: direct manager who validates business need and budget availability.\\n- Approving Officer (Finance/Procurement): validates procurement thresholds, tax, and vendor classification.\\n- Security Reviewer: evaluates data access risk and mandatory controls (SOC2, encryption, contract clauses).\\n- Legal Reviewer: reviews contract terms for vendor agreements above threshold or with custom IP/data terms.\\n- Proc Ops (Vendor Onboarding): completes supplier setup, obtains W-9/COI as applicable.\\n\\nPrinciples\\n----------\\n\\n- Least privilege: grant minimal entitlements required for the job and set automatic expiration where practical.\\n- Segregation of duties: approval and provisioning paths must not be owned by the same individual for medium/high risk requests.\\n- Evidence-first approvals: all approvals must be attached to the request in VendorHub or Access Portal.\\n- Risk proportionality: stricter controls for vendors with data access, privileged infra access, or requests above financial thresholds.\\n\\nAccess & permissions (entitlement lifecycle)\\n-------------------------------------------\\n1) Request process\\n\\n- Use the Access Portal (accessible from the Redwood Console > Tools > Access Request).\\n- Provide: justification, target systems (service name and environment), requested role (exact RBAC role), duration, and manager approval.\\n- For long-lived roles (>90 days), supply quarterly business justification and add reviewer in Access Portal.\\n\\n2) Approval matrix (summary)\\n\\n- Day-to-day access to non-prod systems: manager approval.\\n- Prod read-only access: manager + security notification.\\n- Prod privileged/infra access (SSH, K8s-admin, DB write): manager + security + infra-owner approval.\\n- Emergency elevated access: break-glass procedure (see Runbook ID: RG-2026-breakglass).\\n\\n3) Provisioning and deprovisioning\\n\\n- Provisioning is automated via Okta + Terraform runbooks (Infra-IAC). On approval, provisioning SLA is 2 business days for standard requests, 8 hours for emergency sprints.\\n- Access expirations are enforced: default 30 days for contractor requests, 90 days for internal hires unless renewed.\\n\\n4) Periodic review\\n\\n- Quarterly access attestation: team owners must validate active entitlements and remove stale accounts. Failure to respond triggers automated revocation notices.\\n\\nChange management\\n-----------------\\n\\nScope: Any modification to production services, infra provisioning, IAM policies, or customer-facing configuration.\\n\\nChange categories and approval paths:", "score": 0.76075, "rank": 0, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "ae17ab66-5c66-5561-8b4b-390018946350", "search_unit_id": "ae17ab66-5c66-5561-8b4b-390018946350", "block_from_id": "e0024ee9-c56b-5f47-bfdc-66f91c209941", "block_to_id": "821238ed-e68f-50ce-8fdd-bd820d8a8628", "section_path": "Entitlements And Purchase Pathways Playbook 2030", "document_id": "98b6d795-d34b-588e-9f1d-b236110b9bba", "document_version_id": "9f88e88a-7404-5ed3-aeef-43374be1410f", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_ba7d1565b0694e359983bccaa4bf5977.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "list-20", "heading": "Entitlements And Purchase Pathways Playbook 2030", "content": "- Standard change: pre-approved, repeatable changes (e.g., routine OS patching via controlled pipeline). Requires change ticket and notification to SRE runbook subscribers.\\n- Normal change: requires Change Review Board (CRB) approval for higher impact (planned releases that affect SLAs). CRB meets twice weekly.\\n- Emergency change: immediate fixes that must follow the emergency roll-forward checklist and be retroactively documented in the change ticket.\\n\\nChange windows and freezes:\\n\\n- Quarterly freeze: last two business days of each quarter are freeze windows for major releases unless exception approved by CTO and SRE lead.\\n- High-risk releases: require canary rollout and 30% traffic validation for 24 hours before full rollout.\\n\\nChange request minimum content (ticket):\\n\\n1. Change owner and contact\\n2. Rollout and rollback plan with automation steps\\n3. Expected impact and post-deploy validation steps\\n4. Backout criteria and timeline\\n5. Stakeholder notification list\\n\\nSLOs and audit\\n\\n- All normal changes must have an associated ticket and be auditable for 12 months.\\n- Emergency changes must be documented within 48 hours.\\n\\nData management and classification\\n--------------------------------\\nClassification levels:\\n\\n- Public: content intended for public consumption.\\n- Internal: operational information not intended for external distribution.\\n- Confidential: employee, business, or customer information that requires access controls.\\n- Restricted: regulated or highly sensitive data (PII, payment data, health data) that requires encryption at rest and in transit, strict access controls, and audit logging.\\n\\nHandling rules (summary):\\n\\n- Confidential & Restricted: store only in approved systems (Redwood Console vaults, encrypted S3 with KMS). No vendor transfer without security and legal sign-off.\\n- Data retention: default retention for logs is 90 days; for customer-facing telemetry retention follows contractual obligations.\\n- Data deletion: use Data Erasure Request form and verify via automated deletion job.\\n\\nProcurement and expenses\\n------------------------\\nPurchase approval thresholds (effective):\\n\\n| Amount (USD) | Approvals required | Notes |\\n|--------------|-------------------|-------|\\n| < 2,500 | Manager | Auto-approval in VendorHub if budget tag present |\\n| 2,500 \xe2\x80\x93 50,000 | Manager + Finance | Finance checks budget and tax classification |\\n| > 50,000 | Manager + Finance + Procurement + Legal | Requires exec sponsor and procurement intake form |\\n\\nProcurement steps (numbered):\\n\\n1. Create a request in VendorHub including business justification, vendor name, SOW/quote, and budget tag.\\n2. Attach vendor compliance docs (SOC2, ISO, insurance certificate) when available.\\n3. Finance validates budgets and tax treatment within 3 business days.\\n4. Procurement routes to Legal for >50k or non-standard T&Cs.\\n5. Once approved, Procurement issues purchase order and coordinates supplier setup.\\n\\nExpense reimbursement:\\n\\n- Use ExpenseFlow, attach receipts within 30 days of expense. Per diem caps: domestic $150/day, international $250/day unless pre-approved. Card use: corporate cards are preferred for travel; personal card reimbursements require manager approval.\\n\\nVendor management lifecycle\\n--------------------------\\nOnboarding checklist (timeline expectations):", "score": 0.492144, "rank": 1, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "eb1eb8c6-6ea3-5ad6-92e0-6c6ab30db21c", "search_unit_id": "eb1eb8c6-6ea3-5ad6-92e0-6c6ab30db21c", "block_from_id": "2b58c24b-b826-5921-90f4-0d51b588fdc1", "block_to_id": "b452aab1-1b72-53c0-9ba9-5d89d3944cef", "section_path": "Entitlements And Purchase Pathways Playbook 2030", "document_id": "98b6d795-d34b-588e-9f1d-b236110b9bba", "document_version_id": "9f88e88a-7404-5ed3-aeef-43374be1410f", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_ba7d1565b0694e359983bccaa4bf5977.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "list-38", "heading": "Entitlements And Purchase Pathways Playbook 2030", "content": "- Initial intake: vendor submitted via VendorHub, 1 business day acknowledgement.\\n- Risk assessment: Security performs questionnaire review; expect 5-7 business days for standard vendors, 15-20 days for those handling Restricted data.\\n- Contracting: Legal drafts/negotiates terms; standard NDA/SOW templates for low-risk vendors. Time: 5\xe2\x80\x9315 business days depending on terms.\\n- Procurement & finance: vendor setup (W-9/COI), tax classification, payment terms.\\n\\nMinimum vendor requirements by risk tier:\\n\\n- Low risk (no data access): PO, standard SOE, vendor contact, invoice cadence.\\n- Medium risk (limited data access): PO, signed DPA, security questionnaire, SOC2 Type II preferred.\\n- High risk (customer data or privileged infra access): PO, DPA, SOC2 Type II or penetration test report, system access plan, contractual breach notification clause, indemnity terms.\\n\\nOffboarding and termination:\\n\\n- Termination checklist: revoke credentials, recover assets, enforce data return/deletion, final invoice reconciliation, and a post-termination confirmation from vendor. Procurement must retain termination evidence for 7 years.\\n\\nTravel policy (high level)\\n-------------------------\\n\\nBooking: Use Travel Portal (linked from Redwood Console). Lowest reasonable fare policy applies for economy class. Business class requires exec-level pre-approval for travel over 8 hours.\\n\\nApprovals: Manager approves travel requests in Travel Portal. International travel must include security and people-ops notification if travel is to high-risk countries listed by People Ops.\\n\\nPer diems and expenses: See ExpenseFlow caps. Receipts required for all items >$25.\\n\\nSafety and incident reporting:\\n\\n- In case of an incident while traveling, contact People Ops emergency line and Security: security@redwood.com. All incidents must be reported within 24 hours.\\n\\nTemplates and forms (where to find)\\n----------------------------------\\n\\n- Procurement intake form: VendorHub > New Request > Procurement Intake (use template \'Procurement-Intake-v2\').\\n- Data Erasure Request: Redwood Console > Data Requests.\\n- Change request template: CRB ticket template in Jira (project: RED-CHANGES).\\n- Access request template: Access Portal (select role and environment).\\n\\nExample procurement JSON payload (for VendorHub API)\\n{\\n  \\"requestor\\": \\"alice@example.com\\",\\n  \\"vendor\\": \\"Acme Analytics\\",\\n  \\"amount_usd\\": \\"7500\\",\\n  \\"justification\\": \\"Production observability for dedicated clusters\\",\\n  \\"budget_tag\\": \\"infra-monitoring\\",\\n  \\"required_by\\": \\"2027-02-15\\"\\n}\\nAppendix: enforcement and exceptions\\n-----------------------------------\\n\\n- Exceptions: Managers may request a documented exception for short-lived needs; exceptions require a written business case and a compliance review.\\n- Enforcement: Repeated policy violations (e.g., unmanaged vendor engagements or expired privileged access) will be escalated to the employee\'s manager and may trigger procurement suspension or disciplinary review.\\n\\nContacts and ownership\\n----------------------\\n\\n- Policy owner: Finance-Legal (policy owner contact: procurement@redwood.com).\\n- Security contact for vendor risk: security@redwood.com.\\n- People Ops travel & benefits: people-ops@redwood.com.\\n\\nRevision history\\n----------------\\n\\n- 2026-11-12: Initial draft published by Maya Chen.\\n- 2026-12-03: Updated procurement thresholds and added emergency change SLA (reviewed by Luis Alvarez and Priya Nair).\\n\\nRelated artifacts and references\\n-------------------------------\\n\\n- Runbook RG-2026-breakglass (eng-sre/runbooks).\\n- VendorHub API docs (internal link).\\n- Security questionnaire template (security-and-compliance/audit-logging).\\n\\nEnd of document", "score": 0.400453, "rank": 2, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "57a5f47e-ed1a-5383-a193-851f5d82b984", "search_unit_id": "57a5f47e-ed1a-5383-a193-851f5d82b984", "block_from_id": "280de386-d8df-5223-9b71-7ba5ba4ca576", "block_to_id": "51916c8d-386b-52d6-93f6-dea202c442a1", "section_path": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Incident handling and operational expectations > Break-glass access", "document_id": "eb166774-f9a9-56c9-984c-5fd7406c2bd1", "document_version_id": "76710c2c-2fe6-553c-ba81-ed6c87f0cfe5", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_377cdf4e378f40bebd7196e3a0ff1c38.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-81", "heading": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Incident handling and operational expectations > Break-glass access", "content": "Break-glass access\\n\\n- Break-glass use MUST be:\\n  - time-bound (auto-expire)\\n  - approved per the access process\\n  - logged and included in the incident record", "score": 0.682134, "rank": 3, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "f7a517ae-0405-52eb-98e5-d8ebc0245abc", "search_unit_id": "f7a517ae-0405-52eb-98e5-d8ebc0245abc", "block_from_id": "3cb20a79-9a89-5d4a-9bb5-689991a4f55f", "block_to_id": "43dd021f-47fd-5237-b674-03547a17dbf7", "section_path": "Cross Role Tool Access Governance And Self Service Handbook 2027", "document_id": "4495c7a6-685c-5344-90c0-ef0b6cee8521", "document_version_id": "43048def-240f-53d7-bef2-2be51354fc0d", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_d7f0edbaa28147da807b5b85ea495bd1.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h1-0", "heading": "Cross Role Tool Access Governance And Self Service Handbook 2027", "content": "Cross Role Tool Access Governance And Self Service Handbook 2027\\n\\nSource type: confluence\\nDocument ID: dsid_d7f0edbaa28147da807b5b85ea495bd1\\nRelease: v1.0.0\\nBenchmark: EnterpriseRAG-Bench synthetic upstream data\\nCross-role Tool Access Governance and Self-Service Handbook\\n\\nSummary:\\n\\nThis handbook defines the governance model, operational runbook, and self-service flows for granting, reviewing, and revoking access to Redwood\xe2\x80\x99s internal tools across roles and teams. It is intended for people-ops, engineering managers, security reviewers, and tool maintainers. The goal is to make tool access predictable, auditable, and fast while minimizing over-permissioning.\\n\\nKey Principles:\\n\\n- Least privilege by default: users receive the minimum role required to do their job.\\n- Role-driven access: we prefer role-based assignments with ephemeral exceptions.\\n- Self-service first, manual oversight when necessary: automate safe, common grants.\\n- Clear ownership: every tool has an owner and an escalation path.\\n- Auditable lifecycle: provisioning, reviews and deprovisioning are tracked centrally.\\n\\n1) Scope and Definitions\\n\\n- Tool: any internal SaaS, self-hosted service, or repo that requires explicit credentials or permissions (examples: AWS consoles, Jira admin groups, prod Grafana, CI pipelines).\\n- Role: a named collection of permissions (e.g., developer-readonly, infra-operator).\\n- Access Request: a request submitted to the Access Portal for a role or tool-specific permission.\\n- Exception: temporary access outside standard roles; must have an expiration and approver.\\n\\n2) Ownership and Responsibilities\\n\\n- Tool Owner (team-specified): maintains the role catalog, documents required permissions, defines safe self-service gates, and responds to escalations.\\n- People Ops: owns onboarding/offboarding orchestration, periodic review cadence, and highest-level policy.\\n- Security: defines acceptable exception policies, approves high-risk tools, and performs audits.\\n- Manager (requester approver): verifies business need and ties access to role/mission.\\n\\n3) Access Model (high level)\\n\\n- Role Catalog: canonical list of roles for common tools; stored in the Access Portal.\\n- Self-Service Roles: low-risk roles that can be assigned instantly (examples: docs-edit, ci-reader)\\n- Request-and-Approve Roles: medium-risk roles requiring manager approval (examples: staging-deploy, metrics-writer)\\n- Manual Approval Roles: high-risk roles requiring security review (examples: prod-admin, billing-admin)\\n\\n4) Standard Provisioning Flow (Self-Service preferred)\\n\\n1. User initiates request via Access Portal (or CLI).\\n2. For self-service roles: immediate grant recorded in audit log; user notified.\\n3. For manager-approval roles: manager receives approval email and must respond within 48 business hours; if approved, provisioning executes automatically.\\n4. For security-approval roles: security reviewer staged; expected SLA is 3 business days.\\n5. All grants include metadata: requester, approver, justification, expiration (if exception), and ticket ID.\\n\\n5) Approval Matrix (sample)\\n\\n| Tool Category | Example Tools | Typical Role Name | Approval Path | Max SLA for Approval | Expiration Policy |\\n|---|---:|---|---|---|---|\\n| Low risk | Docs, Internal Wiki | docs-edit | Self-service | Instant | Persistent (attached to employment) |\\n| Medium risk | Staging CI, Dev DB | staging-deploy | Manager | 48 business hours | 90 days (auto-renew) |\\n| High risk | Production infra, Billing | prod-admin | Manager + Security | 3 business days | 7 days (explicit extension only) |\\n\\n6) Exception and Emergency Access", "score": 0.668486, "rank": 4, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "b2cfcb6c-bc13-52f8-91f6-f13b98ca24c4", "search_unit_id": "b2cfcb6c-bc13-52f8-91f6-f13b98ca24c4", "block_from_id": "e65f3b9d-64c0-5db9-b1a8-a84e7afd9820", "block_to_id": "a12c7abf-69e3-519f-97ae-eb989f3e8ce8", "section_path": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Redlines: common asks and recommended responses > 5) \xe2\x80\x9cAudit rights to inspect raw logs.\xe2\x80\x9d", "document_id": "45f6686b-12fc-5fae-9c11-9abaeb20a3e5", "document_version_id": "a4bad94b-544e-5a78-88ce-d2659b6c4f79", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_c52c609c0cdf4211a7e8c57bb1da72e4.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-82", "heading": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Redlines: common asks and recommended responses > 5) \xe2\x80\x9cAudit rights to inspect raw logs.\xe2\x80\x9d", "content": "5) \xe2\x80\x9cAudit rights to inspect raw logs.\xe2\x80\x9d\\n\\n**Position:** No direct customer access to raw multi-tenant logs.\\n**Response:** Provide usage exports, reconciliation support, and audit reports as appropriate; reference access-controls policy.", "score": 0.661451, "rank": 5, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "6cc45cc0-3885-594c-b1d3-4af989140e7a", "search_unit_id": "6cc45cc0-3885-594c-b1d3-4af989140e7a", "block_from_id": "1fe12250-0e2b-5350-9a86-b23fa05d6588", "block_to_id": "d466766a-85ba-52c1-a597-d2775167aa84", "section_path": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > IAM and permission scoping requirements > Baseline principles", "document_id": "eb166774-f9a9-56c9-984c-5fd7406c2bd1", "document_version_id": "76710c2c-2fe6-553c-ba81-ed6c87f0cfe5", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_377cdf4e378f40bebd7196e3a0ff1c38.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-29", "heading": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > IAM and permission scoping requirements > Baseline principles", "content": "IAM and permission scoping requirements\\n\\nBaseline principles\\n\\n- Principle of least privilege: restrict **actions**, **resources**, **conditions**, and **principals**.\\n- Prefer explicit key ARNs/IDs over wildcards.\\n- Prefer conditions that bind requests to known contexts (where supported): encryption context, source VPC endpoints, principal tags, or workload identity.\\n- Separate roles:\\n  - **Runtime role**: encrypt/decrypt/generate data keys required by the service.\\n  - **Rotation role**: permissions to change key version references, update config, manage grants, and perform cutover steps.\\n  - **Break-glass role**: time-bound, audited access used only during incidents with approvals.", "score": 0.639844, "rank": 6, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "d8ab640c-89bf-599d-b59f-47060a0e9c7e", "search_unit_id": "d8ab640c-89bf-599d-b59f-47060a0e9c7e", "block_from_id": "4d749810-42ed-5db5-8849-0584bdb9e806", "block_to_id": "e7f9c7ac-af61-5236-a6b8-86dc91e7c068", "section_path": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > IAM and permission scoping requirements > Minimum permissions (illustrative)", "document_id": "eb166774-f9a9-56c9-984c-5fd7406c2bd1", "document_version_id": "76710c2c-2fe6-553c-ba81-ed6c87f0cfe5", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_377cdf4e378f40bebd7196e3a0ff1c38.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-32", "heading": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > IAM and permission scoping requirements > Minimum permissions (illustrative)", "content": "Minimum permissions (illustrative)\\n\\nActual permissions differ by provider; implement via the Infra baseline modules where available.\\n\\n**Runtime role MUST be limited to:**\\n\\n- Encrypt/Decrypt/GenerateDataKey/ReEncrypt (only if required)\\n- DescribeKey (if required for health validation; otherwise avoid)\\n- No key policy changes\\n\\n**Rotation/admin role MAY include:**\\n\\n- Grant management operations (where applicable)\\n- Ability to update relevant config in Redwood control plane\\n- Access to audit/event logs for evidence collection", "score": 0.635571, "rank": 7, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "abebeba2-5814-5834-ba01-958f3ae32ba4", "search_unit_id": "abebeba2-5814-5834-ba01-958f3ae32ba4", "block_from_id": "eb1b31c1-b23a-508e-8e8d-7e741a0625b6", "block_to_id": "328906f4-a22a-5d64-9520-ecc6279569a7", "section_path": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Purpose", "document_id": "eb166774-f9a9-56c9-984c-5fd7406c2bd1", "document_version_id": "76710c2c-2fe6-553c-ba81-ed6c87f0cfe5", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_377cdf4e378f40bebd7196e3a0ff1c38.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-2", "heading": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Purpose", "content": "Purpose\\n\\nThis standard defines minimum security and reliability requirements for integrating Redwood Inference services with customer-managed or Redwood-managed Key Management Systems (KMS) used for envelope encryption (KEK/DEK patterns), including optional HSM-backed keys.\\n\\nThis document is intended to:\\n\\n- Prevent insecure or brittle KMS usage (overbroad IAM, missing audit evidence, retry storms, unsafe caching).\\n- Make KMS-related failures diagnosable and operable (consistent logs/metrics/traces, runbooks, game-day readiness).\\n- Ensure KMS integrations pass enterprise security reviews for Hosted, Dedicated, and Private deployments.", "score": 0.600278, "rank": 8, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "3a26a5ea-a7ff-5a4f-b4a6-c019d9d23489", "search_unit_id": "3a26a5ea-a7ff-5a4f-b4a6-c019d9d23489", "block_from_id": "9027bdb5-2681-5272-ba8a-cb7ed98183fe", "block_to_id": "45dd1582-60ac-51dd-b6cc-aa2a7415fd04", "section_path": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > IAM and permission scoping requirements > Credential management", "document_id": "eb166774-f9a9-56c9-984c-5fd7406c2bd1", "document_version_id": "76710c2c-2fe6-553c-ba81-ed6c87f0cfe5", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_377cdf4e378f40bebd7196e3a0ff1c38.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-40", "heading": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > IAM and permission scoping requirements > Credential management", "content": "Credential management\\n\\n- MUST avoid long-lived static credentials in code or baked images.\\n- MUST use workload identity (cloud-native) or customer-approved credential injection (Private) with clear rotation paths.", "score": 0.591483, "rank": 9, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "12a5e8b6-3892-5d1d-bb76-b04af8db4714", "search_unit_id": "12a5e8b6-3892-5d1d-bb76-b04af8db4714", "block_from_id": "149f2cc0-c88e-5441-8bcf-e1cffecd53c2", "block_to_id": "4c6e2e43-984f-5d2e-990b-58594ee03a5a", "section_path": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook", "document_id": "45f6686b-12fc-5fae-9c11-9abaeb20a3e5", "document_version_id": "a4bad94b-544e-5a78-88ce-d2659b6c4f79", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_c52c609c0cdf4211a7e8c57bb1da72e4.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h1-0", "heading": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook", "content": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook\\n\\nSource type: confluence\\nDocument ID: dsid_c52c609c0cdf4211a7e8c57bb1da72e4\\nRelease: v1.0.0\\nBenchmark: EnterpriseRAG-Bench synthetic upstream data\\nUsage-Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook (Tokens, Retries, Caching, Credits, Disputes)", "score": 0.582077, "rank": 10, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "880bf395-8a09-5e02-a056-2b014b7a71ba", "search_unit_id": "880bf395-8a09-5e02-a056-2b014b7a71ba", "block_from_id": "d89c008a-dbcd-5b52-8ff7-46ff5c99d32b", "block_to_id": "e6ffa3fe-08c8-5e26-be13-9fd945e686c4", "section_path": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > IAM and permission scoping requirements > Provider-specific notes", "document_id": "eb166774-f9a9-56c9-984c-5fd7406c2bd1", "document_version_id": "76710c2c-2fe6-553c-ba81-ed6c87f0cfe5", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_377cdf4e378f40bebd7196e3a0ff1c38.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-38", "heading": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > IAM and permission scoping requirements > Provider-specific notes", "content": "Provider-specific notes\\n\\n- **AWS KMS**:\\n  - Use key policies to restrict admin operations; avoid granting broad `kms:*`.\\n  - Use grants where appropriate to reduce key policy sprawl.\\n  - Prefer condition keys like `kms:EncryptionContext:*` and `kms:ViaService` when feasible.\\n- **GCP Cloud KMS**:\\n  - Scope permissions at key ring / crypto key level; restrict `cloudkms.cryptoKeyVersions.useToDecrypt`/`useToEncrypt`.\\n- **Azure Key Vault / Managed HSM**:\\n  - Use RBAC where possible; scope to key object and operations; be explicit about `get`, `wrapKey`, `unwrapKey` equivalents.", "score": 0.590749, "rank": 11, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "5c06e5c2-0f5d-57c1-ae6d-b9c1b6bf9f5e", "search_unit_id": "5c06e5c2-0f5d-57c1-ae6d-b9c1b6bf9f5e", "block_from_id": "1fcb2132-aa0e-53e8-b647-8be5ac619388", "block_to_id": "55d1208d-7ad6-5d0d-b5be-644fabb959fc", "section_path": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Purpose", "document_id": "45f6686b-12fc-5fae-9c11-9abaeb20a3e5", "document_version_id": "a4bad94b-544e-5a78-88ce-d2659b6c4f79", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_c52c609c0cdf4211a7e8c57bb1da72e4.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-2", "heading": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Purpose", "content": "Purpose\\n\\nThis playbook provides Redwood Inference\xe2\x80\x99s approved legal guidance and clause library for **usage-based pricing** across Redwood API (Hosted) and related packaging. It is designed to:\\n\\n- Ensure **consistent definitions** (tokens, requests, cache hits, retries) across MSAs, Order Forms, pricing pages, and Sales communications.\\n- Reduce **invoice disputes** by aligning contract language with metering behavior.\\n- Support **revenue recognition (RevRec)** and audit readiness by defining authoritative sources, dispute windows, and credit/refund mechanics.\\n\\nThis page is **restricted** because it contains clause language and internal positions.", "score": 0.562233, "rank": 12, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "510240f0-57f2-5c07-a9e3-3a005bf1f7b2", "search_unit_id": "510240f0-57f2-5c07-a9e3-3a005bf1f7b2", "block_from_id": "30cd06a7-7976-5df7-a700-f3a8db74f6aa", "block_to_id": "5d52101c-4b31-561c-adda-13b2c66323cd", "section_path": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Scope > In scope", "document_id": "eb166774-f9a9-56c9-984c-5fd7406c2bd1", "document_version_id": "76710c2c-2fe6-553c-ba81-ed6c87f0cfe5", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_377cdf4e378f40bebd7196e3a0ff1c38.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-6", "heading": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Scope > In scope", "content": "Scope\\n\\nIn scope\\n\\n- Any code path that calls a cloud KMS/HSM or on-prem KMS interface for: encrypt, decrypt, generate data key, re-encrypt, describe key, list key versions, or grant/permission operations.\\n- Control-plane and data-plane components.\\n- Hosted, Dedicated, and Private deployments.", "score": 0.55935, "rank": 13, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "73fa7392-f532-51ad-9cd4-ecd4b3673263", "search_unit_id": "73fa7392-f532-51ad-9cd4-ecd4b3673263", "block_from_id": "a53a08c6-309c-5d09-807e-35e9007e1c21", "block_to_id": "fd3e425e-4dea-5e56-9775-c6ad1bce3cd4", "section_path": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Scope > Out of scope", "document_id": "eb166774-f9a9-56c9-984c-5fd7406c2bd1", "document_version_id": "76710c2c-2fe6-553c-ba81-ed6c87f0cfe5", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_377cdf4e378f40bebd7196e3a0ff1c38.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-9", "heading": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Scope > Out of scope", "content": "Out of scope\\n\\n- Introducing new cryptographic primitives/algorithms (use existing approved primitives and libraries).\\n- Platform-wide authentication/authorization redesign.", "score": 0.538886, "rank": 14, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "aa618199-1700-5169-9eb9-d9710ea08acd", "search_unit_id": "aa618199-1700-5169-9eb9-d9710ea08acd", "block_from_id": "9c469c8c-f216-5bdc-a650-a06a4de9dcff", "block_to_id": "20c195c7-44df-5317-bc97-cd6c3637ea53", "section_path": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Implementation requirements (engineering checklist) > B) Permissions", "document_id": "eb166774-f9a9-56c9-984c-5fd7406c2bd1", "document_version_id": "76710c2c-2fe6-553c-ba81-ed6c87f0cfe5", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_377cdf4e378f40bebd7196e3a0ff1c38.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-94", "heading": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Implementation requirements (engineering checklist) > B) Permissions", "content": "B) Permissions\\n\\n- [ ] Runtime role has only required KMS operations.\\n- [ ] Resource scoping is explicit (key(s), environment).\\n- [ ] Rotation/admin permissions are separated from runtime permissions.\\n- [ ] No wildcard admin permissions without exception.", "score": 0.535619, "rank": 15, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "4a73af84-66bf-5298-8a9a-fdace2bd5548", "search_unit_id": "4a73af84-66bf-5298-8a9a-fdace2bd5548", "block_from_id": "aa86c8c9-1bc7-51e6-8a5d-4e1900064109", "block_to_id": "cc1448a2-1bb7-5b51-9c59-6d8b6ba5e719", "section_path": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Owner and change management", "document_id": "eb166774-f9a9-56c9-984c-5fd7406c2bd1", "document_version_id": "76710c2c-2fe6-553c-ba81-ed6c87f0cfe5", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_377cdf4e378f40bebd7196e3a0ff1c38.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-109", "heading": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Owner and change management", "content": "Owner and change management\\n\\n- Owner: Security Engineering\\n- Changes to this standard require Security + SRE review and are announced in #eng-security and #eng-sre.\\n\\n---\\nAppendix: Quick guidance for common pitfalls\\n\\n- **AccessDenied in Private deployments**: almost always mis-scoped principal/key policy/region mismatch. Ensure preflight validation checks are enabled and run.\\n- **Throttle spikes**: confirm retry jitter is enabled and that request concurrency has backpressure. Do not \xe2\x80\x9csolve\xe2\x80\x9d throttling by increasing retries.\\n- **InvalidCiphertext during rotation**: treat as potential key/version mismatch; verify dual-read settings and that ciphertext metadata includes the correct key reference.", "score": 0.518422, "rank": 16, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "21b03ced-2f24-5b2a-be7b-8dc7383725fc", "search_unit_id": "21b03ced-2f24-5b2a-be7b-8dc7383725fc", "block_from_id": "6471051c-e571-5c75-9f13-52f6f6f8ca43", "block_to_id": "f4db9761-2752-5b47-ba4b-e7c361512970", "section_path": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Definitions (approved internal meanings)", "document_id": "45f6686b-12fc-5fae-9c11-9abaeb20a3e5", "document_version_id": "a4bad94b-544e-5a78-88ce-d2659b6c4f79", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_c52c609c0cdf4211a7e8c57bb1da72e4.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-11", "heading": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Definitions (approved internal meanings)", "content": "Definitions (approved internal meanings)\\n\\nThe following definitions should be used as the \xe2\x80\x9csource definitions\xe2\x80\x9d when drafting or redlining contract language. If a customer demands alternate language, follow the escalation path below.", "score": 0.522546, "rank": 17, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "96c0225d-edf4-58e1-b032-2e7d8928f2ac", "search_unit_id": "96c0225d-edf4-58e1-b032-2e7d8928f2ac", "block_from_id": "8ab3a2ef-5919-5ef5-a423-2d9c048f17a9", "block_to_id": "1467b681-0d1b-5b51-a8f3-36ac1a15c95a", "section_path": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Policy summary (MUST/SHOULD) > Reliability controls", "document_id": "eb166774-f9a9-56c9-984c-5fd7406c2bd1", "document_version_id": "76710c2c-2fe6-553c-ba81-ed6c87f0cfe5", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_377cdf4e378f40bebd7196e3a0ff1c38.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-17", "heading": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Policy summary (MUST/SHOULD) > Reliability controls", "content": "Reliability controls\\n\\n- MUST use the standardized KMS client wrapper (ADR-007) for timeouts, retries, error taxonomy, and telemetry.\\n- MUST implement bounded retries with jitter and global retry budgets to avoid retry amplification.\\n- MUST include circuit breaker / degrade-mode behavior for KMS dependency failures where service availability requires it.\\n- MUST document expected behavior when KMS is degraded/unavailable (fail closed vs fail open) and obtain Security + SRE sign-off.", "score": 0.518422, "rank": 18, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "788515d0-f050-5715-b3a5-0d78e903641c", "search_unit_id": "788515d0-f050-5715-b3a5-0d78e903641c", "block_from_id": "a4003598-0a69-5a7c-8559-510ed097cf35", "block_to_id": "b86316a7-b0e7-5fb3-a577-634d7db49dbb", "section_path": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Rotation readiness requirements", "document_id": "eb166774-f9a9-56c9-984c-5fd7406c2bd1", "document_version_id": "76710c2c-2fe6-553c-ba81-ed6c87f0cfe5", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_377cdf4e378f40bebd7196e3a0ff1c38.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-71", "heading": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Rotation readiness requirements", "content": "Rotation readiness requirements\\n\\nAll new KMS call sites MUST be compatible with the approved rotation approach (ADR-008):\\n\\n- Support key versioning and cutover without requiring downtime.\\n- Support dual-read/dual-decrypt during the transition window when applicable.\\n- Emit signals to detect mismatch (`InvalidCiphertext` spikes, decrypt failures, version skew).\\n\\nMinimum rotation readiness checklist:\\n\\n- Key identifiers stored with ciphertext/wrapped material in a way that supports selecting the correct key.\\n- Ability to read/decrypt items encrypted under both old and new key versions during the cutover window (where applicable).\\n- Documented rollback plan that does not require data rewrite under incident pressure.", "score": 0.518422, "rank": 19, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "d01356ab-fe3c-5e88-bdcd-047043c4253e", "search_unit_id": "d01356ab-fe3c-5e88-bdcd-047043c4253e", "block_from_id": "da95a97a-c4b5-51eb-970d-64867d44f776", "block_to_id": "ffd0db5e-b969-5503-8de5-c8157e198734", "section_path": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Required logging, metrics, and tracing > Metrics (MUST)", "document_id": "eb166774-f9a9-56c9-984c-5fd7406c2bd1", "document_version_id": "76710c2c-2fe6-553c-ba81-ed6c87f0cfe5", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_377cdf4e378f40bebd7196e3a0ff1c38.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-51", "heading": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Required logging, metrics, and tracing > Metrics (MUST)", "content": "Metrics (MUST)\\n\\nEvery service making KMS calls MUST emit the following metrics (names are illustrative; use the platform standard naming):\\n\\n- `kms_client_request_total{operation,provider,env,region,result,error_category}`\\n- `kms_client_latency_ms_bucket{operation,provider,env,region}` (histogram)\\n- `kms_client_throttled_total{operation,provider,env,region}`\\n- `kms_client_retry_attempts_total{operation,provider,env,region}`\\n- `kms_client_circuit_breaker_state{service,env}` (gauge) where circuit breaker is implemented", "score": 0.518422, "rank": 20, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "18597ccc-716d-5b93-97cd-0d3e0b9dcad8", "search_unit_id": "18597ccc-716d-5b93-97cd-0d3e0b9dcad8", "block_from_id": "1859f289-3709-5156-81d9-a0ef773455fc", "block_to_id": "f05103d1-29a4-5524-95a5-c597259cc72a", "section_path": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Timeouts, retries, circuit breakers, and caching > Caching", "document_id": "eb166774-f9a9-56c9-984c-5fd7406c2bd1", "document_version_id": "76710c2c-2fe6-553c-ba81-ed6c87f0cfe5", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_377cdf4e378f40bebd7196e3a0ff1c38.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-69", "heading": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Timeouts, retries, circuit breakers, and caching > Caching", "content": "Caching\\n\\n- MAY cache KMS key metadata for short durations if it does not create rotation hazards.\\n- MUST NOT cache plaintext DEKs.\\n- MUST ensure caching does not cause stale key version usage that breaks rotation. Any caching around key identifiers or key version metadata MUST include:\\n  - bounded TTLs\\n  - invalidation on cutover\\n  - explicit rollback behavior", "score": 0.518422, "rank": 21, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "7d48ec91-cffa-5dcd-811b-c79294e3d0d1", "search_unit_id": "7d48ec91-cffa-5dcd-811b-c79294e3d0d1", "block_from_id": "5cc14cd2-eba0-5923-afca-6ea8e541298c", "block_to_id": "994f768d-847d-50c5-a2d2-00fda09dac39", "section_path": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Policy summary (MUST/SHOULD)", "document_id": "eb166774-f9a9-56c9-984c-5fd7406c2bd1", "document_version_id": "76710c2c-2fe6-553c-ba81-ed6c87f0cfe5", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_377cdf4e378f40bebd7196e3a0ff1c38.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-13", "heading": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Policy summary (MUST/SHOULD)", "content": "Policy summary (MUST/SHOULD)\\n\\nThe following are mandatory unless an exception is approved (see \xe2\x80\x9cExceptions\xe2\x80\x9d).", "score": 0.527671, "rank": 22, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "44f77ad5-bc99-5f14-b5d9-624c2013380c", "search_unit_id": "44f77ad5-bc99-5f14-b5d9-624c2013380c", "block_from_id": "a39b747b-8cc0-5b2c-aa22-e9e174d9521a", "block_to_id": "37954421-5575-55a2-834d-f84e76f0c7fb", "section_path": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Approved integration patterns > 1) Envelope encryption (recommended default)", "document_id": "eb166774-f9a9-56c9-984c-5fd7406c2bd1", "document_version_id": "76710c2c-2fe6-553c-ba81-ed6c87f0cfe5", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_377cdf4e378f40bebd7196e3a0ff1c38.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-21", "heading": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Approved integration patterns > 1) Envelope encryption (recommended default)", "content": "Approved integration patterns\\n\\n1) Envelope encryption (recommended default)\\n\\n1. Use KMS `GenerateDataKey` (or equivalent) to obtain plaintext DEK + encrypted/wrapped DEK.\\n2. Encrypt data locally with plaintext DEK.\\n3. Store ciphertext + wrapped DEK + key metadata (key ID/ARN, key version if provided, encryption context identifiers).\\n4. Discard plaintext DEK from memory as soon as possible.\\n5. On read, decrypt wrapped DEK via KMS and decrypt data locally.", "score": 0.518422, "rank": 23, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "e519b5dc-46e9-5b8f-b5ba-888faf791a66", "search_unit_id": "e519b5dc-46e9-5b8f-b5ba-888faf791a66", "block_from_id": "30d58a53-bd06-5914-9ca3-fefe7a07a097", "block_to_id": "86a36bb0-3bff-530b-af03-dc3b9fdb5b19", "section_path": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Definitions", "document_id": "eb166774-f9a9-56c9-984c-5fd7406c2bd1", "document_version_id": "76710c2c-2fe6-553c-ba81-ed6c87f0cfe5", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_377cdf4e378f40bebd7196e3a0ff1c38.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-11", "heading": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Definitions", "content": "Definitions\\n\\n- **KEK**: Key Encryption Key (often a KMS-managed key). Used to wrap/unwrap DEKs.\\n- **DEK**: Data Encryption Key (used for encrypting actual payloads; typically generated and wrapped by KMS).\\n- **Envelope encryption**: Data encrypted with DEK; DEK encrypted (wrapped) by KEK.\\n- **Rotation**: Periodic replacement of KEKs and/or DEKs. See ADR-008 for the approved strategy.\\n- **Call site**: A distinct service/component code path that invokes KMS APIs.", "score": 0.518422, "rank": 24, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "fde335d2-bb69-59ce-a101-829673ea0301", "search_unit_id": "fde335d2-bb69-59ce-a101-829673ea0301", "block_from_id": "f7b5af57-16ac-5022-9a4a-dffbe1783a03", "block_to_id": "ce50407e-b3b2-573d-a38c-737676564b20", "section_path": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Required reviews for new KMS call sites > When this standard applies", "document_id": "eb166774-f9a9-56c9-984c-5fd7406c2bd1", "document_version_id": "76710c2c-2fe6-553c-ba81-ed6c87f0cfe5", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_377cdf4e378f40bebd7196e3a0ff1c38.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-83", "heading": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Required reviews for new KMS call sites > When this standard applies", "content": "Required reviews for new KMS call sites\\n\\nWhen this standard applies\\n\\nIf your change introduces any new KMS interaction (new service, new operation, new key, new provider, or new runtime path), you MUST complete this review.", "score": 0.518422, "rank": 25, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "fa605139-78bf-566c-8ec4-06632e82489d", "search_unit_id": "fa605139-78bf-566c-8ec4-06632e82489d", "block_from_id": "5da71c40-387e-51de-8a8e-ca2824d2947c", "block_to_id": "eb84a1c7-a6b0-595d-8469-638fee845ada", "section_path": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > References", "document_id": "eb166774-f9a9-56c9-984c-5fd7406c2bd1", "document_version_id": "76710c2c-2fe6-553c-ba81-ed6c87f0cfe5", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_377cdf4e378f40bebd7196e3a0ff1c38.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-107", "heading": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > References", "content": "References\\n\\n- ADR-007: KMS client wrapper and failure policy\\n- ADR-008: Key rotation strategy (dual-read and cutover)\\n- KMS decrypt failures runbook\\n- IAM baseline and rotation roles standard\\n- Private deployment KMS operator guide", "score": 0.518422, "rank": 26, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "9921121d-90a5-5fbf-a014-851db9e4887d", "search_unit_id": "9921121d-90a5-5fbf-a014-851db9e4887d", "block_from_id": "77e8b112-5ce2-5958-984a-09db2d72587a", "block_to_id": "6932e9e2-5731-57e3-9f20-d3ebf03b766b", "section_path": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Exceptions", "document_id": "eb166774-f9a9-56c9-984c-5fd7406c2bd1", "document_version_id": "76710c2c-2fe6-553c-ba81-ed6c87f0cfe5", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_377cdf4e378f40bebd7196e3a0ff1c38.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-104", "heading": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Exceptions", "content": "Exceptions\\n\\nIf you cannot meet any MUST requirement, you MUST request an exception using the KMS rotation exceptions process:\\n\\n- Provide: scope, duration, risk assessment, compensating controls, and rollback plan.\\n- Approvals: Security Engineering lead + GRC/Compliance as required.\\n- Exceptions are time-bound and must include a plan to remediate.", "score": 0.518422, "rank": 27, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "d45e045b-3feb-5a71-8ada-1a66c858928a", "search_unit_id": "d45e045b-3feb-5a71-8ada-1a66c858928a", "block_from_id": "133f6463-d9a7-56d7-a440-37f0d84a0602", "block_to_id": "e675a519-1acd-5b44-b971-5faa9b3db5d1", "section_path": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Approved integration patterns > 2) Direct KMS encryption (restricted)", "document_id": "eb166774-f9a9-56c9-984c-5fd7406c2bd1", "document_version_id": "76710c2c-2fe6-553c-ba81-ed6c87f0cfe5", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_377cdf4e378f40bebd7196e3a0ff1c38.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-24", "heading": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Approved integration patterns > 2) Direct KMS encryption (restricted)", "content": "2) Direct KMS encryption (restricted)\\n\\nDirect KMS encrypt/decrypt for application payloads is discouraged due to size limits, latency, and cost. It MAY be used only for very small blobs (e.g., short secrets) with explicit Security approval and documented SLO impact.", "score": 0.518422, "rank": 28, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "a5f5ea81-ce94-5540-9890-464d284d5044", "search_unit_id": "a5f5ea81-ce94-5540-9890-464d284d5044", "block_from_id": "8b920fc9-7769-54e2-9454-3810cab1a1a7", "block_to_id": "c54e65bd-a698-5d29-a2fb-da38051d234f", "section_path": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Required logging, metrics, and tracing > Canonical KMS error taxonomy", "document_id": "eb166774-f9a9-56c9-984c-5fd7406c2bd1", "document_version_id": "76710c2c-2fe6-553c-ba81-ed6c87f0cfe5", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_377cdf4e378f40bebd7196e3a0ff1c38.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-48", "heading": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Required logging, metrics, and tracing > Canonical KMS error taxonomy", "content": "Canonical KMS error taxonomy\\n\\nAll KMS provider errors MUST map to the following categories (used for alerting and runbooks):\\n\\n- `AccessDenied`\\n- `NotFound` (key or version not found)\\n- `Throttling`\\n- `Timeout`\\n- `InvalidCiphertext` (includes key mismatch, wrong context, corrupted material)\\n- `KeyDisabled` / `KeyInvalidState`\\n- `DependencyUnavailable` (provider outage / transient 5xx)\\n- `Unknown`", "score": 0.518422, "rank": 29, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "352b8c26-66a6-5c42-99dd-0d5ce152d762", "search_unit_id": "352b8c26-66a6-5c42-99dd-0d5ce152d762", "block_from_id": "2091af71-afa9-54c4-859c-edf9a54e9ff3", "block_to_id": "c50fce31-c9ec-51fe-a714-b215bfdbfb21", "section_path": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Required logging, metrics, and tracing > Logging (application logs)", "document_id": "eb166774-f9a9-56c9-984c-5fd7406c2bd1", "document_version_id": "76710c2c-2fe6-553c-ba81-ed6c87f0cfe5", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_377cdf4e378f40bebd7196e3a0ff1c38.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-42", "heading": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Required logging, metrics, and tracing > Logging (application logs)", "content": "Required logging, metrics, and tracing\\n\\nLogging (application logs)\\n\\nMUST include structured fields on KMS calls and failures:\\n\\n- `kms.provider` (aws|gcp|azure|other)\\n- `kms.operation` (encrypt|decrypt|generate_data_key|reencrypt|describe_key|...)\\n- `kms.key_id` (redacted/normalized identifier; do not log full customer key ARN if customer policy requires redaction)\\n- `kms.region` (if applicable)\\n- `kms.error_category` (canonical taxonomy)\\n- `kms.http_status` or provider status (if available)\\n- `kms.request_id` (provider request id when available)\\n- `deployment_mode` (hosted|dedicated|private)\\n- `env` and `service`\\n\\nMUST NOT log:\\n\\n- Plaintext data\\n- Plaintext DEKs\\n- Wrapped DEKs (unless explicitly approved; default is \xe2\x80\x9cdo not log\xe2\x80\x9d)\\n- Customer secrets, tokens, or credential material", "score": 0.518422, "rank": 30, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "9cd19051-eac7-582d-8cb4-1f69ef766599", "search_unit_id": "9cd19051-eac7-582d-8cb4-1f69ef766599", "block_from_id": "74b96ac8-7ef5-546f-bb22-53683a767e4a", "block_to_id": "a307ff9e-f9d1-5c4f-b427-707fef7de92f", "section_path": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Clause library (approved language) > A. Usage unit (Tokens) \xe2\x80\x94 baseline clause", "document_id": "45f6686b-12fc-5fae-9c11-9abaeb20a3e5", "document_version_id": "a4bad94b-544e-5a78-88ce-d2659b6c4f79", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_c52c609c0cdf4211a7e8c57bb1da72e4.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-41", "heading": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Clause library (approved language) > A. Usage unit (Tokens) \xe2\x80\x94 baseline clause", "content": "A. Usage unit (Tokens) \xe2\x80\x94 baseline clause\\n\\n**Approved clause (standard):**\\n\xe2\x80\x9cUsage is measured in tokens processed by the applicable model. A token is a unit of text determined by the model\xe2\x80\x99s tokenization scheme. Fees are calculated based on the number of billed tokens reported by Redwood for the applicable billing period. Token counts may vary by model and model version.\xe2\x80\x9d\\n\\n**Negotiation notes:**\\n\\n- If customer requests a fixed tokenization algorithm, respond that tokenization is model-dependent and tied to the model provider\xe2\x80\x99s implementation.\\n- If customer requests billing purely on input+output tokens, steer to \xe2\x80\x9cbilled tokens\xe2\x80\x9d and point to reporting transparency.", "score": 0.502703, "rank": 31, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "cf5d70b8-230d-51f7-ba72-9e34beacb681", "search_unit_id": "cf5d70b8-230d-51f7-ba72-9e34beacb681", "block_from_id": "fb63f85b-3221-5e41-9d81-829c574a50d9", "block_to_id": "2f5f1a06-2199-5fe4-8e8c-680aa85c93bd", "section_path": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Appendix: example exhibit (usage definitions)", "document_id": "45f6686b-12fc-5fae-9c11-9abaeb20a3e5", "document_version_id": "a4bad94b-544e-5a78-88ce-d2659b6c4f79", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_c52c609c0cdf4211a7e8c57bb1da72e4.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-108", "heading": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Appendix: example exhibit (usage definitions)", "content": "Appendix: example exhibit (usage definitions)\\n\\nUse only when procurement requires a detailed exhibit; keep it concise.\\n\\n**Exhibit X \xe2\x80\x94 Usage Definitions (Example)**\\n\\n- \xe2\x80\x9cBilled Tokens\xe2\x80\x9d means the token quantity reported by Redwood for billing, which may account for caching adjustments and promotional inclusions, as reflected in Redwood\xe2\x80\x99s usage report.\\n- \xe2\x80\x9cIdempotency Key\xe2\x80\x9d means a unique identifier provided by Customer to allow safe retries without duplicate logical charges.\\n- \xe2\x80\x9cCache Hit\xe2\x80\x9d means a request (or portion thereof) served from Redwood-managed cache, which may be reported as cached usage and may be billed differently as reflected in the usage report.", "score": 0.502703, "rank": 32, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "2c90edb5-1b37-5c98-86ba-49aff0250bdb", "search_unit_id": "2c90edb5-1b37-5c98-86ba-49aff0250bdb", "block_from_id": "e63235e2-2205-59fc-8324-16ab0bf96993", "block_to_id": "e80fc2a2-a569-5021-aa48-25294d5588c0", "section_path": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Drafting guidance (what to include in usage-based terms) > Required building blocks", "document_id": "45f6686b-12fc-5fae-9c11-9abaeb20a3e5", "document_version_id": "a4bad94b-544e-5a78-88ce-d2659b6c4f79", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_c52c609c0cdf4211a7e8c57bb1da72e4.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-34", "heading": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Drafting guidance (what to include in usage-based terms) > Required building blocks", "content": "Drafting guidance (what to include in usage-based terms)\\n\\nRequired building blocks\\n\\nFor any Order Form/SOW with usage-based fees, include:\\n1) Usage unit definition (tokens, embeddings units, requests, GPU-seconds if applicable)\\n2) Billing measurement and reporting source (invoice + usage report)\\n3) Caching and retries treatment (at least at a high level)\\n4) Dispute window + audit mechanics (reasonable; avoids open-ended re-billing risk)\\n5) Credits/refunds policy (when available; how applied)\\n6) Change management notice (especially if customer requests strict metering invariants)", "score": 0.502703, "rank": 33, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "7d9323c1-779b-52c4-afce-8effc47ae8e9", "search_unit_id": "7d9323c1-779b-52c4-afce-8effc47ae8e9", "block_from_id": "29c72803-1641-5997-b711-b3fbfb1fefa1", "block_to_id": "818b466b-43fc-5f95-adae-9481cf038031", "section_path": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Change log", "document_id": "45f6686b-12fc-5fae-9c11-9abaeb20a3e5", "document_version_id": "a4bad94b-544e-5a78-88ce-d2659b6c4f79", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_c52c609c0cdf4211a7e8c57bb1da72e4.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-112", "heading": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Change log", "content": "Change log\\n\\n- 2026-02-24: Updated retry/idempotency position to align with metering hardening work and shadow-billing compare; clarified streaming interruption treatment; added meter-change notice clause.\\n- 2026-01-10: Added caching clause options and dispute window negotiation guidance.", "score": 0.502703, "rank": 34, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "16ac0f78-3244-5ade-ad48-7086d2b5f58a", "search_unit_id": "16ac0f78-3244-5ade-ad48-7086d2b5f58a", "block_from_id": "dc3a50fb-6b76-5c73-be99-25146b9fcf12", "block_to_id": "d3886235-3df8-5801-81d4-aa0e859a78c3", "section_path": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Timeouts, retries, circuit breakers, and caching > Standardized client wrapper", "document_id": "eb166774-f9a9-56c9-984c-5fd7406c2bd1", "document_version_id": "76710c2c-2fe6-553c-ba81-ed6c87f0cfe5", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_377cdf4e378f40bebd7196e3a0ff1c38.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-59", "heading": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Timeouts, retries, circuit breakers, and caching > Standardized client wrapper", "content": "Timeouts, retries, circuit breakers, and caching\\n\\nStandardized client wrapper\\n\\nAll KMS integrations MUST use the Redwood standard KMS client wrapper (ADR-007). Direct provider SDK calls in application code require an exception.", "score": 0.518422, "rank": 35, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "c0071190-f8c1-5f12-8235-37bced749c29", "search_unit_id": "c0071190-f8c1-5f12-8235-37bced749c29", "block_from_id": "d13221b6-fccd-51fd-a2f2-344593f02e6e", "block_to_id": "ad95ac19-2bf7-5438-a0f8-622a834c3d8c", "section_path": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Internal operational guardrails (contracting) > Backfills and corrections", "document_id": "45f6686b-12fc-5fae-9c11-9abaeb20a3e5", "document_version_id": "a4bad94b-544e-5a78-88ce-d2659b6c4f79", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_c52c609c0cdf4211a7e8c57bb1da72e4.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-88", "heading": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Internal operational guardrails (contracting) > Backfills and corrections", "content": "Backfills and corrections\\n\\nIf Redwood discovers a metering bug:\\n\\n- Default approach is **forward-looking fixes** with audit trail.\\n- Retroactive invoice changes require Finance + Legal approval.", "score": 0.502703, "rank": 36, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "370e162e-32b9-520c-8c04-9c911a5be59c", "search_unit_id": "370e162e-32b9-520c-8c04-9c911a5be59c", "block_from_id": "39cef05d-f486-5634-9697-a4722b82d476", "block_to_id": "53c27245-9374-5a1f-9fc7-27e2c77e8d34", "section_path": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations", "document_id": "eb166774-f9a9-56c9-984c-5fd7406c2bd1", "document_version_id": "76710c2c-2fe6-553c-ba81-ed6c87f0cfe5", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_377cdf4e378f40bebd7196e3a0ff1c38.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h1-0", "heading": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations", "content": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations\\n\\nSource type: confluence\\nDocument ID: dsid_377cdf4e378f40bebd7196e3a0ff1c38\\nRelease: v1.0.0\\nBenchmark: EnterpriseRAG-Bench synthetic upstream data\\nKey Management Standard: KMS Integrations", "score": 0.579814, "rank": 37, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "575df704-c2f0-5d38-8e2d-c967b1ca5d44", "search_unit_id": "575df704-c2f0-5d38-8e2d-c967b1ca5d44", "block_from_id": "16f31977-8539-5b20-919d-828c1b4db3fc", "block_to_id": "fb2c2d86-d9ad-503d-b509-03352ece4506", "section_path": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Escalation path (when to pull in Legal/Finance/Engineering) > Escalate to Engineering (Nadia Rahman / Logan Wright)", "document_id": "45f6686b-12fc-5fae-9c11-9abaeb20a3e5", "document_version_id": "a4bad94b-544e-5a78-88ce-d2659b6c4f79", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_c52c609c0cdf4211a7e8c57bb1da72e4.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-104", "heading": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Escalation path (when to pull in Legal/Finance/Engineering) > Escalate to Engineering (Nadia Rahman / Logan Wright)", "content": "Escalate to Engineering (Nadia Rahman / Logan Wright)\\n\\n- Customer requires a written description of metering behavior for retries/streaming/tool calls\\n- Customer reports discrepancy between invoice and usage export needing technical reconciliation\\n- Customer requests special export formats/timezone/day-boundary logic", "score": 0.502703, "rank": 38, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "1477e936-966e-5954-ab55-dd220f8f44b6", "search_unit_id": "1477e936-966e-5954-ab55-dd220f8f44b6", "block_from_id": "552aa740-c785-589b-a1bd-a5d0db1a5be6", "block_to_id": "31da99ae-c752-5812-ba27-d7e69ee179be", "section_path": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Questions", "document_id": "45f6686b-12fc-5fae-9c11-9abaeb20a3e5", "document_version_id": "a4bad94b-544e-5a78-88ce-d2659b6c4f79", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_c52c609c0cdf4211a7e8c57bb1da72e4.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-114", "heading": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Questions", "content": "Questions\\n\\nFor questions or proposed edits to this playbook, contact Sofia Mendes (Commercial Counsel) and tag Emily Stone (RevRec) for changes that affect billing acceptance, dispute windows, or credits/refunds mechanics.", "score": 0.502703, "rank": 39, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "cc4333e7-a779-5eb3-8434-4204fa0b02ea", "search_unit_id": "cc4333e7-a779-5eb3-8434-4204fa0b02ea", "block_from_id": "9ce79966-1063-5f20-b42d-30d1204727b6", "block_to_id": "0beece07-3311-561f-ac6c-c2b1c9759760", "section_path": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Clause library (approved language) > J. Meter changes and notice", "document_id": "45f6686b-12fc-5fae-9c11-9abaeb20a3e5", "document_version_id": "a4bad94b-544e-5a78-88ce-d2659b6c4f79", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_c52c609c0cdf4211a7e8c57bb1da72e4.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-69", "heading": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Clause library (approved language) > J. Meter changes and notice", "content": "J. Meter changes and notice\\n\\n**Approved clause (standard):**\\n\xe2\x80\x9cRedwood may update its measurement and reporting systems from time to time. Redwood will not materially increase charges due solely to a measurement change without providing prior notice and an opportunity to review supporting reporting for the change.\xe2\x80\x9d\\n\\n**Internal guidance:**\\n\\n- If the customer requests strict \xe2\x80\x9cno metering changes\xe2\x80\x9d language, escalate; this conflicts with ongoing hardening efforts (shadow-billing compare, meter v2) and can create operational risk.", "score": 0.502703, "rank": 40, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "8a9bd618-15a8-534b-8254-20fb8b06e8d3", "search_unit_id": "8a9bd618-15a8-534b-8254-20fb8b06e8d3", "block_from_id": "48d5d875-93ff-52a9-8da7-fde290a7f82b", "block_to_id": "749fd03a-e89a-5ad4-a1df-25bc90f25769", "section_path": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Timeouts, retries, circuit breakers, and caching > Retries", "document_id": "eb166774-f9a9-56c9-984c-5fd7406c2bd1", "document_version_id": "76710c2c-2fe6-553c-ba81-ed6c87f0cfe5", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_377cdf4e378f40bebd7196e3a0ff1c38.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-64", "heading": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Timeouts, retries, circuit breakers, and caching > Retries", "content": "Retries\\n\\n- MUST use exponential backoff with jitter.\\n- MUST cap maximum attempts and total retry time.\\n- MUST distinguish retryable vs non-retryable error categories:\\n  - Retryable: `Timeout`, `DependencyUnavailable`, some `Throttling` (with backoff)\\n  - Non-retryable: `AccessDenied`, `NotFound`, `InvalidCiphertext`, `KeyDisabled/InvalidState`", "score": 0.518422, "rank": 41, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "218f287e-5de1-5994-a375-b5e1948bd476", "search_unit_id": "218f287e-5de1-5994-a375-b5e1948bd476", "block_from_id": "02aba8c2-e018-5bea-a2e4-0a0afa4a867c", "block_to_id": "58bf0556-5b9f-562e-9fb6-8a18fc35648f", "section_path": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Clause library (approved language) > I. Credits and refunds (usage-based)", "document_id": "45f6686b-12fc-5fae-9c11-9abaeb20a3e5", "document_version_id": "a4bad94b-544e-5a78-88ce-d2659b6c4f79", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_c52c609c0cdf4211a7e8c57bb1da72e4.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-66", "heading": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Clause library (approved language) > I. Credits and refunds (usage-based)", "content": "I. Credits and refunds (usage-based)\\n\\n**Approved clause (standard):**\\n\xe2\x80\x9cCredits, if any, are applied to future invoices unless otherwise required by law. Except as expressly provided in the Agreement, fees are non-refundable.\xe2\x80\x9d\\n\\n**Optional add-on (when SLA credits apply):**\\n\xe2\x80\x9cService credits are Customer\xe2\x80\x99s sole and exclusive remedy for any failure to meet a service level, and will be calculated and applied as described in the applicable SLA.\xe2\x80\x9d", "score": 0.502703, "rank": 42, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "d4de55ac-eff9-5f1a-a6c5-21d4e1f72bf6", "search_unit_id": "d4de55ac-eff9-5f1a-a6c5-21d4e1f72bf6", "block_from_id": "3c5ed884-ad2f-5669-8d7d-08a388c27338", "block_to_id": "956944cd-431d-5c2e-9fad-af24cee232a7", "section_path": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Drafting guidance (what to include in usage-based terms) > Optional but recommended", "document_id": "45f6686b-12fc-5fae-9c11-9abaeb20a3e5", "document_version_id": "a4bad94b-544e-5a78-88ce-d2659b6c4f79", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_c52c609c0cdf4211a7e8c57bb1da72e4.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-37", "heading": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Drafting guidance (what to include in usage-based terms) > Optional but recommended", "content": "Optional but recommended\\n\\n- Timezone for daily usage exports (default: UTC) if customer cares about day-level reporting\\n- Explicit acknowledgment that tokenization differs by model and may evolve with model upgrades", "score": 0.502703, "rank": 43, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "bb161e6c-fb03-595c-a445-22d112750132", "search_unit_id": "bb161e6c-fb03-595c-a445-22d112750132", "block_from_id": "edc2186d-d71c-57ce-91f9-1011c05d5350", "block_to_id": "213a1e50-7454-5854-b0e6-23f93b84c4c9", "section_path": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Incident handling and operational expectations > Paging and severity guidance", "document_id": "eb166774-f9a9-56c9-984c-5fd7406c2bd1", "document_version_id": "76710c2c-2fe6-553c-ba81-ed6c87f0cfe5", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_377cdf4e378f40bebd7196e3a0ff1c38.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-79", "heading": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Incident handling and operational expectations > Paging and severity guidance", "content": "Paging and severity guidance\\n\\n- `AccessDenied` or `InvalidCiphertext` spikes are treated as correctness/security-impacting until proven otherwise.\\n- Sustained `Timeout`/`DependencyUnavailable` or elevated `Throttling` causing request failures should page SRE based on service SLO impact.", "score": 0.518422, "rank": 44, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "30c1120d-23b6-53f7-8178-8ef304414139", "search_unit_id": "30c1120d-23b6-53f7-8178-8ef304414139", "block_from_id": "41da29ea-0623-5971-9921-1009d4c3732c", "block_to_id": "4b414249-d546-5af5-9684-30f65668e1de", "section_path": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Clause library (approved language) > F. Retries and idempotency", "document_id": "45f6686b-12fc-5fae-9c11-9abaeb20a3e5", "document_version_id": "a4bad94b-544e-5a78-88ce-d2659b6c4f79", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_c52c609c0cdf4211a7e8c57bb1da72e4.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-56", "heading": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Clause library (approved language) > F. Retries and idempotency", "content": "F. Retries and idempotency\\n\\n**Approved clause (standard):**\\n\xe2\x80\x9cCustomer is responsible for implementing idempotency keys for retryable requests. Redwood will use commercially reasonable efforts to avoid duplicate billing for server-side retries performed under the same logical request identifier. Customer-submitted duplicate requests may be billable.\xe2\x80\x9d\\n\\n**Negotiation notes:**\\n\\n- Do not guarantee \xe2\x80\x9cno double billing ever.\xe2\x80\x9d Instead: \xe2\x80\x9ccommercially reasonable efforts\xe2\x80\x9d + dispute process.", "score": 0.502703, "rank": 45, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "513dbec8-4984-549c-bb94-5c2eda4edcfa", "search_unit_id": "513dbec8-4984-549c-bb94-5c2eda4edcfa", "block_from_id": "36e5b51c-1b68-5f74-be42-4809d16c215e", "block_to_id": "60b3ecaf-9edc-53bb-afad-1b9f5c7a90e2", "section_path": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Implementation requirements (engineering checklist) > E) Testing", "document_id": "eb166774-f9a9-56c9-984c-5fd7406c2bd1", "document_version_id": "76710c2c-2fe6-553c-ba81-ed6c87f0cfe5", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_377cdf4e378f40bebd7196e3a0ff1c38.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-100", "heading": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Implementation requirements (engineering checklist) > E) Testing", "content": "E) Testing\\n\\n- [ ] Integration tests cover: throttling, timeouts, AccessDenied, key disabled/invalid state.\\n- [ ] Tests assert retry budgets and latency caps (no retry storms).\\n- [ ] Rotation test (where applicable): decrypt under old+new key versions during dual-read window.", "score": 0.518422, "rank": 46, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "79361228-29eb-5351-b56c-b2764c88b4b9", "search_unit_id": "79361228-29eb-5351-b56c-b2764c88b4b9", "block_from_id": "155e90f2-9b2a-57ea-bc1c-d9899700b7d6", "block_to_id": "ab5ccf3b-c1da-50b3-9e17-2c4ecf4da706", "section_path": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Implementation requirements (engineering checklist) > C) Reliability behavior", "document_id": "eb166774-f9a9-56c9-984c-5fd7406c2bd1", "document_version_id": "76710c2c-2fe6-553c-ba81-ed6c87f0cfe5", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_377cdf4e378f40bebd7196e3a0ff1c38.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-96", "heading": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Implementation requirements (engineering checklist) > C) Reliability behavior", "content": "C) Reliability behavior\\n\\n- [ ] Uses the standard KMS wrapper.\\n- [ ] Explicit timeout configured.\\n- [ ] Retries are bounded, jittered, and category-aware.\\n- [ ] Circuit breaker behavior implemented (if required) and documented.\\n- [ ] Backpressure/throttle budgets considered for high-QPS paths.", "score": 0.518422, "rank": 47, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "66ecb499-298b-591d-b983-662298097ece", "search_unit_id": "66ecb499-298b-591d-b983-662298097ece", "block_from_id": "05af0edb-a48d-5060-9320-371b032fbef2", "block_to_id": "3afd4324-c798-5580-83e1-298272c3d67b", "section_path": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Definitions (approved internal meanings) > 4) \xe2\x80\x9cCaching\xe2\x80\x9d / \xe2\x80\x9cCache Hit\xe2\x80\x9d", "document_id": "45f6686b-12fc-5fae-9c11-9abaeb20a3e5", "document_version_id": "a4bad94b-544e-5a78-88ce-d2659b6c4f79", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_c52c609c0cdf4211a7e8c57bb1da72e4.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-25", "heading": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Definitions (approved internal meanings) > 4) \xe2\x80\x9cCaching\xe2\x80\x9d / \xe2\x80\x9cCache Hit\xe2\x80\x9d", "content": "4) \xe2\x80\x9cCaching\xe2\x80\x9d / \xe2\x80\x9cCache Hit\xe2\x80\x9d\\n\\nCaching may reduce compute performed by Redwood. Contract language must avoid obligating Redwood to charge based on compute cost; instead, define how caching affects billed tokens.\\n\\nInternal position:\\n\\n- We may apply **cache-hit attribution** to reduce billed usage for eligible cached content, as described in product documentation.\\n- Caching behavior can change over time as the service is optimized; the contract should permit evolution while maintaining transparency via reports.", "score": 0.502703, "rank": 48, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "e14d5671-2834-5fc5-8b35-0c23f2b69eee", "search_unit_id": "e14d5671-2834-5fc5-8b35-0c23f2b69eee", "block_from_id": "d75a9876-8214-543a-8245-a881559a2e97", "block_to_id": "02239eee-ebf0-5251-8984-3db7cec7ca50", "section_path": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Definitions (approved internal meanings) > 1) \xe2\x80\x9cToken\xe2\x80\x9d", "document_id": "45f6686b-12fc-5fae-9c11-9abaeb20a3e5", "document_version_id": "a4bad94b-544e-5a78-88ce-d2659b6c4f79", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_c52c609c0cdf4211a7e8c57bb1da72e4.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-13", "heading": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Definitions (approved internal meanings) > 1) \xe2\x80\x9cToken\xe2\x80\x9d", "content": "1) \xe2\x80\x9cToken\xe2\x80\x9d\\n\\n**Token** means a discrete unit of text as processed by the applicable model\xe2\x80\x99s tokenization scheme. Tokenization is model-dependent.\\n\\nImportant internal positions:\\n\\n- Token counts are **model-specific** and may differ between models and versions.\\n- For chat-style endpoints, token counts may include system/developer messages, tool call payloads, and structured output formatting as applicable.\\n- We support (and prefer to contract around) **billed tokens** as the invoicing unit, rather than raw \xe2\x80\x9cinput + output tokens,\xe2\x80\x9d because billed tokens reflects caching/discounting rules.\\n\\nRecommended terminology:\\n\\n- **Input Tokens / Prompt Tokens**: tokens attributable to the request context provided by the customer.\\n- **Output Tokens / Completion Tokens**: tokens generated by the model in response.\\n- **Billed Tokens**: the token quantity used for billing after applying billing rules (e.g., caching adjustments, promotional discounts, free-tier inclusion), as shown on the invoice and/or usage reports.", "score": 0.502703, "rank": 49, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "6746731a-daa1-5002-bcd5-88a0f8f2be71", "search_unit_id": "6746731a-daa1-5002-bcd5-88a0f8f2be71", "block_from_id": "a9b3b00d-e237-5cd0-8402-623ab53b9381", "block_to_id": "248741bc-f238-5b79-9562-e2fb710b589a", "section_path": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Clause library (approved language)", "document_id": "45f6686b-12fc-5fae-9c11-9abaeb20a3e5", "document_version_id": "a4bad94b-544e-5a78-88ce-d2659b6c4f79", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_c52c609c0cdf4211a7e8c57bb1da72e4.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-39", "heading": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Clause library (approved language)", "content": "Clause library (approved language)\\n\\nUse the below clauses as starting points. Do not materially alter without Legal review.", "score": 0.502703, "rank": 50, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "9565c10c-b537-5996-a037-0992caf4437b", "search_unit_id": "9565c10c-b537-5996-a037-0992caf4437b", "block_from_id": "6c592c69-ddd6-5fa9-a2b3-90d05f0dcb63", "block_to_id": "c1c3d4c9-8140-586e-bc13-9421d823f963", "section_path": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Implementation requirements (engineering checklist) > A) Design and data model", "document_id": "eb166774-f9a9-56c9-984c-5fd7406c2bd1", "document_version_id": "76710c2c-2fe6-553c-ba81-ed6c87f0cfe5", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_377cdf4e378f40bebd7196e3a0ff1c38.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-92", "heading": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Implementation requirements (engineering checklist) > A) Design and data model", "content": "A) Design and data model\\n\\n- [ ] Uses envelope encryption (or has approved exception).\\n- [ ] Stores sufficient metadata to select the correct key/version for decryption.\\n- [ ] Defines encryption context usage (if supported) and ensures it is stable across reads.", "score": 0.518422, "rank": 51, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "8e787471-2c93-5e0c-b23c-842011a8c8fd", "search_unit_id": "8e787471-2c93-5e0c-b23c-842011a8c8fd", "block_from_id": "2a6e8634-4078-5d0f-b2b7-5e79838237ac", "block_to_id": "e004a707-7c08-5c60-8df9-8b5d688ee497", "section_path": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Implementation requirements (engineering checklist) > D) Observability", "document_id": "eb166774-f9a9-56c9-984c-5fd7406c2bd1", "document_version_id": "76710c2c-2fe6-553c-ba81-ed6c87f0cfe5", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_377cdf4e378f40bebd7196e3a0ff1c38.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-98", "heading": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Implementation requirements (engineering checklist) > D) Observability", "content": "D) Observability\\n\\n- [ ] Standard metrics emitted with required tags.\\n- [ ] Trace spans added.\\n- [ ] Errors mapped to canonical taxonomy.\\n- [ ] Logs are structured and do not include sensitive material.\\n- [ ] Alerts/dashboards exist or a rationale is documented.", "score": 0.518422, "rank": 52, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "6ecdfac2-e33e-5278-87da-5b4098b241ad", "search_unit_id": "6ecdfac2-e33e-5278-87da-5b4098b241ad", "block_from_id": "0be29afa-0d30-58dd-bcd6-04cb2e43df73", "block_to_id": "7b2f74cb-e57a-53c7-981f-94300da38e70", "section_path": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Clause library (approved language) > E. Caching treatment", "document_id": "45f6686b-12fc-5fae-9c11-9abaeb20a3e5", "document_version_id": "a4bad94b-544e-5a78-88ce-d2659b6c4f79", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_c52c609c0cdf4211a7e8c57bb1da72e4.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-53", "heading": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Clause library (approved language) > E. Caching treatment", "content": "E. Caching treatment\\n\\n**Approved clause (standard):**\\n\xe2\x80\x9cRedwood may employ caching and other optimization techniques. Usage reports may distinguish cached and non-cached usage. Redwood may apply billing adjustments (including reduced billed tokens) for eligible cached content as described in Redwood documentation. Optimization techniques may change over time.\xe2\x80\x9d\\n\\n**Alternative clause (customer requests explicit fairness statement):**\\n\xe2\x80\x9cRedwood will not charge more than once for the same logical request submitted with the same idempotency key, and may reduce charges when caching is applied, as reflected in the usage report.\xe2\x80\x9d", "score": 0.502703, "rank": 53, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "3c4dbdfd-850a-5eda-b22d-9260f8aa52e4", "search_unit_id": "3c4dbdfd-850a-5eda-b22d-9260f8aa52e4", "block_from_id": "66344afb-02a0-51e6-b02d-7924de1a2906", "block_to_id": "ab25f424-feeb-5337-b661-744723da496f", "section_path": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Deal desk checklist (for usage-based terms)", "document_id": "45f6686b-12fc-5fae-9c11-9abaeb20a3e5", "document_version_id": "a4bad94b-544e-5a78-88ce-d2659b6c4f79", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_c52c609c0cdf4211a7e8c57bb1da72e4.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-106", "heading": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Deal desk checklist (for usage-based terms)", "content": "Deal desk checklist (for usage-based terms)\\n\\nBefore sending paper:\\n1) Confirm the usage unit(s) match the product packaging (tokens vs requests vs embeddings)\\n2) Confirm \xe2\x80\x9cbilled tokens\xe2\x80\x9d language is used where available\\n3) Ensure retries/idempotency clause is included if customer is retrying or using streaming\\n4) Confirm dispute window is 30 days (or approved exception)\\n5) Confirm credits policy matches Finance policy and RevRec requirements\\n6) Link to usage reporting source and avoid promises of exact parity with other providers", "score": 0.494518, "rank": 54, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "fa73353e-479d-59b7-8f8c-23b823f7c1cd", "search_unit_id": "fa73353e-479d-59b7-8f8c-23b823f7c1cd", "block_from_id": "7614faee-1317-5351-8e0c-33c7de9b4dfb", "block_to_id": "65890479-98b4-5e87-ac81-26085dea8fce", "section_path": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Definitions (approved internal meanings) > 5) \xe2\x80\x9cRetry\xe2\x80\x9d", "document_id": "45f6686b-12fc-5fae-9c11-9abaeb20a3e5", "document_version_id": "a4bad94b-544e-5a78-88ce-d2659b6c4f79", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_c52c609c0cdf4211a7e8c57bb1da72e4.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-29", "heading": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Definitions (approved internal meanings) > 5) \xe2\x80\x9cRetry\xe2\x80\x9d", "content": "5) \xe2\x80\x9cRetry\xe2\x80\x9d\\n\\nRetry can occur on:\\n\\n- **Client side** (customer\xe2\x80\x99s SDK/app retries)\\n- **Server side** (Redwood retries/fallback routing to preserve availability)\\n\\nInternal positions:\\n\\n- We aim to bill **once per logical request** where retries are transparently handled under the same idempotency key.\\n- If the customer does not use idempotency keys and submits duplicate requests, those may be billable.", "score": 0.502703, "rank": 55, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "8745edb2-5f98-5f90-ad3f-907bf93d1409", "search_unit_id": "8745edb2-5f98-5f90-ad3f-907bf93d1409", "block_from_id": "2254b6cd-38e3-5259-8a80-d658a543de92", "block_to_id": "f0315550-a0dd-5aa6-ac26-c84474028b97", "section_path": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Clause library (approved language) > G. Measurement system and authoritative records", "document_id": "45f6686b-12fc-5fae-9c11-9abaeb20a3e5", "document_version_id": "a4bad94b-544e-5a78-88ce-d2659b6c4f79", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_c52c609c0cdf4211a7e8c57bb1da72e4.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-60", "heading": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Clause library (approved language) > G. Measurement system and authoritative records", "content": "G. Measurement system and authoritative records\\n\\n**Approved clause (standard):**\\n\xe2\x80\x9cFees are based on Redwood\xe2\x80\x99s measurement systems and usage records. Redwood will provide usage reporting via invoice detail, Console, or usage export/API. In the event of conflict, the invoice and supporting usage report for the billing period will control, subject to Customer\xe2\x80\x99s dispute rights.\xe2\x80\x9d", "score": 0.502703, "rank": 56, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "8c28bd50-f6bf-59d3-9055-91b186f0444a", "search_unit_id": "8c28bd50-f6bf-59d3-9055-91b186f0444a", "block_from_id": "77434430-46dd-5420-982a-3ef0d1956b8a", "block_to_id": "18790c8a-c9a5-563b-9417-70535ddb9f47", "section_path": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Required logging, metrics, and tracing > Tracing (MUST)", "document_id": "eb166774-f9a9-56c9-984c-5fd7406c2bd1", "document_version_id": "76710c2c-2fe6-553c-ba81-ed6c87f0cfe5", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_377cdf4e378f40bebd7196e3a0ff1c38.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-54", "heading": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Required logging, metrics, and tracing > Tracing (MUST)", "content": "Tracing (MUST)\\n\\n- All KMS calls MUST create a trace span with:\\n  - operation name, provider, error category, and retry attempt count.\\n- Spans MUST not include sensitive payloads.", "score": 0.518422, "rank": 57, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "9a72d0eb-900f-5e68-88cd-e97e50f00fc2", "search_unit_id": "9a72d0eb-900f-5e68-88cd-e97e50f00fc2", "block_from_id": "d8ea22c8-b3cf-54f3-97fe-6c925c2af709", "block_to_id": "da590bda-659c-55ef-9295-5286ffb99a6f", "section_path": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Required reviews for new KMS call sites > Reviewers (minimum)", "document_id": "eb166774-f9a9-56c9-984c-5fd7406c2bd1", "document_version_id": "76710c2c-2fe6-553c-ba81-ed6c87f0cfe5", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_377cdf4e378f40bebd7196e3a0ff1c38.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-86", "heading": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Required reviews for new KMS call sites > Reviewers (minimum)", "content": "Reviewers (minimum)\\n\\n- Security Engineering reviewer (required)\\n- Infra/Platform IAM reviewer (required)\\n- SRE reviewer (required if the call site is in a latency-sensitive or high-QPS path)", "score": 0.518422, "rank": 58, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "5be1485b-5a7d-59fc-968f-528bf29ca5c1", "search_unit_id": "5be1485b-5a7d-59fc-968f-528bf29ca5c1", "block_from_id": "85820033-d754-5819-9545-b05aaa10c32a", "block_to_id": "dead98dc-0306-55a3-a7b7-e63714450f86", "section_path": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Redlines: common asks and recommended responses > 3) \xe2\x80\x9cCaching must always reduce price.\xe2\x80\x9d", "document_id": "45f6686b-12fc-5fae-9c11-9abaeb20a3e5", "document_version_id": "a4bad94b-544e-5a78-88ce-d2659b6c4f79", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_c52c609c0cdf4211a7e8c57bb1da72e4.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-78", "heading": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Redlines: common asks and recommended responses > 3) \xe2\x80\x9cCaching must always reduce price.\xe2\x80\x9d", "content": "3) \xe2\x80\x9cCaching must always reduce price.\xe2\x80\x9d\\n\\n**Position:** Caching may reduce billed tokens depending on eligibility and product policy.\\n**Response:** Use caching clause; avoid hard commitments. If needed for the deal, define a limited-term promotional adjustment with Finance sign-off.", "score": 0.502703, "rank": 59, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "b1220305-f7c9-5dfb-8648-ec273d3f1c0a", "search_unit_id": "b1220305-f7c9-5dfb-8648-ec273d3f1c0a", "block_from_id": "7c79072c-d40f-5c29-8c33-8f6ae4a8aa87", "block_to_id": "869d56b3-648b-5dcf-8d65-c949ab4a31bf", "section_path": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Definitions (approved internal meanings) > 2) \xe2\x80\x9cRequest\xe2\x80\x9d", "document_id": "45f6686b-12fc-5fae-9c11-9abaeb20a3e5", "document_version_id": "a4bad94b-544e-5a78-88ce-d2659b6c4f79", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_c52c609c0cdf4211a7e8c57bb1da72e4.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-19", "heading": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Definitions (approved internal meanings) > 2) \xe2\x80\x9cRequest\xe2\x80\x9d", "content": "2) \xe2\x80\x9cRequest\xe2\x80\x9d\\n\\nA **Request** is an API call that is accepted by Redwood\xe2\x80\x99s service and results in an attempt to process the call (including streaming requests). Do not tie \xe2\x80\x9crequest\xe2\x80\x9d to \xe2\x80\x9csuccessful response\xe2\x80\x9d unless Product/Finance explicitly approves.", "score": 0.502703, "rank": 60, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "e628dd05-e27c-519c-b9de-86d531da3b27", "search_unit_id": "e628dd05-e27c-519c-b9de-86d531da3b27", "block_from_id": "fc56d52d-d803-53c5-a33b-4261359c99ad", "block_to_id": "3af8a6c9-a2ed-5d6e-947e-0aafa765d342", "section_path": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Implementation requirements (engineering checklist) > F) Documentation", "document_id": "eb166774-f9a9-56c9-984c-5fd7406c2bd1", "document_version_id": "76710c2c-2fe6-553c-ba81-ed6c87f0cfe5", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_377cdf4e378f40bebd7196e3a0ff1c38.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-102", "heading": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Implementation requirements (engineering checklist) > F) Documentation", "content": "F) Documentation\\n\\n- [ ] Runbook updated (or new runbook added) with troubleshooting steps.\\n- [ ] Private/Dedicated operator docs updated if the integration is customer-configurable.", "score": 0.518422, "rank": 61, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "b391d898-19cd-5c5d-90cc-e5bb433478d4", "search_unit_id": "b391d898-19cd-5c5d-90cc-e5bb433478d4", "block_from_id": "93e1b7d6-f5ff-5aef-a6b1-f992516e8fb9", "block_to_id": "ac2c4711-6f53-5f2a-9518-2ed860569075", "section_path": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Redlines: common asks and recommended responses > 1) \xe2\x80\x9cTokens must match OpenAI exactly.\xe2\x80\x9d", "document_id": "45f6686b-12fc-5fae-9c11-9abaeb20a3e5", "document_version_id": "a4bad94b-544e-5a78-88ce-d2659b6c4f79", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_c52c609c0cdf4211a7e8c57bb1da72e4.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-73", "heading": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Redlines: common asks and recommended responses > 1) \xe2\x80\x9cTokens must match OpenAI exactly.\xe2\x80\x9d", "content": "Redlines: common asks and recommended responses\\n\\n1) \xe2\x80\x9cTokens must match OpenAI exactly.\xe2\x80\x9d\\n\\n**Position:** We support OpenAI-compatible endpoints, but tokenization/attribution can differ by model and implementation.\\n**Response:** Offer transparency: billed tokens reported; provide sample usage exports; consider adding a \xe2\x80\x9creporting parity\xe2\x80\x9d exhibit if necessary (requires Product + Eng + Legal review).", "score": 0.502703, "rank": 62, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "d2f49153-a706-57a4-bf58-ff90fd94b9a6", "search_unit_id": "d2f49153-a706-57a4-bf58-ff90fd94b9a6", "block_from_id": "17790f9b-c7ce-5e38-882b-7369e5c819d3", "block_to_id": "7f60b390-f293-59f7-ae78-9f60352ef3d6", "section_path": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Redlines: common asks and recommended responses > 2) \xe2\x80\x9cDo not charge for retries / failed requests.\xe2\x80\x9d", "document_id": "45f6686b-12fc-5fae-9c11-9abaeb20a3e5", "document_version_id": "a4bad94b-544e-5a78-88ce-d2659b6c4f79", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_c52c609c0cdf4211a7e8c57bb1da72e4.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-76", "heading": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Redlines: common asks and recommended responses > 2) \xe2\x80\x9cDo not charge for retries / failed requests.\xe2\x80\x9d", "content": "2) \xe2\x80\x9cDo not charge for retries / failed requests.\xe2\x80\x9d\\n\\n**Position:** If compute is performed, some usage may be reported.\\n**Response:** Use idempotency + commercially reasonable efforts clause. Offer a credits mechanism for verified platform-caused duplicate charges.", "score": 0.502703, "rank": 63, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "0668dbeb-47b5-545e-a50d-bc8108be9c2d", "search_unit_id": "0668dbeb-47b5-545e-a50d-bc8108be9c2d", "block_from_id": "26138765-be49-5fcc-a89f-a7d464efb788", "block_to_id": "82814d31-ce61-5b21-a2cb-f2957f092f42", "section_path": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Internal operational guardrails (contracting) > Customer communications", "document_id": "45f6686b-12fc-5fae-9c11-9abaeb20a3e5", "document_version_id": "a4bad94b-544e-5a78-88ce-d2659b6c4f79", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_c52c609c0cdf4211a7e8c57bb1da72e4.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-91", "heading": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Internal operational guardrails (contracting) > Customer communications", "content": "Customer communications\\n\\nIf contract or procurement asks for a customer-facing explanation:\\n\\n- Sales should use the approved FAQ language (see Sales Enablement page) and avoid promising exact token parity or \xe2\x80\x9cnever bill on retries.\xe2\x80\x9d", "score": 0.502703, "rank": 64, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "895b37e2-d8bd-5241-afae-582155ac8ecc", "search_unit_id": "895b37e2-d8bd-5241-afae-582155ac8ecc", "block_from_id": "a625460e-6aa0-5bfa-8e24-13aaa4178804", "block_to_id": "5ab32288-2a5b-5aac-b86f-761ce8d2fd99", "section_path": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Clause library (approved language) > D. Tool/function calling and structured output", "document_id": "45f6686b-12fc-5fae-9c11-9abaeb20a3e5", "document_version_id": "a4bad94b-544e-5a78-88ce-d2659b6c4f79", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_c52c609c0cdf4211a7e8c57bb1da72e4.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-51", "heading": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Clause library (approved language) > D. Tool/function calling and structured output", "content": "D. Tool/function calling and structured output\\n\\n**Approved clause (standard):**\\n\xe2\x80\x9cWhere the service supports tool/function calling or structured output, tokens attributable to tool call inputs/outputs and associated formatting may be included in token usage as reported by Redwood.\xe2\x80\x9d", "score": 0.502703, "rank": 65, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "7bcbb5c3-7dbe-5883-b0d9-09dc2a1b9982", "search_unit_id": "7bcbb5c3-7dbe-5883-b0d9-09dc2a1b9982", "block_from_id": "416cc4ea-c623-5815-9be2-4828dd785b72", "block_to_id": "39c5304a-822e-5481-ba29-585b5ecfe142", "section_path": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Clause library (approved language) > C. Streaming responses \xe2\x80\x94 how to describe", "document_id": "45f6686b-12fc-5fae-9c11-9abaeb20a3e5", "document_version_id": "a4bad94b-544e-5a78-88ce-d2659b6c4f79", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_c52c609c0cdf4211a7e8c57bb1da72e4.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-47", "heading": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Clause library (approved language) > C. Streaming responses \xe2\x80\x94 how to describe", "content": "C. Streaming responses \xe2\x80\x94 how to describe\\n\\n**Approved clause (standard):**\\n\xe2\x80\x9cFor streaming responses, usage is measured based on tokens processed and reported by Redwood for the request. If a streaming connection is interrupted, Redwood may report usage for tokens processed up to the point of interruption.\xe2\x80\x9d\\n\\n**Negotiation notes:**\\n\\n- Avoid promising that interrupted streams are always free; we can grant credits case-by-case.", "score": 0.502703, "rank": 66, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "1c87281f-dbfe-5fbd-9461-df789b69c43a", "search_unit_id": "1c87281f-dbfe-5fbd-9461-df789b69c43a", "block_from_id": "a0713bfe-dd93-5da5-8860-0a45be846e8e", "block_to_id": "9d839465-01ca-5e88-85fa-b865f8b68e46", "section_path": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Clause library (approved language) > B. Usage unit (Requests) \xe2\x80\x94 when included", "document_id": "45f6686b-12fc-5fae-9c11-9abaeb20a3e5", "document_version_id": "a4bad94b-544e-5a78-88ce-d2659b6c4f79", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_c52c609c0cdf4211a7e8c57bb1da72e4.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-45", "heading": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Clause library (approved language) > B. Usage unit (Requests) \xe2\x80\x94 when included", "content": "B. Usage unit (Requests) \xe2\x80\x94 when included\\n\\n**Approved clause (standard):**\\n\xe2\x80\x9cA request is an API call accepted by the service for processing. Requests that are duplicated by Customer (including due to Customer retries without an idempotency key) may be counted as separate requests.\xe2\x80\x9d", "score": 0.502703, "rank": 67, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "ea4737fc-5fe7-5f0c-b74b-7dbdcc5ce8e6", "search_unit_id": "ea4737fc-5fe7-5f0c-b74b-7dbdcc5ce8e6", "block_from_id": "12304ba3-e446-580a-a52f-921640e2d23a", "block_to_id": "52736ea3-c9e0-5975-8585-1335c8a64991", "section_path": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Escalation path (when to pull in Legal/Finance/Engineering) > Escalate to CFO (Laura Bennett)", "document_id": "45f6686b-12fc-5fae-9c11-9abaeb20a3e5", "document_version_id": "a4bad94b-544e-5a78-88ce-d2659b6c4f79", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_c52c609c0cdf4211a7e8c57bb1da72e4.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-102", "heading": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Escalation path (when to pull in Legal/Finance/Engineering) > Escalate to CFO (Laura Bennett)", "content": "Escalate to CFO (Laura Bennett)\\n\\n- Material concessions affecting revenue recognition or collection\\n- Any exception involving significant credits/refunds or contractual refund obligations", "score": 0.502703, "rank": 68, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "d81c9e94-c067-5bf1-baa8-6409480ba4ba", "search_unit_id": "d81c9e94-c067-5bf1-baa8-6409480ba4ba", "block_from_id": "5a9f924f-c86e-5547-be17-bbff6640c3bf", "block_to_id": "8763f3ba-c52a-5c54-b7ef-c51868bbc04a", "section_path": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Definitions (approved internal meanings) > 3) \xe2\x80\x9cUsage Report\xe2\x80\x9d / \xe2\x80\x9cUsage API\xe2\x80\x9d", "document_id": "45f6686b-12fc-5fae-9c11-9abaeb20a3e5", "document_version_id": "a4bad94b-544e-5a78-88ce-d2659b6c4f79", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_c52c609c0cdf4211a7e8c57bb1da72e4.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-21", "heading": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Definitions (approved internal meanings) > 3) \xe2\x80\x9cUsage Report\xe2\x80\x9d / \xe2\x80\x9cUsage API\xe2\x80\x9d", "content": "3) \xe2\x80\x9cUsage Report\xe2\x80\x9d / \xe2\x80\x9cUsage API\xe2\x80\x9d\\n\\n**Usage Report** means Redwood\xe2\x80\x99s reported usage as displayed in the Console, invoice detail, or usage export/API. Contract language should clarify which report is authoritative for billing.\\n\\nInternal preference:\\n\\n- For contracts: define that **Redwood\xe2\x80\x99s invoice and supporting usage report** is the authoritative basis for fees, subject to the dispute process.", "score": 0.502703, "rank": 69, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "0d2eb2d3-e6f7-5e8c-a043-124b3f125751", "search_unit_id": "0d2eb2d3-e6f7-5e8c-a043-124b3f125751", "block_from_id": "655ae510-32ef-5129-a79c-7aa87473f149", "block_to_id": "5ae54c7b-4a37-56e6-92e9-191ace395d89", "section_path": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Timeouts, retries, circuit breakers, and caching > Timeouts", "document_id": "eb166774-f9a9-56c9-984c-5fd7406c2bd1", "document_version_id": "76710c2c-2fe6-553c-ba81-ed6c87f0cfe5", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_377cdf4e378f40bebd7196e3a0ff1c38.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-62", "heading": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Timeouts, retries, circuit breakers, and caching > Timeouts", "content": "Timeouts\\n\\n- MUST enforce explicit per-call timeouts.\\n- MUST set a maximum end-to-end budget per request path (KMS calls included) and ensure KMS retries do not exceed that budget.", "score": 0.518422, "rank": 70, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "2fa76258-5409-51d1-8693-e36e078e07e8", "search_unit_id": "2fa76258-5409-51d1-8693-e36e078e07e8", "block_from_id": "70d0dd33-69ad-5b70-965f-c9d3ca4837bc", "block_to_id": "7f2bc05f-9a06-585c-a9c8-29459411516a", "section_path": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Escalation path (when to pull in Legal/Finance/Engineering) > Escalate to Commercial Counsel (Sofia Mendes)", "document_id": "45f6686b-12fc-5fae-9c11-9abaeb20a3e5", "document_version_id": "a4bad94b-544e-5a78-88ce-d2659b6c4f79", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_c52c609c0cdf4211a7e8c57bb1da72e4.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-96", "heading": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Escalation path (when to pull in Legal/Finance/Engineering) > Escalate to Commercial Counsel (Sofia Mendes)", "content": "Escalate to Commercial Counsel (Sofia Mendes)\\n\\n- Any requested change to dispute windows, audit rights, or refundability language\\n- Requests for \xe2\x80\x9cmost favored nation\xe2\x80\x9d pricing tied to token definitions\\n- Contractual commitments about caching or retry billing behavior", "score": 0.502703, "rank": 71, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "7bcb548c-af1b-5d06-8e97-dc663e735f55", "search_unit_id": "7bcb548c-af1b-5d06-8e97-dc663e735f55", "block_from_id": "9ff8f6b8-98f4-5311-bc2f-fb7db0987528", "block_to_id": "6f11ce2a-af5a-5c01-8afc-becb62aa3979", "section_path": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Approved integration patterns > 3) Customer-managed keys (CMK / external key)", "document_id": "eb166774-f9a9-56c9-984c-5fd7406c2bd1", "document_version_id": "76710c2c-2fe6-553c-ba81-ed6c87f0cfe5", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_377cdf4e378f40bebd7196e3a0ff1c38.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-26", "heading": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Approved integration patterns > 3) Customer-managed keys (CMK / external key)", "content": "3) Customer-managed keys (CMK / external key)\\n\\nWhen customers provide keys (BYOK), integrations MUST:\\n\\n- Support validating key accessibility at install/preflight time (Private) and at configuration time (control plane).\\n- Require explicit customer ownership of key lifecycle and access control, documented in customer-facing materials.", "score": 0.454586, "rank": 72, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "cf66d80e-fa65-5df1-824e-c378977d0d3b", "search_unit_id": "cf66d80e-fa65-5df1-824e-c378977d0d3b", "block_from_id": "33d45d98-c0f8-5b2a-95d7-d255aad0cb95", "block_to_id": "0b1b30c0-17ad-558f-ab32-cccd435a5bd1", "section_path": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Clause library (approved language) > H. Dispute window (recommended default)", "document_id": "45f6686b-12fc-5fae-9c11-9abaeb20a3e5", "document_version_id": "a4bad94b-544e-5a78-88ce-d2659b6c4f79", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_c52c609c0cdf4211a7e8c57bb1da72e4.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-62", "heading": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Clause library (approved language) > H. Dispute window (recommended default)", "content": "H. Dispute window (recommended default)\\n\\n**Approved clause (standard):**\\n\xe2\x80\x9cCustomer must notify Redwood in writing of any good-faith dispute regarding an invoice within thirty (30) days of the invoice date, describing the basis for the dispute in reasonable detail. If Customer does not dispute an invoice within this period, the invoice will be deemed accepted.\xe2\x80\x9d\\n\\n**Fallback positions:**\\n\\n- 45 days: acceptable for larger enterprise if requested.\\n- 60+ days: requires CFO (Laura Bennett) approval due to RevRec and cash collection risk.", "score": 0.440948, "rank": 73, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "0634e49b-39c2-5aff-af09-d50a3e9c152c", "search_unit_id": "0634e49b-39c2-5aff-af09-d50a3e9c152c", "block_from_id": "05376406-85af-538f-aea0-1b56a66bbf39", "block_to_id": "c1356de9-b29b-5d04-9bb2-62f378cac569", "section_path": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Implementation requirements (engineering checklist)", "document_id": "eb166774-f9a9-56c9-984c-5fd7406c2bd1", "document_version_id": "76710c2c-2fe6-553c-ba81-ed6c87f0cfe5", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_377cdf4e378f40bebd7196e3a0ff1c38.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-90", "heading": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Implementation requirements (engineering checklist)", "content": "Implementation requirements (engineering checklist)\\n\\nUse this checklist for each new KMS call site.", "score": 0.518422, "rank": 74, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "00c72908-ab8f-5f1f-97f4-a27a4dfc0b59", "search_unit_id": "00c72908-ab8f-5f1f-97f4-a27a4dfc0b59", "block_from_id": "68438571-0bfe-5560-b41e-f4b75e0a3cea", "block_to_id": "1d35e0ad-4bf2-50ed-a750-2102a55b6a3a", "section_path": "Cross Role Tool Access Governance And Self Service Handbook 2027", "document_id": "4495c7a6-685c-5344-90c0-ef0b6cee8521", "document_version_id": "43048def-240f-53d7-bef2-2be51354fc0d", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_d7f0edbaa28147da807b5b85ea495bd1.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "list-17", "heading": "Cross Role Tool Access Governance And Self Service Handbook 2027", "content": "- Emergency access (e.g., incident mitigation) uses the Fast-Track Exception flow:\\n  1) Requester files an incident-tagged access request with justification and incident ID.\\n  2) On-call approver (manager or designated incident commander) may grant a 4-hour temporary token via the Access Portal.\\n  3) Security must be notified within 1 hour and will follow up to convert to a formal exception or revoke.\\n- All emergency grants are logged and retroactively reviewed as part of the incident postmortem.\\n\\n7) Deprovisioning and Offboarding\\n\\n- Standard offboarding timeline:\\n  - Day 0: account disabled for interactive access within 4 hours of HR offboarding signal.\\n  - Day 1: short-lived API tokens invalidated; persistent service accounts rotated if necessary.\\n  - Day 7: cloud console roles removed; scheduled backup of any outstanding owner responsibilities.\\n- Manager responsibility: reassign ownership before final removal.\\n- Audit: people-ops runs weekly deprovisioning reports, security runs monthly verification.\\n\\n8) Periodic Access Reviews\\n\\n- Quarterly review for all high-risk roles.\\n- Biannual review for medium-risk.\\n- Annual review for low-risk.\\n- Review process: automated report produced by Access Portal -> owner validates or initiates deprovisioning -> people-ops enforces changes within 7 business days.\\n\\n9) Tool Onboarding Checklist (for Tool Owners)\\n\\n1. Identify required roles and map to least-privilege sets.\\n2. Document roles in the Role Catalog section of the owner page.\\n3. Define which roles are self-service vs require approval.\\n4. Provide an onboarding runbook with contact points and SLOs.\\n5. Register tool owner and escalation email in the Access Portal.\\n6. Provide a test account and verification steps for the access flow.\\n\\n10) Technical Integration Patterns\\n\\n- Recommended: integrate tool with SSO and SCIM for group sync.\\n- Fallback: if SCIM unavailable, implement an API-based provisioning endpoint with scoped tokens and change tracking.\\n- Example access request payload (JSON):\\n\\n{\\n  \\"requester\\": \\"user@redwood.com\\",\\n  \\"tool\\": \\"grafana-prod\\",\\n  \\"role\\": \\"viewer\\",\\n  \\"justification\\": \\"Oncall rotation\\",\\n  \\"expires_at\\": \\"2026-02-28T23:59:00Z\\"\\n}\\n\\n- Example CLI (Access Portal CLI):\\n\\n$ rwd-access request --tool grafana-prod --role viewer --justification \\"oncall\\"\\n\\n11) Monitoring, Auditing and KPIs\\n\\n- KPIs to track: time-to-provision (median), percent self-service, number of active exceptions, time-to-deprovision after offboard.\\n- Reporting cadence: weekly provisioning dashboard, monthly audit exports (CSV) to security vault.\\n- Audit checks: verify no more than 5% of production-admin grants are older than 30 days without re-approval.\\n\\n12) De-Escalation and Dispute Resolution\\n\\n- If a manager or user disputes a grant or removal, escalate to people-ops with the ticket ID. People-ops will convene: manager, tool owner, and security to adjudicate within 5 business days.\\n\\n13) Sample Runbook: Granting Prod-Read Access (Manager-Approved)\\n\\n1. Manager submits request in Access Portal with business justification.\\n2. Portal routes to tool owner notification and manager approval.\\n3. On approval, provisioning job runs (SCIM or API).\\n4. Access granted; audit log written; notification sent to requester and manager.\\n5. After 90 days, system creates a renewal task for the manager.\\n\\n14) Implementation Roadmap (next 18 months)\\n\\n- Q2 2026: Complete SCIM integrations for top 10 tools.\\n- Q3 2026: Launch delegated team-admin roles for large product groups.\\n- Q4 2026: Build exception analytics dashboard and automatic expiration nudges.", "score": 0.425951, "rank": 75, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "01ba8c5d-e794-5106-ac6a-ab5a7d330caa", "search_unit_id": "01ba8c5d-e794-5106-ac6a-ab5a7d330caa", "block_from_id": "e55f3514-6cce-5c85-be36-ac2abfa15c51", "block_to_id": "1f092134-a1e2-5c91-8863-827ddad55207", "section_path": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Escalation path (when to pull in Legal/Finance/Engineering)", "document_id": "45f6686b-12fc-5fae-9c11-9abaeb20a3e5", "document_version_id": "a4bad94b-544e-5a78-88ce-d2659b6c4f79", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_c52c609c0cdf4211a7e8c57bb1da72e4.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-94", "heading": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Escalation path (when to pull in Legal/Finance/Engineering)", "content": "Escalation path (when to pull in Legal/Finance/Engineering)\\n\\nUse this section for routing redlines or customer questions.", "score": 0.502703, "rank": 76, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "c8b7f121-882c-562e-a31a-dcdd814b1a2f", "search_unit_id": "c8b7f121-882c-562e-a31a-dcdd814b1a2f", "block_from_id": "246c7b6b-9d4b-5507-8659-15e9ad4ad5df", "block_to_id": "4adf1f6f-60b2-56fc-b229-7759a247a890", "section_path": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Policy summary (MUST/SHOULD) > Observability controls", "document_id": "eb166774-f9a9-56c9-984c-5fd7406c2bd1", "document_version_id": "76710c2c-2fe6-553c-ba81-ed6c87f0cfe5", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_377cdf4e378f40bebd7196e3a0ff1c38.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-19", "heading": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Policy summary (MUST/SHOULD) > Observability controls", "content": "Observability controls\\n\\n- MUST emit standard metrics and trace spans for every KMS operation.\\n- MUST map provider-specific errors to the canonical Redwood KMS error taxonomy.\\n- SHOULD provide dashboards and alerts (or explicitly document why the integration is low-risk/no alerting needed).", "score": 0.433243, "rank": 77, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "5f1b3e62-ef47-5123-9d26-bafc6514c609", "search_unit_id": "5f1b3e62-ef47-5123-9d26-bafc6514c609", "block_from_id": "0a05eefb-144d-527c-9d1d-2e2a6b91b44a", "block_to_id": "732cb8e4-cd2f-52a7-9b5a-6e95e0538458", "section_path": "Cross Role Tool Access Governance And Self Service Handbook 2027", "document_id": "4495c7a6-685c-5344-90c0-ef0b6cee8521", "document_version_id": "43048def-240f-53d7-bef2-2be51354fc0d", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_d7f0edbaa28147da807b5b85ea495bd1.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "p-37", "heading": "Cross Role Tool Access Governance And Self Service Handbook 2027", "content": "15) Appendix: Common Role Examples\\n\\n- developer-readonly: view-only GitHub repos, dev dashboards.\\n- ci-builder: CI pipeline trigger and artifact write to staging buckets.\\n- infra-operator: deploy to staging, manage infra-as-code prs.\\n- prod-admin: full production console access (high-risk).\\n\\nContact and Escalation\\n\\n- People Ops team: people-ops@redwood.com\\n- Security on-call: security-oncall@redwood.com\\n- Tool owner contact: listed on each tool owner page in the Access Portal\\n\\nChange Log\\n\\n- 2025-03-18: Created by Aisha Patel (initial policy and flows).\\n- 2025-09-10: Added emergency fast-track and SLA clarifications (reviewers: Marcus Liu).\\n- 2026-01-14: Extended roadmap and clarified offboarding SLAs (reviewers: Sofia Ramirez, Ethan Morales).", "score": 0.398946, "rank": 78, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "a7c462a4-9c47-5ef7-8916-ad7dd48a5ee0", "search_unit_id": "a7c462a4-9c47-5ef7-8916-ad7dd48a5ee0", "block_from_id": "e30f6a00-9a33-5158-b1e5-8361b22382d4", "block_to_id": "fbad217c-e523-5d21-af43-796b48c852e1", "section_path": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Required logging, metrics, and tracing > Audit logs (configuration and rotation)", "document_id": "eb166774-f9a9-56c9-984c-5fd7406c2bd1", "document_version_id": "76710c2c-2fe6-553c-ba81-ed6c87f0cfe5", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_377cdf4e378f40bebd7196e3a0ff1c38.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-56", "heading": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Required logging, metrics, and tracing > Audit logs (configuration and rotation)", "content": "Audit logs (configuration and rotation)\\n\\nChanges that affect cryptographic behavior MUST be recorded in audit logs:\\n\\n- Key ID / key version reference updates\\n- Dual-read window enable/disable\\n- Cutover toggles\\n- Policy overrides (retry budget overrides, fail-open toggles, etc.)\\n- Break-glass access activation (where integrated)", "score": 0.41456, "rank": 79, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "b81303a9-5d2b-54b3-9c5d-6eaec15c64b6", "search_unit_id": "b81303a9-5d2b-54b3-9c5d-6eaec15c64b6", "block_from_id": "67f26e69-019c-5136-90a7-e90f42ff19a7", "block_to_id": "09fb4fee-ff0f-503a-b2d6-de53664ad126", "section_path": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Timeouts, retries, circuit breakers, and caching > Circuit breaker / degrade mode", "document_id": "eb166774-f9a9-56c9-984c-5fd7406c2bd1", "document_version_id": "76710c2c-2fe6-553c-ba81-ed6c87f0cfe5", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_377cdf4e378f40bebd7196e3a0ff1c38.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-66", "heading": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Timeouts, retries, circuit breakers, and caching > Circuit breaker / degrade mode", "content": "Circuit breaker / degrade mode\\n\\nWhere KMS failure can cause cascading outages:\\n\\n- MUST implement circuit breaker behavior and document the degrade policy.\\n- MUST define what happens when the circuit is open (examples):\\n  - Fail closed with clear errors and backpressure (default for cryptographic strictness)\\n  - Limited fail open only if data confidentiality/integrity is not reduced (rare; requires Security approval)\\n- MUST have SRE-reviewed alerting for circuit open events.", "score": 0.398056, "rank": 80, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "181cbc1e-380d-530d-ba3d-397b1010b31e", "search_unit_id": "181cbc1e-380d-530d-ba3d-397b1010b31e", "block_from_id": "39467ab4-5093-5296-98ff-4b3e1642e061", "block_to_id": "ccae9c47-cf64-5f43-876b-e230fe8f8a33", "section_path": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Internal operational guardrails (contracting) > Month-end close and late-arriving events", "document_id": "45f6686b-12fc-5fae-9c11-9abaeb20a3e5", "document_version_id": "a4bad94b-544e-5a78-88ce-d2659b6c4f79", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_c52c609c0cdf4211a7e8c57bb1da72e4.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-84", "heading": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Internal operational guardrails (contracting) > Month-end close and late-arriving events", "content": "Internal operational guardrails (contracting)\\n\\nMonth-end close and late-arriving events\\n\\nFinance operates a month-end close process with a usage data freeze window and controlled backfills.\\n\\n- Contract language should not obligate real-time corrections for late events.\\n- Use the dispute clause and reconciliation process to handle exceptions.", "score": 0.375001, "rank": 81, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "4ba438de-8c95-59e5-9f13-4523bc3be121", "search_unit_id": "4ba438de-8c95-59e5-9f13-4523bc3be121", "block_from_id": "560d6049-d96f-5fb9-b442-f0abc3611b6b", "block_to_id": "1cebcc8a-5758-5d0e-bdef-fe6a77f39a8d", "section_path": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Scope", "document_id": "45f6686b-12fc-5fae-9c11-9abaeb20a3e5", "document_version_id": "a4bad94b-544e-5a78-88ce-d2659b6c4f79", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_c52c609c0cdf4211a7e8c57bb1da72e4.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-6", "heading": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Scope", "content": "Scope\\n\\nApplies to:\\n\\n- Hosted API usage-based charges (tokens/requests/embeddings units)\\n- Metered add-ons where usage events are the basis of invoicing\\n- Dedicated and Private agreements only where they incorporate usage-based overages or burst (primary Dedicated meter definitions live elsewhere)\\n\\nOut of scope:\\n\\n- Full MSA templates (see Legal templates repository)\\n- Export-controlled or regulated country-specific addenda (escalate to Legal)", "score": 0.319675, "rank": 82, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "0bfe6446-eca1-502d-a28e-0c174b6d8a7d", "search_unit_id": "0bfe6446-eca1-502d-a28e-0c174b6d8a7d", "block_from_id": "99de7022-df5c-5253-bb50-6f53765c8f2c", "block_to_id": "1fc16377-a5d8-5cce-bc06-bdc6c6ebb135", "section_path": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Redlines: common asks and recommended responses > 4) \xe2\x80\x9cDispute window must be 90 days.\xe2\x80\x9d", "document_id": "45f6686b-12fc-5fae-9c11-9abaeb20a3e5", "document_version_id": "a4bad94b-544e-5a78-88ce-d2659b6c4f79", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_c52c609c0cdf4211a7e8c57bb1da72e4.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-80", "heading": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Redlines: common asks and recommended responses > 4) \xe2\x80\x9cDispute window must be 90 days.\xe2\x80\x9d", "content": "4) \xe2\x80\x9cDispute window must be 90 days.\xe2\x80\x9d\\n\\n**Position:** Generally no.\\n**Response:** Offer 45 days; if deal size justifies, escalate to CFO/GC with RevRec impact assessment.", "score": 0.335618, "rank": 83, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "5e72cfd1-8a0a-526b-ac02-90c9e0f7a90c", "search_unit_id": "5e72cfd1-8a0a-526b-ac02-90c9e0f7a90c", "block_from_id": "d34cc170-6668-5721-bc5c-88f1cd2e41c2", "block_to_id": "90955f24-db81-5ca5-8123-ab32a91885c2", "section_path": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Policy summary (MUST/SHOULD) > Security controls", "document_id": "eb166774-f9a9-56c9-984c-5fd7406c2bd1", "document_version_id": "76710c2c-2fe6-553c-ba81-ed6c87f0cfe5", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_377cdf4e378f40bebd7196e3a0ff1c38.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-15", "heading": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Policy summary (MUST/SHOULD) > Security controls", "content": "Security controls\\n\\n- MUST use envelope encryption for application data at rest when using KMS (DEKs for data; KEKs for wrapping).\\n- MUST scope IAM to least privilege for the specific key(s), operations, and environment.\\n- MUST separate runtime decrypt/encrypt permissions from rotation/admin permissions (separate roles/principals) for Dedicated/Private unless explicitly infeasible.\\n- MUST emit audit-relevant logs for key/rotation configuration changes (cutovers, key ID changes, policy toggles).\\n- MUST not log plaintext, DEKs, or wrapped key material.\\n- SHOULD use KMS/HSM-backed keys for regulated workloads (customer requirement-dependent).", "score": 0.292873, "rank": 84, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "ab85acd3-5019-504f-843c-db483c59f32a", "search_unit_id": "ab85acd3-5019-504f-843c-db483c59f32a", "block_from_id": "856487e4-cd1b-5680-958a-16a39ea7e1cc", "block_to_id": "320933aa-76ab-5bd0-b5b3-3e0521ebe205", "section_path": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Required reviews for new KMS call sites > Evidence to attach to the PR / design review", "document_id": "eb166774-f9a9-56c9-984c-5fd7406c2bd1", "document_version_id": "76710c2c-2fe6-553c-ba81-ed6c87f0cfe5", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_377cdf4e378f40bebd7196e3a0ff1c38.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-88", "heading": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Required reviews for new KMS call sites > Evidence to attach to the PR / design review", "content": "Evidence to attach to the PR / design review\\n\\n- Link to the call site inventory entry (service + operation + key ID class)\\n- IAM policy diff (or Terraform module usage) demonstrating least privilege\\n- Observability screenshots/links (dashboards, metric names) or validation logs from staging\\n- Failure-mode test plan or test results (timeouts, throttling, AccessDenied, key disabled)\\n- Rotation readiness statement (how dual-read and rollback are handled)", "score": 0.286291, "rank": 85, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "61a6fc33-7494-5b50-97dd-c67ee8303465", "search_unit_id": "61a6fc33-7494-5b50-97dd-c67ee8303465", "block_from_id": "eba8e949-aee6-588c-8347-7221061e7b9c", "block_to_id": "755fc66e-bb99-5e60-930a-154c3959b845", "section_path": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Incident handling and operational expectations > Required artifacts", "document_id": "eb166774-f9a9-56c9-984c-5fd7406c2bd1", "document_version_id": "76710c2c-2fe6-553c-ba81-ed6c87f0cfe5", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_377cdf4e378f40bebd7196e3a0ff1c38.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-76", "heading": "Key Management Standard Kms Integrations > Incident handling and operational expectations > Required artifacts", "content": "Incident handling and operational expectations\\n\\nRequired artifacts\\n\\n- A runbook or runbook section describing:\\n  - Symptoms, dashboards, and log queries\\n  - Common root causes (AccessDenied, throttling, timeout spikes, wrong key ID)\\n  - Mitigation steps and safe stopgaps\\n  - Escalation path to Security + Platform\\n- Link the runbook to on-call rotations and ensure it is discoverable.", "score": 0.297783, "rank": 86, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "4311fb7c-ddea-5eae-89a1-d0de071bfe89", "search_unit_id": "4311fb7c-ddea-5eae-89a1-d0de071bfe89", "block_from_id": "4c8251ae-2960-5249-b8e0-e1e099a4df20", "block_to_id": "ee224eb1-bbd0-59c4-94c7-b2cf976c4bc1", "section_path": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Escalation path (when to pull in Legal/Finance/Engineering) > Escalate to GC (Michael Grant)", "document_id": "45f6686b-12fc-5fae-9c11-9abaeb20a3e5", "document_version_id": "a4bad94b-544e-5a78-88ce-d2659b6c4f79", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_c52c609c0cdf4211a7e8c57bb1da72e4.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-98", "heading": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Escalation path (when to pull in Legal/Finance/Engineering) > Escalate to GC (Michael Grant)", "content": "Escalate to GC (Michael Grant)\\n\\n- Any language that constrains Redwood\xe2\x80\x99s ability to modify measurement systems\\n- Any customer request for regulatory/compliance commitments tied to billing logs\\n- Any threat of litigation or formal audit request", "score": 0.313029, "rank": 87, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "82e46b5d-b74a-5476-a3bf-7c58ff699a50", "search_unit_id": "82e46b5d-b74a-5476-a3bf-7c58ff699a50", "block_from_id": "c6586cf1-ece0-56f2-8cc8-4925fef046ae", "block_to_id": "05216408-8f38-5cd5-87ff-0e315b25dd9e", "section_path": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Escalation path (when to pull in Legal/Finance/Engineering) > Escalate to RevRec/Accounting (Emily Stone)", "document_id": "45f6686b-12fc-5fae-9c11-9abaeb20a3e5", "document_version_id": "a4bad94b-544e-5a78-88ce-d2659b6c4f79", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_c52c609c0cdf4211a7e8c57bb1da72e4.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-100", "heading": "Usage Based Pricing Legal Terms Playbook > Escalation path (when to pull in Legal/Finance/Engineering) > Escalate to RevRec/Accounting (Emily Stone)", "content": "Escalate to RevRec/Accounting (Emily Stone)\\n\\n- Requests for extended dispute windows beyond 45 days\\n- Any proposal for retroactive rebates/true-ups\\n- Any complex credits structure (rollover, non-expiring, transferable)", "score": 0.304469, "rank": 88, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}], "events": [], "entities": [], "relations": [], "source_hits": [], "summary": "", "citations": [], "answer_status": "pending", "no_answer_reason": null, "exploration_id": null, "stats": {"canonical_index": true, "ready_versions": 81, "requested_top_k": null, "candidate_top_k": 64, "candidate_unit_pool_limit": 1024, "candidate_pool_saturated": true, "candidate_units_before_cap": 152, "candidate_units_after_cap": 152, "candidate_uni