14:05:59  DEBUG    [8e0aca49dd954433]  sse_starlette.sse  chunk: b'event: summary.delta\r\ndata: {"delta": "The parameter normalizer in the recent update treats an explicit null value for `max_tokens` as \'unset\' and falls back to model defaults, whereas leaving it out entirely is also interpreted as \'unset\' but may not be explicitly documented in the evidence. The normalizer preserves explicit nulls and prefers client-provided values for edge cases, as noted in [1]."}\r\n\r\n'
14:05:59  DEBUG    [8e0aca49dd954433]  sse_starlette.sse  chunk: b'event: completed\r\ndata: {"query": "In the recent update to the chat completions compatibility adapter, how does the parameter normalizer handle a client sending max_tokens as null compared to leaving it out entirely?", "sections": [{"chunk_id": "cf5b46c9-4a57-5b5f-9580-967e9b4683de", "search_unit_id": "cf5b46c9-4a57-5b5f-9580-967e9b4683de", "block_from_id": "552cbf33-1f22-532b-9b2e-ebea2fb02563", "block_to_id": "552cbf33-1f22-532b-9b2e-ebea2fb02563", "section_path": "Pr 96123 Chat V1 Param Normalizer Role Alias Stop Dedupe Stream Backpressure", "document_id": "3bc9d4d3-a261-5f75-933e-8bfa0ff19ea9", "document_version_id": "4b7069dd-19bd-5bf3-bd17-c0cd531ec039", "document_name": "github__dsid_1c53affffb4f477ca476bec3138b60eb.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "p-2", "heading": "Pr 96123 Chat V1 Param Normalizer Role Alias Stop Dedupe Stream Backpressure", "content": "Motivation: Close a set of subtle incompatibilities between our /v1/chat.completions adapter and OpenAI\'s behavior that have been causing developer friction in streaming function-call flows and stop/logprobs handling. This PR implements a compact \'parameter normalizer\' layer and a streaming framing/backpressure handshake to make the adapter tolerant of real-world clients and OpenAI-style payloads. Summary of changes: - Parameter normalizer: unify and sanitize incoming params (max_tokens, temperature, top_p, n, presence_penalty) and map them to our internal API consistently; accept both string and numeric encodings, preserve explicit nulls, and prefer client-provided values for edge cases. - Role aliasing: accept and normalize role names coming from clients (\\"assistant\\", \\"system\\", \\"user\\", \\"tool\\", and legacy aliases like \\"ai\\" or \\"bot\\"); ensure role is preserved in both final and streaming envelopes. - Stop sequence deduplication: support stop as string or array; expand single-string stops into an array; dedupe overlapping sequences (e.g. [\\"\\\\n\\\\n\\", \\"\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n\\"]) and maintain order stability to match OpenAI semantics. - Sparse logprobs: add an opt-in sparse_logprobs mode that mirrors OpenAI\'s sparse token-level logprob structure when requested; keep heavy-weight computation behind an explicit flag to avoid perf regressions. - Streaming framing & backpressure: introduce a light handshake in the stream start (sent as first SSE/delta) that communicates our token framing and heartbeat expectations; implement backpressure signaling for HTTP/2 clients to avoid partial JSON objects when a client pauses mid-stream. - Function-call streaming support: improve chunking for function_call.name/arguments so that streaming deltas assemble deterministically into valid JSON payloads even across reconnects; final chunk action inserts a stable end-of-function marker to make reconstruction robust. - Response envelope parity: normalize streaming deltas to include a minimal structured \'choice\' envelope (id, index, finish_reason) so downstream OpenAI-compat consumers don\'t need ad-hoc heuristics. - Tests & docs: add unit and integration tests for the normalizer, streaming handshake scenarios, and a new example in the docs showing a robust client reconnection strategy. Checklist: - [x] Parameter mapping implemented and unit-tested - [x] Streaming handshake and backpressure implemented with integration tests - [x] Role aliasing covered by parser tests - [x] Stop dedupe logic covered and fuzz-tested - [x] Sparse logprobs gating and tests - [x] Docs updated (compatibility section + example client) - [x] Runtime perf smoke tests run on canary cluster Notable design decisions: - We intentionally do not try to replicate obscure historical OpenAI quirks; instead the normalizer applies conservative, well-documented rules and exposes a strict compatibility flag for customers who really need historical behavior. - The streaming handshake is opt-out via a client header (X-Redwood-Compat: openai-v1) to avoid breaking existing non-OpenAI clients. - Sparse logprobs are computed on-demand and annotated in the response metadata to allow downstream billing/observability. Related: ENG-4321 (parameter normalization epic), SUP-2107 (customer-reported toolcall truncation).\\nSamir: Can you clarify how explicit null values are treated vs missing keys? There was a customer case where max_tokens=null meant \'use default\' rather than \'0\'.\\nAuthor (Evelyn): Normalizer treats explicit null as \'unset\' and falls back to model defaults; added a unit test for that scenario.", "score": 0.793597, "rank": 0, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "12206ef0-490f-572f-a04f-a93409323125", "search_unit_id": "12206ef0-490f-572f-a04f-a93409323125", "block_from_id": "2c0a4f94-8487-57b1-ac7c-8d03a53b65e7", "block_to_id": "6dd5b856-ed16-5ea3-bd60-8f31134e09e4", "section_path": "Pr 96123 Chat V1 Param Normalizer Role Alias Stop Dedupe Stream Backpressure", "document_id": "3bc9d4d3-a261-5f75-933e-8bfa0ff19ea9", "document_version_id": "4b7069dd-19bd-5bf3-bd17-c0cd531ec039", "document_name": "github__dsid_1c53affffb4f477ca476bec3138b60eb.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h1-0", "heading": "Pr 96123 Chat V1 Param Normalizer Role Alias Stop Dedupe Stream Backpressure", "content": "Pr 96123 Chat V1 Param Normalizer Role Alias Stop Dedupe Stream Backpressure\\n\\nSource type: github\\nDocument ID: dsid_1c53affffb4f477ca476bec3138b60eb\\nRelease: v1.0.0\\nBenchmark: EnterpriseRAG-Bench synthetic upstream data\\nchat v1: parameter normalizer, role aliasing, stop dedupe and streaming backpressure improvements for /v1/chat.completions parity", "score": 0.425288, "rank": 1, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "095831e8-2b74-5910-b4cc-0c4c12a7d43f", "search_unit_id": "095831e8-2b74-5910-b4cc-0c4c12a7d43f", "block_from_id": "552cbf33-1f22-532b-9b2e-ebea2fb02563", "block_to_id": "552cbf33-1f22-532b-9b2e-ebea2fb02563", "section_path": "Pr 96123 Chat V1 Param Normalizer Role Alias Stop Dedupe Stream Backpressure", "document_id": "3bc9d4d3-a261-5f75-933e-8bfa0ff19ea9", "document_version_id": "4b7069dd-19bd-5bf3-bd17-c0cd531ec039", "document_name": "github__dsid_1c53affffb4f477ca476bec3138b60eb.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "p-2", "heading": "Pr 96123 Chat V1 Param Normalizer Role Alias Stop Dedupe Stream Backpressure", "content": "Asha: The backpressure header naming looks fine, but please add a short blurb in the docs about HTTP/1 clients where we emulate the behavior over SSE.\\nAuthor (Evelyn): Added docs section and an SSE emulation implementation for older clients.\\nLeo: Sparse logprobs look good; make sure we annotate toggles in telemetry so customers can track extra compute costs.\\nAuthor (Evelyn): Telemetry annotation added (adapter.openai_v1.sparse_logprobs=true) and documented cost footnote.", "score": 0.420553, "rank": 2, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}], "events": [], "entities": [], "relations": [], "source_hits": [], "summary": "The parameter normalizer in the recent update treats an explicit null value for `max_tokens` as \'unset\' and falls back to model defaults, whereas leaving it out entirely is also interpreted as \'unset\' but may not be explicitly documented in the evidence. The normalizer preserves explicit nulls and prefers client-provided values for edge cases, as noted in [1].", "citations": [{"kind": "internal", "n": 1, "document_id": "3bc9d4d3-a261-5f75-933e-8bfa0ff19ea9", "document_version_id": "4b7069dd-19bd-5bf3-bd17-c0cd531ec039", "document_name": "github__dsid_1c53affffb4f477ca476bec3138b60eb.md", "version_no": 1, "chunk_id": "cf5b46c9-4a57-5b5f-9580-967e9b4683de", "search_unit_id": "cf5b46c9-4a57-5b5f-9580-967e9b46