14:06:05  DEBUG    [5c887396ef3b48b1]  sse_starlette.sse  chunk: b'event: result\r\ndata: {"query": "What is the expected turnaround time for security to approve access to a high risk internal tool role in Redwood\'s tool access governance process?", "sections": [{"chunk_id": "f7a517ae-0405-52eb-98e5-d8ebc0245abc", "search_unit_id": "f7a517ae-0405-52eb-98e5-d8ebc0245abc", "block_from_id": "3cb20a79-9a89-5d4a-9bb5-689991a4f55f", "block_to_id": "43dd021f-47fd-5237-b674-03547a17dbf7", "section_path": "Cross Role Tool Access Governance And Self Service Handbook 2027", "document_id": "4495c7a6-685c-5344-90c0-ef0b6cee8521", "document_version_id": "43048def-240f-53d7-bef2-2be51354fc0d", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_d7f0edbaa28147da807b5b85ea495bd1.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h1-0", "heading": "Cross Role Tool Access Governance And Self Service Handbook 2027", "content": "Cross Role Tool Access Governance And Self Service Handbook 2027\\n\\nSource type: confluence\\nDocument ID: dsid_d7f0edbaa28147da807b5b85ea495bd1\\nRelease: v1.0.0\\nBenchmark: EnterpriseRAG-Bench synthetic upstream data\\nCross-role Tool Access Governance and Self-Service Handbook\\n\\nSummary:\\n\\nThis handbook defines the governance model, operational runbook, and self-service flows for granting, reviewing, and revoking access to Redwood\xe2\x80\x99s internal tools across roles and teams. It is intended for people-ops, engineering managers, security reviewers, and tool maintainers. The goal is to make tool access predictable, auditable, and fast while minimizing over-permissioning.\\n\\nKey Principles:\\n\\n- Least privilege by default: users receive the minimum role required to do their job.\\n- Role-driven access: we prefer role-based assignments with ephemeral exceptions.\\n- Self-service first, manual oversight when necessary: automate safe, common grants.\\n- Clear ownership: every tool has an owner and an escalation path.\\n- Auditable lifecycle: provisioning, reviews and deprovisioning are tracked centrally.\\n\\n1) Scope and Definitions\\n\\n- Tool: any internal SaaS, self-hosted service, or repo that requires explicit credentials or permissions (examples: AWS consoles, Jira admin groups, prod Grafana, CI pipelines).\\n- Role: a named collection of permissions (e.g., developer-readonly, infra-operator).\\n- Access Request: a request submitted to the Access Portal for a role or tool-specific permission.\\n- Exception: temporary access outside standard roles; must have an expiration and approver.\\n\\n2) Ownership and Responsibilities\\n\\n- Tool Owner (team-specified): maintains the role catalog, documents required permissions, defines safe self-service gates, and responds to escalations.\\n- People Ops: owns onboarding/offboarding orchestration, periodic review cadence, and highest-level policy.\\n- Security: defines acceptable exception policies, approves high-risk tools, and performs audits.\\n- Manager (requester approver): verifies business need and ties access to role/mission.\\n\\n3) Access Model (high level)\\n\\n- Role Catalog: canonical list of roles for common tools; stored in the Access Portal.\\n- Self-Service Roles: low-risk roles that can be assigned instantly (examples: docs-edit, ci-reader)\\n- Request-and-Approve Roles: medium-risk roles requiring manager approval (examples: staging-deploy, metrics-writer)\\n- Manual Approval Roles: high-risk roles requiring security review (examples: prod-admin, billing-admin)\\n\\n4) Standard Provisioning Flow (Self-Service preferred)\\n\\n1. User initiates request via Access Portal (or CLI).\\n2. For self-service roles: immediate grant recorded in audit log; user notified.\\n3. For manager-approval roles: manager receives approval email and must respond within 48 business hours; if approved, provisioning executes automatically.\\n4. For security-approval roles: security reviewer staged; expected SLA is 3 business days.\\n5. All grants include metadata: requester, approver, justification, expiration (if exception), and ticket ID.\\n\\n5) Approval Matrix (sample)\\n\\n| Tool Category | Example Tools | Typical Role Name | Approval Path | Max SLA for Approval | Expiration Policy |\\n|---|---:|---|---|---|---|\\n| Low risk | Docs, Internal Wiki | docs-edit | Self-service | Instant | Persistent (attached to employment) |\\n| Medium risk | Staging CI, Dev DB | staging-deploy | Manager | 48 business hours | 90 days (auto-renew) |\\n| High risk | Production infra, Billing | prod-admin | Manager + Security | 3 business days | 7 days (explicit extension only) |\\n\\n6) Exception and Emergency Access", "score": 0.771622, "rank": 0, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "00c72908-ab8f-5f1f-97f4-a27a4dfc0b59", "search_unit_id": "00c72908-ab8f-5f1f-97f4-a27a4dfc0b59", "block_from_id": "68438571-0bfe-5560-b41e-f4b75e0a3cea", "block_to_id": "1d35e0ad-4bf2-50ed-a750-2102a55b6a3a", "section_path": "Cross Role Tool Access Governance And Self Service Handbook 2027", "document_id": "4495c7a6-685c-5344-90c0-ef0b6cee8521", "document_version_id": "43048def-240f-53d7-bef2-2be51354fc0d", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_d7f0edbaa28147da807b5b85ea495bd1.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "list-17", "heading": "Cross Role Tool Access Governance And Self Service Handbook 2027", "content": "- Emergency access (e.g., incident mitigation) uses the Fast-Track Exception flow:\\n  1) Requester files an incident-tagged access request with justification and incident ID.\\n  2) On-call approver (manager or designated incident commander) may grant a 4-hour temporary token via the Access Portal.\\n  3) Security must be notified within 1 hour and will follow up to convert to a formal exception or revoke.\\n- All emergency grants are logged and retroactively reviewed as part of the incident postmortem.\\n\\n7) Deprovisioning and Offboarding\\n\\n- Standard offboarding timeline:\\n  - Day 0: account disabled for interactive access within 4 hours of HR offboarding signal.\\n  - Day 1: short-lived API tokens invalidated; persistent service accounts rotated if necessary.\\n  - Day 7: cloud console roles removed; scheduled backup of any outstanding owner responsibilities.\\n- Manager responsibility: reassign ownership before final removal.\\n- Audit: people-ops runs weekly deprovisioning reports, security runs monthly verification.\\n\\n8) Periodic Access Reviews\\n\\n- Quarterly review for all high-risk roles.\\n- Biannual review for medium-risk.\\n- Annual review for low-risk.\\n- Review process: automated report produced by Access Portal -> owner validates or initiates deprovisioning -> people-ops enforces changes within 7 business days.\\n\\n9) Tool Onboarding Checklist (for Tool Owners)\\n\\n1. Identify required roles and map to least-privilege sets.\\n2. Document roles in the Role Catalog section of the owner page.\\n3. Define which roles are self-service vs require approval.\\n4. Provide an onboarding runbook with contact points and SLOs.\\n5. Register tool owner and escalation email in the Access Portal.\\n6. Provide a test account and verification steps for the access flow.\\n\\n10) Technical Integration Patterns\\n\\n- Recommended: integrate tool with SSO and SCIM for group sync.\\n- Fallback: if SCIM unavailable, implement an API-based provisioning endpoint with scoped tokens and change tracking.\\n- Example access request payload (JSON):\\n\\n{\\n  \\"requester\\": \\"user@redwood.com\\",\\n  \\"tool\\": \\"grafana-prod\\",\\n  \\"role\\": \\"viewer\\",\\n  \\"justification\\": \\"Oncall rotation\\",\\n  \\"expires_at\\": \\"2026-02-28T23:59:00Z\\"\\n}\\n\\n- Example CLI (Access Portal CLI):\\n\\n$ rwd-access request --tool grafana-prod --role viewer --justification \\"oncall\\"\\n\\n11) Monitoring, Auditing and KPIs\\n\\n- KPIs to track: time-to-provision (median), percent self-service, number of active exceptions, time-to-deprovision after offboard.\\n- Reporting cadence: weekly provisioning dashboard, monthly audit exports (CSV) to security vault.\\n- Audit checks: verify no more than 5% of production-admin grants are older than 30 days without re-approval.\\n\\n12) De-Escalation and Dispute Resolution\\n\\n- If a manager or user disputes a grant or removal, escalate to people-ops with the ticket ID. People-ops will convene: manager, tool owner, and security to adjudicate within 5 business days.\\n\\n13) Sample Runbook: Granting Prod-Read Access (Manager-Approved)\\n\\n1. Manager submits request in Access Portal with business justification.\\n2. Portal routes to tool owner notification and manager approval.\\n3. On approval, provisioning job runs (SCIM or API).\\n4. Access granted; audit log written; notification sent to requester and manager.\\n5. After 90 days, system creates a renewal task for the manager.\\n\\n14) Implementation Roadmap (next 18 months)\\n\\n- Q2 2026: Complete SCIM integrations for top 10 tools.\\n- Q3 2026: Launch delegated team-admin roles for large product groups.\\n- Q4 2026: Build exception analytics dashboard and automatic expiration nudges.", "score": 0.522755, "rank": 1, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "5f1b3e62-ef47-5123-9d26-bafc6514c609", "search_unit_id": "5f1b3e62-ef47-5123-9d26-bafc6514c609", "block_from_id": "0a05eefb-144d-527c-9d1d-2e2a6b91b44a", "block_to_id": "732cb8e4-cd2f-52a7-9b5a-6e95e0538458", "section_path": "Cross Role Tool Access Governance And Self Service Handbook 2027", "document_id": "4495c7a6-685c-5344-90c0-ef0b6cee8521", "document_version_id": "43048def-240f-53d7-bef2-2be51354fc0d", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_d7f0edbaa28147da807b5b85ea495bd1.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "p-37", "heading": "Cross Role Tool Access Governance And Self Service Handbook 2027", "content": "15) Appendix: Common Role Examples\\n\\n- developer-readonly: view-only GitHub repos, dev dashboards.\\n- ci-builder: CI pipeline trigger and artifact write to staging buckets.\\n- infra-operator: deploy to staging, manage infra-as-code prs.\\n- prod-admin: full production console access (high-risk).\\n\\nContact and Escalation\\n\\n- People Ops team: people-ops@redwood.com\\n- Security on-call: security-oncall@redwood.com\\n- Tool owner contact: listed on each tool owner page in the Access Portal\\n\\nChange Log\\n\\n- 2025-03-18: Created by Aisha Patel (initial policy and flows).\\n- 2025-09-10: Added emergency fast-track and SLA clarifications (reviewers: Marcus Liu).\\n- 2026-01-14: Extended roadmap and clarified offboarding SLAs (reviewers: Sofia Ramirez, Ethan Morales).", "score": 0.512359, "rank": 2, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "cd97969a-d664-5c44-b40d-29de8e3aed7c", "search_unit_id": "cd97969a-d664-5c44-b40d-29de8e3aed7c", "block_from_id": "8e6320c4-e6f8-5d54-93df-d1029f47c012", "block_to_id": "57ca5e74-583f-5358-b18f-940f2bd5d127", "section_path": "Entitlements And Purchase Pathways Playbook 2030", "document_id": "98b6d795-d34b-588e-9f1d-b236110b9bba", "document_version_id": "9f88e88a-7404-5ed3-aeef-43374be1410f", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_ba7d1565b0694e359983bccaa4bf5977.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h1-0", "heading": "Entitlements And Purchase Pathways Playbook 2030", "content": "Entitlements And Purchase Pathways Playbook 2030\\n\\nSource type: confluence\\nDocument ID: dsid_ba7d1565b0694e359983bccaa4bf5977\\nRelease: v1.0.0\\nBenchmark: EnterpriseRAG-Bench synthetic upstream data\\nentitlements-and-purchase-pathways-playbook-2030\\nOverview\\n=======\\n\\nPurpose: This playbook consolidates company-wide procedures for entitlements (access and permissions), change governance, data handling expectations, procurement and expense approvals, vendor lifecycle management, and travel approvals. It is intended for all Redwood employees and contractors who request or approve resources, commit changes to production, or manage third-party relationships.\\n\\nScope: Applies to hosted, dedicated, and private deployment teams, platform and infra teams, procurement interactions, people-ops travel arrangements, and any third party that will access Redwood systems or customer data.\\n\\nQuick links: Access Portal (Okta + Access Request), VendorHub (procurement back-end), ExpenseFlow (employee expenses), Legal intake form, Security questionnaire (security.redwood.local).\\n\\nRoles and responsibilities\\n--------------------------\\n\\n- Requestor: person initiating an access, change, purchase, vendor relationship, or travel booking. Responsible for completeness and business justification.\\n- Manager/Approver: direct manager who validates business need and budget availability.\\n- Approving Officer (Finance/Procurement): validates procurement thresholds, tax, and vendor classification.\\n- Security Reviewer: evaluates data access risk and mandatory controls (SOC2, encryption, contract clauses).\\n- Legal Reviewer: reviews contract terms for vendor agreements above threshold or with custom IP/data terms.\\n- Proc Ops (Vendor Onboarding): completes supplier setup, obtains W-9/COI as applicable.\\n\\nPrinciples\\n----------\\n\\n- Least privilege: grant minimal entitlements required for the job and set automatic expiration where practical.\\n- Segregation of duties: approval and provisioning paths must not be owned by the same individual for medium/high risk requests.\\n- Evidence-first approvals: all approvals must be attached to the request in VendorHub or Access Portal.\\n- Risk proportionality: stricter controls for vendors with data access, privileged infra access, or requests above financial thresholds.\\n\\nAccess & permissions (entitlement lifecycle)\\n-------------------------------------------\\n1) Request process\\n\\n- Use the Access Portal (accessible from the Redwood Console > Tools > Access Request).\\n- Provide: justification, target systems (service name and environment), requested role (exact RBAC role), duration, and manager approval.\\n- For long-lived roles (>90 days), supply quarterly business justification and add reviewer in Access Portal.\\n\\n2) Approval matrix (summary)\\n\\n- Day-to-day access to non-prod systems: manager approval.\\n- Prod read-only access: manager + security notification.\\n- Prod privileged/infra access (SSH, K8s-admin, DB write): manager + security + infra-owner approval.\\n- Emergency elevated access: break-glass procedure (see Runbook ID: RG-2026-breakglass).\\n\\n3) Provisioning and deprovisioning\\n\\n- Provisioning is automated via Okta + Terraform runbooks (Infra-IAC). On approval, provisioning SLA is 2 business days for standard requests, 8 hours for emergency sprints.\\n- Access expirations are enforced: default 30 days for contractor requests, 90 days for internal hires unless renewed.\\n\\n4) Periodic review\\n\\n- Quarterly access attestation: team owners must validate active entitlements and remove stale accounts. Failure to respond triggers automated revocation notices.\\n\\nChange management\\n-----------------\\n\\nScope: Any modification to production services, infra provisioning, IAM policies, or customer-facing configuration.\\n\\nChange categories and approval paths:", "score": 0.72422, "rank": 3, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "238e4ad6-1425-50fc-9f18-bb0556a3b03f", "search_unit_id": "238e4ad6-1425-50fc-9f18-bb0556a3b03f", "block_from_id": "c07c1ffd-685d-5061-8196-cfd8189a2747", "block_to_id": "3b741f46-59a5-50f4-8e65-5697328750f2", "section_path": "Abm Pilot Security Evidence Pack Index > How to request evidence (internal process) > Turnaround targets", "document_id": "9e945a2c-4051-5cc3-99ca-a95c267f6bdf", "document_version_id": "c6871709-6afb-56d9-883f-81f2536ab49e", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a9a67d815b07451e90ed8c3d1734d007.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-65", "heading": "Abm Pilot Security Evidence Pack Index > How to request evidence (internal process) > Turnaround targets", "content": "Turnaround targets\\n\\n- Standard pack (SOC 2 + diagrams + policy statements): **2 business days**\\n- Custom questionnaire + custom evidence mapping: **3\xe2\x80\x935 business days**\\n- Rush requests: same-day only with Security approval and clear business justification\\n\\n---", "score": 0.697999, "rank": 4, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "25561c5f-d513-5ce6-beac-acce49aae704", "search_unit_id": "25561c5f-d513-5ce6-beac-acce49aae704", "block_from_id": "7947130a-10de-592a-ae10-7feb7e2c18a6", "block_to_id": "ee5a375e-e60e-5cac-b642-d6803c644150", "section_path": "Abm Pilot Security Evidence Pack Index > Purpose", "document_id": "9e945a2c-4051-5cc3-99ca-a95c267f6bdf", "document_version_id": "c6871709-6afb-56d9-883f-81f2536ab49e", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a9a67d815b07451e90ed8c3d1734d007.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-2", "heading": "Abm Pilot Security Evidence Pack Index > Purpose", "content": "Purpose\\n\\nThis page is the single index for Redwood Inference\xe2\x80\x99s prospect-facing **Security Evidence Pack** used during the Vertical ABM pilot (and reusable beyond) for regulated workloads (financial services, healthcare, and other compliance-driven buyers).\\n\\nIt describes:\\n\\n- What artifacts are included (and what we do *not* share)\\n- How Sales/SEs request access for a prospect\\n- How Security/GRC shares evidence securely and tracks distribution\\n- Confidentiality rules and common \xe2\x80\x9cgotchas\xe2\x80\x9d (SOC 2 handling, retention/data boundary language)\\n\\nThis page is **restricted** because it references the internal sharing process and controlled artifacts.\\n\\n---", "score": 0.641211, "rank": 5, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "0831657e-8401-56f0-9627-4cbebab0650d", "search_unit_id": "0831657e-8401-56f0-9627-4cbebab0650d", "block_from_id": "625b5926-73a8-54c5-8b6e-46a2a938a372", "block_to_id": "168dded9-63c3-5978-9a34-302313635e29", "section_path": "Abm Pilot Security Evidence Pack Index", "document_id": "9e945a2c-4051-5cc3-99ca-a95c267f6bdf", "document_version_id": "c6871709-6afb-56d9-883f-81f2536ab49e", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a9a67d815b07451e90ed8c3d1734d007.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h1-0", "heading": "Abm Pilot Security Evidence Pack Index", "content": "Abm Pilot Security Evidence Pack Index\\n\\nSource type: confluence\\nDocument ID: dsid_a9a67d815b07451e90ed8c3d1734d007\\nRelease: v1.0.0\\nBenchmark: EnterpriseRAG-Bench synthetic upstream data\\nABM Pilot: Security Evidence Pack Index (Regulated Workloads)", "score": 0.614239, "rank": 6, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "a90526d6-9770-5f65-be0b-7359dcd0cbdf", "search_unit_id": "a90526d6-9770-5f65-be0b-7359dcd0cbdf", "block_from_id": "69685f00-74df-5b60-8358-03b57a51b1b5", "block_to_id": "0f34d99f-cd84-5c84-b939-4f85c7b4ca15", "section_path": "Abm Pilot Security Evidence Pack Index > Evidence pack contents (prospect-facing) > C) Logging, auditability, and access controls", "document_id": "9e945a2c-4051-5cc3-99ca-a95c267f6bdf", "document_version_id": "c6871709-6afb-56d9-883f-81f2536ab49e", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a9a67d815b07451e90ed8c3d1734d007.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-34", "heading": "Abm Pilot Security Evidence Pack Index > Evidence pack contents (prospect-facing) > C) Logging, auditability, and access controls", "content": "C) Logging, auditability, and access controls\\n\\n7) **Audit log sample (redacted) + field reference**\\n\\n- Includes a redacted JSON sample of key audit log event types and a field glossary.\\n- Typical fields covered:\\n  - event_time, event_type\\n  - actor (user/service principal), auth_method\\n  - resource (project, deployment, model), action\\n  - request_id / trace_id\\n  - admin actions (policy updates, key configuration updates, retention config changes)\\n- Important: samples are representative and may omit environment-specific fields.\\n\\n8) **Audit log export patterns (overview)**\\n\\n- Describes supported export mechanisms and operational considerations (format, delivery options, and recommended controls).\\n- Used during technical deep dives for regulated buyers.\\n\\n9) **SSO/SAML + RBAC overview (one-page)**\\n\\n- High-level explanation of authentication options and role-based access control for the Console and admin functions.\\n- Includes SCIM provisioning support language where applicable.", "score": 0.576058, "rank": 7, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "2c824612-e636-550a-ac74-0c9964a63829", "search_unit_id": "2c824612-e636-550a-ac74-0c9964a63829", "block_from_id": "e98f4e0f-f722-5307-b02c-e778833085f3", "block_to_id": "1a953221-7c0e-56d9-a576-0c9ac7edd877", "section_path": "Abm Pilot Security Evidence Pack Index > When to use this evidence pack", "document_id": "9e945a2c-4051-5cc3-99ca-a95c267f6bdf", "document_version_id": "c6871709-6afb-56d9-883f-81f2536ab49e", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a9a67d815b07451e90ed8c3d1734d007.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-8", "heading": "Abm Pilot Security Evidence Pack Index > When to use this evidence pack", "content": "When to use this evidence pack\\n\\nUse the evidence pack when a prospect:\\n\\n- Requests \xe2\x80\x9cproof\xe2\x80\x9d beyond the Security FAQ (e.g., **SOC 2**, pen test attestation, encryption diagrams)\\n- Is moving into **security review**, **procurement**, **POC**, or **Private/Dedicated architecture** discussions\\n- Requires security documentation before allowing a technical pilot or data access\\n\\nIf the prospect only needs high-level posture statements, start with the **Regulated Workloads Security FAQ** and only escalate to evidence if requested.\\n\\n---", "score": 0.572359, "rank": 8, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "2469d4d0-949d-5293-a069-fe296d2894fc", "search_unit_id": "2469d4d0-949d-5293-a069-fe296d2894fc", "block_from_id": "f22b9c33-b69b-5f0e-bc85-2d5ba5386aa1", "block_to_id": "67a1d84b-4826-5c08-9e13-0747a4f25110", "section_path": "Abm Pilot Security Evidence Pack Index > Audience and roles", "document_id": "9e945a2c-4051-5cc3-99ca-a95c267f6bdf", "document_version_id": "c6871709-6afb-56d9-883f-81f2536ab49e", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a9a67d815b07451e90ed8c3d1734d007.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-13", "heading": "Abm Pilot Security Evidence Pack Index > Audience and roles", "content": "Audience and roles\\n\\n**Primary users (internal):** AEs, SEs, PMM, Security/GRC.\\n\\n**Owners:**\\n\\n- Evidence pack operations + distribution: **Daniel Carter (Security/Compliance)**\\n- Questionnaires + GRC workflow: **Olga Petrov (GRC)**\\n- External security posture approvals / escalation: **Dr. Aisha Rahman (CISO)**\\n- Security/compliance product alignment: **Naomi Feldman (Security)**\\n- NDA / legal terms and redlines: **Michael Grant (Legal)**\\n\\n---", "score": 0.551419, "rank": 9, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "00569f12-4695-570f-ba94-a9f687015bc0", "search_unit_id": "00569f12-4695-570f-ba94-a9f687015bc0", "block_from_id": "311959b0-6977-5ac9-ae94-08b6b70ca891", "block_to_id": "6f343d30-ae6b-583f-868c-dc5e60696e94", "section_path": "Abm Pilot Security Evidence Pack Index > Standard prospect-facing language (use verbatim where possible) > SOC 2", "document_id": "9e945a2c-4051-5cc3-99ca-a95c267f6bdf", "document_version_id": "c6871709-6afb-56d9-883f-81f2536ab49e", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a9a67d815b07451e90ed8c3d1734d007.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-77", "heading": "Abm Pilot Security Evidence Pack Index > Standard prospect-facing language (use verbatim where possible) > SOC 2", "content": "Standard prospect-facing language (use verbatim where possible)\\n\\nSOC 2\\n\\n\xe2\x80\x9cWe can provide our most recent SOC 2 Type II report under NDA. If you confirm the recipients and NDA status, our GRC team will share a secure, access-controlled link.\xe2\x80\x9d", "score": 0.530479, "rank": 10, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "5e83c1dd-76b2-5da9-ba7a-50a42b8dfa61", "search_unit_id": "5e83c1dd-76b2-5da9-ba7a-50a42b8dfa61", "block_from_id": "183c3d39-5691-5fb9-92cc-06f2963e33ec", "block_to_id": "02925590-6b67-5022-b7ac-598c2810964f", "section_path": "Abm Pilot Security Evidence Pack Index > Common requests mapped to artifacts", "document_id": "9e945a2c-4051-5cc3-99ca-a95c267f6bdf", "document_version_id": "c6871709-6afb-56d9-883f-81f2536ab49e", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a9a67d815b07451e90ed8c3d1734d007.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-85", "heading": "Abm Pilot Security Evidence Pack Index > Common requests mapped to artifacts", "content": "Common requests mapped to artifacts\\n\\n- \xe2\x80\x9cSend your SOC 2\xe2\x80\x9d \xe2\x86\x92 SOC 2 Type II report (NDA required)\\n- \xe2\x80\x9cHow do you encrypt data?\xe2\x80\x9d \xe2\x86\x92 Encryption overview diagram + data flow diagram\\n- \xe2\x80\x9cDo you have audit logs we can export?\xe2\x80\x9d \xe2\x86\x92 Audit log sample + export patterns overview\\n- \xe2\x80\x9cWhat do you retain and for how long?\xe2\x80\x9d \xe2\x86\x92 Retention policy statement + (if needed) residency statement\\n- \xe2\x80\x9cDo you support SSO/SAML?\xe2\x80\x9d \xe2\x86\x92 SSO/SAML + RBAC overview (and Security FAQ)\\n\\n---", "score": 0.530479, "rank": 11, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "835e4b28-cf88-50fa-af45-cbf85efa2c04", "search_unit_id": "835e4b28-cf88-50fa-af45-cbf85efa2c04", "block_from_id": "3b6fde36-eb81-51fb-a6a3-0ebe18a83e99", "block_to_id": "af968eb5-e0cb-5267-9ec3-8c7369271498", "section_path": "Abm Pilot Security Evidence Pack Index > Evidence pack contents (prospect-facing) > B) Security architecture and encryption", "document_id": "9e945a2c-4051-5cc3-99ca-a95c267f6bdf", "document_version_id": "c6871709-6afb-56d9-883f-81f2536ab49e", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a9a67d815b07451e90ed8c3d1734d007.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-27", "heading": "Abm Pilot Security Evidence Pack Index > Evidence pack contents (prospect-facing) > B) Security architecture and encryption", "content": "B) Security architecture and encryption\\n\\n4) **Encryption overview diagram**\\n\\n- Covers:\\n  - Encryption in transit (TLS)\\n  - Encryption at rest\\n  - Key management model (including KMS/HSM integration options for Private deployments)\\n- Includes clear scoping language for Hosted vs Dedicated vs Private.\\n\\n5) **Data flow / request processing diagram (serving plane)**\\n\\n- Illustrates request path (API ingress \xe2\x86\x92 routing \xe2\x86\x92 inference runtime \xe2\x86\x92 logging/metrics), with explicit callouts for where content may be processed.\\n- Used to answer \xe2\x80\x9cWhere does data go?\xe2\x80\x9d and \xe2\x80\x9cWhat is persisted?\xe2\x80\x9d questions.\\n\\n6) **Network boundary overview (Dedicated/Private)**\\n\\n- Describes reference topologies (VPC peering / private endpoints / customer-managed networking patterns).\\n- Includes shared responsibility notes.", "score": 0.530479, "rank": 12, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "243fc1b8-41ae-5cae-94e3-f5339836603d", "search_unit_id": "243fc1b8-41ae-5cae-94e3-f5339836603d", "block_from_id": "76366aee-90bb-5169-9549-dc08515ba3a1", "block_to_id": "e86d67d5-dc92-533a-b071-87e1db3ae212", "section_path": "Abm Pilot Security Evidence Pack Index > Confidentiality, handling, and safe-claim guidance", "document_id": "9e945a2c-4051-5cc3-99ca-a95c267f6bdf", "document_version_id": "c6871709-6afb-56d9-883f-81f2536ab49e", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a9a67d815b07451e90ed8c3d1734d007.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-88", "heading": "Abm Pilot Security Evidence Pack Index > Confidentiality, handling, and safe-claim guidance", "content": "Confidentiality, handling, and safe-claim guidance\\n\\n- Treat all evidence pack artifacts as **Confidential / Controlled**.\\n- Do not modify controlled artifacts (SOC 2, formal statements). If you need a tailored statement, request it via GRC.\\n- Do not make absolute claims (e.g., \xe2\x80\x9cHIPAA certified\xe2\x80\x9d, \xe2\x80\x9cfully compliant with X\xe2\x80\x9d) unless explicitly approved in the Security FAQ.\\n- If a prospect requests a signed attestation, route to **Michael Grant (Legal)** and **Olga Petrov (GRC)**.\\n\\n---", "score": 0.530479, "rank": 13, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "6ba932e5-e3ac-5178-acc1-a2cbd515131c", "search_unit_id": "6ba932e5-e3ac-5178-acc1-a2cbd515131c", "block_from_id": "5a825b8e-94c9-5a5f-9a40-d09318186cb7", "block_to_id": "4828cc63-2ba8-5b1b-85c5-8ceb7e71074f", "section_path": "Abm Pilot Security Evidence Pack Index > How evidence is shared (distribution rules) > Not approved", "document_id": "9e945a2c-4051-5cc3-99ca-a95c267f6bdf", "document_version_id": "c6871709-6afb-56d9-883f-81f2536ab49e", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a9a67d815b07451e90ed8c3d1734d007.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-71", "heading": "Abm Pilot Security Evidence Pack Index > How evidence is shared (distribution rules) > Not approved", "content": "Not approved\\n\\n- Emailing SOC 2 as an attachment\\n- Uploading to a prospect\xe2\x80\x99s procurement portal without Security + Legal approval\\n- Storing evidence in uncontrolled folders or personal drives", "score": 0.530479, "rank": 14, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "bf7b8c11-b250-57a8-883b-87d00556de9e", "search_unit_id": "bf7b8c11-b250-57a8-883b-87d00556de9e", "block_from_id": "9c66d0db-63a9-5cc1-87d7-16de0856fe04", "block_to_id": "d9338132-8f83-508a-8358-87eaadd6c991", "section_path": "Abm Pilot Security Evidence Pack Index > Evidence pack contents (prospect-facing) > E) Assurance supporting materials (as needed)", "document_id": "9e945a2c-4051-5cc3-99ca-a95c267f6bdf", "document_version_id": "c6871709-6afb-56d9-883f-81f2536ab49e", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a9a67d815b07451e90ed8c3d1734d007.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-46", "heading": "Abm Pilot Security Evidence Pack Index > Evidence pack contents (prospect-facing) > E) Assurance supporting materials (as needed)", "content": "E) Assurance supporting materials (as needed)\\n\\n12) **Pen test attestation letter / executive summary (when available)**\\n\\n- High-level summary appropriate for procurement/security reviewers.\\n- Full reports are generally not shared; exceptions require CISO + Legal approval.\\n\\n13) **Vulnerability management + incident response policy summaries**\\n\\n- Policy summaries suitable for \xe2\x80\x9cdoes your program exist?\xe2\x80\x9d questions.\\n- Not intended to replace detailed internal runbooks.\\n\\n---", "score": 0.530479, "rank": 15, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "1e4e71b3-5f51-57f6-bd1d-f572d0d9bbe4", "search_unit_id": "1e4e71b3-5f51-57f6-bd1d-f572d0d9bbe4", "block_from_id": "a05bea6d-5cf4-51c3-98a4-7bbd726a3675", "block_to_id": "20c76424-30df-5d27-9f60-4dfdd25bf32b", "section_path": "Abm Pilot Security Evidence Pack Index > How to request evidence (internal process) > Request submission", "document_id": "9e945a2c-4051-5cc3-99ca-a95c267f6bdf", "document_version_id": "c6871709-6afb-56d9-883f-81f2536ab49e", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a9a67d815b07451e90ed8c3d1734d007.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-60", "heading": "Abm Pilot Security Evidence Pack Index > How to request evidence (internal process) > Request submission", "content": "Request submission\\n\\nSubmit an evidence request with:\\n\\n- Company name + opportunity link (HubSpot)\\n- Primary recipient(s): name, title, email domain\\n- Requested artifacts (from the list above)\\n- Deadline and meeting date (if any)\\n- Any special handling (e.g., \xe2\x80\x9cno email attachments\xe2\x80\x9d, \xe2\x80\x9cupload to their portal\xe2\x80\x9d)\\n\\n**Where to submit:**\\n\\n- Primary: Security/GRC intake (internal) \xe2\x80\x94 route to **Olga Petrov**\\n- Backup: Email **security-evidence@redwoodinference.com** (internal alias)\\n- Coordination: Slack **#eng-security** for urgency only (do not paste artifacts into Slack)", "score": 0.530479, "rank": 16, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "d406fa30-276e-53f3-9fc0-b949e7aa51bf", "search_unit_id": "d406fa30-276e-53f3-9fc0-b949e7aa51bf", "block_from_id": "e199143d-8e88-5b70-997d-ba86542b6558", "block_to_id": "eda74822-b95f-55cd-8f0b-99c2cbf37426", "section_path": "Abm Pilot Security Evidence Pack Index > Change log", "document_id": "9e945a2c-4051-5cc3-99ca-a95c267f6bdf", "document_version_id": "c6871709-6afb-56d9-883f-81f2536ab49e", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a9a67d815b07451e90ed8c3d1734d007.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-97", "heading": "Abm Pilot Security Evidence Pack Index > Change log", "content": "Change log\\n\\n- 2025-06-06: Updated audit log sample description and export guidance; tightened \xe2\x80\x9cdo not share\xe2\x80\x9d list and distribution rules.\\n- 2025-05-15: Added retention/residency statements and clarified NDA gating for SOC 2.\\n- 2025-04-29: Initial publication for ABM regulated workloads pilot.", "score": 0.530479, "rank": 17, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "4f1e3288-89aa-5951-ba49-c115984a9cd6", "search_unit_id": "4f1e3288-89aa-5951-ba49-c115984a9cd6", "block_from_id": "3f480f37-08c1-5167-b58f-da00f1c723c2", "block_to_id": "3044f3ae-0217-510e-98e8-c60148e3effd", "section_path": "Abm Pilot Security Evidence Pack Index > Evidence pack contents (prospect-facing) > D) Data retention, residency, and data handling statements", "document_id": "9e945a2c-4051-5cc3-99ca-a95c267f6bdf", "document_version_id": "c6871709-6afb-56d9-883f-81f2536ab49e", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a9a67d815b07451e90ed8c3d1734d007.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-41", "heading": "Abm Pilot Security Evidence Pack Index > Evidence pack contents (prospect-facing) > D) Data retention, residency, and data handling statements", "content": "D) Data retention, residency, and data handling statements\\n\\n10) **Data retention policy statement (customer-facing)**\\n\\n- Clarifies retention and deletion behavior for different data categories (e.g., operational metadata vs request content), including scoping by deployment type.\\n- Includes:\\n  - Default retention windows (as applicable)\\n  - Configurable retention controls (where supported)\\n  - Deletion request process and escalation\\n\\n11) **Data residency / region availability statement**\\n\\n- High-level statement of supported regions for Hosted/Dedicated and options for Private.\\n- Includes language on how region selection interacts with support and failover.", "score": 0.530479, "rank": 18, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "a4a5ab98-ac71-5149-90ac-40167effe4de", "search_unit_id": "a4a5ab98-ac71-5149-90ac-40167effe4de", "block_from_id": "a3a62208-9621-5bc5-8801-8cd6026e399f", "block_to_id": "b7cc8d5e-b8cf-5dba-b7ee-a0cb9c078e23", "section_path": "Abm Pilot Security Evidence Pack Index > Evidence pack contents (prospect-facing)", "document_id": "9e945a2c-4051-5cc3-99ca-a95c267f6bdf", "document_version_id": "c6871709-6afb-56d9-883f-81f2536ab49e", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a9a67d815b07451e90ed8c3d1734d007.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-18", "heading": "Abm Pilot Security Evidence Pack Index > Evidence pack contents (prospect-facing)", "content": "Evidence pack contents (prospect-facing)\\n\\nBelow is the standard set of artifacts we can share. Availability depends on the prospect\xe2\x80\x99s stage and whether an NDA is in place.", "score": 0.530479, "rank": 19, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "263f8e8a-fa12-5743-9644-354acec3560b", "search_unit_id": "263f8e8a-fa12-5743-9644-354acec3560b", "block_from_id": "da4d3356-1d63-5bae-8621-69e4f2150f04", "block_to_id": "fbdd4e78-afc2-5953-89af-f5cfad5dc1b2", "section_path": "Abm Pilot Security Evidence Pack Index > How to request evidence (internal process) > Eligibility checklist (before requesting)", "document_id": "9e945a2c-4051-5cc3-99ca-a95c267f6bdf", "document_version_id": "c6871709-6afb-56d9-883f-81f2536ab49e", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a9a67d815b07451e90ed8c3d1734d007.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-57", "heading": "Abm Pilot Security Evidence Pack Index > How to request evidence (internal process) > Eligibility checklist (before requesting)", "content": "How to request evidence (internal process)\\n\\nEligibility checklist (before requesting)\\n\\n1) Confirm the prospect name, domain, and opportunity stage.\\n2) Confirm whether an **NDA is executed** (required for SOC 2 and most controlled artifacts).\\n3) Confirm what the prospect actually needs (avoid oversharing). Ask: \xe2\x80\x9cWhich control domains are you validating and what is the deadline?\xe2\x80\x9d", "score": 0.530479, "rank": 20, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "e17370ce-da6a-5ebc-a9e7-5268533bbb9e", "search_unit_id": "e17370ce-da6a-5ebc-a9e7-5268533bbb9e", "block_from_id": "10470b72-f499-578e-a14a-0f7dc93d14ba", "block_to_id": "ed63b370-f426-5175-8502-47a10f1de74c", "section_path": "Abm Pilot Security Evidence Pack Index > Standard prospect-facing language (use verbatim where possible) > Retention / data boundaries", "document_id": "9e945a2c-4051-5cc3-99ca-a95c267f6bdf", "document_version_id": "c6871709-6afb-56d9-883f-81f2536ab49e", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a9a67d815b07451e90ed8c3d1734d007.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-82", "heading": "Abm Pilot Security Evidence Pack Index > Standard prospect-facing language (use verbatim where possible) > Retention / data boundaries", "content": "Retention / data boundaries\\n\\n\xe2\x80\x9cWe can share our customer-facing retention statement covering what data is stored for operational purposes and what retention controls apply by deployment type. If you have a specific retention requirement (e.g., X days), we\xe2\x80\x99ll confirm feasibility in the context of your desired deployment (Hosted, Dedicated, or Private).\xe2\x80\x9d\\n\\n---", "score": 0.530479, "rank": 21, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "85491455-d406-503e-a459-b54a0e317d99", "search_unit_id": "85491455-d406-503e-a459-b54a0e317d99", "block_from_id": "505d7a71-906f-51da-8a2f-16bb8623a5f1", "block_to_id": "9221a317-d1d4-5e53-aba4-641e40801628", "section_path": "Abm Pilot Security Evidence Pack Index > How evidence is shared (distribution rules) > Tracking requirements", "document_id": "9e945a2c-4051-5cc3-99ca-a95c267f6bdf", "document_version_id": "c6871709-6afb-56d9-883f-81f2536ab49e", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a9a67d815b07451e90ed8c3d1734d007.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-73", "heading": "Abm Pilot Security Evidence Pack Index > How evidence is shared (distribution rules) > Tracking requirements", "content": "Tracking requirements\\n\\nFor every controlled artifact share (especially SOC 2):\\n\\n- Record the recipients and date shared\\n- Record the NDA status\\n- Attach/share the distribution note in the CRM opportunity (or link to the request record)\\n\\n---", "score": 0.530479, "rank": 22, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "aa536da1-fc3b-537e-9974-380591b801c2", "search_unit_id": "aa536da1-fc3b-537e-9974-380591b801c2", "block_from_id": "5197ce0f-8cfe-5bde-8890-29b5a5c1b8a6", "block_to_id": "afb656de-2641-52ae-a2e0-9bfb19888a2a", "section_path": "Abm Pilot Security Evidence Pack Index > Escalations", "document_id": "9e945a2c-4051-5cc3-99ca-a95c267f6bdf", "document_version_id": "c6871709-6afb-56d9-883f-81f2536ab49e", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a9a67d815b07451e90ed8c3d1734d007.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-91", "heading": "Abm Pilot Security Evidence Pack Index > Escalations", "content": "Escalations\\n\\nEscalate immediately if:\\n\\n- Prospect requests full pen test report or vulnerability details\\n- Prospect requires portal uploads or broad internal distribution\\n- Prospect asks for contractual security commitments not in standard terms (custom SLAs, residency guarantees, audit rights)\\n\\nEscalation contacts:\\n\\n- GRC workflow: **Olga Petrov**\\n- Legal terms/redlines: **Michael Grant** / **Sofia Mendes**\\n- Security exec escalation: **Dr. Aisha Rahman**\\n\\n---", "score": 0.530479, "rank": 23, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "768b9e45-99b0-565d-8f72-d3caf446cd14", "search_unit_id": "768b9e45-99b0-565d-8f72-d3caf446cd14", "block_from_id": "2bd7a69d-66d2-508a-beca-31e2f00fdfd5", "block_to_id": "b14cd8f1-c124-5773-a5e1-1bc0fad64ab9", "section_path": "Abm Pilot Security Evidence Pack Index > How evidence is shared (distribution rules) > Approved sharing methods", "document_id": "9e945a2c-4051-5cc3-99ca-a95c267f6bdf", "document_version_id": "c6871709-6afb-56d9-883f-81f2536ab49e", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a9a67d815b07451e90ed8c3d1734d007.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-68", "heading": "Abm Pilot Security Evidence Pack Index > How evidence is shared (distribution rules) > Approved sharing methods", "content": "How evidence is shared (distribution rules)\\n\\nApproved sharing methods\\n\\n- **Secure link** from an access-controlled repository (preferred)\\n  - Recipient-specific access\\n  - Expiring link when possible\\n  - Watermarking for SOC 2", "score": 0.530479, "rank": 24, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "9cf8ff01-c68e-57b1-b689-31cf778a3fe7", "search_unit_id": "9cf8ff01-c68e-57b1-b689-31cf778a3fe7", "block_from_id": "9333e634-1275-5864-b5fe-cd1438d48319", "block_to_id": "e2516875-38f1-5de4-9730-420fba5fc71e", "section_path": "Abm Pilot Security Evidence Pack Index > Standard prospect-facing language (use verbatim where possible) > Audit logs", "document_id": "9e945a2c-4051-5cc3-99ca-a95c267f6bdf", "document_version_id": "c6871709-6afb-56d9-883f-81f2536ab49e", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a9a67d815b07451e90ed8c3d1734d007.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-80", "heading": "Abm Pilot Security Evidence Pack Index > Standard prospect-facing language (use verbatim where possible) > Audit logs", "content": "Audit logs\\n\\n\xe2\x80\x9cWe support audit logging for administrative and access events. We can share a redacted sample and a field glossary so your security team can confirm the level of detail and export patterns.\xe2\x80\x9d", "score": 0.530479, "rank": 25, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "eb1eb8c6-6ea3-5ad6-92e0-6c6ab30db21c", "search_unit_id": "eb1eb8c6-6ea3-5ad6-92e0-6c6ab30db21c", "block_from_id": "2b58c24b-b826-5921-90f4-0d51b588fdc1", "block_to_id": "b452aab1-1b72-53c0-9ba9-5d89d3944cef", "section_path": "Entitlements And Purchase Pathways Playbook 2030", "document_id": "98b6d795-d34b-588e-9f1d-b236110b9bba", "document_version_id": "9f88e88a-7404-5ed3-aeef-43374be1410f", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_ba7d1565b0694e359983bccaa4bf5977.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "list-38", "heading": "Entitlements And Purchase Pathways Playbook 2030", "content": "- Initial intake: vendor submitted via VendorHub, 1 business day acknowledgement.\\n- Risk assessment: Security performs questionnaire review; expect 5-7 business days for standard vendors, 15-20 days for those handling Restricted data.\\n- Contracting: Legal drafts/negotiates terms; standard NDA/SOW templates for low-risk vendors. Time: 5\xe2\x80\x9315 business days depending on terms.\\n- Procurement & finance: vendor setup (W-9/COI), tax classification, payment terms.\\n\\nMinimum vendor requirements by risk tier:\\n\\n- Low risk (no data access): PO, standard SOE, vendor contact, invoice cadence.\\n- Medium risk (limited data access): PO, signed DPA, security questionnaire, SOC2 Type II preferred.\\n- High risk (customer data or privileged infra access): PO, DPA, SOC2 Type II or penetration test report, system access plan, contractual breach notification clause, indemnity terms.\\n\\nOffboarding and termination:\\n\\n- Termination checklist: revoke credentials, recover assets, enforce data return/deletion, final invoice reconciliation, and a post-termination confirmation from vendor. Procurement must retain termination evidence for 7 years.\\n\\nTravel policy (high level)\\n-------------------------\\n\\nBooking: Use Travel Portal (linked from Redwood Console). Lowest reasonable fare policy applies for economy class. Business class requires exec-level pre-approval for travel over 8 hours.\\n\\nApprovals: Manager approves travel requests in Travel Portal. International travel must include security and people-ops notification if travel is to high-risk countries listed by People Ops.\\n\\nPer diems and expenses: See ExpenseFlow caps. Receipts required for all items >$25.\\n\\nSafety and incident reporting:\\n\\n- In case of an incident while traveling, contact People Ops emergency line and Security: security@redwood.com. All incidents must be reported within 24 hours.\\n\\nTemplates and forms (where to find)\\n----------------------------------\\n\\n- Procurement intake form: VendorHub > New Request > Procurement Intake (use template \'Procurement-Intake-v2\').\\n- Data Erasure Request: Redwood Console > Data Requests.\\n- Change request template: CRB ticket template in Jira (project: RED-CHANGES).\\n- Access request template: Access Portal (select role and environment).\\n\\nExample procurement JSON payload (for VendorHub API)\\n{\\n  \\"requestor\\": \\"alice@example.com\\",\\n  \\"vendor\\": \\"Acme Analytics\\",\\n  \\"amount_usd\\": \\"7500\\",\\n  \\"justification\\": \\"Production observability for dedicated clusters\\",\\n  \\"budget_tag\\": \\"infra-monitoring\\",\\n  \\"required_by\\": \\"2027-02-15\\"\\n}\\nAppendix: enforcement and exceptions\\n-----------------------------------\\n\\n- Exceptions: Managers may request a documented exception for short-lived needs; exceptions require a written business case and a compliance review.\\n- Enforcement: Repeated policy violations (e.g., unmanaged vendor engagements or expired privileged access) will be escalated to the employee\'s manager and may trigger procurement suspension or disciplinary review.\\n\\nContacts and ownership\\n----------------------\\n\\n- Policy owner: Finance-Legal (policy owner contact: procurement@redwood.com).\\n- Security contact for vendor risk: security@redwood.com.\\n- People Ops travel & benefits: people-ops@redwood.com.\\n\\nRevision history\\n----------------\\n\\n- 2026-11-12: Initial draft published by Maya Chen.\\n- 2026-12-03: Updated procurement thresholds and added emergency change SLA (reviewed by Luis Alvarez and Priya Nair).\\n\\nRelated artifacts and references\\n-------------------------------\\n\\n- Runbook RG-2026-breakglass (eng-sre/runbooks).\\n- VendorHub API docs (internal link).\\n- Security questionnaire template (security-and-compliance/audit-logging).\\n\\nEnd of document", "score": 0.462415, "rank": 26, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "ae17ab66-5c66-5561-8b4b-390018946350", "search_unit_id": "ae17ab66-5c66-5561-8b4b-390018946350", "block_from_id": "e0024ee9-c56b-5f47-bfdc-66f91c209941", "block_to_id": "821238ed-e68f-50ce-8fdd-bd820d8a8628", "section_path": "Entitlements And Purchase Pathways Playbook 2030", "document_id": "98b6d795-d34b-588e-9f1d-b236110b9bba", "document_version_id": "9f88e88a-7404-5ed3-aeef-43374be1410f", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_ba7d1565b0694e359983bccaa4bf5977.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "list-20", "heading": "Entitlements And Purchase Pathways Playbook 2030", "content": "- Standard change: pre-approved, repeatable changes (e.g., routine OS patching via controlled pipeline). Requires change ticket and notification to SRE runbook subscribers.\\n- Normal change: requires Change Review Board (CRB) approval for higher impact (planned releases that affect SLAs). CRB meets twice weekly.\\n- Emergency change: immediate fixes that must follow the emergency roll-forward checklist and be retroactively documented in the change ticket.\\n\\nChange windows and freezes:\\n\\n- Quarterly freeze: last two business days of each quarter are freeze windows for major releases unless exception approved by CTO and SRE lead.\\n- High-risk releases: require canary rollout and 30% traffic validation for 24 hours before full rollout.\\n\\nChange request minimum content (ticket):\\n\\n1. Change owner and contact\\n2. Rollout and rollback plan with automation steps\\n3. Expected impact and post-deploy validation steps\\n4. Backout criteria and timeline\\n5. Stakeholder notification list\\n\\nSLOs and audit\\n\\n- All normal changes must have an associated ticket and be auditable for 12 months.\\n- Emergency changes must be documented within 48 hours.\\n\\nData management and classification\\n--------------------------------\\nClassification levels:\\n\\n- Public: content intended for public consumption.\\n- Internal: operational information not intended for external distribution.\\n- Confidential: employee, business, or customer information that requires access controls.\\n- Restricted: regulated or highly sensitive data (PII, payment data, health data) that requires encryption at rest and in transit, strict access controls, and audit logging.\\n\\nHandling rules (summary):\\n\\n- Confidential & Restricted: store only in approved systems (Redwood Console vaults, encrypted S3 with KMS). No vendor transfer without security and legal sign-off.\\n- Data retention: default retention for logs is 90 days; for customer-facing telemetry retention follows contractual obligations.\\n- Data deletion: use Data Erasure Request form and verify via automated deletion job.\\n\\nProcurement and expenses\\n------------------------\\nPurchase approval thresholds (effective):\\n\\n| Amount (USD) | Approvals required | Notes |\\n|--------------|-------------------|-------|\\n| < 2,500 | Manager | Auto-approval in VendorHub if budget tag present |\\n| 2,500 \xe2\x80\x93 50,000 | Manager + Finance | Finance checks budget and tax classification |\\n| > 50,000 | Manager + Finance + Procurement + Legal | Requires exec sponsor and procurement intake form |\\n\\nProcurement steps (numbered):\\n\\n1. Create a request in VendorHub including business justification, vendor name, SOW/quote, and budget tag.\\n2. Attach vendor compliance docs (SOC2, ISO, insurance certificate) when available.\\n3. Finance validates budgets and tax treatment within 3 business days.\\n4. Procurement routes to Legal for >50k or non-standard T&Cs.\\n5. Once approved, Procurement issues purchase order and coordinates supplier setup.\\n\\nExpense reimbursement:\\n\\n- Use ExpenseFlow, attach receipts within 30 days of expense. Per diem caps: domestic $150/day, international $250/day unless pre-approved. Card use: corporate cards are preferred for travel; personal card reimbursements require manager approval.\\n\\nVendor management lifecycle\\n--------------------------\\nOnboarding checklist (timeline expectations):", "score": 0.410301, "rank": 27, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "d3945569-c0ff-57e9-a6cb-89ea8e6df83c", "search_unit_id": "d3945569-c0ff-57e9-a6cb-89ea8e6df83c", "block_from_id": "7cf720fd-3280-5679-aad5-739793494b7f", "block_to_id": "55e743c3-872b-5aaf-9736-d282393e113a", "section_path": "Abm Pilot Security Evidence Pack Index > Evidence pack contents (prospect-facing) > A) Compliance reports and attestations", "document_id": "9e945a2c-4051-5cc3-99ca-a95c267f6bdf", "document_version_id": "c6871709-6afb-56d9-883f-81f2536ab49e", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a9a67d815b07451e90ed8c3d1734d007.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-20", "heading": "Abm Pilot Security Evidence Pack Index > Evidence pack contents (prospect-facing) > A) Compliance reports and attestations", "content": "A) Compliance reports and attestations\\n\\n1) **SOC 2 Type II report (most recent period)**\\n\\n- Includes: auditor\xe2\x80\x99s opinion, system description, control activities, and test results for the audit period.\\n- Notes:\\n  - Shared **only under NDA**.\\n  - Distributed via secure, access-controlled link (see \xe2\x80\x9cSharing rules\xe2\x80\x9d).\\n  - Watermarked per recipient.\\n\\n2) **SOC 2 bridge/coverage letter (if required between audit periods)**\\n\\n- Used when a prospect needs an update between SOC 2 reporting periods.\\n- Shared under NDA.\\n\\n3) **Security program overview (one-page)**\\n\\n- High-level summary of security governance, risk management, and control domains.\\n- Suitable for early-stage security conversations.", "score": 0.331394, "rank": 28, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "9adc00a6-be46-55a0-b8c2-57aa6fd35f53", "search_unit_id": "9adc00a6-be46-55a0-b8c2-57aa6fd35f53", "block_from_id": "34f5703f-c1e3-5740-9958-da6df7619bb6", "block_to_id": "c1408256-d151-54a6-b958-3235d04779d3", "section_path": "Abm Pilot Security Evidence Pack Index > What we do NOT share (default)", "document_id": "9e945a2c-4051-5cc3-99ca-a95c267f6bdf", "document_version_id": "c6871709-6afb-56d9-883f-81f2536ab49e", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a9a67d815b07451e90ed8c3d1734d007.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-52", "heading": "Abm Pilot Security Evidence Pack Index > What we do NOT share (default)", "content": "What we do NOT share (default)\\n\\nTo reduce risk and keep evidence consistent, the following are **not shared** with prospects unless explicitly approved by Security + Legal:\\n\\n- Raw penetration test report details (tool output, exploit steps, full findings list)\\n- Internal runbooks, on-call procedures, or detailed incident postmortems\\n- Source code, internal architecture docs with sensitive implementation details\\n- Customer lists, identifiable customer configurations, or production screenshots\\n- Any artifact containing secrets, internal hostnames, private IPs, or employee personal data\\n\\nIf a prospect requests any of the above, route to **Olga Petrov** (GRC) and **Michael Grant** (Legal) before responding.\\n\\n---", "score": 0.293498, "rank": 29, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}], "events": [], "entities": [], "relations": [], "source_hits": [], "summary": "", "citations": [], "answer_status": "pending", "no_answer_reason": null, "exploration_id": null, "stats": {"canonical_index": true, "ready_versions": 81, "requested_top_k": null, "candidate_top_k": 32, "candidate_unit_pool_limit": 1024, "candidate_pool_saturated": true, "candidate_units_before_cap": 74, "candidate_units_after_cap": 74, "candidate_units_truncated": 0, "semantic_candidates": 41, "lexical_candidates": 41, "candidates": 74, "relevant": 56, "filtered_irrelevant": 18, "fusion_method": "rrf", "selection_method": "authorized_content_dedup_mmr", "cross_scope_merge": "rank_interleave", "coverage": {"candidate_count": 64, "deduplicated_count": 0, "diversity_weight": 0.5, "near_duplicate_similarity": 0.98, "required_anchor_count": 0, "covered_anchor_count": 0, "anchor_coverage": "not_required", "status": "unknown", "canonical_locator_verified": true, "semantic_answerability": "unknown"}, "routing": {"planner": {"planner_version": "qsp-v1", "requested_strategy": "AUTO", "effective_strategy": "LOCAL_FACTUAL", "modifiers": [], "reason_codes": ["DEFAULT_LOCAL_FACTUAL"], "multi_hop_eligible": false}, "request_snapshot_id": "1c2533af-dc43-4fb2-8a44-9bd77817c4ff", "groups": [{"project_id": "b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c", "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "partition_id": "b3086c26ae3c45b6b8