14:06:33  DEBUG    [709a643a8a0742bf]  sse_starlette.sse  chunk: b'event: result\r\ndata: {"query": "In the customer docs plan for the opt-in quantization profile feature, what are the review roles required before the documentation can be merged?", "sections": [{"chunk_id": "0be8035a-e262-535d-b66c-d1eeb2d13d2b", "search_unit_id": "0be8035a-e262-535d-b66c-d1eeb2d13d2b", "block_from_id": "e458343b-c5a1-546c-a071-c413f9fe098a", "block_to_id": "4f929011-3f1d-585b-99cd-7cb2460c29a5", "section_path": "Quantization Profiles Customer Docs Plan > Review, launch gating, and update cadence", "document_id": "f258ae94-d90e-5b1e-8afd-2c4acf87793c", "document_version_id": "8c99c721-acba-5c00-9f81-25a2b151e29c", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a2983978ba0d4d70a795eb7e13de8670.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-78", "heading": "Quantization Profiles Customer Docs Plan > Review, launch gating, and update cadence", "content": "Review, launch gating, and update cadence\\n\\n**Reviewers required before docs merge**\\n\\n- Applied ML: Arjun Desai (profiles lead) + Selene Huang (guardrails)\\n- Runtime: Noah Patel (runtime architect)\\n- Platform/Console: Chloe Martin (Console backend lead)\\n- SRE/Release: Connor O\'Brien (rollout lead)\\n- Security/RBAC: Naomi Feldman (RBAC/audit requirements)\\n\\n**Release stages and docs behavior**\\n\\n- Beta/allowlist:\\n  - Docs are public but clearly marked \xe2\x80\x9cBeta\xe2\x80\x9d with known limitations.\\n  - Include a \xe2\x80\x9cContact Support to enable\xe2\x80\x9d note if feature is behind an allowlist.\\n\\n- GA:\\n  - Remove Beta banner.\\n  - Publish compatibility matrix link and clear deprecation policy.\\n\\n**Update cadence**\\n\\n- Compatibility matrix and profile coverage: weekly updates (aligned with profile publishing cadence).\\n- Troubleshooting section: update after each beta incident/support trend.", "score": 0.801815, "rank": 0, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "7646cd71-d913-5f78-b5e9-8a7f26b15aab", "search_unit_id": "7646cd71-d913-5f78-b5e9-8a7f26b15aab", "block_from_id": "b4eb7c52-7671-5dc4-8730-077f536d661e", "block_to_id": "5b285f03-183d-544e-af91-0a79aa4a2be2", "section_path": "Quantization Profiles Customer Docs Plan > Summary", "document_id": "f258ae94-d90e-5b1e-8afd-2c4acf87793c", "document_version_id": "8c99c721-acba-5c00-9f81-25a2b151e29c", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a2983978ba0d4d70a795eb7e13de8670.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-2", "heading": "Quantization Profiles Customer Docs Plan > Summary", "content": "Summary\\n\\nThis page defines the plan for customer-facing documentation for the Quantization Profile Library (opt-in). The goal is to help customers safely enable quantization profiles per route, understand limitations and compatibility, run appropriate evaluations, interpret observability signals, and roll back quickly if needed.\\n\\nThis is an internal planning doc for Redwood Docs + DevEx and will be used as the source of truth for docs IA, required examples, and cross-team review gates.", "score": 0.794375, "rank": 1, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "1c6c2841-0025-5c72-8a85-5a70d8ae4479", "search_unit_id": "1c6c2841-0025-5c72-8a85-5a70d8ae4479", "block_from_id": "18789623-7dd3-5eb3-ba5b-ba0b52eb6294", "block_to_id": "6f69facf-3a49-52b1-b8be-9664f7e7e170", "section_path": "Quantization Profiles Customer Docs Plan > Information architecture (public docs) > Page 1: Overview (concept + safety model)", "document_id": "f258ae94-d90e-5b1e-8afd-2c4acf87793c", "document_version_id": "8c99c721-acba-5c00-9f81-25a2b151e29c", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a2983978ba0d4d70a795eb7e13de8670.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-21", "heading": "Quantization Profiles Customer Docs Plan > Information architecture (public docs) > Page 1: Overview (concept + safety model)", "content": "Page 1: Overview (concept + safety model)\\n\\n**Proposed title:** \xe2\x80\x9cQuantization Profiles (Preview/Beta)\xe2\x80\x9d (or \xe2\x80\x9cQuantization Profiles\xe2\x80\x9d once GA)\\n\\n**Outline**\\n\\n- What quantization profiles are and why they reduce cost.\\n- Opt-in and route-scoped behavior.\\n- High-level lifecycle: published profiles, versioning, deprecations.\\n- Safety model summary:\\n  - Compatibility checks before enablement.\\n  - Deterministic selection.\\n  - Fallback to baseline.\\n  - Auditability and change history.\\n\\n**Callouts**\\n\\n- \xe2\x80\x9cStart with a canary route; expand after evals.\xe2\x80\x9d\\n- \xe2\x80\x9cNot all models/regions support all profiles.\xe2\x80\x9d", "score": 0.719503, "rank": 2, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "19a23fa9-30f9-5b4d-a213-54f312d1876f", "search_unit_id": "19a23fa9-30f9-5b4d-a213-54f312d1876f", "block_from_id": "eac25ee0-be0e-5fdd-9d15-5acc8a9a3e5a", "block_to_id": "827985e0-dd9a-5e1b-a57b-a814b4bd895d", "section_path": "Quantization Profiles Customer Docs Plan", "document_id": "f258ae94-d90e-5b1e-8afd-2c4acf87793c", "document_version_id": "8c99c721-acba-5c00-9f81-25a2b151e29c", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a2983978ba0d4d70a795eb7e13de8670.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h1-0", "heading": "Quantization Profiles Customer Docs Plan", "content": "Quantization Profiles Customer Docs Plan\\n\\nSource type: confluence\\nDocument ID: dsid_a2983978ba0d4d70a795eb7e13de8670\\nRelease: v1.0.0\\nBenchmark: EnterpriseRAG-Bench synthetic upstream data\\nQuantization Profiles (Public Docs) \xe2\x80\x94 Customer Documentation Plan", "score": 0.721198, "rank": 3, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "4d7347a5-096f-5ac7-860e-9979992e6c5d", "search_unit_id": "4d7347a5-096f-5ac7-860e-9979992e6c5d", "block_from_id": "ddf7a771-8304-5cb6-832a-ae2a8af1fc85", "block_to_id": "30a4dab5-6fdd-5805-9f34-661b11f33a58", "section_path": "Quantization Profiles Customer Docs Plan > Notes", "document_id": "f258ae94-d90e-5b1e-8afd-2c4acf87793c", "document_version_id": "8c99c721-acba-5c00-9f81-25a2b151e29c", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a2983978ba0d4d70a795eb7e13de8670.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-92", "heading": "Quantization Profiles Customer Docs Plan > Notes", "content": "Notes\\n\\n- Keep customer docs consistent with the PRD\xe2\x80\x99s promise: **opt-in**, **auditable**, **deterministic**, and **reversible**.\\n- Prefer \xe2\x80\x9chow to verify\xe2\x80\x9d sections over deep internals; customers need confidence that the setting is actually applied and understand when/why fallback happens.", "score": 0.531743, "rank": 4, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "74b07f05-28cd-5aad-8122-cab0d3bd7f40", "search_unit_id": "74b07f05-28cd-5aad-8122-cab0d3bd7f40", "block_from_id": "e5d36016-a479-55d4-b559-948bac3c641b", "block_to_id": "ce446240-9b81-53bd-8d90-6a3d82e8a281", "section_path": "Quantization Profiles Customer Docs Plan > Required code/examples (public docs)", "document_id": "f258ae94-d90e-5b1e-8afd-2c4acf87793c", "document_version_id": "8c99c721-acba-5c00-9f81-25a2b151e29c", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a2983978ba0d4d70a795eb7e13de8670.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-63", "heading": "Quantization Profiles Customer Docs Plan > Required code/examples (public docs)", "content": "Required code/examples (public docs)\\n\\nWe will maintain a single authoritative set of snippets and import them into the docs site.\\n\\n**REST (pseudo)**\\n\\n- GET route settings (show current model + quant state)\\n- PATCH route settings to set profile ref\\n- PATCH route settings to disable / reset to default\\n\\n**Python SDK**\\n\\n- Update route quantization setting\\n- Validate compatibility result handling\\n- Verify applied profile via response metadata\\n\\n**TypeScript SDK**\\n\\n- Same as Python, plus typing for errors.\\n\\nDocs dependencies:\\n\\n- Final field names and error shapes must match control-plane API.\\n- Confirm the exact response fields that indicate `applied` vs `fallback` vs `disabled`.", "score": 0.471693, "rank": 5, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "8c6f53fd-47c1-590f-9b57-aed5fbaf2eda", "search_unit_id": "8c6f53fd-47c1-590f-9b57-aed5fbaf2eda", "block_from_id": "9c89cf06-9164-5a9c-a25e-0091e5dc8c5f", "block_to_id": "ab589696-3112-5474-bd23-13ca903f0de0", "section_path": "Quantization Profiles Customer Docs Plan > Action items", "document_id": "f258ae94-d90e-5b1e-8afd-2c4acf87793c", "document_version_id": "8c99c721-acba-5c00-9f81-25a2b151e29c", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a2983978ba0d4d70a795eb7e13de8670.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-90", "heading": "Quantization Profiles Customer Docs Plan > Action items", "content": "Action items\\n\\n- (Docs) Elliot Price: draft public docs pages 1\xe2\x80\x935 and route through review (target by 2025-03-14).\\n- (DevEx) Monica Patel: finalize Python + TS snippets and ensure they match SDK releases.\\n- (Console) Chloe Martin: confirm final Console labels, error strings, and change history UX for screenshot capture.\\n- (Applied ML) Arjun Desai / Selene Huang: approve public-facing evaluation guidance and guardrail language.\\n- (SRE) Connor O\'Brien: verify rollback instructions align with operational reality and dashboards customers can access.", "score": 0.472806, "rank": 6, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "e46e9665-5e68-5602-835e-4412a9458ccd", "search_unit_id": "e46e9665-5e68-5602-835e-4412a9458ccd", "block_from_id": "d2060c24-223b-56d9-a3fe-d8efbdcdba89", "block_to_id": "0ad92fd4-46fc-557a-b3d9-774168a62974", "section_path": "Quantization Profiles Customer Docs Plan > Goals (docs)", "document_id": "f258ae94-d90e-5b1e-8afd-2c4acf87793c", "document_version_id": "8c99c721-acba-5c00-9f81-25a2b151e29c", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a2983978ba0d4d70a795eb7e13de8670.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-10", "heading": "Quantization Profiles Customer Docs Plan > Goals (docs)", "content": "Goals (docs)\\n\\n- Make it clear this is **opt-in** and **route-scoped** (v1), with baseline behavior unchanged when disabled.\\n- Provide a simple \xe2\x80\x9chappy path\xe2\x80\x9d enablement flow with copy-pastable examples (Console + API/SDK).\\n- Set expectations on **compatibility constraints** and **fallback behavior** (deterministic, baseline precision fallback).\\n- Provide a lightweight but concrete evaluation best-practices section that customers can follow without needing Redwood internal harnesses.\\n- Provide troubleshooting steps tied to the actual product signals customers will see (Console warnings/errors, request metadata, audit history, and dashboard panels).", "score": 0.473296, "rank": 7, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "ebd96e14-9ba0-53d9-b0dd-ce3d7dd51b15", "search_unit_id": "ebd96e14-9ba0-53d9-b0dd-ce3d7dd51b15", "block_from_id": "a2a7f6b9-d8a0-53bc-bdd2-8b0a432c26a3", "block_to_id": "1f01d606-6c27-5830-95ca-f71aba5dbf02", "section_path": "Quantization Profiles Customer Docs Plan > Audience and use cases", "document_id": "f258ae94-d90e-5b1e-8afd-2c4acf87793c", "document_version_id": "8c99c721-acba-5c00-9f81-25a2b151e29c", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a2983978ba0d4d70a795eb7e13de8670.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-5", "heading": "Quantization Profiles Customer Docs Plan > Audience and use cases", "content": "Audience and use cases\\n\\n**Primary audiences**\\n\\n- Software engineers and ML engineers integrating Redwood routes who want to reduce cost/token.\\n- Platform teams managing production change control (audit logs, RBAC, rollbacks).\\n\\n**Customer use cases we need to support in docs**\\n\\n1. Enable an approved quantization profile for a single route (hosted API).\\n2. Enable profile for a route with region/tier constraints (Dedicated + multi-region hosted).\\n3. Validate quality and latency before expanding traffic.\\n4. Diagnose output changes, elevated fallback rate, or latency regressions.\\n5. Roll back (route-level disable; global kill-switch is internal-only but mention its existence at a high level).", "score": 0.450693, "rank": 8, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "cc921cea-a194-5fd0-a3c3-444f55842c1b", "search_unit_id": "cc921cea-a194-5fd0-a3c3-444f55842c1b", "block_from_id": "23388bd6-d651-5038-b4dc-3ff7a05da5c3", "block_to_id": "fdc32665-72dd-5179-ada4-07ad52b809d8", "section_path": "Quantization Profiles Customer Docs Plan > Open questions", "document_id": "f258ae94-d90e-5b1e-8afd-2c4acf87793c", "document_version_id": "8c99c721-acba-5c00-9f81-25a2b151e29c", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a2983978ba0d4d70a795eb7e13de8670.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-88", "heading": "Quantization Profiles Customer Docs Plan > Open questions", "content": "Open questions\\n\\n1. **Alias semantics:** Will we expose \xe2\x80\x9crecommended/latest\xe2\x80\x9d aliases in v1 GA or only pinned profile IDs/versions? If aliases exist, we must document how we prevent silent changes (e.g., aliases only change on customer action vs Redwood updates).\\n2. **Customer-facing compatibility matrix:** What is the minimum viable matrix we can keep current without excessive operational load? (Proposal: publish for top 10 models + major GPU classes first.)\\n3. **What can we safely publish about quality thresholds?** We should align with Applied ML on whether to include specific numeric deltas or keep it as qualitative guidance.\\n4. **Request metadata surface:** What is the final customer-visible mechanism to confirm applied profile (headers, response fields, trace attribute)? This must be stable.", "score": 0.439589, "rank": 9, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "50c3f0f6-fbbd-56f0-bbc4-4fbe79e26e88", "search_unit_id": "50c3f0f6-fbbd-56f0-bbc4-4fbe79e26e88", "block_from_id": "18002474-dfa8-5a48-a3ee-80834a7f06e7", "block_to_id": "9cee9dcd-788f-54af-8684-f64533fd223a", "section_path": "Quantization Profiles Customer Docs Plan > Information architecture (public docs)", "document_id": "f258ae94-d90e-5b1e-8afd-2c4acf87793c", "document_version_id": "8c99c721-acba-5c00-9f81-25a2b151e29c", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a2983978ba0d4d70a795eb7e13de8670.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-19", "heading": "Quantization Profiles Customer Docs Plan > Information architecture (public docs)", "content": "Information architecture (public docs)\\n\\nWe will publish a small cluster of pages under: **Optimize \xe2\x86\x92 Quantization Profiles**.", "score": 0.44918, "rank": 10, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "2a614da6-d475-5fe2-866b-83e728ca3baa", "search_unit_id": "2a614da6-d475-5fe2-866b-83e728ca3baa", "block_from_id": "e36a0bb8-d45f-57a9-9d3c-b0135e23f98f", "block_to_id": "76e6d722-0cb4-5f5c-90a0-f9e92a934ef7", "section_path": "Quantization Profiles Customer Docs Plan > Information architecture (public docs) > Page 2: Enablement guide (Console + API/SDK)", "document_id": "f258ae94-d90e-5b1e-8afd-2c4acf87793c", "document_version_id": "8c99c721-acba-5c00-9f81-25a2b151e29c", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a2983978ba0d4d70a795eb7e13de8670.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-27", "heading": "Quantization Profiles Customer Docs Plan > Information architecture (public docs) > Page 2: Enablement guide (Console + API/SDK)", "content": "Page 2: Enablement guide (Console + API/SDK)\\n\\n**Proposed title:** \xe2\x80\x9cEnable a quantization profile for a route\xe2\x80\x9d\\n\\n**Required elements**\\n\\n- Console walkthrough (with screenshots once UX is final):\\n  1) Navigate to Route \xe2\x86\x92 Performance/Optimize \xe2\x86\x92 Quantization\\n  2) Choose model variant + eligible profiles\\n  3) Read compatibility warnings\\n  4) Confirm change (modal) and review expected impact\\n  5) Verify enablement and view change history\\n\\n- API example (REST) for updating route config\\n  - Show setting `quantization_profile_ref` to a specific profile ID/version.\\n  - Show how to reset to `default` / disable.\\n\\n- SDK examples\\n  - Python and TypeScript: configure route setting; retrieve route state; handle incompatibility errors.\\n\\n**Verification steps**\\n\\n- Confirm in Console that route shows \xe2\x80\x9cEnabled\xe2\x80\x9d and which profile is selected.\\n- Show how to verify in request metadata (e.g., response headers or trace attributes) that a profile was applied vs fallback.\\n- Show where to find fallback/latency/cost deltas in dashboards.", "score": 0.440729, "rank": 11, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "e33eb813-b9f0-5d6e-90fe-6c8e9413ba23", "search_unit_id": "e33eb813-b9f0-5d6e-90fe-6c8e9413ba23", "block_from_id": "d2e81a44-73ff-5152-bb27-f42ae6ccb42b", "block_to_id": "df3b2e31-bddd-5df9-8c5c-32e0452ee7ec", "section_path": "Quantization Profiles Customer Docs Plan > Success criteria (docs)", "document_id": "f258ae94-d90e-5b1e-8afd-2c4acf87793c", "document_version_id": "8c99c721-acba-5c00-9f81-25a2b151e29c", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a2983978ba0d4d70a795eb7e13de8670.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-86", "heading": "Quantization Profiles Customer Docs Plan > Success criteria (docs)", "content": "Success criteria (docs)\\n\\n- \xe2\x89\xa580% of beta design partner enablements completed without synchronous Redwood help.\\n- Reduction in support tickets that are purely \xe2\x80\x9chow do I enable/disable?\xe2\x80\x9d (shift to higher-signal issues).\\n- Median time-to-rollback for customers (self-serve) < 10 minutes after following docs.\\n- Docs telemetry: high completion rates on enablement guide; low bounce on troubleshooting due to missing information.", "score": 0.432294, "rank": 12, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "f02921ae-85f7-5fbf-912f-6e2f2e9b37a1", "search_unit_id": "f02921ae-85f7-5fbf-912f-6e2f2e9b37a1", "block_from_id": "1c6bd5d5-5801-5ad1-bda3-88a868f769df", "block_to_id": "ff3dadf7-e0dd-5564-a394-0233eb63a37a", "section_path": "Quantization Profiles Customer Docs Plan > Product language and terminology", "document_id": "f258ae94-d90e-5b1e-8afd-2c4acf87793c", "document_version_id": "8c99c721-acba-5c00-9f81-25a2b151e29c", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a2983978ba0d4d70a795eb7e13de8670.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-14", "heading": "Quantization Profiles Customer Docs Plan > Product language and terminology", "content": "Product language and terminology\\n\\nWe need consistent, customer-friendly wording:\\n\\n- **Quantization profile**: A versioned, Redwood-validated configuration for running a specific model variant using a specific quantization method/precision combination.\\n- **Profile library**: The set of published profiles per model variant. Customers choose a profile for a route.\\n- **Route-level enablement**: Profiles are enabled per route, not globally for all tenant traffic (v1).\\n- **Fallback**: If a request is incompatible (hardware/sequence length constraints) or profile application fails safe checks, Redwood serves using baseline precision for that request (or route) while emitting an event.\\n\\nAvoid ambiguous language:\\n\\n- Avoid saying \xe2\x80\x9cRedwood automatically picks the best profile.\xe2\x80\x9d\\n- Avoid \xe2\x80\x9clossless\xe2\x80\x9d claims. Use \xe2\x80\x9caims to preserve quality\xe2\x80\x9d and emphasize eval/monitoring.", "score": 0.427726, "rank": 13, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "4391a4d2-f816-5a90-b9b3-c55f8d8d19fa", "search_unit_id": "4391a4d2-f816-5a90-b9b3-c55f8d8d19fa", "block_from_id": "61ddbab1-713b-59ca-b5b6-41d752770b2b", "block_to_id": "0b9fc5d1-22b9-5e5e-8740-130caff9aa90", "section_path": "Quantization Profiles Customer Docs Plan > Console UX copy and warnings (alignment)", "document_id": "f258ae94-d90e-5b1e-8afd-2c4acf87793c", "document_version_id": "8c99c721-acba-5c00-9f81-25a2b151e29c", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a2983978ba0d4d70a795eb7e13de8670.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-73", "heading": "Quantization Profiles Customer Docs Plan > Console UX copy and warnings (alignment)", "content": "Console UX copy and warnings (alignment)\\n\\nWe will mirror Console language in docs to minimize confusion.\\n\\nWarnings to standardize:\\n\\n- \xe2\x80\x9cThis change may affect output quality. Evaluate before ramping traffic.\xe2\x80\x9d\\n- \xe2\x80\x9cThis profile is only compatible with <constraints>. Requests outside constraints will fall back to baseline.\xe2\x80\x9d\\n- \xe2\x80\x9cPinning a profile version ensures deterministic behavior until you change it.\xe2\x80\x9d\\n\\nWe will coordinate final wording with Tessa Morgan (UX lead) and Kenji Nakamura (rollout/controls designer).", "score": 0.428283, "rank": 14, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "ff37a1ff-7807-586e-aae5-ad80bafca494", "search_unit_id": "ff37a1ff-7807-586e-aae5-ad80bafca494", "block_from_id": "83125c02-e5eb-50b3-8ddb-317d37c9a2d7", "block_to_id": "e40816dd-66b8-540c-afd0-0338eebd6f84", "section_path": "Quantization Profiles Customer Docs Plan > Information architecture (public docs) > Page 4: Evaluation best practices", "document_id": "f258ae94-d90e-5b1e-8afd-2c4acf87793c", "document_version_id": "8c99c721-acba-5c00-9f81-25a2b151e29c", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a2983978ba0d4d70a795eb7e13de8670.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-42", "heading": "Quantization Profiles Customer Docs Plan > Information architecture (public docs) > Page 4: Evaluation best practices", "content": "Page 4: Evaluation best practices\\n\\n**Proposed title:** \xe2\x80\x9cHow to evaluate quality and latency before rollout\xe2\x80\x9d\\n\\n**Customer-friendly guidance**\\n\\n- Suggested evaluation approach:\\n  - Identify representative prompts (production samples + edge cases).\\n  - Run baseline vs profile-enabled comparisons.\\n  - Use A/B sampling (e.g., 1\xe2\x80\x935% traffic) with a rollback threshold.\\n\\n- What to measure\\n  - Quality: task-specific metrics (pass@k, exact match, ranking metrics) + human review where appropriate.\\n  - Latency: p50/p95 decode latency and time-to-first-token.\\n  - Cost: cost/token and throughput.\\n\\n- Rollout strategy\\n  1) Enable in staging on a non-critical route\\n  2) Canary in production (small % traffic)\\n  3) Expand gradually with monitoring\\n\\n- Provide explicit \xe2\x80\x9cstop conditions\xe2\x80\x9d\\n  - Elevated fallback rate\\n  - Increased error rate\\n  - Statistically meaningful quality regression on a defined slice\\n\\n**Note:** We cannot publish Redwood\xe2\x80\x99s internal thresholds verbatim if they are considered sensitive, but we can publish recommended guardrails (e.g., \xe2\x80\x9cpredefine acceptable deltas and require sign-off\xe2\x80\x9d). We will align with Selene Huang (quality guardrails) on what\xe2\x80\x99s safe to disclose.", "score": 0.420359, "rank": 15, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "08ec1d53-1b52-5d65-bd35-1bb0b8681a57", "search_unit_id": "08ec1d53-1b52-5d65-bd35-1bb0b8681a57", "block_from_id": "e0c9a4a5-f182-5b49-bcba-b84b222a7c0a", "block_to_id": "ab0a1be4-d9cb-52ac-918e-be0ea1a96119", "section_path": "Quantization Profiles Customer Docs Plan > Information architecture (public docs) > Page 5: Troubleshooting + rollback", "document_id": "f258ae94-d90e-5b1e-8afd-2c4acf87793c", "document_version_id": "8c99c721-acba-5c00-9f81-25a2b151e29c", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a2983978ba0d4d70a795eb7e13de8670.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-50", "heading": "Quantization Profiles Customer Docs Plan > Information architecture (public docs) > Page 5: Troubleshooting + rollback", "content": "Page 5: Troubleshooting + rollback\\n\\n**Proposed title:** \xe2\x80\x9cTroubleshooting quantization profiles\xe2\x80\x9d\\n\\n**Structure: symptom \xe2\x86\x92 likely cause \xe2\x86\x92 how to confirm \xe2\x86\x92 resolution**\\n\\nRequired symptoms:\\n\\n- Console says profile is incompatible\\n  - Common causes: wrong model variant, unsupported GPU class, context length exceeds profile limit.\\n  - Resolution: choose another profile; reduce max tokens/context; use baseline.\\n\\n- Output quality changed unexpectedly\\n  - Confirm: compare baseline vs profile, check whether fallback occurred (mixed behavior can look inconsistent).\\n  - Resolution: disable profile; run eval; contact support with request IDs.\\n\\n- p95 latency increased\\n  - Confirm: look at per-route latency panels; check TTFT vs decode; check batching/caching changes.\\n  - Resolution: disable profile; adjust route concurrency/batching; consult Redwood support.\\n\\n- Elevated fallback rate\\n  - Confirm: dashboard panel + route events.\\n  - Likely causes: requests exceed profile constraints; region/GPU mismatch; deployment drift.\\n  - Resolution: tighten route constraints; pick compatible profile; disable.\\n\\n- 5xx errors after enabling\\n  - Confirm: error class; check if errors correlate with specific profile version.\\n  - Resolution: disable; provide audit event ID and request IDs to support.\\n\\nRollback instructions (customer-actionable)\\n\\n- Disable at route level (Console + API snippet).\\n- Verify disablement and that requests are using baseline.\\n\\nWe should also include:\\n\\n- \xe2\x80\x9cWhat information to include in a support ticket\xe2\x80\x9d checklist:\\n  - Org/tenant ID\\n  - Route name/ID\\n  - Model + variant\\n  - Profile ID/version\\n  - Region/deployment mode\\n  - Approx timeframe\\n  - Request IDs/traces\\n  - Observed metrics (fallback rate, p95 latency)", "score": 0.417081, "rank": 16, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "4622cdd4-4d3a-5420-b0d5-f41d74392353", "search_unit_id": "4622cdd4-4d3a-5420-b0d5-f41d74392353", "block_from_id": "7a0586a6-7879-5894-95b9-bee24cbc8884", "block_to_id": "e0539165-9f19-51ad-9f7a-a35af0115631", "section_path": "Quantization Profiles Customer Docs Plan > Non-goals (docs)", "document_id": "f258ae94-d90e-5b1e-8afd-2c4acf87793c", "document_version_id": "8c99c721-acba-5c00-9f81-25a2b151e29c", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a2983978ba0d4d70a795eb7e13de8670.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-12", "heading": "Quantization Profiles Customer Docs Plan > Non-goals (docs)", "content": "Non-goals (docs)\\n\\n- Do not position this as automatic tuning/recommendations (out of scope for v1).\\n- Do not publish internal-only implementation details (artifact signing specifics, internal service names, kill-switch runbooks).\\n- Do not promise universal profile coverage across all models/GPU SKUs.", "score": 0.395364, "rank": 17, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "a92d0a02-9af2-5e32-b03c-1b7fbdd1ff45", "search_unit_id": "a92d0a02-9af2-5e32-b03c-1b7fbdd1ff45", "block_from_id": "c271ef94-9892-59d0-8925-6f6c4c272d68", "block_to_id": "e3084a02-cf23-52f9-a7a5-bbc1b4c60ba5", "section_path": "Quantization Profiles Customer Docs Plan > Information architecture (public docs) > Page 3: Compatibility + limitations", "document_id": "f258ae94-d90e-5b1e-8afd-2c4acf87793c", "document_version_id": "8c99c721-acba-5c00-9f81-25a2b151e29c", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a2983978ba0d4d70a795eb7e13de8670.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-35", "heading": "Quantization Profiles Customer Docs Plan > Information architecture (public docs) > Page 3: Compatibility + limitations", "content": "Page 3: Compatibility + limitations\\n\\n**Proposed title:** \xe2\x80\x9cCompatibility, constraints, and fallback behavior\xe2\x80\x9d\\n\\n**Include**\\n\\n- What compatibility depends on:\\n  - Model ID + model variant\\n  - Deployment mode (Hosted/Dedicated/Private as applicable)\\n  - GPU class/SKU (expressed as customer-friendly names)\\n  - Max context / sequence length limits\\n  - Region constraints (if/when supported in route policy)\\n\\n- Customer-facing compatibility matrix\\n  - If we can\xe2\x80\x99t maintain a full matrix, we must at least publish:\\n    - \xe2\x80\x9cSupported GPUs by profile type\xe2\x80\x9d (e.g., INT8 supported on X, FP8 on Y)\\n    - \xe2\x80\x9cMax supported context per profile\xe2\x80\x9d for popular models\\n  - Decide format: table in docs + downloadable CSV updated weekly (recommended).\\n\\n- Fallback semantics\\n  - Define what happens when incompatible:\\n    - If enablement time: block with clear error and remediation.\\n    - If request time: safe fallback to baseline; emit a signal; no infinite retry loops.\\n\\n- Limitations / known caveats\\n  - Output differences are possible.\\n  - Some profiles may be labeled \xe2\x80\x9cExperimental\xe2\x80\x9d with narrower guardrails.\\n  - If customers pin to a profile version, it won\xe2\x80\x99t change unless they update.\\n  - If we ever add \xe2\x80\x9crecommended\xe2\x80\x9d aliases, document that aliases may move and how we prevent silent changes (see Open Questions).", "score": 0.389652, "rank": 18, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}], "events": [], "entities": [], "relations": [], "source_hits": [], "summary": "", "citations": [], "answer_status": "pending", "no_answer_reason": null, "exploration_id": null, "stats": {"canonical_index": true, "ready_versions": 81, "requested_top_k": null, "candidate_top_k": 32, "candidate_unit_pool_limit": 1024, "candidate_pool_saturated": true, "candidate_units_before_cap": 74, "candidate_units_after_cap": 74, "candidate_units_truncated": 0, "semantic_candidates": 42, "lexical_candidates": 42, "candidates": 74, "relevant": 63, "filtered_irrelevant": 11, "fusion_method": "rrf", "selection_method": "authorized_content_dedup_mmr", "cross_scope_merge": "rank_interleave", "coverage": {"candidate_count": 64, "deduplicated_count": 0, "diversity_weight": 0.5, "near_duplicate_similarity": 0.98, "required_anchor_count": 0, "covered_anchor_count": 0, "anchor_coverage": "not_required", "status": "unknown", "canonical_locator_verified": true, "semantic_answerability": "unknown"}, "routing": {"planner": {"planner_version": "qsp-v1", "requested_strategy": "AUTO", "effective_strategy": "TEMPORAL", "modifiers": [], "reason_codes": ["TEMPORAL_CUE_PRESENT"], "multi_hop_eligible": false}, "request_snapshot_id": "573a170f-5437-45c5-8c81-93ebdad572f9", "groups": [{"project_id": "b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c", "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "partition_id": "b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c", "snapshot_id": "2bf867da-e9bb-411f-bc6d-ac88fd712fd5", "request_snapshot_id": "573a170f-5437-45c5-8c81-93ebdad572f9", "acl_scope_fi