14:08:08  DEBUG    [16710f99862049e7]  sse_starlette.sse  chunk: b'event: result\r\ndata: {"query": "In the enterprise tenant cutover go-live runbook, what latency threshold triggers escalation based on the 95th percentile being too high, and how long does it need to be sustained?", "sections": [{"chunk_id": "c5b4a601-736f-5571-93cf-9f8d798aa176", "search_unit_id": "c5b4a601-736f-5571-93cf-9f8d798aa176", "block_from_id": "64b71eb2-acf0-5873-bd86-8196a12ccdb4", "block_to_id": "d6f32d2a-0056-5287-a4ad-bd0c859db1cb", "section_path": "Go Live Protocols Cross Org Communications Escalation 2027", "document_id": "c1cb92b0-f42c-5fdf-9753-22cf1f569b80", "document_version_id": "a96eb210-903b-56d1-a33c-9bd4347e8b15", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_9c8cb10d65324c03a8ededbd98c1b058.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h1-0", "heading": "Go Live Protocols Cross Org Communications Escalation 2027", "content": "Go Live Protocols Cross Org Communications Escalation 2027\\n\\nSource type: confluence\\nDocument ID: dsid_9c8cb10d65324c03a8ededbd98c1b058\\nRelease: v1.0.0\\nBenchmark: EnterpriseRAG-Bench synthetic upstream data\\nGo-Live Protocols: Cross-Org Communications & Escalation\\nSummary\\n-------\\nThis document defines the cross-organizational go-live protocol used by Redwood Inference for enterprise tenant cutovers. It focuses on communications, stakeholder coordination, and an escalation ladder tailored for high-risk or high-visibility customers. Use this runbook as the canonical checklist for the 72 hours before, during, and 72 hours after a cutover where multiple teams (Customer Success, SRE, Solutions Engineering, Product, and Sales) must be coordinated.\\n\\nScope\\n-----\\n\\n- Applies to: Dedicated and Private deployment go-lives and tenant migrations with SLA commitments (any customer with an enterprise contract or > $50k monthly spend).\\n- Out of scope: self-serve trial accounts, routine model-only updates without routing changes.\\n\\nGoals and SLOs to Protect\\n-------------------------\\n\\n- Availability SLA target to protect during cutover: 99.9% (monthly) for production routes.\\n- Immediate remediation thresholds (trigger escalation):\\n  - Error rate spike: sustained >5% errors for 5 minutes across tenant endpoints.\\n  - Latency spike: P95 latency >2000ms for 10 minutes.\\n  - Token cost anomaly: >200% of projected token spend in 30 minutes.\\n  - KV cache miss-rate >30% sustained for 15 minutes (for cache-sensitive workloads).\\n\\nPre-Cutover (T-72 to T-1 hours)\\n-------------------------------\\n\\n1. Confirm stakeholders and channels\\n   - Primary CSM (Customer Success Manager): name + mobile number.\\n   - Tech lead (Customer): contact + escalation path.\\n   - Solution Engineer (SE): responsible for ingress, API contract verification.\\n   - Oncall SRE/Platform owner: PagerDuty schedule and runbook owner.\\n   - Slack channels: #cs-<customer>-go-live (private channel), #oncall-redwood, #se-ops.\\n2. Telemetry sanity checks \xe2\x80\x94 must pass before proceeding:\\n   - Synthetic journey (happy path) passes end-to-end: <customer> -> Redwood API -> response < 1s.\\n   - PromQL checks: error_rate/instance < 0.005 for 10m; p95_latency_query < 1500ms.\\n3. Canary plan and acceptance criteria\\n   - Canary traffic: route 1% of production for 30 minutes with zero critical errors.\\n   - Acceptance: no P0/P1 incidents during canary and no regression in model quality metrics (if applicable).\\n4. Whitelist and firewall confirmations\\n   - Verify ingress IP ranges, customer egress rules, and TLS client certs.\\n\\nDuring Cutover (T0 to +4 hours) \xe2\x80\x94 Immediate Checklist\\n----------------------------------------------------\\n\\n- Primary communications protocol:\\n  - All updates posted to #cs-<customer>-go-live every 10 minutes during the first hour, then every 30 minutes until stable.\\n  - The CSM posts customer-facing status updates; technical details posted to private channel only.\\n- Live monitoring dashboard (owner: Oncall SRE):\\n  - Tenant-specific dashboard showing throughput, p50/p95/p99 latency, error rate, KV cache hits, token consumption.\\n- Escalation triggers (first responder must escalate within 5 minutes if triggered):\\n  1) P0: service unavailable for customer routes \xe2\x80\x94 immediate page to P1 oncall and notify Engineering Director.\\n  2) P1: sustained SLO breach (see thresholds above) \xe2\x80\x94 page SE and PM, start RCA and mitigation steps.\\n  3) P2: model quality regression detected \xe2\x80\x94 notify Applied ML and SE; consider traffic switch to verified model snapshot.\\n\\nEscalation Ladder (contact order and responsibilities)\\n----------------------------------------------------", "score": 0.75274, "rank": 0, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "d4d28dbf-f9ec-5e64-81cc-730e9fc10ed1", "search_unit_id": "d4d28dbf-f9ec-5e64-81cc-730e9fc10ed1", "block_from_id": "82335435-9c35-5b4e-8472-b32d274cf408", "block_to_id": "44984730-99d8-5d84-a2fe-54d8b24e2cd5", "section_path": "Go Live Protocols Cross Org Communications Escalation 2027", "document_id": "c1cb92b0-f42c-5fdf-9753-22cf1f569b80", "document_version_id": "a96eb210-903b-56d1-a33c-9bd4347e8b15", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_9c8cb10d65324c03a8ededbd98c1b058.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "tbl-11", "heading": "Go Live Protocols Cross Org Communications Escalation 2027", "content": "| Level | Trigger example | Primary contact | Secondary contact | Action required |\\n|-------|-----------------|-----------------|-------------------|-----------------|\\n| L1 (CSM) | Customer questions, minor errors | CSM | SE | Acknowledge to customer within 15m, open internal thread |\\n| L2 (SRE) | Error rate >5% | Oncall SRE | SRE Lead | Execute diagnostics, apply mitigations (rate-limit, route switch) |\\n| L3 (SE/PM) | Persistent degradation >30m | Solutions Engineer | Product Manager | Coordinate config changes, model fallback, communicate to customer executives |\\n| L4 (Exec) | SLA breach or major incident | Head of Customer Success | Head of Engineering | Declare incident, engage legal/finance if SLA credits likely |\\n\\nNote: The table above is intended as a quick reference. The full escalation paging list with phone numbers and PagerDuty IDs is stored in /confluence/people-ops/rosters and in the private channel pinned messages.\\n\\nCommon Mitigations (ordered by lowest customer impact first)\\n----------------------------------------------------------\\n\\n- Increase routing to a higher-capacity pool (if Dedicated: burst pool)\\n- Apply tenant-level throttles to protect shared resources (quota reduce to 30% of projected steady-state)\\n- Enable model fallback: route to last-known-stable model snapshot\\n- Temporarily switch customer to hosted API endpoint (if allowed by contract)\\n- Quiesce long-running batch jobs from the customer side\\n\\nRollback and Safe-fail Strategies\\n--------------------------------\\n\\n1. Safe rollback to previous routing config (SE executes):\\n   - Command: curl -X POST https://ops-api.internal.redwood/v1/route/revert -d \'{\\"tenant\\":\\"<tenant-id>\\",\\"to_config\\":\\"<previous-config-id>\\"}\' \\n   - Confirm routing table via: kubectl get svc ingress-<tenant> -o yaml (requires ops role)\\n2. Tenant quiesce API (customer-facing graceful shutdown):\\n   - POST https://api.redwood.com/v1/tenants/<tenant>/quiesce?actor=ops\\n   - Expected behavior: existing requests drain, new requests return 429 with Retry-After header.\\n3. Emergency switchback to hosted region: update DNS TTL and apply traffic policy TTL=30s for faster re-routing.\\n\\nCommunication Templates\\n-----------------------\\n\\n- Customer-facing 1-line (acknowledge): \\"We are investigating increased latency for your production routes and will provide an update within 15 minutes. No action required from your side unless we ask.\\"\\n- Customer-facing status update (10m cadence): include short bullet list: observed metric, action taken, owner, ETA for next update.\\n- Internal P0 page message sample:\\n  - \\"P0: <customer> production routes returning 503s since 08:12 UTC. Oncall SRE investigating. Initial hypothesis: ingress proxy thread exhaustion. Paging SRE Lead and SE. Next update in 5 minutes\\"\\n\\nTelemetry checks / Queries (examples)\\n----------------------------------\\n\\n- PromQL (errors): sum(rate(http_requests_total{tenant=\\"<tenant>\\",status=~\\"5..\\"}[5m])) / sum(rate(http_requests_total{tenant=\\"<tenant>\\"}[5m])) > 0.05\\n- Token consumption anomaly (example):\\n  - Query: increase(token_count_total{tenant=\\"<tenant>\\"}[30m]) / expected_token_rate > 2.0\\n- Synthetic validation command (curl):\\n  - curl -s -X POST https://api.redwood.com/v1/generate -H \\"Authorization: Bearer <key>\\" -d \'{\\"input\\":\\"synthetic health check\\"}\' | jq \'.latency_ms\'\\n\\nPost-Cutover (T+4 to T+72 hours)\\n--------------------------------\\n\\n- Stability window monitoring: SRE to keep watch for 72 hours; escalate on any SLO breach.\\n- Cost and quota reconciliation: Finance Ops and CSM to review token consumption, forecast delta, and apply quota protections if needed.\\n- Customer QBR prep: collect first-week metrics and any incident notes for the 30-day QBR.\\n\\nRunbook Ownership and RACI\\n-------------------------", "score": 0.482173, "rank": 1, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "83d18350-c1bb-5872-ac05-5fbc8c02f296", "search_unit_id": "83d18350-c1bb-5872-ac05-5fbc8c02f296", "block_from_id": "a5acc818-750a-5c18-bb02-9bf043739249", "block_to_id": "e844c72c-f808-5d8b-b173-b3c0a0341314", "section_path": "Go Live Protocols Cross Org Communications Escalation 2027", "document_id": "c1cb92b0-f42c-5fdf-9753-22cf1f569b80", "document_version_id": "a96eb210-903b-56d1-a33c-9bd4347e8b15", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_9c8cb10d65324c03a8ededbd98c1b058.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "list-24", "heading": "Go Live Protocols Cross Org Communications Escalation 2027", "content": "- CSM: customer comms and executive escalation.\\n- SE: onboarding technical lead, API contract signoff, whitelist verification.\\n- Oncall SRE: monitoring, mitigation, and platform config changes in emergencies.\\n- Product/Applied ML: model quality regressions and rollbacks.\\n- Finance Ops: post-cutover cost anomalies and quota adjustments.\\n\\nAppendix A \xe2\x80\x94 Playbook Checklist (copyable)\\n-----------------------------------------\\n\\n- [ ] Confirm private channel and all stakeholder contacts pinned\\n- [ ] Telemetry smoke test passed (synthetic happy path)\\n- [ ] Canary plan scheduled and accepted by SE and SRE\\n- [ ] Firewall/whitelist config validated by Network team\\n- [ ] PagerDuty rotations confirmed and escalation contacts available\\n- [ ] Customer-facing status template approved by CSM\\n- [ ] Post-cutover QBR slot scheduled with customer (within 30 days)\\n\\nAppendix B \xe2\x80\x94 Links and References\\n--------------------------------\\n\\n- Tenant cutover checklist (internal): /confluence/customer-success-and-support/enterprise-onboarding/onboarding-handback-and-first-90-days-ops-guide-2026\\n- Incident comms templates: /confluence/eng-sre/incident-communication-templates\\n- PagerDuty runbook: https://pagerduty.com/orgs/redwood-incidents (private)\\n\\nAppendix C \xe2\x80\x94 Escalation Contact Quickview\\n----------------------------------------\\n\\n- Oncall SRE: pagerduty (PD ID: PD12345), Slack: @oncall-sre, mobile: +1-555-0102\\n- SE on duty: Slack: @se-ops, mobile: +1-555-0148\\n- CSM (Primary): Priya Patel, Slack: @priya.cs, mobile: +1-555-0190\\n\\nRevision History\\n----------------\\n\\n- 2027-02-10: Created by Priya Patel.\\n- 2027-03-02: Reviewed and clarified rollback steps; added expense reconciliation task (Marisol Gomez).\\n\\nNotes and governance\\n--------------------\\nKeep this page updated after every enterprise go-live. If the customer contract contains additional communication obligations (e.g., weekly executive summaries), add them to the post-cutover tasks and pin them in the customer channel.", "score": 0.440976, "rank": 2, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "3673b29b-cfa7-5efa-8aa9-5ff8dd44023f", "search_unit_id": "3673b29b-cfa7-5efa-8aa9-5ff8dd44023f", "block_from_id": "f48154e7-ac7a-58ae-bcf2-0955daab830c", "block_to_id": "cba6a8ae-ef1b-5d20-827b-830f9be9b71c", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Default Thresholds (v1) > Latency (p95 end-to-end)", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-52", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Default Thresholds (v1) > Latency (p95 end-to-end)", "content": "Latency (p95 end-to-end)\\n\\n- Warning: p95 E2E latency **+10%** vs baseline for **2 out of 3** consecutive evaluation windows.\\n- Paging: p95 E2E latency **+20%** vs baseline for **3 out of 4** consecutive evaluation windows.", "score": 0.697978, "rank": 3, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "048dcbdb-3ef2-5adb-aaa1-7b3d09b59784", "search_unit_id": "048dcbdb-3ef2-5adb-aaa1-7b3d09b59784", "block_from_id": "19c4bfbb-325e-5713-b50c-5c5bc52048b7", "block_to_id": "29816627-69c4-5de1-9925-50d061e7922c", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h1-0", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds", "content": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds\\n\\nSource type: confluence\\nDocument ID: dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83\\nRelease: v1.0.0\\nBenchmark: EnterpriseRAG-Bench synthetic upstream data\\nADR-0142: Perf Canary Baselines, Regression Thresholds, Min Sample Sizes, and Anti-Flap Logic", "score": 0.614221, "rank": 4, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "3c29ae8f-333e-571e-99bd-aa3c7ff9aeab", "search_unit_id": "3c29ae8f-333e-571e-99bd-aa3c7ff9aeab", "block_from_id": "6342bbc2-b5e5-53b5-b00c-de7baf7de1a6", "block_to_id": "587fa100-5b3c-50ef-870a-e03488252f55", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Status", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-2", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Status", "content": "Status\\n\\nPublished.", "score": 0.593281, "rank": 5, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "2eebb20a-591d-506c-b85a-40583bdabfb8", "search_unit_id": "2eebb20a-591d-506c-b85a-40583bdabfb8", "block_from_id": "6534390e-d337-5fa5-867c-5f7d360901cd", "block_to_id": "5d87204c-d905-5235-a7bd-28e6127d93ce", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Regression Definition > Core comparison method (v1)", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-42", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Regression Definition > Core comparison method (v1)", "content": "Core comparison method (v1)\\n\\nFor each metric M and key K in each evaluation window W:\\n\\n- Compute observed metric value O(K, W).\\n- Fetch baseline value B(K) and baseline variability estimates when available.\\n- Compute percent change: \xce\x94 = (O - B) / B.\\n\\nWe use percent change thresholds with guardrails (min samples + sustained breach). Percent thresholds are chosen because:\\n\\n- Different models have different absolute latencies.\\n- p95 is the primary SLO-relevant tail metric.", "score": 0.573437, "rank": 6, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "032225b4-4174-53d9-88dc-f54e70fe0c00", "search_unit_id": "032225b4-4174-53d9-88dc-f54e70fe0c00", "block_from_id": "63f9d991-c068-50ac-b7b3-df4816644d74", "block_to_id": "5157e419-583c-5b22-977d-03cd517a3125", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Summary", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-4", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Summary", "content": "Summary\\n\\nThis ADR defines how the production performance canary computes baselines and evaluates regressions for per-model serving performance (primarily p95 latency and tokens/sec). It documents:\\n\\n- Baseline computation approach (rolling vs fixed) and when each is used.\\n- Regression thresholds (warning vs paging) and how they are applied.\\n- Minimum sample sizes and confidence requirements to avoid noisy alerts.\\n- Anti-flap / dedupe logic to prevent alert storms during drift, telemetry delays, or small-sample variance.", "score": 0.572342, "rank": 7, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "829619c6-5bb2-5336-b599-41394e4d318e", "search_unit_id": "829619c6-5bb2-5336-b599-41394e4d318e", "block_from_id": "14f1eecf-4873-5552-ac97-9814fbb2085d", "block_to_id": "25fdbf57-8bd8-5b95-81cc-c2f2996c61b9", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Metrics Covered", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-32", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Metrics Covered", "content": "Metrics Covered\\n\\nBaselines and regressions are computed for:\\n\\n- End-to-end latency: p50, p95, p99 (ms)\\n- Runtime-only latency: p50, p95, p99 (ms) (excludes network/client)\\n- Prefill latency and decode latency (ms)\\n- Queueing time (ms) (scheduler-level)\\n- Tokens/sec (overall, and decode tokens/sec where available)\\n- Batch size distribution (for attribution)\\n- KV cache hit rate (where applicable; informational at v1)", "score": 0.567634, "rank": 8, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "4e8c1606-f72d-5136-9ce8-fabf763777a9", "search_unit_id": "4e8c1606-f72d-5136-9ce8-fabf763777a9", "block_from_id": "ede7f74b-3902-5925-8fcd-a7d922089b06", "block_to_id": "b5d12f89-a1c5-5889-b71c-39ea90694fee", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Context / Problem", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-7", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Context / Problem", "content": "Context / Problem\\n\\nRedwood\xe2\x80\x99s serving runtime changes frequently (kernel selection updates, scheduler heuristics, model config changes, GPU fleet changes, and staged rollouts). We need an always-on canary that:\\n\\n- Detects real p95 latency regressions and throughput drops early.\\n- Produces actionable signals for attribution (kernel vs scheduler vs infra).\\n- Avoids paging on expected variance and baseline drift (e.g., slow fleet mix changes or regional differences).\\n\\nThe key design tension is baseline choice:\\n\\n- A **fixed baseline** is stable and easy to reason about during rollouts, but can become stale as hardware/driver stacks and workloads evolve.\\n- A **rolling baseline** adapts over time, but can drift (masking regressions) or create false positives if drift is misinterpreted as regression.", "score": 0.551403, "rank": 9, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "6f7e3532-0cff-5a22-ab1c-2e305dbbeba2", "search_unit_id": "6f7e3532-0cff-5a22-ab1c-2e305dbbeba2", "block_from_id": "5ee061d6-2f11-5f40-a4e4-e60a4b37ec3b", "block_to_id": "8f416c20-0392-5b72-8f2c-8ee37dee92c9", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Implementation Notes / Requirements", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-109", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Implementation Notes / Requirements", "content": "Implementation Notes / Requirements\\n\\n1. Baseline artifacts must be stored in an access-controlled, versioned store with auditability (who/when created).\\n2. Canary config must support per-model overrides:\\n   - thresholds by severity\\n   - whether region-specific keys are enabled\\n   - \xe2\x80\x9ctop model\xe2\x80\x9d flag affecting paging eligibility\\n3. Alert payloads must include:\\n   - observed value, baseline value, percent change\\n   - sample counts and token counts\\n   - runtime_build_id, kernel_set_id, hardware_sku, region\\n   - links to dashboards, traces, and runbook\\n4. Changes to default thresholds must go through an ADR update or SRE-approved change request.", "score": 0.530463, "rank": 10, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "4d7afc92-5ba0-53c2-a694-97e612d826d5", "search_unit_id": "4d7afc92-5ba0-53c2-a694-97e612d826d5", "block_from_id": "5c4aa2bf-81ed-523c-af27-8fd745dc2af1", "block_to_id": "92efbd3f-2398-549e-b0e0-8089a7e21326", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Decision Drivers", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-12", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Decision Drivers", "content": "Decision Drivers\\n\\n1. **Low noise / high trust**: warnings should be useful; pages should be rare and high-confidence.\\n2. **Fast detection**: detect regressions within ~10\xe2\x80\x9330 minutes for top models in covered regions.\\n3. **Attribution**: baseline keys must align to dimensions needed for root cause (runtime build, kernel tags, SKU).\\n4. **Operational simplicity**: SRE/on-call should have a predictable interpretation of \xe2\x80\x9cregression vs baseline,\xe2\x80\x9d including during ongoing rollouts.\\n5. **Guardrails against drift and telemetry issues**: avoid alert storms caused by baseline drift, delayed metric ingestion, and label cardinality errors.", "score": 0.530463, "rank": 11, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "0bab4b61-2347-5b3a-845d-6f3bba6297b1", "search_unit_id": "0bab4b61-2347-5b3a-845d-6f3bba6297b1", "block_from_id": "09185fbc-2dd2-59de-843f-99f5f6a2f45f", "block_to_id": "9cc7b2e5-b278-5170-b574-b901af5c2821", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Baseline Keys (What defines \xe2\x80\x9clike-for-like\xe2\x80\x9d)", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-24", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Baseline Keys (What defines \xe2\x80\x9clike-for-like\xe2\x80\x9d)", "content": "Baseline Keys (What defines \xe2\x80\x9clike-for-like\xe2\x80\x9d)\\n\\nBaseline artifacts and regression evaluation are keyed by the following dimensions:\\n\\n**Required baseline key fields (v1):**\\n\\n- model_id (canonical model identifier)\\n- model_version (registry version / hash)\\n- runtime_build_id (serving runtime build tag)\\n- kernel_set_id (kernel selection/version identifier)\\n- hardware_sku (e.g., H100-80GB, A100-80GB)\\n\\n**Optional fields (only when variance requires it):**\\n\\n- region (enabled for regions with materially different fleet/network characteristics)\\n- capacity_tier (hosted vs dedicated pools) when pools differ materially\\n\\nNotes:\\n\\n- We do NOT key baselines by customer, endpoint, or prompt content (privacy + cardinality constraints).\\n- Scheduler configuration flags that materially change behavior must be reflected either in runtime_build_id or an explicit scheduler_profile tag (introduced only if needed; kept off by default to control cardinality).", "score": 0.530463, "rank": 12, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "23d59747-a1af-515c-8f79-528d93c99d09", "search_unit_id": "23d59747-a1af-515c-8f79-528d93c99d09", "block_from_id": "9cd681e5-97cb-5376-8e9e-4eebb60ae8c3", "block_to_id": "5ea39e5e-dfbb-5c06-b745-2e0fbead0881", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Baseline Computation > Rolling health baseline (calibration only)", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-38", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Baseline Computation > Rolling health baseline (calibration only)", "content": "Rolling health baseline (calibration only)\\n\\n- Window: trailing 7 days, excluding periods marked as \xe2\x80\x9crollout\xe2\x80\x9d or \xe2\x80\x9cincident.\xe2\x80\x9d\\n- Aggregation: daily aggregates with robust statistics (median-of-daily-p95) to reduce sensitivity to short spikes.\\n- Purpose:\\n  - detect slow drift (e.g., fleet changes) that may warrant generating a new fixed baseline\\n  - suggest region/SKU overrides when variance is consistently higher", "score": 0.530463, "rank": 13, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "e9bc9610-465d-5c8f-8485-93b1933c48c3", "search_unit_id": "e9bc9610-465d-5c8f-8485-93b1933c48c3", "block_from_id": "bf3f536f-4574-5dfb-bb65-6c1bd9f7bf3a", "block_to_id": "e39cb70f-0d0a-5536-ac7f-20b2c8af4561", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Alternatives Considered > A) Pure rolling baseline (always updated)", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-85", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Alternatives Considered > A) Pure rolling baseline (always updated)", "content": "Alternatives Considered\\n\\nA) Pure rolling baseline (always updated)\\n\\nPros:\\n\\n- Adapts to drift without explicit re-baselining.\\n\\nCons:\\n\\n- Risk of masking slow regressions (baseline chases the regression).\\n- Hard to use for rollout gating (\xe2\x80\x9cmoving goalposts\xe2\x80\x9d).\\n- Susceptible to alert storms if rolling logic is impacted by label bugs or ingestion gaps.\\n\\nDecision: Rejected for paging/gating. Allowed only as a secondary calibration signal.", "score": 0.530463, "rank": 14, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "a5d10308-dc0f-5092-9f54-e1a24e98ff47", "search_unit_id": "a5d10308-dc0f-5092-9f54-e1a24e98ff47", "block_from_id": "0d177d2f-be12-544e-9675-b65e52bb4ff4", "block_to_id": "ec4642d0-ae24-5d9b-8056-43ad7ef0f699", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Appendix A: Example Per-Model Overrides (illustrative)", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-115", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Appendix A: Example Per-Model Overrides (illustrative)", "content": "Appendix A: Example Per-Model Overrides (illustrative)\\n\\n- Top model (customer-critical): paging at +15% p95 E2E, -12% tokens/sec, stricter min token count.\\n- High-variance model: warning only, wider thresholds (+15% / -10%), region-specific baseline enabled.\\n- New kernel rollout candidate: temporary tighter warning (+8%) during rollout ring, but paging remains at default until validated.", "score": 0.530463, "rank": 15, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "88c5d01c-3c5f-5fa7-90a8-6dc5fafff25b", "search_unit_id": "88c5d01c-3c5f-5fa7-90a8-6dc5fafff25b", "block_from_id": "37c58785-6dda-52d4-840e-3f394dea5e3f", "block_to_id": "6be03658-1bd7-5836-8f16-cd17ebcdc45e", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Minimum Sample Sizes and Windowing > Minimum samples (per key K, per window)", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-64", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Minimum Sample Sizes and Windowing > Minimum samples (per key K, per window)", "content": "Minimum samples (per key K, per window)\\n\\n- **Latency metrics**: minimum **200 successful canary requests** per window.\\n- **Tokens/sec**: minimum **200 successful canary requests** per window AND minimum **50,000 total generated tokens** per window.\\n\\nIf sample requirements are not met:\\n\\n- No alert state change is allowed (prevents flapping in low-coverage periods).\\n- Dashboard panels display \xe2\x80\x9cinsufficient sample\xe2\x80\x9d annotation.\\n\\nRationale:\\n\\n- Tail latency (p95/p99) is unreliable with very small N.\\n- Tokens/sec needs sufficient token volume to smooth per-request variance.", "score": 0.530463, "rank": 16, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "17d628e9-e2bb-54f0-aaa9-04f6cff1f5c6", "search_unit_id": "17d628e9-e2bb-54f0-aaa9-04f6cff1f5c6", "block_from_id": "947e3463-cf65-52cf-aeba-ec29d28e5d30", "block_to_id": "567b9445-f73d-5d9d-a334-719d01923415", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Baseline Computation > Fixed baseline artifact", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-35", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Baseline Computation > Fixed baseline artifact", "content": "Baseline Computation\\n\\nFixed baseline artifact\\n\\n- Source: controlled perf-canary runs using the approved synthetic prompt distribution.\\n- For each baseline key, we store:\\n  - distribution summaries (p50/p95/p99) for each latency metric\\n  - mean and standard deviation where stable enough to be meaningful\\n  - tokens/sec distribution summaries\\n  - run metadata (time range, sample count, canary config version)\\n- Baseline validity: baseline is considered valid only if it meets minimum sample size requirements (see below) and passes sanity checks (no telemetry gaps, no error-rate spikes).", "score": 0.530463, "rank": 17, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "425c4351-2cde-5cad-ac56-fba6f0b5456e", "search_unit_id": "425c4351-2cde-5cad-ac56-fba6f0b5456e", "block_from_id": "bc4038c4-da3b-50a6-8ee9-0bef7e1a8c79", "block_to_id": "4a9bca18-96ce-55f7-bd43-b729429267df", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Appendix B: Ownership", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-117", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Appendix B: Ownership", "content": "Appendix B: Ownership\\n\\n- Baseline pipeline and artifact integrity: Telemetry Platform (Logan Wright) + Metrics/Baselines (Nadia Rahman)\\n- Threshold standards and paging hygiene: SRE (Sean Gallagher, Allison Grant)\\n- Model list and rollout gating integration: Serving Runtime (Noah Patel) + Release Engineering (Connor O\'Brien)", "score": 0.530463, "rank": 18, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "811fe0c3-2593-5368-9d98-111da48a8a12", "search_unit_id": "811fe0c3-2593-5368-9d98-111da48a8a12", "block_from_id": "24166ce2-b07a-5310-95d0-4fa4c91ab798", "block_to_id": "0b672f8b-beee-5069-9b9b-64d2681d7531", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Consequences > Negative / Tradeoffs", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-107", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Consequences > Negative / Tradeoffs", "content": "Negative / Tradeoffs\\n\\n- Requires baseline artifact generation whenever major runtime/kernel changes land for covered models/SKUs.\\n- Some true regressions may be detected slightly later due to sustained-breach requirements.\\n- Optional region/tier overrides add complexity when enabled.", "score": 0.530463, "rank": 19, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "7b700c43-46fe-59a4-a0bb-d3cd1c2a7f01", "search_unit_id": "7b700c43-46fe-59a4-a0bb-d3cd1c2a7f01", "block_from_id": "b5a87d99-1d52-5998-9ee1-f3bc88581b1a", "block_to_id": "96de10ac-0596-5756-8478-56b0fc50e039", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Rollout Guidance", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-111", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Rollout Guidance", "content": "Rollout Guidance\\n\\n- Phase 1 (single region): warnings only, tune per-model overrides until noise is acceptable.\\n- Phase 2: enable paging only for top models with proven low variance and stable baselines.\\n- Phase 3: integrate gating with release engineering once paging signal is trusted (warning can gate early as \xe2\x80\x9csoft fail,\xe2\x80\x9d paging as \xe2\x80\x9chard fail\xe2\x80\x9d).", "score": 0.530463, "rank": 20, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "3c486a70-00a3-5591-af7a-f282b4184282", "search_unit_id": "3c486a70-00a3-5591-af7a-f282b4184282", "block_from_id": "264e1948-923a-5782-8b89-7dfd048bedc5", "block_to_id": "046385dd-2761-521d-aa1b-81e7f72587a7", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Alternatives Considered > C) Per-region baselines always on", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-98", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Alternatives Considered > C) Per-region baselines always on", "content": "C) Per-region baselines always on\\n\\nPros:\\n\\n- Reduces false positives due to cross-region fleet differences.\\n\\nCons:\\n\\n- Baseline explosion (more artifacts and config), operational overhead.\\n\\nDecision: Region is optional and only enabled for models/regions where observed variance requires it.", "score": 0.530463, "rank": 21, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "dce37664-4c7a-5cd2-aff9-2b8b05d93b21", "search_unit_id": "dce37664-4c7a-5cd2-aff9-2b8b05d93b21", "block_from_id": "6d4588a0-f081-5ee0-9394-bddc1b49fd75", "block_to_id": "648b9fdc-1229-5e63-b445-0ffa22b1fc1a", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Default Thresholds (v1) > Runtime-only attribution signals (non-paging by default)", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-56", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Default Thresholds (v1) > Runtime-only attribution signals (non-paging by default)", "content": "Runtime-only attribution signals (non-paging by default)\\n\\nThese are emitted to dashboards and included in alert payloads, but do not page unless explicitly enabled for a model:\\n\\n- Queueing time p95 +25% (suggests scheduler/fleet saturation)\\n- Prefill p95 +15% (suggests kernel/model config regressions)\\n- Decode p95 +15% (suggests kernel/model config regressions)\\n\\nRationale:\\n\\n- Paging should be driven by end-to-end customer-impact proxy (E2E p95 and tokens/sec).\\n- Breakdown metrics improve triage but are often noisier and more sensitive to load mix.", "score": 0.530463, "rank": 22, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "4a890abb-a268-5f6c-8bd8-8190ba739f96", "search_unit_id": "4a890abb-a268-5f6c-8bd8-8190ba739f96", "block_from_id": "0deabef5-6329-59bf-ba97-4e7537d0c14d", "block_to_id": "b2185789-0f79-580c-91cf-f2daa95dc8af", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Consequences > Positive", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-104", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Consequences > Positive", "content": "Consequences\\n\\nPositive\\n\\n- Stable, versioned baselines support rollout gates and high-confidence paging.\\n- Rolling health baseline provides drift visibility without undermining safety.\\n- Anti-flap controls reduce alert noise and prevent incident-bot storms.", "score": 0.530463, "rank": 23, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "6cf7edd0-441f-57e7-9770-a53c1e8cc21c", "search_unit_id": "6cf7edd0-441f-57e7-9770-a53c1e8cc21c", "block_from_id": "dc7c96c3-d4c6-599e-893c-84cfaa30ab4e", "block_to_id": "59cddb0f-3c7c-5ec1-8952-2ab0ac38445c", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Alternatives Considered > B) Pure fixed baseline (never updated unless manual)", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-92", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Alternatives Considered > B) Pure fixed baseline (never updated unless manual)", "content": "B) Pure fixed baseline (never updated unless manual)\\n\\nPros:\\n\\n- Extremely stable; easy to reason about.\\n\\nCons:\\n\\n- Becomes stale as fleet/hardware/driver changes accumulate; increases false positives over time.\\n- Forces frequent manual work to remain relevant.\\n\\nDecision: Rejected as the only strategy. Adopted as primary baseline with explicit regeneration workflows.", "score": 0.530463, "rank": 24, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "f37db93e-b81a-5ba4-8d45-7c2934d4367c", "search_unit_id": "f37db93e-b81a-5ba4-8d45-7c2934d4367c", "block_from_id": "c64b2220-dfdd-542d-9218-86e48adf63ea", "block_to_id": "91573533-ff3d-56bc-8378-b75fd72b0c0d", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Regression Definition > Threshold levels", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-47", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Regression Definition > Threshold levels", "content": "Threshold levels\\n\\nTwo alert levels exist:\\n\\n- **Warning**: actionable signal for runtime team triage; routed to #eng-runtime.\\n- **Paging**: sustained, high-confidence regression on top models; routed to on-call rotation.", "score": 0.530463, "rank": 25, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "a445ba42-6f63-5e30-bbff-d9e81f181849", "search_unit_id": "a445ba42-6f63-5e30-bbff-d9e81f181849", "block_from_id": "665a2693-48f7-5964-b2f2-5385ab4f0885", "block_to_id": "1f2673e0-819a-5ceb-a3a7-130f139dfaca", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Anti-Flap, Dedupe, and Hysteresis > Cooldown", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-77", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Anti-Flap, Dedupe, and Hysteresis > Cooldown", "content": "Cooldown\\n\\nAfter an alert transitions to firing, we enforce a cooldown before re-triggering a new incident thread for the same key:\\n\\n- Warning cooldown: 60 minutes\\n- Paging cooldown: 120 minutes", "score": 0.530463, "rank": 26, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "66d7594b-8436-5080-9aef-e0793b071050", "search_unit_id": "66d7594b-8436-5080-9aef-e0793b071050", "block_from_id": "b054f4e8-bbac-5499-945b-0a4e35e10b2a", "block_to_id": "ced36613-e0ec-5017-b3a5-8e6157be9809", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Minimum Sample Sizes and Windowing > Evaluation window", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-61", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Minimum Sample Sizes and Windowing > Evaluation window", "content": "Minimum Sample Sizes and Windowing\\n\\nEvaluation window\\n\\n- Default evaluation window: **10 minutes**.\\n- Windows are evaluated continuously and require sustained breach rules (see anti-flap).", "score": 0.530463, "rank": 27, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "f6abcbc2-e8a0-55b0-b881-e05dd8c11289", "search_unit_id": "f6abcbc2-e8a0-55b0-b881-e05dd8c11289", "block_from_id": "fa187574-c2df-5d98-94fe-8213b8cb55e1", "block_to_id": "2f7b581d-7720-58fa-b392-2204cfd086bc", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Changelog", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-119", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Changelog", "content": "Changelog\\n\\n- 2026-02-12: Clarified cooldown timers, added telemetry delay protection rule, and tightened tokens/sec minimum token count requirement.", "score": 0.530463, "rank": 28, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "7eb972fc-c055-5e16-b256-ab258597491c", "search_unit_id": "7eb972fc-c055-5e16-b256-ab258597491c", "block_from_id": "1c77e0e1-0c02-5b5d-967f-9caf072d965c", "block_to_id": "e38a1a5f-91dc-5cbb-a233-80d234957dba", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Anti-Flap, Dedupe, and Hysteresis > Dedupe key", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-80", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Anti-Flap, Dedupe, and Hysteresis > Dedupe key", "content": "Dedupe key\\n\\nIncident-bot dedupes based on:\\n\\n- model_id + model_version + runtime_build_id + kernel_set_id + hardware_sku (+ region if present) + metric_type + severity", "score": 0.530463, "rank": 29, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "11e07925-978c-5589-a759-600b153ded4d", "search_unit_id": "11e07925-978c-5589-a759-600b153ded4d", "block_from_id": "be65d402-742a-5e74-b3dd-89badbc8f639", "block_to_id": "ec1f642b-4a53-5e57-a104-739d0f9859df", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Anti-Flap, Dedupe, and Hysteresis > Alert clear (hysteresis)", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-74", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Anti-Flap, Dedupe, and Hysteresis > Alert clear (hysteresis)", "content": "Alert clear (hysteresis)\\n\\nAlerts clear only when performance returns closer to baseline:\\n\\n- Warning clears when \xce\x94 < +6% (latency) and \xce\x94 > -5% (tokens/sec) for 3/3 windows.\\n- Paging clears when \xce\x94 < +12% (latency) and \xce\x94 > -10% (tokens/sec) for 4/4 windows.", "score": 0.530463, "rank": 30, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "27698a5d-d93e-55bc-9e85-1ea0b026d5f6", "search_unit_id": "27698a5d-d93e-55bc-9e85-1ea0b026d5f6", "block_from_id": "52c4cb61-c56f-5cf9-a932-5f55b94704eb", "block_to_id": "4d4a53fe-b57d-5204-82ee-bd71a6c3810e", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Regression Definition", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-40", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Regression Definition", "content": "Regression Definition\\n\\nWe define regression as a statistically and operationally meaningful deviation from the fixed baseline.", "score": 0.530463, "rank": 31, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "727341b2-7485-5498-b317-52936582e1ca", "search_unit_id": "727341b2-7485-5498-b317-52936582e1ca", "block_from_id": "72526615-4309-5311-b017-ea8575fcc639", "block_to_id": "461f557f-a9ae-56b2-a8f6-4cdb7deb0121", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Anti-Flap, Dedupe, and Hysteresis > Sustained breach logic", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-70", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Anti-Flap, Dedupe, and Hysteresis > Sustained breach logic", "content": "Anti-Flap, Dedupe, and Hysteresis\\n\\nSustained breach logic\\n\\nWe use \xe2\x80\x9cM out of N windows\xe2\x80\x9d to reduce sensitivity to transient spikes:\\n\\n- Warning: 2/3 consecutive windows breach\\n- Paging: 3/4 consecutive windows breach", "score": 0.530463, "rank": 32, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "84971e12-3b85-562f-a47a-0616d6f1282d", "search_unit_id": "84971e12-3b85-562f-a47a-0616d6f1282d", "block_from_id": "0fcf622d-1f62-51a2-a7a7-d75470f483a7", "block_to_id": "ede8256a-24a2-5244-87e0-c2190dbea2b1", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Default Thresholds (v1)", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-50", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Default Thresholds (v1)", "content": "Default Thresholds (v1)\\n\\nThresholds are configurable per model, with these platform defaults used unless overridden.", "score": 0.530463, "rank": 33, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "ccfb0303-74f9-5f6e-8453-2020a0773c5b", "search_unit_id": "ccfb0303-74f9-5f6e-8453-2020a0773c5b", "block_from_id": "86f27c7d-f46e-5b7c-a28c-65cdf007658d", "block_to_id": "65b7d661-0827-5da3-b943-5e2ade9df157", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Decision", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-14", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Decision", "content": "Decision\\n\\nWe adopt a **hybrid baseline strategy**:\\n\\n1) **Primary baseline = Fixed, versioned baseline per (model, model_version, runtime_build, kernel_set_id, hardware_sku) with optional region override**\\n\\n- Baselines are generated from controlled canary runs (prod-like load) and stored as immutable artifacts.\\n- Baselines are explicitly tied to the runtime build and kernel selection identifiers so comparisons remain meaningful.\\n- This is the baseline used for rollout gating and for paging.\\n\\n2) **Secondary baseline = Rolling \xe2\x80\x9chealth baseline\xe2\x80\x9d used for drift monitoring and threshold calibration (not for paging)**\\n\\n- We compute a rolling reference from recent stable periods (default: last 7 days) to detect slow environmental drift and to inform recalibration.\\n- Rolling baseline is not used to auto-suppress a fixed-baseline regression; it is used as a triage and tuning signal.\\n\\n3) **Baseline freeze rules**\\n\\n- During a runtime rollout (canary/gradual), the baseline used for alerts is **frozen** to the most recent fixed baseline for the currently active runtime build on that ring.\\n- If an incident is declared for a perf regression, baseline updates are **paused** for affected keys until incident closure.\\n\\n4) **Threshold evaluation requires minimum sample size + sustained breach + hysteresis**\\n\\n- Alerts require both a minimum number of canary requests and sustained breach across multiple evaluation windows.\\n- Alert clear conditions are stricter than trigger conditions (hysteresis) to reduce flapping.", "score": 0.473679, "rank": 34, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "cc63d243-50c2-55eb-8bfb-acf236cce502", "search_unit_id": "cc63d243-50c2-55eb-8bfb-acf236cce502", "block_from_id": "1ce02a38-b4d8-5934-ad66-cff6f5a6f9dd", "block_to_id": "090ecf90-66c7-5753-99a3-c362c5d606c8", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Open Questions (tracked outside ADR)", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h2-113", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Open Questions (tracked outside ADR)", "content": "Open Questions (tracked outside ADR)\\n\\n- Whether to introduce a scheduler_profile tag in baseline keys (cardinality vs attribution benefit).\\n- Whether to page on runtime-only p95 for certain enterprise-dedicated pools (when E2E has additional network variance).\\n- Whether to incorporate a lightweight statistical test (e.g., bootstrap CI on p95) for models with unusually high variance.", "score": 0.305637, "rank": 35, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "a40f8598-2951-5778-a15f-0707398d2692", "search_unit_id": "a40f8598-2951-5778-a15f-0707398d2692", "block_from_id": "327d6dc6-1a59-5f1e-9cd7-461d51c1c722", "block_to_id": "feb530dd-d138-526c-96b8-1f12f157c7ec", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Anti-Flap, Dedupe, and Hysteresis > Telemetry delay protection", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-83", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Anti-Flap, Dedupe, and Hysteresis > Telemetry delay protection", "content": "Telemetry delay protection\\n\\nIf telemetry ingestion delay exceeds 2x the evaluation window (e.g., >20 minutes), alert evaluation is suspended and a separate \xe2\x80\x9ctelemetry delay\xe2\x80\x9d warning is emitted to #eng-platform.", "score": 0.298681, "rank": 36, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}, {"chunk_id": "82e5de62-ab2f-52ee-a327-f8ae85a98506", "search_unit_id": "82e5de62-ab2f-52ee-a327-f8ae85a98506", "block_from_id": "f2167597-0d78-51c4-98ac-6e6b5709a336", "block_to_id": "ee939171-e136-5ca2-917d-48f955d2b50a", "section_path": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Default Thresholds (v1) > Throughput (tokens/sec)", "document_id": "c055d063-a555-5cdf-b541-fe036031cb1b", "document_version_id": "57c83493-8d9e-5467-903c-46c7977b91fb", "document_name": "confluence__dsid_a3f94972391244f38ef773c05926af83.md", "version_no": 1, "page_from": 1, "page_to": 1, "anchor": "h3-54", "heading": "Adr Perf Canary Baseline And Thresholds > Default Thresholds (v1) > Throughput (tokens/sec)", "content": "Throughput (tokens/sec)\\n\\n- Warning: tokens/sec **-8%** vs baseline for **2 out of 3** windows.\\n- Paging: tokens/sec **-15%** vs baseline for **3 out of 4** windows.", "score": 0.309129, "rank": 37, "source_id": "b17fa25ce7d34acab77e3ad6267b5159", "source_name": "Project b3086c26ae3c45b6b8710f3c"}], "events": [], "entities": [], "relations": [], "source_hits": [], "summary": "", "citations": [], "answer_status": "pending", "no_answe